window.FWN_BLACK_TECH_INTERNET_CAFE_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_BLACK_TECH_INTERNET_CAFE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":601,"title":"Chapter 601 - Time to Counterattack!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Damn! Damn it! Oh! The damn Thorn Flower and Flame Bird! Why don’t you use your hidden cards? What are you waiting for!?” Wiping the tea that he just spewed out on the desk with a paper towel, Luther tried to regain his composure, pacing in the room like an ant on a hot pan.","How could he show these battles to the public?!","“What are these people doing? Your opponents are only lowly barbaric natives!” Luther cussed in his room.","After calming down, he fixed his tie.","Among the families believing in the God of Radiant Light Judgement, the Thorn Flower Family and the Flame Bird Family were two elite families and had many unknown hidden cards.","It was time for them to unleash their full force.","In the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection, Luther saw ‘Land of Thorns’, the black-robed man who was as steady as land, slowly standing up.","At this moment, the level 9 black-armored knight Aude, the last knight guarding the palace, had unleashed his full force. With godly power, he had reached level 9, the pinnacle point of his strength.","If they continued to hide their strengths, they would be disgraced after the war regardless if they won or not.","At this moment, Luther finally saw something he liked.","The fighter covered in blood finally fell to the ground, and his body was covered in shocking sword wounds. Obviously, even with the blessing of a paladin, he, a warrior who had just reached level 7, was no match for a level 9 knight who had supreme power.","After breaking the neck of this maniac warrior, Godly Punisher Aude exhaled a sigh of relief. His bright armor became ragged, and he had a few wounds on his body. These were all disgraces for him.","He tossed away Gabriel’s blood-covered corpse like a broken sack.","“Sorry, everyone. We had a small problem with the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection, but it’s been fixed.” Finally, Luther released the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection again after a while. “Oh! Look at the insolent barbaric native! His impulsive behavior only lead to the capture of his companions since they are facing Mr. Aude.”","“Yes, this brave and fierce knight that you see in black dragon armor is Mr. Aude, the ‘Godly Punisher’! However, I think being captured might be a good fate for these natives.”","While was Luther babbling about the situation on the battlefield, many people on White Pigeon Square exclaimed, “Look! What’s that?!”","Gabriel, who had been silent and seemed dead, suddenly got up from the ground in a weird way.","Strengthened by dragon blood, he was more difficult to kill than ordinary people. Right now, his eyes were filled with crazy lights as if he couldn’t feel any pain.","When this man was on the verge of death, the endless potential hidden in his body crack open. The faint light from it merged with the huge blood essence and turned into a source of life.","Strangely, his deadly wounds were all healed.","Resistance to Death!","For some fighters, they would challenge their enemies even if it meant death. They pursued explosive and fierce force by sacrificing everything they had.","The closer to death they were, the greater strength they would have.","The berserkers who constantly flirted with death would gradually gain an instinctive ability to resist death.","The blood-red figure leaped up like a demonic god from Hell and hacked down his huge sword with whistles of destructive force.","Boom!","With huge metal-colliding noises, the super level 9 knight retreated a step!","Aude felt like he was facing a vicious fierce beast instead of a human.","“You are seeking death!” Aude’s face was wicked with fury; he was pressured into this state by a level 7 ant!","They were now very close. Condensing warrior energy in his left hand, he stabbed his fingers sheathed in hard knight gauntlet forward with vicious force.","Instantly, his fingers pierced his enemy’s chest.","At this moment, the middle-aged man in a blue robe behind Gabriel chanted something.","Fountain of Life!","The dimmed eyes suddenly emitted lights of life again.","“This man... can’t be killed?!” Seeing this, everyone roared in their mind. Even Aude felt impatient.","He was sure that the damages inflicted on his enemy were enough to kill ten level 7 fighters who were like this ant.","However, instead of being killed, his enemy launched fiercer attacks at him.","Endless blood essence condensed behind Gabriel and transformed into half a blade.","The blood-shadow-like sword moved so fast that it transformed into a huge curtain of blood, almost swallowing Aude whole!","“Maniac! He’s maniac! He will die! I’m sure he will die soon!” Luther shivered uncontrollably. Then, he saw on another battlefield that the shadow killer took out a parchment scroll that emitted dark presence. “You’ll die without regret since you forced me to use this godly spell scroll!”","“This is...” At this moment, even some people sitting in St. Heinz’ grand palace looked amazed. “This is...?!”","“Darkness Under the Godly Light! It’s Darkness Under the Godly Light!” Someone recognized it immediately. “It seems like the Thorn Flower Family is well prepared for the war!”","World Mage Hematon said with a nod. “With techniques, one can perceive the opponents’ positions from the slight changes in sounds and winds. The masters can sense others’ existences by sensing their energies.”","“This barbaric native now meets his nemesis in the Darkness Under the Godly Light.”","Darkness Under the Godly Light could deprive people’s five senses. According to the rumors, this powerful spiritual spell could even rob people of their senses of magical and spiritual energy. Even super masters couldn’t escape from it!","Now, they were using it on an ant who hadn’t even reached level 8.","The strange golden patterns on the foreheads of the dark judgement knights shined through the pitch-black armor.","The gloomy, mud-like presence flew out from the ancient parchment scroll. This force was chillier than anything in the world as if it were a soul-taking fierce ghost from Hell.","The force was stranger than anything in the world, and it was silent and invisible.","Crack!","Almost simultaneously, Zong Wu felt an extremely weird force striking him before he could react.","The extremely chilly force dragged him into a dark abyss almost instantly.","Around him, there were no light, sounds, or even wind. He felt like he was totally isolated from the outer world.","“This time, let’s see how you dodge our attacks!” This time, the knights only needed to deal with an ordinary person who had been dragged into a dark abyss.","They emitted horrifying energies as if they were knights in the light instead of killers hidden in darkness.","They didn’t need to hide anymore since they had deprived their enemy of his senses.","Only at this moment did Luther dare to turn the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection to this battle.","With four dark judgement knights dealing with a barbaric native warrior without his senses, Luther was sure of the outcome of the battle.","However, the moment Luther showed this battle to the public, the audience sitting in White Pigeon Square including the golden griffin knights and Sala saw horrifying sword energies condense and turn into wings of light behind Zong Wu!","He looked like Agni, who was proudly standing in the sky!","[TL Note: Agni is a Sanskrit word meaning fire and connotes the Vedic fire god of Hinduism.]","Wave Eye!","Although the players could instantly master techniques in the game, they must spend time to practice these combat techniques in the real world. Zong Wu had only understood half of this techniques by now.","After all, awakening skills were not so easy to master, even for Zong Wu who had one foot in the Grand Emperor Warrior Realm.","He had only mastered the Wave Eye!","However, it was enough for him.","The dark judgement knights stayed in the sky, and they unleashed horrifying sword energies which erupted up like a volcano; it seemed as if many cracks appeared in the sky, and the chaotic energy from the void was spilling into this world.","Zong Wu slashed out his sword leisurely, and the sword energy swept out like a vortex.","The scroll of godly skill was almost useless! All the dark judgement knights were instantly swept into the vortex of sword energies!","“How come it has no effect at all?!’ The people who knew the power of the scroll were truly astonished!","“AHH!” The White Pigeon Square was engulfed in gasps and shouts. It seemed like everyone in the world was watching this scene in which the asura stood proudly like a god in the sky with long wings spreading behind him!","“People of the Spiritual State, it’s time to counterattack!”","At this moment, the whole world was shocked. Counterattack?! These people are really going to fight back?!"]},{"number":602,"title":"Chapter 602 - War Weapons!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","The battles all over the huge battlefields were commanded through different communication methods.","These cultivators had their own communication methods either in the real world or in the games.","Inspired by StarCraft, they had improved their communication spiritual artifacts used in battlefields.","Obviously, Dajin’s army, the ancient families, major families, and independent cultivators of the Spiritual State had made detailed plans for the battles. They were morons.","Putting soldiers against soldiers and generals against generals was the most common way to battle. The six sky knights and three prophets, the most powerful subordinates of ‘Land of Thorns’, had encountered their counterparts.","Gu Tingyu was never a rookie commander, nether in games or in reality.","Despite some uncontrollable factors such as Gabriel and others attacking the godly palace in the sky, everything was in this old man’s control.","As a grandmaster, it wasn’t difficult for him to spread his spiritual senses around the battlefields with the aid of spiritual artifacts.","It wasn’t a coincidence that Zhu Yanxiao went to the rescue of the civilian warriors in the battlefield outside Dajin.","Therefore, it wasn’t an impulsive decision when Zong Wu said that it was time to counterattack.","Sitting in the flagship, Fairy Qing Yun calculated the unknown elements of danger that might happen on the battlefields with her slim and tender fingers. She looked chill and idle, and that wasn’t far from the truth.","“Oh! My spiritual essence is running low.”","She gulped down some iced red tea. After wiping the sweat off her forehead, she continued with her calculation.","The people working behind the scenes didn’t have time to fight on the battlefields like others.","During the battles, Gu Tingyu spread open scrolls of information about the enemies on the desk.","Comparing the intelligence reports sent to him from all battlefields, he could see that the enemies were the strongest on the Spiritual State Battlefield. After all, the Spiritual State had the most powerful cultivators and warriors across the whole continent.","...","“Counterattack?” The Thorn Flower Family and the Flame Bird Family had never imagined that these barbaric natives would dare or have the ability to counterattacks. ‘Land of Thorns’ was angered, and his expression was as chilly as ice.","Indeed, it was time for them to unleash a greater level of force.","With furious roars, lights flashed on the foreheads of the most powerful knights while a horrifyingly powerful force spread from their foreheads to all over their bodies.","The three prophets rose from the battlefield and formed a triangle-shaped array with shiny golden lights.","The sounds that they created seemed to come from the heavens. A hole suddenly appeared in the dense, gloomy clouds, and it seemed like the whole world was bathed in golden light.","The godly light shone on the land, and the knights and mages from the Judgement Godly Palace bathed in the light and were dyed golden.","The knights and mages had felt that their stamina and energy were running out. Now, they instantly felt that their strength was replenished and increased; they were even stronger than before!","Godly Spell! It was a Godly Spell of War!","“Godly power... This is indeed godly power!”","The knights of the Thorn Flower Family who had been forced to back off stopped their steps. Some of them raised their huge swords and shouted, “Attack!”","They charged forward fiercely.","A knight wearing silver armor with golden patterns shot forward before the others with an extremely fierce presence.","At this moment, Jiang Xiaoyue, stepping on a small sword, was about to charge forward with Yue Bai, Mu Qing, and Li Lanruo.","However...","“Ugh?! How come they are charging toward us again?!” Their enemies looked even fiercer and stronger than before!","Followed by several elite knights, the silver-armored knight charged toward the girls as if they were a flock of white sheep. He raised his huge sword and roared, “Judgement!”","Besides the girls, other fighters also encountered similar situations. The knights and mages looked like a turbulent golden river, intending to burst through the armies of cultivators and warriors.","As for the knights who were fighting with Vice Academy Master Zhang Hao and the ancient family masters, they had also grown stronger with the aid from that force.","“Oh! This is a great scene! Can anyone defeat such a legion?” Luther said with a calm smile.","In the next moment, Li Lanruo yelled, and a huge round shield of essence appeared around them as protection.","Meanwhile, Nen Guards appeared all over the battlefield like blooming lotuses with thousands of petals!","Like huge boulders, these Nen Guards resisted against the golden currents and split them into many sections!","“Weapon of Light!”","“Presence of Wind!”","“Dragon Tiger Roar!”","“...”","Lights flashed around these people one after another.","The overbearing knight struck his sword onto the Nen Guard. Meanwhile, Jiang Xiaoyue’s spear and Yue Bai’s sword emitted a wave of astonishing radiant light.","“Palm Blast”","“Light Shadow Strike!”","The girls unleashed explosive forces which were twice as powerful as before. The knights who just got close to attack were sent flying as if they were struck by huge hammers!","The weapons in the hands of the cultivators and warriors of Spiritual State had dazzling white light dancing on them. Fearless, they obtained footholds with the aid of Nen Guards, tearing that streak of golden current apart.","Meanwhile, the bugle signaling the counterattack sounded in the Deserted Sea Realm as well.","With sword energies flowing around her feet, Nalan Mingxue struck out with her Snow-Drinking Saber. The chilly blade was like a flash of light, and the silver-armored knight before her fell with horror on his face.","While laughing, Song Qingfeng swung out his flame-engulfed hot fist, sending a knight flying.","With ice bullets pouring from her hands, Xu Zixin was fearless on the battlefield.","A few years ago, they had been a group of innocent and clumsy young people. For most of them, today was their first time on a real battlefield.","“They are charging toward the grand palace hovering in the sky,” Nalan Mingxue said chillingly, “Should we battle our way to this grand palace as well?”","Land of Thorn Wilson in the Spiritual State Battlefield, Morning Star of Flames Austin in the Deserted Sea Realm Battlefield, and Alex who was in charge of the Morning Star Sea Realm Battlefield couldn’t remain calm anymore.","Their eyes turned cold.","“Since this is the case, I won’t show any mercy to these people.”","Buzz!","With a series of deep rumbles, rows of strange characters lit up around the muzzles of the three giant cannons on the huge stone palace. These characters seemed to be in the language used by gods and followed some natural laws.","A horrifying vortex of spiritual essence condensed at each black muzzle, and destructive magic light suddenly lit up inside the cannons!","Such huge cannons were activated not only in the Spiritual State Battlefield but in the other two battlefields as well!","Pitch-black muzzles aimed at Nalan Hongwu and the others who were charging forward as well as those cultivators of the Morning Star Sea Realm who were about to dash into the grand palace.","“They are really about to use these huge cannons! They are going to use the Destroyers!” Luther exclaimed, “Oh! These damn barbaric natives forced them to use these weapons!”","Obviously, they hadn’t planned to use such super war weapons, but now...","Damn ants, we’ll show you the real difference in power between us!"]},{"number":603,"title":"Chapter 603 - Misfire?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","There were certain ways to control what to see with the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection. For example, at this moment, it had zoomed out so that the audience could only see one side being defeated but wouldn’t see anything that was too hardcore and inappropriate to show.","At this moment, Luther turned the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection to the battlefield near Dajin in the Deserted Sea Realm.","– In the sky outside Dajin in the Deserted Sea Realm –","From the huge spiritual ships that were flying in the sky, cultivators rode on flying swords or demon beasts and shot out shiny sword energies and surges of essences. Meanwhile, the golden current continued to retreat.","Morning Star of Flames Austin flew up high into the sky. At his order, the huge black cannon that was as dark as an abyss was activated.","The huge cannon with a length of dozens of meters gave people a strong sense of suppression.","Destructive light began to gather around the cannon, and the force was so huge that even one-tenth of its power gave people a sense of doom.","While this force continued to gather, Nalan Hongwu, who was closer to it, could clearly see that space was being distorted by it.","He even suspected that this weapon could turn everyone here into ashes.","While the energy gathered at the muzzle, the cannon turned and aimed at the central area where the most elites were at.","He must stop the activation of this horrifying weapon!","The sword energy beneath Nalan Hongwu’s feet flashed, and he turned into a beam of light as he dashed toward the huge cannon!","“Stop him!”","Many elite knights tried to block Nalan Hongwu’s way.","This huge cannon was heavily guarded.","Besides, pure white lights flashed on the magic array disks around the grand palace, and several destructive white light beams crashed toward Nalan Hongwu!","Boom! Boom! Boom!","Stepping on his flying sword, Nalan Hongwu seemed to have shifted when the godly light beam struck down.","With a slight shift, he had shot through the destructive white light beams that almost formed a curtain!","He passed them intact!","“F*ck!?”","“Z-Shake?!”","Waves of exclamations instantly rose behind him.","In the blink of an eye, the white-clothed figure plunged into the knight legion, and the elite knights engulfed in golden light were forced to retreat!","Looking down from the high sky, the white-clothed figure cut through the huge army like a sharp saber!","The audience in White Pigeon Square happened to see this scene as well.","“My goodness!” The Elf Girl, Sala, watched the scene with widened eyes as she let out an exclamation.","“Oh! That’s awesome! Yeah!” The two figures hiding in the dark corner of White Pigeon Square never came out into the light, but it didn’t stop them from watching the battle.","With his shoulders shaking uncontrollably, the lean and short one seemed more excited than the audience members who were sitting in White Pigeon Square. “Oh! It’s time for these damn self-important guys to learn a lesson!","“The damn Flame Bird Family and Thorn Flower Family are receiving a pathetic defeat in the so-called barbaric natives’ land. They are being defeated in front of everyone! Hahahaha! I want to laugh when I think of their expressions now!”","“Ok. The war isn’t over yet. As much as I want them to lose, we must be patient and wait until it ends,” his companion said.","“Anyone who retreats will die!” Morning Star of Flames, Austin, let out a furious roar. Meanwhile, the two level 9 knights entered the fray.","Nalan Hongwu looked grim as if he were making calculations in his head.","The huge cannon began to take aim and was about to fire.","At this moment, Nalan Hongwu looked hesitant as if he knew that he couldn’t stop it anyway!","“It’s ready!” Austin, the Morning Star of Flames, sneered at the barbaric native who had intended to stop the firing of the huge destructive cannons. “You and your army will soon say goodbye to this world!”","“Oh! These damn people! Finally, we’ll give them a lesson!” Luther watched the scene excitedly. It was clear that the huge destructive cannon had finished gathering energy, and these damn barbaric natives would be turned into ashes in the next instant. After all, no one, not even themselves, could withstand such a strike!","“Fire!” Austin stared at Nalan Hongwu with a cold smile.","However, he saw Nalan Hongwu also giving him a cold smile.","Crack!","A loud noise sounded, but it wasn’t from the huge destructive cannon.","It was...","If the StarCraft players were here, they would recognize the sound. It was the sound of a ghost using the lockdown ability!","From a corner that no one noticed, a missile shot out with a sharp whistle.","Austin froze in mid-air.","He looked back subconsciously and saw that the area around the huge cannons was engulfed in a strange pale energy field.","The destructive energy that had turned bright in the huge destructive cannons dimmed and then vanished!","It misfired!","Lockdown missiles could cut off energy from all machines within its area of effect, including the Protoss carriers.","“No! Impossible!” Luther almost howled. Except for the godly artifacts described in legends, he had never heard of anything that could stop the huge destructive cannons from firing!","How can these barbaric natives have this stuff?!","Not far from the grand palace that was hovering in the air, some young people waved at the other fighters. Nalan Mingxue lifted her C-10 Mk. VI and placed it onto her shoulder with a smirk.","At this moment, no one in St. Heinz’ grand palace could remain calm anymore.","“What...is this?! A godly artifact?!” Morning Star of Flames Austin’s face became wicked and distorted.","“Is it... something left here from the ancient war?!”","“Impossible! How can they have such a thing!”","Princess Isabella was also surprised. “It seems that Mr. Heinz’s side will lose this war?”","“...” Even St. Heinz looked livid.","– In the group chat named Internet Café Army Against Outlanders –","Nalan Mingxue said, [Great teamwork!]","Nalan Hongwu replied, “<img class=\"emoji\" draggable=\"false\" src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/12.0.0-1/svg/1f601.svg\" alt=\"&#x1F601;\"> These morons! They didn’t even see that I was only distracting them with my attacks!”","Mr. Fang chimed in, [Awesome! Full score!]","Everyone added, [Full score! Full score!]"]},{"number":604,"title":"Chapter 604 - Withdrawal?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“You... are all seeking death!” The Morning Star of Flames, Austin, a super master who had reached level 9 without the aid of any godly power, was extremely furious.","“Do you think that’s all we have, and we don’t have more hidden cards?!” At this moment, he nodded at the black-robed old man beside him, and the latter took out a pale golden scroll.","“Summon Spatial Storm?!” Luther exclaimed, “They even brought out this scroll in this war?!”","When the scroll was taken out, even Nalan Hongwu sensed the great danger. But when he tried to fight his way to the old man, Austin blocked his path in person.","Austin lifted his huge sword, and a horrifying golden godly light beam shot up into the sky. “All of you will be destroyed.”","On the other side, three level 9 knights and several level 8 knights surrounded the old man to ensure that no one could get to him.","This time, they were determined not to repeat their mistake.","Blocking Nalan Hongwu, Austin thought that he had gotten everything in control, and no threat was left.","In the distant sky, a beautiful woman stood in mid-air with her dark hair and white skirt fluttering in the wind. She was surrounded by several knights of the Flame Bird Family who had extremely powerful auras.","Su Tianji’s fingertips released dazzling lightning energy that shined all over the sky.","Crack!","A thunderbolt cracked, and lightning energy danced like snakes, and all the lightning energy in the area started to gather around her!","Her chilly eyes stared at the black-robed mage who was holding the scroll.","Horrifying lightning energy gathered like dancing dragons and snakes!","...","“No! Another battlefield also has huge destructive cannons!” Seeing that the huge cannons was locked down, Luther lost his composure and frantically turned the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection to another battlefield.","In this battlefield, Alex and Rain of the Flame Bird Family were commanding the war.","They were aiming a huge cannon toward all the cultivators of the Morning Star Sea Realm.","“What’s this thing?” On the flagship, Duan Yue froze for a moment when he saw the cannon.","Reincarnation King, one of the four kings of Half City, said, “It doesn’t matter! Now that we’re fighting back, we don’t have to hide it anymore!”","Then, a strange-looking round mirror made of neither metal nor jade flew out from their spiritual ship on its own.","Heavenly Mirror!","Before the huge cannon could fire, the mirror released a beam of white light!","Different from the mimic that they had made in a hurry to deal with a big demon, the white light beam released from this mirror was several times more powerful than last time!","Made with all the resources in the Morning Star Sea Realm, this mimic of the Heavenly Mirror was almost perfect and could basically be considered a complete replica of the original!","The moment that the white light beam shot down, the huge cannon and everyone around it was frozen.","“This... this can’t be real! It can’t be real!”","Then, Luther turned the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection to the battlefield in the Spiritual State.","...","At this moment, Gu Tingyun nodded and said, “Take out the new spiritual artifacts that we just made!”","In a white robe, Gu Tingyun walked out onto the deck of the spiritual flagship.","The Tang Family Master nodded; he was one of the main artifact masters who produced the three spiritual artifacts.","Soon, the decks of the foremost giant ships opened, and three machines with a length of ten meters and a height of six meters slowly rose from the central deck.","Made with star-patterned godly iron, the machines had pale blue spiritual light flashing on the inside. At a closer look, one could see strange flowing patterns in the shape of an eight-trigram. A streak of strange runes spread out with flowing spiritual light to the body of the cannon, and the strange runes turned pale golden as rumbling thunder could be heard from the inside!","The Tang Family Master yelled, “Put in the Vital Magnetic Golden Arrow!”","Immediately, someone brought out a pale golden arrow covered in dense and complicated runes.","At this moment, everyone watching the war in White Pigeon Square were shocked, and their mouths opened wide, forming a perfect O-shape.","“My goodness!”","Crack!","A lightning bolt flashed in the sky!","At the same time, the three strange spiritual artifacts of the Spiritual State lit up with lightning energy!","As the rows of runes lit up, it could be clearly seen that an indigo lightning energy flowed in a circle, and the runes on both sides of the spiritual artifact lit up one after another, forming many lightning coils.","More and more lightning energy came in.","Crack! Boom!","A heavenly thunderbolt crashed down, turning everyone’s face white.","The thunder power squarely fell in the Eight-Trigram Disk which in turn emitted more dazzling spiritual light.","Hiss...","Many thick lightning snakes danced and jumped into the coils of lightning energy.","Fairy Qing Yun moved her fingers and calculated as she said, “Move left to Yuji Star Position; move right to Yaoguang Star Position...”","The three magical and mysterious spiritual artifacts adjusted positions at her instructions.","Both sides fired almost at the same time. Three destructive light beams shot out of the huge stone palace with horrifying energy that intended to devour everything!","While lightning bolts danced in the sky like snakes, three lightning beams shot through the sky like heavenly lightning punishments, looking like shooting stars. Then, they collided with the three horrifying beams of magic light in the sky.","Horrendous energy exploded in the mid-air while the destructive force spread out and turned all the members of the Thorn Flower Family in its range into ashes!","As if it were hit with a huge earthquake, the stone palace began to shake violently. While being shined on by the powerful light, the ground beneath the three huge cannons suddenly collapsed!","The horrendous momentum and energy spread out and squeezed the surrounding huge stones which began to move like waves and ripples. Streaks of miraculous golden runes lit up in the godly palace as if they were trying to withstand this streak of power, and they emitted horrifying presence.","Boom! Boom! Boom!","Then, the golden runes cracked and collapsed!","Boom!","A huge dust cloud surged up, and loud explosions shook the sky.","At this moment, everyone’s mind turned blank.","What is that?! Is it a godly artifact?!","But where did these barbaric natives get such a godly artifact?!","In the grand palace, Godly Punisher Aude was the only person guarding the palace, and he was disheveled with wounds all over his body.","The grand palace shook violently as if it would collapse any moment.","The ground cracked, and many boulders crashed down from the sky.","“Godly palace... How can it be?!”","While he was astonished by the scene, a flash of sword energy hacked toward him.","Phantom Slash!","With crazy roars, Gabriel hacked down his huge saber that was engulfed in blazing flames.","Containing endless fury and blood presence, the violent power shot out from the sword and pierced Aude’s body.","Beneath them, the ground exploded wide open and shattered, turning into scalding lava!","“Move!” The middle-aged man wearing the bright blue robe finally got the chance to rescue their king.","“Heehaa-!” Gabriel’s huge sword pressed down on the struggling Aude and pushed him into the surging lava which soon swallowed the latter in whole!","Meanwhile, on the battlefield outside Dajin, a bright light beam shot across the high sky!","Boom!","It crashed onto the old man who was opening the scroll. It swallowed everything in the area in an instant!","However, some of the horrifying power sealed inside the spiritual spell scroll leaked out.","In the next moment, the whole space seemed to freeze.","Then, a horrifying power suppressed the space!","Everything in space stopped moving. It seemed like time had stopped!","World-Ending Sword 23!","After spending lots of time to improve his control of the technique, Nalan Hongwu had gradually mastered Sword 23!","Almost instantly, the power from Sword 23 suppressed this leaked power!","“You... You!!” Everyone was stupefied at this moment.","They had regarded these barbaric natives as ants, but these ants turned out to be giant prehistoric beasts!","The lofty existences in St. Heinz’ grand palace had never been so astonished before!","“Withdraw! Tell them to withdraw!” St. Heinz issued the order with a livid face.","No one had expected St. Heinz to issue the order of withdrawal!"]},{"number":605,"title":"Chapter 605 - All of You Can Stay","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Oh! Are these people the weak and stupid barbaric natives they told us about?” For the audience in White Pigeon Square, the war was already over.","The Spiritual Spell Visual Projection had been turned off since they couldn’t show the frantic withdrawal of troops of two big families to the public.","“Oh! Didn’t they say that these people are filthy and despicable and live in an ignorant nation?” Stupefied, the members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion found that what they heard didn’t match up with what they saw.","They saw magnificent figures wearing white robes instead of armor on the distant and ancient land. The bloody, maniac-like figure dashing to the forefront of the battle, the miraculous godly mirror, the huge lightning cannons, and the white-clothed figure who forced tens of thousands of people to retreat with a sword...","They saw that in another continent, the people lived differently and had their own glamour. Those people were definitely not a group of ignorant people living in misery and waiting to be rescued.","“Oh! These damn people are using such despicable tricks to fool the ignorant citizens and beautify their invasion again. But obviously, their lies backfired this time!” In an alley behind White Pigeon Square, a figure wearing a cloak whispered to his peer.","“I praise those people. If our kingdom was half as strong as them, it wouldn’t have...” Another person said with envy and excitement, and he spoke louder and louder and attracted some attention. He quickly lowered his voice and added, “Oh, I’m sorry. I got a little too excited.”","“Let’s go, brothers. We’ll soon enter the battlefield. That damn big mouth monster, Luther, even said that he is going to bring the godly light to the elves...”","“This time, we must teach him a good lesson. They’ll get a taste of the power of our Underground Council!”","“I heard that our brothers of the council could have come here...”","“Oh! I wish for the arrival of dawn!”","“I hope we’ll say goodbye to the smelly sewers and hard black bread soon!”","“Hahaha! Your dream should be bigger, Brother.”","“Unlike you, I grew up in the slums...”","“...”","As they went away, their voices gradually disappeared in the alley.","At this moment, Mr. Fang who had been watching the war in White Pigeon Square was long gone.","...","For the cultivators of the Spiritual State and Deserted Sea Realm, the war wasn’t over.","“They want to run!” On the Spiritual State Battlefield, the space behind the almost ruined stone palace suddenly cracked open!","After these outlanders opened the portals, they just hid them instead of taking the time to seal them.","They didn’t expect that their act to save energy now became their saving grace.","The legion of the Thorn Flower Family deserted the huge palace and retreated to the dark void under the cover of the small stone arrays.","However, they saw a small golden battleship flying to them. It was the Corsair!","In the blink of an eye, that horrifying energy beam shot from the Corsair almost destroyed most of the magic stone arrays flying in the front!","Meanwhile, the spiritual ships behind the Corsair turned bright with dazzling light of spiritual spells, swallowing the flying objects left behind.","At this moment, the outlanders found that even withdrawal was a luxury that they couldn’t afford!","Without protection, no one could pass that portal alive!","At this moment, Land of Thorns Wilson turned into a colorful light beam. With his explosive godly power and extremely high speed, he got away from the many spiritual spells shot from the spiritual ships of the Spiritual State and the attacks from the Corsair, flying toward the tunnel in the void!","“Don’t let him get away!” Furious yells sounded on the battlefield. The cultivators of the Spiritual State would allow some ordinary knights and mages to escape, but they couldn’t let the evil leader go.","“Do you think that you can stop me if I want to leave?!” Wilson’s pale and slightly weathered face was vicious and distorted. “Do you want to fight with me to the death!?”","Unlike the others, he had reached level 9 without the aid of godly power.","He was a true level 9 super master! He didn’t believe that anyone in the world could kill him. If these barbaric natives tried to keep him here at any price, he could kill most of these damn people alone!","He still had some treasures which could help him dodge those heavy cannons and land on his opponents’ spiritual ships.","At least, he could kill most of the elite fighters on this battlefield.","Also, he was sure that these people had used up of all their hidden cards.","He was also sure that not every one of these barbaric natives wanted to fight with him to the death.","In fact, the Morning Star of Flames, Austin, had the same thoughts.","With his great power, he could see that Nalan Hongwu and Su Tianji had used lots of energy in the previous powerful attacks. They might not have enough energy to deal with him.","A gloomy sneer appeared on his face as he said, “Despite the order from Mr. St. Heinz, I think... we are not in a hurry to withdraw.”","After being defeated, he hated these damn barbaric natives to the guts. Seeing that Nalan Hongwu and the other masters had used lots of their energy, he was eager to take this opportunity to kill more people to vent his anger.","“I admit that you have enough strength to protect yourselves.” Hovering in the high sky, Austin stared down with cold eyes. “You can freeze space and have a spiritual spell that has similar power to those huge destructive cannons. I must compliment you for your abilities, but you barbaric natives are still stupid!”","He snickered and said, “You used all your strength to protect those... cannon fodders?”","“As masters, you must protect yourselves. After all, you can be called a master only when you’re alive,” Austin said with a sneer, “You’re nothing when you’re dead.”","When he spoke, the sky suddenly turned gloomy.","It began to drizzle even in the cold snowy mountains in the Ultimate West Realm, which was the Spiritual State Battlefield since it was on the edge of the border.","The rain was so chilly that Jiang Xiaoyue even sneezed.","“How come it’s so cold?!”","The gloomy clouds seemed to come from the dark abyss, and they condensed into two figures who were hidden in black robes; others couldn’t see their faces.","“I think all of you can stay.”","The two figures said simultaneously. Right now, one of them was in the Deserted Sea Realm, and the other was in the Ultimate West Realm."]},{"number":606,"title":"Chapter 606 - You Bunch of Noobs; Don’t Ever Come Again","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Black winds surged up like turbulent waves.","The Morning Star of Flames, Austin, turned his head and saw the big black robe that was fluttering in the crazy wind.","With a huge sickle in his hand, this figure looked like the God of Death from Hell.","Before Land of Thorns Wilson hovered a figure who seemed to be condensed from the falling raindrops.","Different from the black-robed figure before Austin, this figure looked slimmer, and her sickle emitted a dark golden light.","“What did you say?” Wilson looked as if he had heard a hilarious joke.","His strength was even greater than Austin’s; he was the strongest of the whole invasion army.","But now, he heard a barbaric native claim that they would keep him here?!","Even in his own continent fraught with masters, no one dared to say these words to him, let alone a place like this!","“That is...” At this moment, many Spiritual State cultivators and warriors froze in puzzlement.","“It seems to be Rosen Rain.”","“The person who won the championship in the F1 World Championship for Dungeon Fight Online!”","“F*ck! The champion of the E-sports competition shows her hand!”","“Tsk! Tsk! Tsk!” Wilson stared at the figure hidden in the black cloak. The presence emitting from the person almost reached level 9.","Meanwhile, Austin had also noticed that the big figure before him only had half a foot into the level 9 realm. Therefore, they were not slightly worried. “I don’t remember anyone lower than level 9 daring to speak so arrogantly to me!”","The moment he said it, Austin saw two beams of weird red light shooting out from the darkness below the hood of the cloak.","The figure reached out his hand, and the huge palm gradually turned dark-grey while his body expanded so much that his bulging muscles were about to burst out from his wide robe.","He pulled up his hood, showing Austin a horrifying scene. Under the hood wasn’t a human face; it was a scary demon’s face with two huge demonic horns on the forehead and two crimson-lantern-like eyes that could give people nightmares!","Snap!","His robe was burst open by the bulging muscles several times larger than that of humans, revealing steel-like dark-grey skin. His fingers slowly turned into sharp claws, and he let out a roar. This roar sounded like it was going to tear apart everything in the world.","Meanwhile, the tall and thin figure before Wilson also emitted a suffocating demonic presence.","The curvy figure and the long slim tail made this person look like a non-human.","They looked at the scene in horror. They had only borrowed godly power, but these two were real demons!","“My goodness!”","“The avenger has awakened?!”","“The mistress has awakened?!”","The cultivators and warriors of the Spiritual State and Deserted Sea Realm were stupefied by this scene, let alone the people in St. Heinz’s grand palace.","“What did you just say?” The deep, heavy voice seemed to shake the world when this person just spoke.","“No! Impossible! How can you barbaric natives...” On the battlefield at the Ultimate West Realm, before Wilson could finish his words, he saw a blood-red light flashing before him. Without seeing a movement from his opponent, he suddenly felt some pain in his lower body.","He looked down and saw an ugly wound after a blade cut through his fancy armor. Even the tremendous godly power and the power of laws that he comprehended himself couldn’t protect him!","The laws of nature that lit up around him instantly dimmed at the next moment.","Soon, someone posted a photo of this scene in the group chat.","“F*ck! First awakening plus Scud the Wrathful Demon?!”","“It’s a epic battle sickle! She really got it?!”","“No wonder she is the champion of the E-sports competition...”","“She shattered a sickle when she tried to reinforce it to level 14 in the livestream. Where did she get this one?”","The champion’s face twitched.","She almost went broke to make this weapon...","...","St. Heinz suddenly stood up from his chair.","“An existence of the saint level... Even if this person isn’t at the saint level, the saint level isn’t too far away from their reach! Also, she even has a powerful godly artifact?! These barbaric natives...” His squinted eyes had never looked so chilly before.","Others in the palace also looked gloomy.","“It’s a pity that she hasn’t reached the saint level.” With her wavy black hair reaching her waist, Princess Isabella’s exquisite and elegant face looked disappointed while she gazed at the projected screen. “Otherwise, she might have the ability to fight with me.”","In the Morning Star Sea Realm Battlefield, Alex and Rain, who were weaker than the Land of Thorns and the Morning Star of Flames, had been surrounded by fighters led by Ning Bi who was a female slayer with a demonic bloodline.","Meanwhile, the Morning Star of Flames, Austin, was at the disadvantage under the horrifying demon’s attacks.","Damn it! Damn it! Austin roared silently while the sharp claws left bloody wounds all over his body with moves too fast for him to detect.","At this moment, St. Heinz couldn’t bear it anymore.","In the battle, Austin suddenly saw a dazzling golden light appearing in the sky.","A white-robed old man with white hair and a long beard appeared in the holy light as if a true immortal had descended.","The projected image of Mr. St. Dulan? Austin was shocked.","St. Dulan was one of St. Heinz’s most important assistants!","Emitting holy presence, the old man suggested, “Shall we stop the war now? Let them go, and we’ll repay you to your satisfaction.”","Everyone looked at this figure in the light. Even the demon, who was clutching Austin’s neck with an arm that looked like a giant clamp, stopped moving.","Then...","Crack!","They heard the sound of a neck being broken.","The old man’s face instantly darkened. Seeing the scene, St. Heinz’s face dropped as well.","“Are you going to break everything and fight it out?!”","“Sir, you’re shameless,” Nalan Hongwu said with a chuckle, “Do you think that you can come and go at will?”","“The Thorn Flower and Flame Bird are only two subordinate families,” St. Dulan said in a cold voice, “Don’t think that you are powerful just because you won this small war. The realm of the true masters is beyond your imagination!”","Nalan Hongwu, Lan Mo, Su Tianji, and the others looked at each other and laughed.","“What are you laughing about?” The old man said chillily.","“They are laughing at your ignorance.” The demon had returned to his former self where he was covered in his black robe.","Su Tianji said, “I do nothing but watch TV Series and grow vegetables every day. If you can’t even defeat me, how can you brag about knowing masters?”","“Do you... have more powerful figures among you?” The old man looked at them in surprise.","“More powerful figures?!” Everyone in St. Heinz’s grand palace was dumbfounded.","Su Tianji took out her communication jade and said, “Sir, say something to them?”","Mr. Fang had almost fallen asleep right now. He replied as he suddenly opened his eyes, “What?”","“I think I’m not needed here.” Mr. Fang opened the chatbox and sent a voice message, “Damn it! You bunch of noobs; don’t ever come again.”","“Done.” Su Tianji clicked on her iPhone communication jade and chose the option to play the voice message on speaker. “This is his warning to you.”","Soon, Mr. Fang’s voice message sounded from the communication jade. “Damn it! You bunch of noobs; don’t ever come again.”","Everyone in St. Heinz’s grand palace fell silent. “...!!??”","St. Heinz’s face instantly darkened.","World Mage Hematon’s face darkened. “...”","Sword Saint Claus, “...”","Princess Isabella, “...”","They all looked livid.","Damn it!"]},{"number":607,"title":"Chapter 607 - Announcement of A New Game?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","The negotiation with the Continent of Immortal Relics failed. With their people killed, there was no need to continue the peace talk.","“You bunch of noobs; don’t ever come again?” The people in St. Heinz’s grand palace exchanged a look.","For one instant, they had the urge to kill people.","They could all see the shock and other complicated feelings in each other’s eyes.","“This damn arrogant barbaric native!”","“I’ve never seen such an arrogant and self-important man before!”","“Who does he think he is?”","“Damn it! Who will teach him a lesson?!”","Voices sounded in the grand palace, causing a mess.","At this moment, even people like the World Mage Hematon, who enjoyed a lofty status among the saint-level masters, said, “These people are indeed arrogant.","“But... they don’t know about Mr. St. Heinz or any of us in this palace. Therefore, I think their arrogance is understandable.”","Hearing his words, many people nodded in agreement.","“Well...” The woman wearing the crown yawned and said lazily, “Despite the surprises, I do find this war waged by St. Heinz quite interesting.","“It would be boring to watch a war with a predictable result.”","“You’re right, Your Highness.” St. Heinz obviously was suppressing his fury. It felt like he was never this furious before, but he hid it well.","His face turned livid after all the projected images disappeared from the grand palace.","He looked like a volcano that was on the verge of erupting after being dormant for 10,000 years.","“My Lord, what should we do now?” The white-robed old man asked him respectfully.","“The Thorn Flower Family and Flame Bird Family were arrogant and severely underestimated the enemies, causing the undesirable result of this war! They must be dealt with immediately!” St. Heinz’s cold voice resonated in the palace.","“How about Carl and the others...” The old man asked again.","“Tell people that they have been rescued. From now on, don’t mention it again. Put more efforts on the promotion of the new mystic realms.”","“Yes!” The old man knew what to do.","He said to a servant beside him, “Tell that Luther to keep a low profile for the time being.”","He believed that people would soon forget the whole thing.","...","For elf girls like Sala, the knights of Golden Griffin Knight Legion such as Helen and Elven, and ordinary mercenaries like Big Sword Crete, a cross-continental war was something very distant from their daily lives.","This war was something to talk about after eating but not a main event in their lives.","“I envy the people living on that continent... they can fly on swords and even grow wings made of swords. They even have the spiritual spell that can heal any injuries and wounds. It’s a magical, romantic, and elegant place!” Elf Girl Sala sat on a bench on the square and looked up at the sky. Some white pigeons landed on the back of the bench while another flew into her arms.","The sun was setting, and she was enjoying some rare break time.","“Do you think so, Ms. Helen?”","“I think their words are very philosophical.” Helen nodded and then copied the Nalan Hongwu’s words with a straight face, “Only sincere people can reach the pinnacle stage of swordsmanship!”","“He’s indeed a sword master!” Sala exclaimed, “He defeated an opponent who was one realm higher than him with only one sword strike. It’s unimaginable!”","“The people who dared to challenge Godly Punisher Aude are so brave!” Helen said in high spirits.","“Do you mean that maniac? It was so scary!” Sala covered her mouth and said, “For several times, I was worried that he would fail and die. I just can’t believe it...”","...","– Meanwhile, in the Yuanyang City Shop –","Two people of Ultimate West Realm were slowly walking toward the internet café while carrying a specially-made chair. The ‘brave warrior’ who the two girls had mentioned was now wrapped in white bandages with only his eyes exposed to the air.","Three janitors walked out of the shop with brooms in their hands.","They yelled, “Only three seats are left! Hurry up!”","“Ahh-” The man covered in bondage yelled, “Hurry! Hurry! There will be no seats for us if we don’t hurry!”","The two people of the Ultimate West Realm began to run with the chair.","Snap!","Snap!","The arms of this brave warrior bumped up and flipped around, dislocating themselves from their sockets again.","Behind them, Ebley’s face twitched, “No! The bones broke again...”","“Can’t we heal him with some spiritual spell...”","“We tried it many times; it didn’t work...”","“Ahhh!”","Pathetic screams sounded in the area.","When they walked into the shop, they saw a white-clothed fairy taking the last chair.","“Waiting for 1,000 years...” While humming, she began to watch the TV Series.","“...”","“Ahh-!” More screams rose.","...","For players in the Yuanyang City, Half City, and Jiuhua City, this war seemed to have little impact on their daily lives.","They continue to cultivate and kill Abyss Demons, doing things that they had been doing before the war.","...","Different from people in the old shops, the people in this new city regarded the game in the shop as an exquisitely-made mystic realm. Everyday, like the elves who had stumbled into the shop by accident, Joseph, Cia, and other young people who came in out of curiosity, and others with other intentions, many new players came into the shop.","...","At this moment, they saw a message jump out in the game.","In the group chat, they saw a link to the post-bar. After clicking it open, they found that it was an announcement about a new game.","“Assassin’s Creed?”","This game even had a cinematic trailer?!","“But... assassins?”","Subconsciously, many players frowned.","Even the players in the old shops were baffled about this new game.","Also, just release the game! Now with this all these cinematics, we can’t play...","The worst part of this was that they still clicked on the cinematics to watch it."]},{"number":608,"title":"Chapter 608 - Assassins Are like This?!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","In the most magnificent palace located in the center of the Capital of the Radiant Light Godly Nation.","Despite his fury towards the defeat of his two subordinate families in the war, St. Heinz controlled himself and didn’t do anything to disgrace himself.","After all, they were lofty existences looking down on ordinary people, not some losers who stayed in the godly palace all day doing nothing but wishing for victory.","In fact, it wasn’t the first time that they were defeated by another continent since they couldn’t send all the masters of the godly palace to the war. The Thorn Flower and Flame Bird were just two upper-level families who believed in the powerful God of Radiant Light Judgement.","Of course, it didn’t mean that he would forget this defeat.","“Let these clowns enjoy their victory for a while longer.” He inhaled deeply and turned his gaze to the map of the vast continent.","This man’s attention was on the whole continent instead of on a small setback. The result of one war couldn’t have a large impact on his plans for the future.","They had more important things to do. For example, they needed to bring godly light to places that it wasn’t shining on, such as the peaceful Silver Moon Forest.","For another instance, they were building a brand-new cultivation mystical realm with great efforts.","Yes, a cultivation mystical realm.","On this continent, the Alchemist Union wasn’t the only force that could make magic items for cultivation.","Inside the Radiant Light Godly Nation existed an alchemist workshop named the Dulan Workshop which belonged to the most powerful mage and alchemist under St. Heinz, St. Dulan. He was also the person who had been sent to negotiate with the Continent of Immortal Relics with his projected image.","It was one of the most famous workshops for making cultivation mystical realms on the continent.","Their cultivation mystical realms focused on realistic combat. Some of them had been derived from combat in the real world, which ranged from small ones such as hunting down magical beasts and scouting in war to big ones such as wars between nations or all over the continent.","They usually promoted the new mystical realms by using geniuses of the younger generation such as Jessica, Carl, and Kevin, who looked bright and elegant.","Although they always added propaganda content about the radiant light of their god in the cultivation mystical realms, these mystical realms were of high quality and were exquisitely made, and thus they were the most popular ones among fans of cultivation mystical realms despite their disapproval of certain contents.","The radiant image of the Judgement Godly Palace had been gradually established in the public view this way.","Even some people in the Morning Light Empire believed in the God of Radiant Light Judgement.","...","Different from the players in the old shops, for the players in the new shop such as Elf Girl Sala, the mentioning of assassins would conjure up the images of pathetic people who hid in the shadows while wearing filthy rags.","They were fugitives, criminals, and despicable villains who sneak-attacked people.","Of course, for elves such as Sala who had lived more than one hundred years, they had never seen any assassins who were rumored to be as lowly as mice.","In fact, Helen, who came from an aristocrat family and was a member of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion, hadn’t met any real assassins either.","They only heard about these despicable people who did nothing but sneak-attack people from the gossip of knights and other people.","They harbored an instinctive dislike for assassins.","That was why few people clicked open the cinematic trailer of Assassin’s Creed even though there were many players in the new shop now.","Only a few of them including Sala and Helen clicked it open due to curiosity.","...","While these girls were watching the cinematic trailer of Assassin’s Creed, a real assassination was taking place in the godly palace of Gray Eagle City, a neighboring city of Canglan City.","Wearing a luxurious red fur coat, Luther strolled into the grand palace flanked by his envoy group.","The priests around him bowed to him in respect.","He looked so lofty that it seemed like he was a king inspecting his own kingdom.","“Mr. Luther, welcome!”","At this moment, these assassins had just sneaked into this palace.","Why didn’t they assassinate this man on his way here? The high-level officials of the godly palace traveled only through magic arrays or with magic flying items, which made it highly difficult to intercept them.","As rumors claimed, these assassins were plainly dressed, and some of them were dressed like ordinary mercenaries.","They were not as filthy as the rumors said, but they were not doing much better.","Right now, they were hiding in the dark corners outside the godly palace.","“Can we really accomplish this feat?” A young voice sounded a bit anxious.","“Oh! There are many traps here; we must be very careful.”","...","At this moment, Sala and Helen, who were watching the cinematic trailer suddenly covered their mouths while intently staring at their screens; they almost exclaimed.","Before them was a vast land dotted with many buildings and eagles flying high in the sky. A white-robed figure stood on the edge of an extremely high bell tower, and the clean white robe made the figure radiate the grace of a scholar and the elegance of a priest.","That figure was alone and proud like the eagles that were soaring high in the sky. The white pointy hood added a special mystery to the figure.","He spread out his arms and leaped down from the high bell tower like a free eagle!","“We work in the dark to serve the light.”","The scene before them changed as the nine words were left in the darkness.","It was only a split-second video clip, but they were shocked. Is this guy an assassin?!","How can they assassinate their targets wearing white robes in the dark night?!","After all, assassins are people who sneak-attack from behind. Why are they talking about the light? !","The two girls only clicked in here due to curiosity, but they were now hooked and continued watching subconsciously.","The Vast sky and land appeared before them again.","That eagle freely flew through the snowy mountains and jungles and dashed into the prosperous city.","The scene changed, and the freely flying eagles seemed to have transformed into assassins wearing white robes with pointy hoods. Like eagles, they moved above the city.","Then, they jumped down from the high sky. When they lifted their heads, Sala and Helen didn’t see darkness but the light of freedom in the eyes of the assassins.","Yes. This was the light that the assassins believed in. They fought for freedom, and their firm gazes never wavered.","“Oh! My goodness!”","They couldn’t believe that these people were assassins!","..."]},{"number":609,"title":"Chapter 609 - The Release Date Is Not Set?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","While slowly walking toward the center of the palace, Luther talked with assurance, “Do you know why I’m never worried about being assassinated?”","“Mr. Luther.” Another old man in a priest robe said respectfully, “This city has activated the highest-level anti-spatial magic array. Even the Nimble Spirit of Cat, the spell that mages use to increase their ability to leap, can’t be used in the city. I’m sure that no assassins can enter this palace.”","...","Meanwhile, Sala and Helen were watching the assassins in the trailer climbing and jumping between tall towers and city walls like nimble cats. “They look powerful, but are these moves... useful? After all, true masters can fly!”","...","In the grand hall of the godly palace, the luxuriously dressed Luther held a tall glass of red wine. “Tsk, tsk, tsk! Sir, your eyesight is too low. In this palace, there are many magic traps made by our highly skillful mages. Even mages can’t find them with spiritual detection.”","“I assure you that before those lowly people can see me, they will be...”","He made a gesture by opening his hands and said, “Bang! Do you understand, sir?”","...","At this moment, Sala and Helen saw this scene. The visions of the assassins turned pale grey. In the pale grey world, some figures and objects became bright and stood out!","“My goodness! What’s that?!”","...","Luther sipped his wine with enjoyment as if he had totally forgotten his previous displeasure.","“I heard that those damn lowly mice are promoting our defeat in the invasion.” He snickered and then turned chilly. “I think it’s time to teach them a lesson!”","At this moment, a few assassins sneaked into the grand palace with great efforts.","Suddenly, their expressions changed drastically. “No! Ambush!”","“One can only use godly spells and godly power in this palace. All other forms of energies are suppressed.” Luther revealed a chilly smile. “Catch them all! They can’t get away!”","...","Meanwhile, Sala and Helen watched the assassins in the trailer silently fall from high places and hit their targets with precision. Then, they vanished into the crowds without a trace.","“Nothing is true, everything is permitted.”","The screens dimmed, and only six words remained before them.","They were shocked.","From these scenes and video clips, they saw assassins who were totally different! At least totally different from the ones in their mind!","Are these people assassins?!","How are assassins like this?!","At this moment, their minds were filled with the assassins who wore white robes and flew freely like eagles.","Their kills... No, those shouldn’t be called kills since their smooth combat techniques looked as beautiful as a dance.","They traveled through in the shadows in the darkness and resisted the templars, who craved for the holy items, the Pieces of Eden, and tried to control people’s mind and freedom with these items. This felt very different compared to those assassins who slaughtered the innocent.","The girls almost couldn’t believe their eyes. Due to this short trailer, they had a totally different image of assassins in their minds.","It seemed like the trailer didn’t show them the assassins of this time but another group of people in another time and space.","Eager, Sala walked to the counter and asked, “Sir, where is the entrance of the mystical realm named Assassin’s Creed?”","“Ugh?” Mr. Fang glanced at the elf girl who had exquisite facial features and wore a set of pale green leather armor. “It’s not released yet.”","“When will it be released...” The cinematic trailer had piqued her interest, and she was eager to try, but the shop owner told her that it wasn’t yet available?","“Um...” Mr. Fang explained, “The release date is not decided. If I have information about it...”","He pointed at the small blackboard behind him. “I’ll write it on the board.”","“What?! It’s not released?!” Helen was also frustrated.","– Meanwhile, in the old shops –","Su Tianji was lounging on a couch. “I just finished the new episodes of Legend of the White Snake. I’m bored and want to play new games.”","As an idle and lazy player, she mainly watched TV Series and grew vegetables. In fact, there were more people like her in the shops.","Fairy Qing Yun was one of them. Different from the addicted and moronic players such as Gabriel who came to the shop to deplete his fatigue points and use the horns to shout in the world channel even in bandages, they didn’t care to focus all their attention on one game.","For some people, they could obtain cultivation strength and combat experience by playing anything they wanted in the shop; they didn’t think it was necessary to stick to one game.","“Master! Master!” Fenghua and Yuexin joined her on the couch. “Did you watch the trailer for Assassin’s Creed?”","“Of course!” Hearing of mentioning of the new game, Su Tianji brightened up.","She sat up and said solemnly, “According to my years of experience with games, I’m sure that we can learn that strange way of intuitively sensing things. With this skill, we’ll be much safer when we enter and adventure in relics.”","After all, few spiritual spells or arrays could provide them with a sixth sense.","“I wonder what treasure the Pieces of Eden are...” Fenghua said, “It can even control people’s mind; it’s scary!”","“As for that...” Su Tianji picked up her communication jade.","[Sir, when will you release this game?!<img class=\"emoji\" draggable=\"false\" src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/12.0.0-1/svg/1f620.svg\" alt=\"&#x1F620;\">] She had been enthralled by the free leap of faith in the sky and the smooth assassination moves.","As an elder of great talents, she had never assassinated people before.","She was eager to try it.","Mr. Fang glanced at the progress of the task.","Damn it! The number of players in the new shop is still low, and there are still no assassins in the shop yet. The release date...","“It will be released this year!”","“Pu-!” She felt like killing someone."]},{"number":610,"title":"Chapter 610 - The Small Shop That No One Will Visit","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","On this continent, no one liked assassins; they were instinctively repulsed by them.","The kind and elegant elves who loved life and freedom had the same feelings about assassins.","The assassins had no faith and wouldn’t be blessed by gods.","They were like the outcasts of the world. In the courtyard inside the Judgement Godly Palace in Gray Eagle City, the blood-colored setting sun shined on the figures who scrambled away with wounded bodies, putting an end to this failed assassination attempt.","...","– The next day, in Canglan City –","Cute pigeons always gathered on White Pigeon Square. Fearless of strangers, they rested on the shoulders of people who sat around on the square. The people here were good to these birds and would bring some grains with them to feed these cute creatures.","“Oh! I’m sorry, brothers.” In an alley outside White Pigeon Square, a figure stood in the shadow habitually. He watched the bustling crowds on the square in a daze.","His eyes looked helpless and sad. After praying to an unknown god silently, he hurried away.","...","A red-haired woman sat on a long bench on the square with the balmy breeze brushing her pale face under the sun. She raised her hand to fix her hair that was being fluttered by the wind while the white pigeon flapped its wings and left her palm.","...","Elves usually lived much longer than humans.","That was why they seldom made friends with humans. Except for the true masters, their friendships were usually established with the old and dying human seniors.","Elves had always hated wars and killing. However, they weren’t brainless and didn’t oppose it all the time. When it was necessary, they would pick up swords and protect themselves.","Sala was calculating the days before her return.","I wonder if this damn small shop will release Assassin’s Creed before I go back, she thought resentfully. She had never seen a shop that showed things but wouldn’t let customers buy it.","“Does the owner know how to make money or not?” She stomped her foot in a huff, deciding that if the shop didn’t release the game before she returned to Silver Moon Forest, she wouldn’t give her money to this shop.","Humph!","...","The mercenaries of the Mercenary Union were a big group of ordinary people whose spending level wasn’t too low. Therefore, they were probably the biggest group of customers of cultivation mystical realms.","They also visited some little-known cultivation mystical realms for the lower prices, which was something that aristocrats wouldn’t do.s","At this moment, a few mercenaries walked out of the tavern of their union.","The news that a small shop was going to release a mystical realm featuring assassins had become a popular topic among them.","“Hey! Did you hear that a small shop in the city will release a new mystical realm focusing on assassins?”","“Assassins? Are you sure? Does the shop owner hope that assassins will enter his mystical realm for cultivation?” a mercenary laughed.","“If any assassin dares to show up, I’m afraid that this person will be kicked out of the city before he can enter the shop,” another person said with a smirk.","“By the way, I heard that the Dulan Workshop is going to release a new cultivation mystical realm soon.”","“Are you sure?”","“Of course. I went to the area near the godly palace yesterday and heard lots of news.”","“Should we go and check it out?”","“Sure. Let’s go now.”","...","In fact, not only mercenaries but the lofty knights of Golden Griffin Knight Legion were anticipating the new mystical realm that would soon be released by Dulan Workshop, even though they couldn’t see the beautiful Ms. Jessica and the elegant Mr. Carl this time. After all, they had all become janitors in an unknown small shop.","People had great expectations toward this new mystical realm.","They came very early and waited in the grand hall of the godly palace.","“Oh, I admit that the cultivation mystical realm in Origins Internet Café is excellent, but the quality of the products of Dulan Workshop is always guaranteed.” Legion Commander Elven shrugged and said, “We must come here and check it out.”","He seemed to be murmuring to himself, but it also seemed like he was talking to Helen and the other knights of the legion.","At this moment, a middle-aged man wearing a priest robe was presenting something with great passion in the front of the hall.","“I think this is the best cultivation mystical realm that our Dulan Workshop has ever built.” In the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection, a bright-looking young man was sitting cross-legged on a strange stone array disk which emitted pale blue light that followed complicated patterns.","It seemed to be the inside of a tower, and there were stone steps leading up.","While the array light flowed, the scene before the audience gradually became a vast forest as if they had been teleported to the forest. Beyond the forest, people could see the vague outer shapes of a big city and godly palaces. It looked extremely real.","Of course, only big workshop such as Dulan Workshop could make such exquisite scenes. No other cultivation mystical realms could do the same.","“As you know, there are many excellent mystical realms in Canglan City. Are you sure that the new mystical realm can stand out from the rest?” A mage of Alchemist Union stood with the white-robed man.","“Of course. I believe that this mystical realm will create a new trend in the entire city,” the middle-aged priest introduced the mystical realm with great passion.","“It’s said that this new mystical realm has some contents on how to deal with assassins?”","“Yes. The anti-assassination portion of the new mystical realm is taken from a classic anti-assassination battle. You’re right; it comes from the attempted assassination of Mr. St. Dulan. I believe it will teach people who cultivate in this mystical realm how to handle the sneak-attacks of those stealthy people.”","“In this anti-assassination battle, can we choose to be a participating knight and even execute the whole anti-assassination plan?”","“Of course.” The middle-aged priest said naturally. “We always strive to do the best.”","“What do you think of the rumor that a shop in the city plans to release Assassin’s Creed?” Obviously, the news about the imminent mystical realm featuring assassins had spread to this high-level official of the Alchemist Union.","“Assassins?” The middle-aged man in the priest robe said with a smile, “Do you guys think anyone would want to become a filthy and pathetic person who can only sneak-attack from dark corners?”","His words instantly made a lot of people laugh.","“I think the creator of that mystical realm is probably crazy; I don’t think people will visit such a shop.”"]},{"number":611,"title":"Chapter 611 - An Assassination in Daylight?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","When the morning sunlight shined through the glass door, Mr. Fang wrote down the second cinematic trailer of Assassin’s Creed on the small blackboard.","A mystical realm focusing on assassins...","It made many people doubt the sanity of this ‘creative’ alchemist.","After all, making a mystical realm cost a big fortune.","Even enough it was made by the System, a ton of the crystals that the shop earned was invested into this project.","In fact, it wasn’t unheard of that some big alchemist workshops went bankrupt when they couldn’t earn back the great sum of money that they had put into the creation of mystical realms.","Even the Dulan Workshop, which was supported by the powerful Judgement Godly Palace, didn’t dare to do anything outrageous except for adding some extra content about the godly palace.","However, a new shop in the city planned to release Assassins’ Creed?","Almost everyone who heard the news felt baffled.","They were sure that this alchemist was crazy.","However, it seemed like the shop wasn’t affected by all the rumors.","...","“Ms. Elina, did you hear that?” In a tavern not far from White Pigeon Square, a middle-aged man with short hair and a short beard said in a low voice from a corner.","If they listened carefully, they could hear some people in the tavern talking about something like Assassin’s Creed.","“Assassin mystical realm? Creed?” Elina was exasperated. “What does these people know about assassins?”","They even came up with something like... Assassin’s Creed?!","How come I didn’t know that we have a creed of some sort?","However, she didn’t have time to think about this.","“I’m afraid that the assassins in the Morning Light Empire won’t recover for a long time,” she signed as self-blame appeared in her bright eyes.","“Don’t blame yourself, Ms. Elina. You’re the ‘Rose of Moon’ and have a noble bloodline. You’re here to lead the assassins to fight against the damn Judgement Godly Palace. If you lose confidence...” The middle-aged man shook his head and said, “I think all the assassins in this area would be doomed.”","Elina shook her head, feeling a bit lost.","Her heart seemed to sink into the bottom of a dark abyss. Perhaps the assassins would never see light again.","...","However, Big Sword Crete and Mage Lily, who had watched the first trailer of Assassin’s Creed had different thoughts about the game.","“Oh! This is awesome!”","“I can’t believe that assassins are like this!”","Hearing the gossip in the tavern, Crete said, “I think it’s time to show these ignorant people the assassins in the shop!”","“Is the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection ready, Ms. Lily?”","...","“In fact, I think the shop owner is crazy as well!” In only a few days, the news that the shop would release an assassin mystical realm had spread all over the city. As a player of this shop, Elvin, the Commander of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion, felt ashamed.","Coming into Origins Internet Cafe during the casual time in the evening, Elven plunked down on a computer chair and sipped from his cup of milk tea. “I admit that Resident Evil is awesome, and the milk tea is delicious, but it’s true that no one would want to play as those damned assassins. There’s no market for it. Oh, I can’t even tell my peers that I visit this shop’s cultivation mystical realm every day.”","The moment he said that, he saw a white-robed figure leaping down from a bell tower like a white eagle flying in the sky on Helen’s screen.","“What is that?” Some members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion immediately looked over.","“Is it another game?”","On the other side, Sala was talking to her elf friends. “The shop released a new trailer for Assassin’s Creed. Should we watch it?”","Meanwhile, in the tavern where Elina was sitting in, a Spiritual Spell Visual Projection appeared, showing the same scene as in the shop.","They could vaguely see the screen of a computer. Obviously, the projection was aimed at a computer screen.","“??? Assassin’s Creed?!” Everyone froze.","Eating spicy sticks, Helen was watching attentively.","On Helen’s screen, the assassin wearing a white robe with a pointy hood ambled through the crowd and walked up the execution platform.","Seeing this scene and recognizing that this figure was an assassin, everyone thought that he was going to rescue the person who was about to be executed.","No... Is he really an assassin?! Then why is he wearing a white robe and walking up in front of everyone?","Shouldn’t he sneak up from behind his enemies?","Is this assassin here to seek his death?","While people thought that this assassin was here to commit suicide, they saw the white-robed assassin using a longsword and hand crossbow, knocking down several soldiers around him. Then, he leaped into the air like a soaring eagle, shot down the last enemy with a hidden blade, and left without a trace.","With great skills and clean, crisp movements, he ended the battle before the audience could understand what was happening.","When the audience snapped back to their senses, the white figure had vanished into the crowd.","“Pu-!?”","Is he really an assassin?!","Shouldn’t these assassins excel in stealth abilities and utilize their great skill in sneak-attacks?","How come this person just walked up under everyone’s gazes and finished the mission with a few smooth movements?!","The audience saw a type of high-level skill in the trailer.","At the same time, the people’s blood-boiling passion and heroism were ignited by the assassin’s ability to kill enemies with ease and vanishing without a trace.","They didn’t really understand what assassins were, but they had a strong urge to watch more of it.","“What’s the creed that you mentioned before?”","“Nothing is true. Everything is permitted. You must understand that we’re executors of our own actions, and we must take the consequences of our acts, regardless if it brings us glory or a tragic ending.”","The figures getting ready for the mission flashed on the screen, and every viewer who saw this was stunned.","“These are the creeds passed down from our ancestors. One, stay your blade from the flesh of an innocent. Two, Hide in plain sight. Three, never compromise the Brotherhood.”","“Take these as your creed. You can follow it and obey it. If you break it, you must bear the consequences.”","The conversation accompanying the trailer talked about the creed of this ancient organization. They were strict but not rigid; they had their own codes of conduct."]},{"number":612,"title":"Chapter 612 - The Whole Place Is Stunned","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“These assassins...?!” Watching these scenes, Elven had a vague feeling that they could accept assassins among them, just not the ones who were filthy and despicable as described in the rumors.","They couldn’t accept the unruly assassins who were always related to deaths and all kinds of filthy business.","In the tavern, Elina suddenly covered her mouth as disbelief appeared in her eyes.","She stared at the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection without blinking.","Only real assassins could understand this feeling.","“Rise, assassins!” The assassin on the screen was standing on a high mountain peak while looking into the distant snowy scenery.","“If you value life and freedom, then follow our call and battle in this chaotic age with us!” The eagle flew to the distance, leaving behind a long and piercing roar that resonated in the high sky!","At this moment, the assassins who happened to watch the trailer in the tavern stood up subconsciously with clenched fists.","“Oh! It’s awesome!” Even the elves looked stunned. After all, life and freedom were the things that they valued the most!","At this moment, the music became loud and passionate. The white-robed assassins moved with leisurely elegance while their enemies fell one by one under their excellent combat techniques and killing skills.","“Never give up.”","“Work together!”","The assassins on the screen all unsheathed their hidden blades.","“Everyone’s equal before hidden blades!”","“Oh! Brothers, do you see this?” Having grown up in a slum, the Assassin called Harrison had also participated in the previous assassination.","Clearly, they had failed, failed miserably.","For a while, Harrison felt like he was indeed as lowly and despicable as the mice that people described them as.","He felt weak and powerless, yet he always dreamed about doing the impossible.","Once, he had been lost in the darkness.","But after watching this Spiritual Spell Visual Projection, he felt a fire beginning to burn inside him all of a sudden.","He had never imagined that assassins could look so glorious!","At this moment, they felt like shouting.","Meanwhile, Elven, the Commander of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion, wondered, Oh. If every assassin was this self-disciplined, how much more trouble would we have?!","The freedom-loving elves looked as if they were in a daze.","They had seen an emotion that they had never thought that an assassin could possess. It wasn’t humbleness or lowliness but pride for being an assassin!","They had never imagined that assassins could have such an emotion.","Meanwhile, the freedom-loving elves couldn’t help but feel proud for these assassins, especially when they saw the assassins leaping down tall buildings like birds.","The things that these assassins pursued were the same things that the elves loved.","Sala even had the urge to join these assassins.","“Unbelievable...!","“After this Assassin’s Creed is released, I must try it!” She vowed silently with clenched hands.","“Where’s this small shop?!” Long after the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection had ended, Elina snapped back to reality.","In fact, she was worried that her interest in the game would expose her identity.","At this moment, she found that almost all the mercenaries and mages in the tavern had stood up, and they asked, “Is this Assassin’s Creed? Are these people assassins?”","This visual projection might be a prank, but they didn’t care to find out who did it right now.","In fact, most of them had never seen assassins before. In their mind, assassins were despicable. But now, this image changed drastically in their minds.","In the past, assassins represented filthy mice in their minds. But now, the assassins were elegant, mysterious, and highly skillful with combat techniques... the assassins were like pure white eagles!","“I want to try Assassin’s Creed. Tell me where I can try it!” a short and lean mercenary said eagerly.","In his team, he was a scout. He believed that this mystical realm would greatly benefit him.","“Please tell me too!” A mage stood up. Then, he saw many people glancing at him, wondering why a mage wanted to try this mystical realm.","“Of course, I’m not an assassin.” He scratched his head in embarrassment. “I just want to know what these people are really like.”","“Me too!”","“Count me in!”","Driven by curiosity and the interest of their peers, many people decided to follow the trend.","“...”","Elina and the other assassins in the tavern were dumbfounded by the scene.","It was a scene that they had never seen before. In the past, they would leave immediately when so many people stood up since it only meant that they were in trouble.","But now, to their astonishment, so many people were willing to learn about assassins.","Mercenary Crete and his companions who started all this was shocked. They were surprised that the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection of the trailer of Assassin’s Creed caused such an uproar.","“Oh! So many people...” Crete suddenly exclaimed. “Hurry back to the shop! Otherwise, there won’t be seats left for us!”","...","– Inside Origins Internet Café –","Mr. Fang was playing Resident Evil on the computer that was close to the counter.","The business was moderate in the shop. There were a few customers and not many.","Suddenly, a large group of people swarmed in.","“Shop owner? Where’s the shop owner?”","Mr. Fang saw a red-haired girl rushing over with red eyes before slamming her hand on the counter. “Tell me where the shop owner is!”","“I’m here, I’m here.” Mr. Fang exited the game and walked to the counter. “You guys want to get online?”","“I want to try that Assassin’s Creed!”","“I want to try Assassin’s Creed too!”","“So do I!”","“Me too!”","At this moment, everyone was staring at Mr. Fang expectantly.","Mr. Fang waved his hand and said, “Assassin’s Creed isn’t released yet.”","“...”","“When will it be released?” Elina looked frantic as if she wanted to grab Mr. Fang and force him to release the game.","“This... maybe this year.” After all, Mr. Fang couldn’t recognize the assassin even if they stood before him.","“This year?!”","“Maybe?!”","“What did you say?!”","Their voices were louder than the next.","At this moment, even the peace-loving Elf Girl Sala had the urge to rush over and strangle the shop owner."]},{"number":613,"title":"Chapter 613 - Assassin’s Creed I","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Seeing people swarming into the shop. Mr. Fang knew that it was probably time to expand the space inside the shop again.","As for when to release the game...","He glanced at the task list and found that the requirement for assassins visiting the shop had been met.","Right now, many players who had come for Assassin’s Creed began to play Resident Evil 2 while waiting for the release of the new game. Some of the visitors couldn’t even squeeze into the door. Besides, many passersby also tried to get in due to curiosity.","From the looks of it, after the space was expanded tomorrow, the other part of the task requirement would be met.","On the next day, even though the shop’s capacity had been expanded to 1,000 computers, there were way more customers compared to the day before.","Different from the old shops, the people here were only mildly surprised at the expansion of the space in the shop. They only thought that the shop owner had a powerful background and weren’t shocked.","In fact, the Alchemist Union had a similar setup. If necessary, the Judgement Godly Place could achieve this as well. As for the Royal Clan of the Elves, they had their own independent small plane.","Therefore, when Sala entered the shop, she didn’t pay much attention to the space expansion.","Smoothly, she bought a bowl of instant noodles and poured in hot water before adding a sausage in it. Then, she looked at the despicable shop owner and thought, Will you release Assassin’s Creed today?","Harrison came into the shop early today. As an assassin who grew up in the slums, he never lacked the character of hard work.","With short gray hair, this man looked to be about 50 years old. Dressed plainly, he looked like a simple farmer instead of an assassin if he didn’t talk.","In fact, everyone who escaped from the intricate traps in the godly palace after that failed assassination attempt were all excellent assassins.","Comparatively, Elina, who was sitting across from him on a couch looked quite different. She always sat straight and gracefully, giving people the impression that she would never do anything impolite in any occasion.","Of course, no one knew that this red-haired woman who was busy eating spicy sticks was the famous ‘Rose of Moon’ who had successfully assassinated a high-rank priest.","“Ah-!” While she ate spicy sticks, she heard Sala’s exclamation.","Sala had just noticed the words [Trailer 2] had been erased from yesterday’s announcement of [Assassin’s Creed Trailer 2] on the small blackboard.","They were replaced by the number [1], and the announcement now read [Assassin’s Creed 1].","“Ahh-!” She yelled again as if she couldn’t believe what she had seen. “Assassin’s Creed is released?!”","“What?!” Elina also exclaimed on the spot, almost dropping her spicy sticks. She had been sleepless last night with excitement after watching the trailer, wishing that she could sleep on the floor of the shop until Assassin’s Creed was released. To her astonishment, the game was released today!","“Really?!” Many people looked over in disbelief.","Meanwhile, the players in the old shops were also eagerly anticipating the release of Assassin’s Creed since they hadn’t had new single-player games for a long time.","At the same time, they encountered trouble on the highest difficulty level of Resident Evil 2. Some of them could pass the ordinary difficulty level with a dagger, but not the high difficulty level. Trying to pass the highest difficulty level with only a dagger was too depressing.","That was why Nalan Hongwu was a bit idle these days. Song Qingfeng was even more so.","As for Mo Xian and other people of the Nanhua Faction, they were eager to be the first players of any new games.","Hearing the news that the new game was released, they immediately jumped up from the couches and shouted, “Activate it for me! Activate it for me!”","Jiang Xiaoyue also wanted to play the new game. “Boss, I want to play it too!”","The task for the Assassin’s Creed series contained several points. After the game was unlocked, the System showed the requirements for unlocking the sequels after Assassin’s Creed 1.","At this moment, Fang Qi was looking at the information on the System Interface.","After finishing the first task, Mr. Fang found that he not only activated the right to publish Assassin’s Creed 1, but he also got an assassin-shaped prototype badge.","[Prototype Badge: When a game, a movie, or a TV Series has other prototype characters, it can only be activated when all the prototype badges are collected...]","There was more information about prototype badges underneath.","“What’s this thing?” Mr. Fang continued to read, trying to find out the function of this thing. Meanwhile, many people had entered the game.","The first scene that they saw was an image consisting of many genetic sequences which finally formed a round logo.","“Ubisoft?” As a legit researcher, Li Haoran looked at it curiously. “So many genetic sequences? Is this senior named Ubisoft an expert in unlocking the genetic locks?”","By now, the players were quite familiar with the words ‘genetic locks’ even though none of them had truly unlocked it.","Before them was a medieval city. They saw Altair was leaping down from a bell tower to kill his target; they had watched this scene in the trailer.","However, this scene was more detailed compared to that in the trailer, showing how he assassinated the target, used visual illusions to deceive the pursuing soldiers, killed a soldier who was alone, and then vanished into the crowd.","For Sala who had no experience with assassinations, it didn’t look extraordinary, but Elina’s eyes lit up. In the system version, the soldiers were no different from their counterparts in the real world, completely unlike dull NPCs. It was not as easy to dodge as in the original version.","With some simple steps, he had dodged everyone’s eyes in a matter of seconds before finding a chance to leave without a fuss. If the assassins in the real world had possessed such skills, the godly palace wouldn’t have caught any of them in Gray Eagle City even if they botched the mission.","After this interlude, they entered the game.","Instead of the city that they had seen a moment ago, their vision before them turned pale grey as if they had put on a pair of big goggles.","For one moment, they found themselves in that medieval city. In the next moment, their vision turned pale grey again. They felt like they were in a dream.","Then, they saw a huge lab. Hearing their conversation, the players were amazed. “Can this object retrieve the ancestral memories stored in the bloodline?”","“It’s a projector which renders genetic memories in three dimensions.”","What if I told you the human body not only housed an individual’s memories, but the memories of his ancestors as well?","“Genetic memory, if you will. Migration, hibernation, reproduction... How do animals know when and where to go? What to do?”","“Ugh?” Jiang Xiaoyue froze. “Can I display the memories of my ancestors?”","Li Haoran was also astonished. !!?? I can’t believe that this little game about assassins holds such a piece of cutting-edge black technology!","After all, everyone in this world had powerful ancestors if they traced back far enough into the ancient times.","The players in the new shop were at a loss for words.","They felt puzzled as they couldn’t understand what was going on, but they were awed at the same time!"]},{"number":614,"title":"Chapter 614 - Master Assassin Su Tianji’s Livestream","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","The players of the new shop had thought that this game was only a basic mystical realm for practicing combat techniques, just like the other mystical realms in the city.","But after they started, they were astonished.","Of course, for people like Sala and Elven, they didn’t think too much about the genetic memories. After all, no workshop would simulate things exactly as they were in the real world.","They began playing Assassin’s Creed cheerfully.","However, for the scientific researchers such as Li Haoran and Lan Mo and the Tang Family’s elders who were cultivators that excelled in making artifacts, they began to wonder, “Hiss... Wow! Can we study this stuff...?”","“Auch! Don’t cover my eyes! Let me have one more look of it!”","While others were playing games, these people tried to research, which was quite an oddity.","In the lab, the elders of the Tang Family who tried to study the machine were dragged to the platform and tied to it by the lab assistants. Then, the machine was activated and started the game.","Animus, the machine that the players were using to access Altair’s memories, was bright silver. When it was in operation, the user’s head would be covered by a glass panel from the side.","Different from the traditional virtual reality, this was a projected virtual reality in which the Animus could read the user’s genetic memories and transcode them into a three-dimensional world.","It was an almost complete three-dimensional world.","The events and skills shown in the virtual reality would be reflected in the real world. It could be used to get information about the Brotherhood of Assassins and Pieces of Eden, and it could be used for virtual training as well.","It meant that...","“We are playing a virtual reality game inside a virtual reality game?!”","Su Tianji froze for a moment and then entered the world inside Animus.","On the side, she clicked open QQ Livestream and titled it [New Game Review].","Even in the old shops, many players were hesitating about playing the game.","“Elder Su is livestreaming!”","“Ugh? New Game Review?”","“Let me see! Let me see!”","After all, she was a good gamer and had blown off the Godly Palace Army’s super magic spell, Spatial Storm, with her railgun. Many people were eager to watch her livestream.","Coming into the shop, people like Mo Xian and Liu Ningyun were about to have their breakfast of instant noodles when they noticed that someone was live streaming and reviewing the new game. Immediately, they turned on their new communication jade to watch on QQ Livestream.","The livestream had the tags such as [Technology] and [Godly Player]. She even changed her name to Master Assassin Elder Su, which sounded lofty and powerful.","Even though she had been lazy and watching anime, she was doing it to study the super spiritual spell named Super Su Tianji Cannon.","“It’s Elder Su!”","“How come the shop owner isn’t livestreaming today?”","“Let’s watch this first!”","Even the Xichi Spiritual Master joined them on the couch. “I remember that Daoist Friend Su is a very good game player. She even won second place in the Counter Strike Group Competition. I must watch it.”","On the other side, the two black-robed figures who had fought the last two crucial battles with the Judgement Godly Palace were still low-profiled.","They still sat in a corner and said, “Let’s watch it and see if the new game is useful to us.”","...","At this moment in the new shop, the Elf Girl Sala and the Assassin Elina had started their journey in the new game.","While getting herself familiar with the gaming operations, Su Tianji glanced at her livestream room and found that the viewers were several times more than usual.","Master Assassin Elder Su asked, “How come there are so many people today?”","“Today, I’ll do an... um... review of the new game for you guys.”","She entered a silver space which was not a complete virtual reality space. It was used to better synchronize the main character with the memory of his ancestors.","For players, it was a tutorial of the basic operations.","In the game, the players must abide by the code of conduct of the ancestors and not do anything against it. Otherwise, they would lose synchronization and exit from the virtual reality world created by the Animus using the main character’s genetic memories.","It was also what happens when the players were severely wounded or died.","In the original game, the players must change to the first-person perspective and observe the faceless people around them. But in the system version, the players must focus their attention on these people’s movements and minuscular changes in expressions.","With proficiency, Su Tianji finished this step quickly.","“This is so easy!” Su Tianji was more confident in herself. “Until now, this game is quite friendly.”","Soon, bullet comments shot up on the screen.","Song Qingfeng typed: [Well done.]","Nalan Mingxue sent her three goose eggs.","“Thank you, Mr. Fang, for the gift,” Master Assassin Elder Su said, “The shop owner is watching my livestream, too?”","Mr. Fang had played this game before, and he answered casually, [Of course.]","“...” Surprised that the shop owner came to watch her livestream instead of focusing on his own business, Su Tianji was at a loss for words. Soon, the scene before her changed to bustling crowds.","Beyond the crowds was a vague circle of genetic sequences which signified the end of the quest.","In the original game, the players only needed to pass through the crowds without bumping them so much that the pots fell from their heads.","However, in the real world, even a rookie assassin could achieve this with ease.","In the original game, the players were ordinary people instead of real assassins, which was why this step was greatly simplified.","Now, the System didn’t need to simplify this step since the players were cultivators and warriors. How could a real assassin pass the bustling crowds?","The researcher’s voice came from outside the virtual reality. “Please use the knowledge of your ancestor to go through the crowds and get to the gene sequences without being discovered.”","“What?!” Not only Su Tianji, but the viewers of the livestream were astonished as well.","Even the assassin in the new shops were shocked.","Before them was a bright and flat path without any place for hiding. How can we walk over without being discovered?!","Su Tianji was frustrated and wondered, Are you kidding me?","At this moment, an idea suddenly jumped out in her mind. If every position and step that I take is in everyone’s blind spot, I can go through the crowds without being discovered!"]},{"number":615,"title":"Chapter 615 - Watch How I Assassinate the Target","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","These new assassins quickly used the skills from their memories. Combining that with their first step of learning concentrated observation skills, they started to monitor their surroundings more carefully, taking note of each person’s movements including their postures, blinking, and shifts of their attention.","Of course, it was a tutorial for beginners and thus had lower standards. In this tutorial, it was acceptable if the passersby only saw a flash of a white shadow and weren’t disturbed.","Obviously, this step was much more difficult than the previous one. However, Su Tianji was indeed smart and passed it after trying several times. “Haha! I did it!”","At this moment, she heard the game prompt: [Basic profile – high/low profile]","In the original game, using high-profile would make it easy for the players to gain momentum but would also attract attention. In this profile, they might not be able to instantly kill their targets with their hidden blades and had to engage a in hand-to-hand combat, exposing themselves in public and in danger. In contrast, the low-profile was more secretive and would be less likely to be discovered.","However, in the real world, would people only see a person when he walked in high profile and turn a blind eye to a person walking in a low-profile?","The answer was negative.","As everyone knew, most veteran soldiers would acquire a sharp intuition to danger. The assassins lived in a chaotic time, which meant that people in this world had experienced many years of war and danger, and the bosses in the game wouldn’t just stand there dumbly, waiting to be killed.","Sometimes, they could even dodge an attack without using their eyes.","Now that the players had synchronized with the basic skill of visual deception, they must synchronize the basic skill of sense deception and detection.","At this moment, the players faced a soldier and were required to walk over directly and toss him into the gene sequences before them.","They must show no murderous spirit or hostility. Standing on the edge of the soldier’s vision, they must adjust their presence and other things to merge into the surroundings, giving the soldier the impression that they were only a harmless passersby, a stone, or a wall.","Even grand cultivators and warriors wouldn’t pay attention to such people and things, let alone an ordinary soldier.","Soon, the audience watching the livestreams saw that Su Tianji controlled the main character to walk up to the soldier, who looked like a blind person, and grab the latter before tossing him into the gene sequences.","The synchronization was finished.","“Awesome!”","“F*cking superb...”","Many people watched the scene with widened eyes.","This visual effect stunned them.","The high-profile meant that one must use their strength perfectly and achieve 200 percent the effects with only 100 percent the strength. Of course, in the tutorial, the players only needed to outrun one soldier of similar physique and reach the circle of gene sequences to finish this step.","By now, Su Tianji had come to the last step in synchronization. She needed to use the knowledge that she acquired and carry out a complete assassination.","Of course, she only needed to assassinate an ordinary soldier and get away from the scene under another solder’s pursuit.","With these synchronized skills, even a beginner would find assassinating one soldier quite easy.","Then, they encountered a scene similar to the one shown in the cinematic trailer of Assassin’s Creed.","A white-robed assassin ambled over, unsheathed his hidden blade, dodged the chase of the other soldiers, and vanished in the crowd.","As an ordinary swordswoman, Sala was still trying to understand these skills. But the real assassins such as Elina and Harrison understood them immediately.","How did they hide themselves normally? They would cast a spiritual spell that was like an energy cloak to stop others from seeing them and stop spiritual spells from detecting them.","Yes, the assassins in this world knew spiritual spells but used them in different areas than mages.","How did the Judgement Godly Palace block these assassination attempts? They used higher-level spiritual spells to spot the presence of the assassins by detecting the extra surges of energy.","They also used spiritual spells to cancel out the assassins’ stealth state and destroy the energy system.","In turn, the assassins had to find and create more powerful spiritual spells to avoid detection. The disguise method used by the shadow killer when he fought with Zong Wu was one of such spiritual spells.","Then, how did the Judgement Godly Palace deal with this spell?","They used godly spells. After all, there were few, if any, things that were even more powerful than godly spells.","As for the assassins, they had to find spiritual spells that could conceal them before godly spells.","However, human intelligence was no match for that of gods who had existed for countless years, which made it impossible for the assassins to win in this cycle of competition.","But now, the assassins seemed to see a glimpse of hope.","At this moment, Su Tianji continued to watch the cinematics of the game in which the main character Altair, who had great talent and became an Master Assassin in his twenties, botched a quest due to his arrogance. In the mission of retrieving the Piece of Eden from Solomon’s Temple, he violated three tenets of the assassin’s creed, which were killing an innocent old man, exposing himself, and leading the templar knights to the headquarters of assassins, endangering the brotherhood.","At this moment...","“Well! Now, I’ll demonstrate to you guys how a master assassin eliminates a target with a perfect assassination.” Having finished the tutorial and a smooth assassination mission, Su Tianji was full of confidence.","“We must not repeat Altair’s mistakes,” Su Tianji said solemnly, “Now, let me demonstrate what a true master assassin does.”","She looked quite professional.","At this moment, templar knights had killed their way into the village.","“Watch carefully. This templar knight is dressed luxuriously and must be a high-ranking knight.” Su Tianji found one templar knight. “Now, we must adjust our position to the blind spot of his vision.”","The audience watched attentively.","“Let’s walk toward him,” Su Tianji said, “Watch how I assassinate the target.”","“This distance is good enough!” Su Tianji walked forward directly. Then, she leapt up high like a huge eagle sweeping down from the sky, striking her hidden blade toward the vital organ of the templar knight!","Ding! A sword light flashed. It parried and then turned in a twist.","She was instantly killed by a parry strike.","On her screen came the message, [Desynchronization]","Seeing the black-and-white image on the screen, Su Tianji was at a loss for words.","“Ahh-!” She was extremely frustrated.","[Awesome!]","[Master Assassin Elder Su.]","[Instant kill with one sword strike! Unrivaled!]","[Awesome! Awesome!]","Bullet comments flooded the screen.","“No! How come the skills that I’ve learned are useless?!” Su Tianji yelled while slapping her hand on her thigh.","Calmly, the templar knight withdrew his sword.","You only passed the tutorial and want to show off your skills in front of me now?!","[Thanks to Song Qingfeng for 66 goose eggs; thanks to Mr. Fang for 99 goose eggs.]","“Hehehehe...”","Su Tianji said, “It doesn’t count! It doesn’t count!”","“Oh... The mentor is calling us to make the leap of faith! Let’s switch!”"]},{"number":616,"title":"Chapter 616 - Sellers’ Show and Buyers’ Show","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","[TL Note: The title is a meme in China. It refers to the difference between the images that online sellers show and the images that buyers took when they got the product.]","For elves, freedom was a highly romantic and graceful word. They valued freedom even more than their lives.","For the assassins in the Morning Light Empire, they were drawn to the game by something indescribable which might be a spirit or a will. It was vague, but Elina was sure that she could find it here.","For elves, the throbbing of freedom was something that drew them in.","Whenever she saw assassins leaping down from the tall towers and castles like flying eagles, Sala was always struck by a sense of glory.","It was a beautiful feeling.","“I can’t believe that I’m going to make this leap of faith too!” She clenched her hands, feeling a bit nervous.","After the templar knights had followed Altair to the assassins’ headquarters, the mentor arranged for him and the other assassins to leap down the high cliff with a leap of faith, so they could take a detour to the back of the templar knights and activate the pre-arranged traps and defense mechanisms.","Many other players had come to this part at this moment, including Elina and Harrison, who were assassins in the real world.","“It’s really a moment of glory...” While lamenting, Elina climbed up the tower.","In the old shop, Su Tianji had also climbed to the top of the tower. Standing on the extension plank on the top, she looked at the distant mountains and spread out her arms like a white bird that was flying. It was a beautiful and romantic scene in her mind.","As a romantic and artistic clan, the elves understood this romantic feeling.","They all recalled the cool and smooth moves of those white-robed assassins in the trailer who spread their arms toward the wind as if they were embracing the sky and the distant mountains.","The ground below the tall cliff was covered by thick layers of hay. For real assassins with faith, they didn’t even need any buffers or cushions.","Standing on the plank, Sala felt the mountain wind brushing over her face with her eyes closed. If seemed like she could move forward by one step and enter a paradise.","“...!!??”","Everything turned silent.","I won’t take the step forward unless I’m crazy!","Then, she suddenly plunged down!","“Ahh...!” She screamed all the way down. On her screen, an assassin flailed his arms and legs while plunging down from the sky.","She landed on the ground face first.","“Ahhh...”","“Ah–!”","One after another, the assassins stuck their heads out from the hay with straws all over their faces, and they looked around with confusion in their eyes. “...”","In Su Tianji’s livestream room, the audience saw an assassin plunging into the pile of hay head first with two feet waving outside.","“Wuuu-! Let me out!”","“Where’s the shop owner?!” Looking at her screen which had turned black-and-white again, Su Tianji was extremely frustrated. While looking around, it seemed like she was looking for weapons to grab.","It was totally different from what they had seen in the trailer!","How could the leap of faith look like that?!","They were deceived! Completely deceived!","– In the livestream room –","[Cool!]","[Master Assassin!]","[Landing on your face with a leap of faith.]","[Unrivalled.]","[Nalan Mingxue sent you ten goose eggs.]","[Mr. Fang sent you 20 goose eggs.]","“...”","Su Tianji had the urge to throw goose eggs at Mr. Fang’s face!","She even suspected that the trailer had only shown the first part of the leap of faith, and all the assassins had in fact fallen to the ground this way in the second half of the leap.","Su Tianji rubbed her face.","This is...","...","As a real assassin, even though the process was tough, Elina finally stumbled her way to the assassination – a real assassination mission.","To punish Altair for breaking the tenets, botching the mission, even leading the templar knights to their headquarters, and causing death to many assassins, the mentor let him experience death.","Of course, the mentor didn’t kill the disciple who he had trained with care. Instead, he used this near-death experience to warn him. After taking away all his strength and equipment, the mentor sent him to kill the nine leaders of the templar knights.","As an assassin, Elina was confident in herself.","Therefore, she set out.","To avoid landing face first as she had done before, she didn’t leap down from a high point. Instead, she sneaked into the place.","There were many people in the market; Elina felt like she could copy the scenes shown in the trailer in which the white-robed assassin walked through the crowd, attacked with a longsword and the hidden blade at the same time to kill the target, and then vanished.","The neat and smooth killing skills were very dashing! For real assassins, the feeling of easily killing targets was very enjoyable.","She planned these moves in her mind.","Then, she pushed through the crowd and walked up.","– Ten seconds later –","“Ahh-!”","[Desynchronization]","On the screen, the assassin was knocked down to the ground by a large group of people.","“...”","Damn it!","– One day later –","– Two days later –","Su Tianji slammed her hand on the table. “Sir!”","All the players shouted, “Sir!!??”","What is wrong with this Assassin’s Creed?!","In the trailer, the leap of faith looked as free as a flying eagle.","But when we did it, we fell like a moron with flailing limbs. Some of us even landed face first!","In the trailer, the killing was done silently and instantly.","But when we did the missions, we swaggered out from the blind spot of the people’s vision, unsheathed the hidden blade, and were instantly killed!","In the trailer, the assassin walked into the enemies alone and killed them smoothly with a hand crossbow and a hidden blade in their hands.","In contrast, when we tried the missions, we were killed and lost synchronization when we pushed through the crowd and shot while attacking with both hands!","“Sir! You deceived us!”","“We’re not playing as assassins!”","Even Elina felt like she couldn’t play as an assassin anymore, let alone cultivators like Su Tianji.","[Sir!] Mr. Fang immediately received a protesting message from Su Tianji. [Take my cannon strike!]","Then, she sent him a screenshot of when she used Super Su Tianji Cannon in combat. Obviously, someone had taken this picture at the risk of their lives.","“This cultivation mystical realm of yours is a scam!” even Elf Sala protested.","She had practiced the leap of faith for days now! Her face was now even swollen due to repeated falls!","At this moment, Mr. Fang had just walked down from the second floor while wiping the sweat off his face.","Then, a group of people surrounded him.","“What’s wrong with you guys?”","“I can’t possibly learn the so-called leap of faith in this cultivation mystical realm!” Sala almost wept in fury.","“And the so-called assassination and the blind spot of vision! Who assassinates targets in public like this?” Elina gritted her teeth; she had copied the cool moves shown in the trailer but was beaten senseless and killed within ten seconds.","She had the urge to drag the shop owner out and beat him to death.","“This...” Mr. Fang looked exasperated. “You’re still newbies and noobs and can’t expect to learn everything so soon. Which beginner can do high-level plays anyway?”","“Newbies? Noobs?” Elina was furious. After all, she was a senior and elite assassin, but the shop owner just called her a newbie?!","Do you know whom I assassinated?! Do you know my background?!","She was even more furious since she couldn’t expose her identity.","Those soldiers in the game each had acute senses and high-level parry skills. The players might be able to deal with them with cultivation strength. However, without any cultivation strength, the players could barely fight with one, let alone a group of them in each assassination mission.","“Show us if you can do it!”"]},{"number":617,"title":"Chapter 617 - Don’t Assassinate; Use Musou","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","[Sir!<img class=\"emoji\" draggable=\"false\" src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/12.0.0-1/svg/1f61a.svg\" alt=\"&#x1F61A;\">] At this moment, a loli’s profile photo lit up on Mr. Fang’s communication jade. He turned it on and read her message, [How come Assassin’s Creed is so difficult to play? (Husky’s fierce face)]","Despite the great power of the monsters, the players in Resident Evil had guns and RPGs and thus didn’t find it too hard to handle those monsters who had no brains. The players could clear the stage as long as they didn’t venture into the highest difficult level.","However, in Assassin’s Creed, there were people and soldiers everywhere. With one misstep, they would be surrounded without any guns or cannons at their disposal.","While monsters who were infected by T-virus were without brains, the real soldiers were intelligent, which made the game quite difficult to play.","Su Tianji said, [Hurry! Play it on the livestream, or I’ll quit the game!]","Soon, he received another message.","Nalan Mingxue said, [(Husky’s disdainful face) Did you add special effects in your trailer?]","With poor experiences in her own livestream, Su Tianji forced Mr. Fang to put on a livestream with the threat of quitting the game.","Damn it! She just couldn’t continue her livestream anymore!","...","“Show us if you can do it!” Elina was furious.","In the new shop, many people stood around the counter.","As the owner of the shop, Mr. Fang didn’t want people to say that he had added many special effects in the trailer of the game.","So, Fang Qi sat down before a computer and turned on the game and the big-screen livestream, which was Mr. Fang’s privilege.","“Hey! The shop owner turned on the livestream!”","In the old shops, Su Tianji, Jiang Xiaoyue, Song Qingfeng, and the others all sat on the couches in the lounge area. After all, Mr. Fang hadn’t done a livestream for a long time.","A real assassin, Elina bought a box of spicy sticks. Regardless if the games in the shop were good or not, she found that the spicy sticks were quite delicious. She watched the livestream while eating.","Of course, she was just here to watch how the shop owner would fail since she didn’t believe that anyone would have better assassination skills than her.","Standing behind her, the Elf Girl Sala watched the show with a cup of milk tea in her hand.","All the members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion walked over with sulky expressions. Obviously, they had been tortured by Assassin’s Creed so much that they couldn’t even perform as knights, let alone assassins.","They wished that they had gone to try Dulan Workshop’s new cultivation mystic realm instead.","At this moment, Mr. Fang entered the game and got ready.","Altair stood on a tall tower, looking down on the whole city like an eagle.","“Ugh?! Where’s this place?!” Obviously, Mr. Fang’s map was different. Most players had just come to the first assassination mission in which there were mostly low residential houses and no guards on the roofs.","However, in Mr. Fang’s map, they could see a huge harbor zone with Byzantine-style buildings. Also, many archers hid in concealed places on the roofs.","On the main roads and ships stood many templar knights. In previous missions, there were more ordinary people and fewer templar knights. This mission was clearly different.","Looking forward into the distance, people could see about ten templar knights surrounding several white-robed scholars and yelling at them.","“...!? How come there are so many of them?!” Sala was astonished.","“Where’s this place?!” Elina exclaimed too while her hand was feeding spicy sticks into her mouth, and her eyes stared at the screen intently.","When they played the game, they had seen bustling crowds and could hide themselves among the ordinary people. Besides, there were no secret guards on the roofs or so many templar knights.","Of course, Mr. Fang’s game progress was much faster than others. By now, due to the repeated assassinations, the templar knights began to suspect that the scholars were accomplices of assassins since they all wore white robes.","From the distance, they could see a scholar being knocked down.","“Ugh?! How did the shop owner go there?!” Soon, they saw Mr. Fang coming to the pier.","“What assassin is he?!” Elina was enraged. The tutorial had told them how to get into their opponents’ blind spots of vision. Even if they couldn’t sneak up this way, they must keep themselves in concealment. But now, she saw Mr. Fang just walking up directly?!","Loud whistling sounds came.","Obviously, the archers on the roof had shot out more than one hidden arrow at him.","Meanwhile, a nearby templar knight was charging at Mr. Fang with a saber.","“Do you know how to play an assassin?!” Elina demanded.","She thought that he was a big moron.","Mr. Fang looked impatient. On the screen, Altair turned his body and whipped out his hidden blade with the momentum of turning. Then, the templar knight clutched his own neck while blood gushed out from his fingers.","Two more templar knights dashed up. On the screen, Fang Qi controlled Altair to move to the side, blocking them with his left hand while whipping out his right hand. The two soldiers fell to the ground almost simultaneously.","Altair continued to walk toward his target without stopping.","A templar knight sneaked up to him silently and raised his sword with both hands.","Altair turned and parried the attack. Following the momentum of the counterattack, he sent the sword into the knight’s chest!","“!!??” Not only Sala and the members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion, but the assassins were frozen by the scene as well.","The smooth killing skills and the elegant moves looked as easy as if he were strolling around.","Is he moving exactly the same as the character in the trailer?!","While killing the knights, Mr. Fang said, “Don’t assassinate, use musou. There’s not much time in life for you to achieve total synchronization. If you hate him, then kill him. Killing all the witnesses is the perfect assassination. Sneaking up is no use because you’ll be discovered sooner or later. If someone sees you, just kill him, either with your sword or throwing knife if they are far away. The worst that will happen is losing synchronization, but losing synchronization is the norm while you play the game...”","[TL Note: This is a dig at Assassin’s Creed since players feel like the game’s stealth feature is lacking. Instead, it is a great fighting game like Dynasty Warrior. That is where the reference ‘musou’ comes from.]","Before he finished his monologue, the ground was covered by bodies. Meanwhile, more templar knights swarmed towards him.","Mr. Fang continued to hack and slash.","Everyone was at a loss for words.","How can you play an assassin this way?! Elina almost went crazy.","“The second tenet of the creed for assassins is hiding yourself; you are breaking the creed and will certainly lose synchronization!” Elina said loudly.","After all, assassins would lose synchronization not only in death but also when they deviated from the character’s code of conduct.","But a moment later, when all the templar knights were killed, she saw a prompt appearing on Mr. Fang’s screen, [Mission accomplished.]","“!!??” Elina gaped at the screen.","The mission is completed?! Can we do it this way?!","The assassins felt like crying.","Elina had the feeling that Mr. Fang had played the real Assassin’s Creed while she...","While biting into a spicy stick, she thought that maybe she had been playing Assassin’s Spicy Sticks.","Some players hadn’t gotten the chance to watch Mr. Fang’s livestream. For example, Ning Bi had just finished her gameplay and sent a message in the group chat for Assassin’s Creed in QQ. [How come Assassin’s Creed is so difficult to play? How did you guys do the assassinations?]","Song Qingfeng posted a screenshot of Mr. Fang’s livestream, showing Altair standing over dead bodies all over the ground. [Perfect Assassination.]","“Pu-!”"]},{"number":618,"title":"Chapter 618 - The Meaning of ‘Nothing Is True, Everything Is Permitted’","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Mr. Fang glanced at the tasks for this series and found that the first few were comparatively simple, such as the ones for Assassin’s Creed 2 and Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood.","Mr. Fang made some comparisons and found that the task for Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood was the easiest one to finish among others this series. It only required the number of players of Assassin’s Creed to reach 2,000.","The 2,000 players included those from the old shops.","At this moment, there were hundreds of assassin players in the new shop. As for the old shops, many players were still playing online games. After all, not everyone could have all the top-tier equipment such as Senior Nalan – only one out of 10,000 could do this.","The total number of players for Assassin’s Creed in the three old shops was only a little more than that of the new shop.","Despite all this, the right to release Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood would soon be unlocked.","...","Elina was now extremely frustrated.","She was certain that the shop owner was making excuses for his act, but she found it was hard to dispute with him.","Should I play an assassin in this way too?!","She began to look at the word ‘assassin’ in a new light.","...","As a young peace-loving elf, Sala was obviously not misled by Mr. Fang. Still, she found Mr. Fang’s battle method inspiring.","It seems the game had anticipated the potential failure of sneaking up and prepared some methods to deal with it.","They included the powerful battling skills that Fang Qi used when he killed his way into the crowd.","Except for Fang Qi’s own combat skills, parrying was a crucial skill that the game contained.","Parrying was a counterattack skill where the player could block the opponent’s sword and make the latter lose balance from the momentum before striking their vital points.","This method was similar to Devil May Cry’s Release skill.","However, few humans could have the fast reflex that Release required. In the long time that Devil May Cry had been available, only Ning Bi could use it in real battles.","Even Mr. Fang didn’t like to use this method in real battles when he wasn’t completely synchronized with Dante, and Nalan Hongwu hadn’t mastered it, let alone others. This method could only be used by those non-humans whose physical attributes were much more superior than humans. If ordinary people used it, they would get killed most of the time.","But parrying was different. Even ordinary people could learn this skill which was a high-level method to transfer the incoming force to attack the opponent.","When one parried with a sword, even if the move failed, they could still protect oneself by blocking the opponent’s attack, which made the skill highly safe to use.","Besides parrying, Altair, as a master assassin, had high-level combat skills, especially when he engaged in hand-to-hand combat with other people.","Human life was fragile. With a sharp weapon, one could kill a master without using any force when their aim wasn’t off.","This master assassin excelled in all kinds of efficient killing skills. Whenever his opponents made a minor mistake, he could make a kill easily.","These skills had merged into his genes.","Elves were never a dogmatic race. Sala thought that these combat skills might be useful in the future. However, her top priority right now was the leap of faith.","Regardless of how she jumped, even with the buffers such as grass and layers of hay, she almost fell to death after each leap. Although it didn’t affect her game progress, it greatly dampened her enthusiasm for the game.","“Why can’t I make a graceful leap of faith?” Sala was frustrated.","She had watched the shop owner jump almost the same way as the character in the trailer.","Since the leap of faith wasn’t fake, it only meant that she didn’t do it right.","Without the support of faith, the leap of faith meant death.","As a smart elf, Sala finally thought about the leap with faith.","Meanwhile, Elina, Harrison, and the other assassins had also made the connection while doing the leap of faith repeatedly.","But they were still puzzled. After all, assassins didn’t believe in gods. Then what was their faith?","Another thing that puzzled her was that when Altair did the assassination missions in broad daylight, he exposed himself to the templar knights, which meant that he broke the second tenet. But why didn’t he lose the synchronization?","Controlling Altair, she assassinated again and again.","But she still didn’t understand what the assassins’ faith was.","Like Altair going to Solomon’s Temple with arrogance and conceit, Elina had gone through assassination missions with pride belonging to this world’s assassins.","After each successful assassination, Altair would have a mental conversation with the target.","In the world of Assassin’s Creed, assassins and templar knights fought with each other over the Pieces of Eden. The templar knights wanted to use this advanced technology created by the first civilization to control the minds of humans and thus make an orderly world where people’s spiritual world was the same.","However, assassins thought free will was the thing that humans truly needed.","In this era, there were many tenets and codes for assassins. Altair had broken the three basic tenets before.","For Altair, he had only one creed –’nothing is true, everything is permitted.’","When Altair eliminated the targets, who were templar knights one by one, their words before death made Altair reflect on the code of conduct, purpose, and meaning of being an assassin.","He realized that the creed of ‘nothing is true, everything is permitted’ was right, but it didn’t mean that he could be arrogant.","Altair finally shed his arrogance and conceit and grew into a clear-headed and wise assassin, embarking on the journey to a true master assassin.","Of course, even though Mr. Fang killed all the witnesses and called it a perfect assassination, he didn’t mean that everyone should assassinate this way.","Instead, he tried to tell the players that they must use their own brains, instead of following others’ paths.","This was the meaning of ‘nothing is true, everything is permitted’.","Elina had been very proud, but as Altair’s reflections went deeper, she fell silent.","Meanwhile, Sala and other elves, the knights of theGolden Griffin Knight Legion, and the mercenaries in Canglan City fell silent as well.","They suddenly realized that Assassin’s Creed wasn’t just a cultivation mystic realm teaching them assassination skills.","It allowed them to experience a pearl of wisdom."]},{"number":619,"title":"Chapter 619 - The Collective Building-Jumping Incident in This World","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","‘Nothing is true, everything is permitted’ wasn’t an excuse for people to do anything they wanted. People learned the combat skills in Assassin’s Creed not to become war machines who knew nothing but killing.","When Altair killed the last templar knight, he found that his mentor was also a templar knight. The latter intended to use him to kill the other nine templar knights and become the sole owner of the Pieces of Eden.","It took Elina a long time to reach the end of the plot.","In the ordinary difficulty level, Altair had recovered all his strength by now, making the battles less difficult than she had imagined.","After defeating his mentor, Altair said to the Piece of Eden, “What do you bring to us? Faith or destruction?”","When Sala saw this, an indescribable sadness spread in her heart.","“When other people’s minds are blinded by the so-called truth, remember – nothing is true.”","“When people’s actions are limited by morality or law, remember, everything is permitted.”","This was the respect for free will. Only with it could human civilization make continuous progress.","This was the assassins’ faith and soul.","Only with this faith could the assassins break free from the complicated tenets and rise again and again despite repeated corruption and falls.","This was the inspiration that Altair, the first master assassin in this series, had obtained and passed down.","“He’s a truly great master...!” Elf Girl Sala hadn’t cleared the stage yet, but her slow progress in the game didn’t stop her from watching the final video after other players finished the game.","From now on, she began to see these assassins in a new light.","The faith needed in the leap of faith wasn’t faith in any gods but rather in free will.","“Awesome!” Sala had never expected that a cultivation mystic realm would give her such deep inspirations.","She was eager to introduce it to her people in the Silver Moon Forest.","Since they shared the same craving for freedom, Sala was sure that they could understand the meaning shown in the game.","Having reached the end of the game, Elina froze for a long time while something dawned on her. She finally understood why these master assassins had never looked lost.","Were they stronger than the templar knights? No. But their faith had always been firm.","For the old players in the shops, they might not follow assassins’ creed, and many of them just took it as a game, but it didn’t stop them from admiring these white-robed assassins fighting for free will.","At this moment, Elina stood at the assassins’ headquarters of Masyaf in the game.","The mountain was still grand and vast white clouds floated around it. Looking down, Elina could see gurgling creek below the high and steep cliff. At this moment, the stone platform which she had crashed down heavily onto so many times looked very tiny. It felt like anyone would be smashed into pieces if they made a misstep.","Elina stood on the plank that was extending from the tower.","She spread out her arms, and she leaped down like an eagle flying freely in the air.","Meanwhile, Sala also stood on the top of a tall tower. Like an arrow, she leaped down decisively.","“Shirk-!” In the gust, they seemed to hear an eagle’s clear shriek.","They landed perfectly!","“I...”","“I did it?!”","Sala looked at herself in disbelief. Although the previous leaps didn’t kill her, she had been smashed senseless by the crashes. But this time, she had landed perfectly!","“It’s unbelievable!”","Assassin Elina watched her leap of faith in surprise; she did it!","“Awesome!” In pleasant surprise, she covered her mouth in stupefaction, not daring to believe her eyes.","Lance, the captain of the elf guardian team, was also standing at the bottom of the valley. He inhaled deeply after his perfect leap of faith.","“It’s a wonderful feeling!”","“Oh! I did it!” The young men from the preparatory team of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion cheered.","“I want to try it in the real world!” Sala said.","“Me too! It’s so cool!” Helen said in excitement, “I want to try it now!”","At this moment, Commander Elven was still trying his leap of faith in frustration. “I nearly broke my legs again...”","It was comforting that he had made some progress. In the previous attempts, he had always lost synchronization after being paralyzed from the leap.","He took off his virtual reality headset and glanced around. “Ugh? How come they’re all gone?!","“Wait for me!”","...","In the beautiful Canglan City which was located beside a river and a mountain, the castles in the middle were very eye-catching.","It was the aristocratic zone of the city, and the City Hall and other administrative offices were all located in these castle-like buildings.","It was the highest point of the city.","At this moment, on the top level of the huge bell tower of this castle stood a row of people.","Like Altair, they leaned forward, stepping on the outmost stones.","The gusts at this height flapped their robes and clothes against their bodies.","They looked forward and saw the screen-like mountains in the distance and the sparkling lights on the peaceful lake at the foot of the mountains.","In the streets of the city were bustling crowds and horse-drawn carriages.","Looking down, they could see the base of the bell tower that looked tiny from up-high.","On the ground were piles of golden layers of hay.","Although assassins with firm faith didn’t need any buffers, it was their first leap in the real world after all.","The feeling of freely flying in the air without any restrictions from any forces was exhilarating.","Sala closed her eyes subconsciously.","In fact, Helen did the same.","As an extremely artistic and romantic clan, the elves understood this romantic gesture.","Captain Lance also closed his eyes and wanted to try it.","They all closed their eyes, enjoying this feeling.","Meanwhile, the people below them yelled, “What are they doing up there...?”","“No idea... They seem to be members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion and the elves who came to visit our city a while ago?”","“What are they doing up there?”","Only a few people were around the bell tower. But soon, many people showed up.","Elf Girl Sala seemed to find the feeling and leaped down from the bell tower before the others.","Then, the others fell like dumplings that were being dropped into a boiling pot.","“Ahh-! No! Commander Elven is leading the members in his legion and the elves in a group suicide!” The audience froze in fear.","They were so scared that their minds turned blank."]},{"number":620,"title":"Chapter 620 - You’ll Lose Money If You Do Business This Way","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“No! Commander Elven is leading the members in his legion and the elves in a group suicide!” The audience froze in fear when they saw the figures falling from the sky one after another.","Sala opened her eyes subconsciously. “How come there are so many people down there?!”","There are even people yelling things like group suicide? These ignorant people know nothing! This is free will! It is the leap of...","Then, she felt like something wasn’t right...","“Ahhh...!” With legs and arms flailing, a large group of people fell from the sky.","Thud!","...","The whole place went quiet.","A while later, heads began to poke out from the layers of hay, and they looked around in confusion.","“...”","The audience in the area all fell silent.","Despite their great strength, the members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion and the elves still felt as if their butts had cracked after falling from such a great height","“That sly shop owner!” They felt like they were tricked again!","What was more...","Looking around the audience, they thought to themselves, “If this news gets passed back to Silver Moon Forest, my later years as an elf will...”","The elves were terrified just thinking about it.","“Ahhh-!” Sala and the other elves felt like dying.","“...” Frightened, Commander Elven stepped back!","Looking at the elves and members of the knight legion who had crashed onto the ground, he stood on the top of the bell tower, combed his wind-blown hair, and said calmly, “This is... a new training method for my legion. Obviously, they haven’t totally understood the skill. I’m sorry for the disturbance that we caused you.”","“Go... Hurry!” Elven’s face turned livid.","He had almost made a perfect leap in the cultivation mystic realm, but standing here, he felt like something was not right!","...","“Sir!” By now, Mr. Fang had cleared Assassin’s Creed 1.","Suddenly, he heard a yell from outside of the shop. Then, a group of people strode in with fierce expressions.","The aristocrats and elves walked in, looking disheveled. Some of them even had straws on their head. “What’s wrong with this leap of faith?!”","Sala felt like crying. She had planned to broadcast her lofty free will to the public but ended up crashing onto the ground again on her face.","Commander Elven was also furious. He had wanted to take this opportunity to show to the public the glorious image of his Golden Griffin Knight Legion. He had imagined the public’s exclamation, “Look! The knights flying freely like eagles are perfect matches for the name of golden griffins!”","However, this incident almost ruined the image of the legion!","Frantically, Elven hoped that his awkward explanation had saved him.","Meanwhile, he was glad that he hadn’t jumped with everyone else.","Mr. Fang looked at them in confusion. “What’s going on with you guys again?”","“Your leap of faith... It has issues!” Elf Girl Sala pointed at the computer and said in a fury, “We just tried it; it didn’t work!”","Mr. Fang swiveled to face them while sitting in his computer chair and asked them with a serious expression, “Who is the main character that you control in the game?”","“Why do you ask this? It’s Altair!” Sala said with conviction.","“How can you talk about the leap of faith without understanding the basic plot of this game?” Mr. Fang said, “The main character is Desmond, the modern-day main character who was forced to enter the Animus to receive his ancestor’s memories, and you tell me it’s Altair?”","“Um...” Everyone froze.","Soon, Sala reacted and replied in anger, “Sly shop owner, don’t distract us. It has nothing to do with the leap of faith.”","Fang Qi pointed at the character in the computer and said, “It means that you’re Desmond in the game instead of Altair. Did you see Desmond make the leap of faith?”","The members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion and the elves shook their heads.","“That’s it.” Mr. Fang shrugged his shoulders. “Then, why did you think that you can make the leap of faith? Blind self-confidence?”","“Hey!” Even Sala and the other elves felt dizzy by the logic in the shop owner’s words, let alone the members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion.","Thinking for a while, Sala asked dizzily, “You mean we can use the leap of faith after Desmond masters it?”","“Then, when will Desmond master the leap of faith?!” Commander Elven asked immediately.","He also heaved a sigh of relief.","Anyway, the leap of faith wasn’t a scam. Otherwise, he would think that his intelligence had been insulted if he were fooled.","It was comforting to know that the leap of faith was at least a real thing.","At this moment, Mr. Fang wrote on the small blackboard, [Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood will be released soon!]","“Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood?!” A true assassin, Elina walked up, and so did the other assassins.","In fact, except for Sala who had paused here and there to enjoy the scenery and study the leap of faith, the others had all finished the game. After getting familiar with the game, the elves, as well as the knights who were born in the city famous for its combat techniques, had both the talent and skills to finish the game.","“When will it be released?!” Sala asked in disapproval.","Having finished their errand, these elves should have returned home long ago. They had stayed here just to play Assassin’s Creed.","They had played it for over ten days now.","Now, they had to wait some more?!","“If the release date is too late, we’ll have to give it up!” Sala said, “Right, Captain?”","Oblivious to the few straws clinging on the back of his head, the handsome and elegant elf captain raised three fingers crisply and said, “I think we’ll wait three...”","Looking at his fingers and then the eagerness in the eyes of the other elves, he added two more fingers. “Five days...”","If it’s not released in five days... Sala calculated with her slim fingers and thought, Should I beg the captain to wait another five days...","“Right. I think we’ll wait for five days at the most!” The elf captain vowed, oblivious to the calculations in the minds of his teammates.","“Besides...” Sala asked, “Can you sell the cultivation mystic realm to us?”","“I think our people in the Silver Moon Forest will like this mystic realm too!” Sala wanted them to feel the wonderful sensation of the leap of faith!","Mr. Fang said, “I don’t sell anything. If anyone wants to experience it, they must come here!”","“What-!?”","“Why?!” Sala wailed. After all, the Dulan Workshop had worked hard trying to introduce its cultivation mystic realm into the Silver Moon Forest, but this shop owner even refused her offer to promote for him?!","“Do you know how to do business or not?!” Even Elina couldn’t help but comment in disdain, “You’ll lose money if you do business this way!”"]},{"number":621,"title":"Chapter 621 - I Heard You Found Clues to the Assassins Who Tried to Assassinate Luther?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Mr. Fang was unmoved by Elina’s disdainful comments.","In fact, even the Mercenary Crete thought that the shop owner wasn’t a good businessman. If he were the shop owner, he would have used this opportunity to get rich overnight!","“Humph! If the new game isn’t released in a few days, we’ll go and try the new mystical realm released by the Dulan Workshop!” One knight of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion said with a snort.","...","As an important city for foreign exchange and trade in the Morning Light Empire, Canglan City was also a good example of the empire’s traditional value on combat techniques.","The Golden Griffin Knight Legion was the city’s highest-level guardian force, and Commander Elven was a powerful late-stage level 7 warrior. In the legion, there were several high-level mages, and even the ordinary knights were on and above level 6.","The legion commander position of the knight legion was usually appointed by the Hymia Family.","The Hymia Family attached great value to cultures and arts and had been promoting cultivation mystical realms, playing an important role in strengthening the warriors and mages with great combat techniques.","As one of the few human forces which deserved to be called an empire on the continent, the Morning Light Empire had a powerful saint level master as its emperor. However, even in this empire, not many people had reached level 8 or level 9.","In this empire, it had its own ranking system for evaluating combat techniques. The evaluations were usually done jointly by the specific professional union and the Alchemist Union.","This ranking and evaluation system had been started and promoted by the Hymia Family.","Master was a high rank. Below it, there were four ranks including high rank, middle rank, low rank, and apprentice.","Those who were called masters had high-level comprehension of combat techniques.","For example, this old man with short gray hair was one of them.","“Lately, that Elven is getting more and more out of hand!” The old man wearing black aristocratic clothes said in disapproval.","“What did he do?” In a clean and tidy study room inside a grand castle, a dignified middle-aged man in black silk clothes sat on a chair before a desk piled with documents and files.","His broad forehead and blazing eyes showed his unusual intelligence. In one glance, people would see that he was a man with great vision.","“His stupid training method... jumping from the bell tower?!” The old aristocrat said with a snort, “It is a disgrace!”","Instead of talking about this issue, the middle-aged man asked, “The elves have finished their business here, right? Are they still in the city?”","“Yes, My Lord,” The old man said, “They are close to Ms. Helen. I wonder what this Elven is up to. Even Ms. Helen joined this moronic...”","“Okay.” Hearing her name, a faint genial smile appeared on the middle-aged man’s face while he looked at the sunshine that was pouring into the room through the windows. “I got it, Mr. Bassak. If that’s all, I’ll take some rest now.”","The old man said in reluctance, “Yes, My Lord.”","After the old man was gone, the middle-aged man walked to the window and looked up at the sky while murmuring to himself, “This world is bigger than we can imagine. Sometimes, we encounter things that are... unexpected.”","...","The mercenary tavern was boisterous as usual with all kinds of people coming and going. They traded rumors in the city, information about magic beasts, and news about the mystical realms.","At this moment, a few weirdly-dressed people walked in. They all wore pure-white robes.","They all wore wide yellow leather belts on which hung two daggers and a leather-sheathed long sword. The white hoods concealed their heads, revealing only the lower half of their faces.","They looked secretive, but the white robes gave them an elegant and pure look of scholars. While the white robes made them stand out from the crowd, the hoods kept their faces hidden.","They looked mysterious and low-profiled.","“Wow... is this the newest style this year?” A young mercenary gaped at these newcomers.","“I’ve never seen people dressed like this before. What profession is this? Warriors?”","“They look like mages, but why are they carrying so many melee weapons?”","“Coo!” A female mercenary dressed in sexy clothes asked, “These cool guys are newcomers in the city?”","Instantly, everyone in the tavern looked toward them.","The female mercenary dressed in sexy clothes walked up. “Do you guys want to have a drink with me?”","The man in the middle pulled over his hood, revealing a thin face under blond hair. He looked around in bafflement.","“Crete?!”","The female mercenary spat out, “Pu-!”","“How come you’re dressed like this?!” an acquaintance asked.","“From now on, please call me Master Assassin Crete!” Crete said proudly.","“Assassin?” The mercenaries froze and then burst into laughter. “Are you serious?”","“Assassin?!”","“Do you mean those lowly and filthy people?” A brown-haired man walked up and slapped his hand on Crete’s chest while saying with a smirk.","“No! No! No! I think you’re mistaken, Buddy.” Crete looked at him in disdain and said, “Brother, you’ve never heard of Assassin’s Creed? Don’t be so ignorant; you must come out and get to know the world. Now, even the members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion are ordering this outfit.”","“Golden Griffin Knight Legion? Assassins?” The brown-haired mercenary laughed. “Brother, are you still sleeping?”","“I think it’s you who need to wake up.” With a serious expression, Crete pointed out the door.","Several mercenaries were standing on the top of the building across from the tavern. Regardless if they were wearing white robes, they all spread out their arms.","“What are they doing up there?”","“A group building-jumping event?!”","“What are they doing?” At this moment, the mercenaries in the tavern froze in fear as they had no idea of what was going on.","“Ahh...!” The group of people leaped down from the top of the building.","It was easy for the mercenaries to jump down from a building that was only three stories.","They landed perfectly!","Seemingly unsatisfied, they got up again with crisp movements. This time, more people walked out from the crowd and joined the jumping group.","“Oh...!”","What is wrong with these guys?!","They stared at the scene in shock.","What the heck?!","It would be acceptable if it was one person’s antics, but there were so many of them!","More importantly, they found that these people indeed looked graceful when they leaped down from the sky as if they were flying.","Are they practicing some new combat techniques?!","The most puzzling is that these guys are mumbling something about ‘assassins’ and the ‘leap of faith.’","What are those things?!","As an assassin, Elina usually pretended to be a mercenary and moved with them.","But now, she suddenly saw so many fake assassins!","I, a real assassin, haven’t shown off yet, and you imposters are trying to show off now?","Immediately, she climbed to the highest point and thought, I will show you what the real leap of faith looks like.","“My goodness!”","“That woman...!?”","“So high?!”","“What’s happening to this world?!”","The audience was baffled as if they couldn’t understand this world anymore.","“What combat techniques are they practicing?!”","“I remember it! The Golden Griffin Knight Legion have done this before!”","The godly palace had always been sensitive to assassins, especially after their attempt on assassinating Luther.","“These damn remaining evil doers. We must catch them and torture them!” A man wearing the knight armor of the Judgement Godly Palace said gloomily.","“Mr. Glass, I heard that you’ve found clues about those escaped assassins?” A man wearing a priest robe asked in a low voice.","“Yes. They are hiding in the Mercenary Union,” the armored knight said in a cold voice.","“But, we’re in Canglan City. I’m afraid we can’t...” another man in a priest robe said with worry in his voice.","“If we capture them and find evidence that they tried to assassinate Mr. Luther, even the Duke can’t stop us!”","The armored knight hurried to the tavern and said, “I heard that there are assassins here? I’m looking for assassins who tried to kill Mr. Luther. I hope you can help us. After all, I don’t think you want these villains to hide among you.","“We only want to know who the assassins are!” the man in armor asked coldly.","“I am!” All the people on the roof looked down.","“We all are.”","“!!??”","..."]},{"number":622,"title":"Chapter 622 - The Release of Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Seeing the team of godly palace knights, Elina who climbed to the highest point of the roof shivered and almost fell to the ground.","However, she froze when everyone around her fiercely shouted that they were all assassins.","Knight Captain Glass, who was wearing the godly palace armor also froze.","“How come there are so many assassins!?”","“Mr. Glass, what should we do now?!” one knight asked in a low voice.","“...”","...","“Damn it!” While leaving the Mercenary Union, Glass looked gloomy.","As the captain of the local godly palace knight legion, he was responsible for catching the escaped assassins.","Despite the many privileges they enjoyed, the priests and missionaries who were here to spread their religion didn’t have the right to ignore the local laws.","The law of this empire didn’t allow him to arrest anyone who lied and claimed to be assassins since it wasn’t a crime. If there had been only a couple of imposters, Glass would have arrested them and beaten them senseless. But with so many people saying that they were assassins, it wasn’t easy to handle.","“Damn it!” He slammed his fist onto the wall. “I should have arrested all those reckless people! If they didn’t blur the situation and stall for time, I would have found those assassins!”","“The senior level officials warned us to keep low for a while because the previous war has greatly damaged our reputation in different empires and nations!” Behind him, a senior priest in a red robe walked up slowly.","“I think someone is working against us!” Glass said in a cold voice, “I will find him and catch him!”","“I hope you won’t do that, Mr. Glass.” The red-robed senior priest said coldly, “If it were one month ago, you might be able to do that. But now, it’s impossible.”","“Why?!” Glass said coldly, “This man must be harboring the assassins and accomplices!”","“You’d better go out and look around instead of sitting here and complaining, Mr. Glass.” The red-robed priest said mildly, “Many aristocrats and even elves are cultivating in that shop. Mr. Luther will soon set out to Silver Moon Forest, which means that we must be on friendly terms with the elves. Don’t do anything to disturb the plan!","“If you disturb that lord’s plan, you wouldn’t be able to make up for it even with ten of your lives!” the red-robed priest said with a sneer.","“Then, should we just sit and watch?!” Glass asked in a deep voice.","“Don’t worry. These assassins are weak,” the red-robed senior priest said indifferently, “In the new mystical realm, we put special efforts in the promotion of anti-assassinations. We’ll tell the world that the assassins are just a joke to us! I believe the aristocrats will make the right choice!”","“Besides, Mr. Luther will bring along the new mystical realm made by the Dulan Workshop when he visits the Elf Clan. We’ll take this opportunity to promote it more. I think even the elves will be amazed by this mystical realm.","“Mr. Luther will let any elf try it out. They can even choose to play as assassins to check the effectiveness of this realm.” He chuckled. “If we’re lucky, we might be able to apply for a precious Spiritual Spell Visual Projection and use it to promote.”","“I can’t wait to watch the elves’ astonished faces!” Glass sneered.","...","When the morning sunlight shined into the shop, another day filled with hope began.","At this moment, some elves had just entered Origins Internet Café, hoping that Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood would be released soon.","“I wonder when the shop owner will release Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood.” By now, even Elf Girl Sala had finished Assassin’s Creed 1, let alone other masters.","Of course, Sala’s combat techniques were not bad, and her strength had reached level 6. Her progress in the game was faster than ordinary mercenaries.","As for Commander Elven and the elite assassins such as Elina and Harrison, they had begun playing the game for the second time with a higher difficulty level a few days ago.","Then, she saw the words on the small blackboard – [Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood]","“Ya-! It’s released!?” Elf Girl Sala stared at the small blackboard in pleasant surprise. “The sly shop owner has a conscience after all!”","As she did each day, she sat down on a chair close to the street. She liked the unique design of the shop. Pulling open the curtains, she looked to the left and could see the prosperous street through the glass wall.","The unique layout inside the shop gave people the illusion that they had entered another world. But pulling open the curtains and looking outside, people could see the garden-like city of white walls and red tiles fraught with bustling mercenaries, carriages driven by aristocrats, and patrolling knights. She enjoyed the sight very much.","Lounging on the wide leather computer chair, Sala sipped the delicious milk tea. Together with other elves, she paid with the remaining crystals deposited in her membership card and activated the new game – Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood.","Eagerly, she clicked on the icon to start the game and put on the virtual reality headset.","As the first game in the series, Assassin’s Creed 1 used the 1.28 version Animus which had limited functions. It told a story about Master Assassin Altair who went through all kinds of hardships and finally understood the true meaning of assassin’s creed.","Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood told the story of another master assassin named Ezio during his prime. In this game, the players could do many more things such as training in virtual reality, playing online with other players, training junior assassins, and doing multi-player missions.","After the flashing logo of Ubisoft, Sala soon found herself back in the lab, still playing as that man named Desmond.","The scene was gray, which showed that he was recalling something. “I thought no one would wake up and find himself caught in the fight between two big secret organizations.”","“I don’t want this, but it still happened to me...”","As the narrator, Desmond gave a brief introduction of the story.","In the 1930’s, the modern-day Templar created a mysterious machine in Norway in the disguise of German’s nucleus weapon program. With knowledge acquired from the Apple of Eden, this machine was created to retrieve memories of the ancestors of humans.","Desmond had been a member of the modern Brotherhood of Assassins. A while ago, a templar knight found him and forced him to enter Animus, trying to find the Pieces of Eden from his ancestor’s memories."]},{"number":623,"title":"Chapter 623 - The Beginning of Brotherhood in the New World, and the Elves Who Are Learning Musou","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Fortunately, Desmond was rescued by Lucy, the researcher who had navigated Desmond into the Animus in Assassin’s Creed 1. She was, in fact, a member of the Assassin Order.","To counter the modern templar knights, he had to enter another Animus and find his path forward by tapping into the memories of another ancestor named Ezio. Through the Bleeding Effect, Desmond himself was gradually becoming a real assassin.","Meanwhile, the game told the players that the modern templar knights had found out the assassins’ hideout and forced them to move to another place.","Animus 2.0 was the updated version developed by an assassin engineer named Rebecca Crane. With the fragmental blueprint delivered secretly to them by Lucy Stillman, who was an assassin spy in the Roman branch of the Templar Order, Rebecca made this new version in the hideout of the Brotherhood.","This was a red machine looking like a portable recliner, and its functions were much more advanced than the previous version.","“Wow! This magic item has been upgraded,” Sala exclaimed.","“It will make everything feel realer, just like the magic array made by Dulan Workshop. I’m sure that it’s not real!” a golden griffin knight sitting across from Sala assured her and picked up the bottle of iced red tea with his right hand.","“I wish that I can come here every day,” Sala said excitedly, “I like this plot. This cultivation mystic realm has a complete and thrilling story.” She was eager to find out what would happen in this new story.","After sipping her milk tea gracefully, Helen said, “But I like the environment of this shop more.”","The computers lined up against the windows in rows of two with thick leather chairs. With Helen sitting next to her, Sala had other elves sitting behind her and the golden griffin knights across from her. As for Elina and the other assassins, they sat at the long oval stone table close to the counter.","These were the seats that the elves would pass by on their way to the counter.","When they had time, the players would walk over and watch others play, cheering for the good plays when they saw them. In contrast, other cultivation mystical realms gave each of the users a private cultivation room. No one would see their excellent performances in battles if it wasn’t broadcasted by Spiritual Spell Visual Projection.","Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood told the story about Ezio who had gotten a Piece of Eden and grown into a true master assassin.","Thinking that the war was over, Ezio wasn’t someone who possessed great ambition. Like Altair, he had also understood the true meaning of the assassin’s creed.","He would have returned to his peaceful life, but Cesare Borgia, a templar knight and the son of the Pope, broke into Ezio and his Uncle Mario’s villa with troops. To ensure the townspeople’s safe retreat, his Uncle Mario was killed while Ezio escaped from the slaughter and traveled to Rome.","As a person who would use every means to get what he wanted, Cesare Borgia not only craved for the Pieces of Eden but was scheming to overthrow his father to gain power. To counter the templar knights led by the ambitious Cesare Borgia, Ezio had no choice but to reassemble the Brotherhood.","Meanwhile, the modern-day plot continued in Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood. For example, their hideout was the villa left by Mario. The Main Character Desmond was trained in virtual reality as well.","By now, Desmond had learned most of the assassin skills from his ancestors. including Eagle Vision and the Leap of Faith.","At this moment, Elina had passed the introduction of the game. Before her was a silver-gray memory zone. Soon, she saw training options for different combat techniques such as counterattack, techniques with different weapons, hidden blade assassination, and combo kills.","Combo kills was a newly-added skill which required swift and smooth movements to kill each target. Any blocking or dodging from the target and missing the vital organs would be regarded as a failure. Meticulous attention to details was a great challenge in the use of combo kill.","In fact, with combo kill, Ezio could slaughter a city alone in the original game. The System had re-created this skill, but to master it and use it smoothly without any warrior qi or spiritual essence required the players to have ultimate control of their body.","As an master assassin, Ezio could do it. But the players...","“Ahh-!” With a shriek, Elina was knocked down by over ten well-armed templar knights.","After passing Assassin’s Creed 1, she could deal with two to three opponents, but it was impossible to kill more than ten templar knights, each with one strike.","After all, these well-trained and well-armed knights were not morons!","Even Elina, who was an assassin in real life, paled when she saw this inhuman training method...","“Is this training designed for humans?!”","“Forget it...” After several failed attempts, she decided to check out the plot first and try to learn something by watching how Ezio reassembled the Brotherhood.","After all, the assassins in the Morning Light Empire had almost collapsed.","They were going to learn the combo kill later.","“Auch!” Failing again, Elf Girl Sala felt like crying while she stared at the gray screen.","“Why can’t I master it...”","In fact, she found that this combat technique was quite cool. After all, she was lousy at stealthy movements and could only fight her way to her target.","It emphasized the advantage of techniques. It would be so cool to murmur what Mr. Fang said before, which was ‘Don’t assassinate; use musou’ during the process! At the thought that she could return to Silver Moon Forest equipped with this high-level technique, she was a little thrilled.","Glancing around, she found that her teammates were also practicing this technique!","“Oh! I must work harder on it!”","Thinking that she was going to return to Silver Moon Forest soon, she put more efforts in her training.","...","Meanwhile, in the godly palace church in Canglan City.","“Mr. Luther and the masters of Dulan Workshop are about to set off, right?” The red-robed senior priest looked toward the distance and said mildly, “Soon, the glorious light of God will shine into that tranquil and peaceful forest!”","“It’s time for those complacent elves to be amazed by the top-quality craftsmanship of our Judgement Godly Palace!” Glass laughed coldly."]},{"number":624,"title":"Chapter 624 - The Assassination at Castel Sant’Angelo","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","It must be noted that the Eagle Vision re-created by the System was a combination of intuitive senses and eyes. On the screen, the players could see that important objects were highlighted while the background turned gray.","The players could use this skill to do many other things besides finding certain objects, including seeing through things, sharing visions, marking targets, and tracking, etc.","Eagle Vision could also locate targets, which had helped Altair in his final battle with his mentor Al Mualim, who created many illusions of himself with a Piece of Eden. With Eagle Vision, Altair had detected Al Mualim’s true self hidden in the crowd.","It was why his mentor Al Mualim lost to him even though the former had the powerful godly artifact.","When Eagle Vison evolved to Eagle Sense, it could heighten all the user’s senses, allowing them to foresee danger and see certain scenes in the past or in the future.","For example, when Shay was ambushed by assassins, he would hear heavy panting and whispers if he didn’t activate Eagle Vison. If he did, he could detect the exact spot of the danger.","The plot of Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood consisted of several sequences.","After training in the real world, the main character would enter the first sequence. It was when Ezio first came to Rome; it was the desolate Rome under the ruling of Borgia.","In the second sequence, he began to form an alliance with the thieves and mercenaries in Rome. After Ezio had gained his foothold, the game entered the next memory sequence in which Ezio began to reassemble the Brotherhood, recruiting novices, and acquiring weapons of war.","The ancient world in Assassin’s Creed wasn’t like the traditional renaissance era of Earth. Due to the existence of the Pieces of Eden, there were some... black technologies.","The weapons used in this era were ancient versions of machine guns, gliders, tanks, and marine cannons created by Da Vinci with the knowledge derived from the Pieces of Eden.","Of course, they were all in the ancient style.","Obviously, Ezio had a different personality from that of Altair. The latter was a clear-headed and wise master who was a pioneer in setting the new code of conduct for assassins. His grand life was mainly spent in the battle for the freedom and cause of assassins. However, Ezio was more multi-faceted. In Florence, he was sentimental and romantic, looking more human compared to his ancestor Altair, who was a saint in the series of Assassin Creed.","In this sequence, when Ezio saw that Caterina was captured by the Borgia Family at the bridge outside Castel Sant’Angelo, the first thing he did was entering the castle alone to rescue her.","Across the sparkling wide river sat a wide arched bridge paved with white rocks and lined with twelve statues of angels. Beyond the bridge were a grand high tower and dense buildings protected by the high castle walls.","“Can anyone break into this castle alone with only techniques and no strength...?” Elina was excited. “It’s awesome!”","After all, when they tried to assassinate Luther, that godly palace wasn’t as big as this castle.","Breaking into a castle was obviously a huge challenge for one person.","In the original game, the players could choose to sneak in or break in from the main gate with force, A.K.A musou. Of course, in the system version, breaking in with force would be extremely difficult. After all, there were firearms in this era instead of only arrows, as it was in Altair’s time.","At this moment, the other assassins were doing this mission too.","“What do you think?” Harrison asked in excitement.","“The design is awesome!” another assassin said, “Sneaking into such a huge and heavily-guarded castle without the aid of any stealth spiritual spells is thrilling.”","“Let’s begin! If we can make it a success, I think the anti-stealth spiritual spells and anti-air spiritual spells in the godly palace will be useless against us because we won’t need any stealth spiritual spells at all!” Elina chose the safest way and sneaked to the bottom of the castle from below the bridge outside Castel Sant’Angelo.","As a qualified assassin, one must sneak up to the target! she thought.","Ezio moved swiftly like a swallow flying low under the bridge close to the water. While dodging the guards on the watchtowers, he soon came to the outside of the castle wall.","After climbing up the wall, he found two soldiers patrolling along the wall close to the flowerbed platform. There was another guard standing on the platform.","Having just climbed onto the wall, Elina killed one of the patrolling guards with a smooth attack of her hidden blade.","“Assassin! Assassin-!” The other two guards began to yell in alarm.","“My goodness!” Elina exclaimed, turning pale when she saw many soldiers swarming toward her. “Are you guys in? I failed to sneak in!”","“I’m using musou now!” Harrison yelled.","“I’ve killed about four soldiers!” another assassin shouted, “I failed to sneak in; I’ll try that again next time!”","“...”","“Yaaa-!” Drawing out her longsword, Elina yelled and charged at the soldiers.","In a flash, she killed one with a counterattack.","“Wow-! This counterattack is awesome!” From behind her came Elf Girl Sala’s exclamation.","“Oh...” Hearing this melodious praise, Elina perked up with confidence.","Then, she lifted her left hand and shot one soldier dead. Next, she hacked and slashed with her sword at the soldiers.","“Ayahhh...” She used ‘musou’ and battled.","Surrounded by enemies, she swung her blade and killed them without even taking a better look.","– Several minutes later –","“Hu...” On the screen, Ezio, whose white robe had turned red from blood, heaved a sigh of relief, and Elina said, “I’ve killed about a dozen of them. No one sees me now; I can continue to sneak in ...”","She was on the outer range of the castle, and the soldiers would come in groups of four or five instead of ten, which meant that she could take care of them and continue the game.","Another assassin said, “... I lost synchronization.”","Assassin Harrison said, “My HP is low, and I will soon lose synchronization. I’ll recover first. No one knows where I am now; I’ll sneak in...”","“Wow... You killed more than ten guards!” Elf girl Sala exclaimed, “Awesome!”","Elina turned her head and saw that it came from an elf girl.","“Do you want to play together?” Elina remembered that they could play the multiplayer mode in the later stage.","“Okay!” Happily, Elf Girl Sala added Elina as her friend.","At this moment, the whole castle tightened its security with the discovery of intruders. Elina still thought that she, a qualified assassin, must do the assassination in a stealthy way.","Before the next group of soldiers came, she leaped onto the roof of the castle to avoid them. While she moved on the roof, she witnessed Cesare’s ambition and schemes.","“Are you practicing combo kills and preparing for musou?” Elf Girl Sala asked curiously.","“No...” Elina’s pretty face twitched. As a real assassin, she must assassinate in a stealthy way!","She said immediately, “I’m doing an assassination.”","Then, she moved along the eaves silently.","“If I move stealthily, no one will discover me!” As a real assassin, she certainly couldn’t act in the same way as ordinary people. Elina decided to show the friendly elf girl her true strength.","She controlled Ezio to stick out his head and glance around. Glancing at the patrolling guard on the roofs, he took out his hand crossbow silently. “Look. I’ll just shoot him with the hand crossbow, and he won’t see me.”","Then, she shot out an arrow with her crossbow.","“He’s here!” Suddenly, Elina heard a yell. It came from a guard hidden in a spot dozens of meters away from the dead patrolling soldier.","“Ahhh-!” Aware that the elf girl was watching her play, Elina was furious that she was spotted by this sharp-eyed guard. Erupting into action, she dashed over and slashed her sword furiously.","“My goodness! I was spotted again!” Beside her, Harrison yelled, “Were you guys spotted?”","“No. I’m still sneaking in!” With gritted teeth, Elina looked at the bodies lying all around her with a blush on her pretty face. “Now, no one discovered me!”","She continued to move stealthily."]},{"number":625,"title":"Chapter 625 - The Silver Moon Forest","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","After killing all the soldiers who had spotted her, Elina controlled Ezio to swiftly climb up to the huge round tower in the center of the castle. After dodging all the pursuing soldiers, she would be able to gather a lot of intelligence in this place.","While soldiers were searching for Ezio in at least half of the castle, Elina controlled Ezio to stand outside of the window of the round tower and watched Cesare and his sister flirt and kiss, putting on a German incest show.","“Oh, my goodness! Such a hot scene!” Elina found the life of an assassin thrilling. Moving in stealth provided her with lots of fun.","After putting down her virtual reality headset, she opened a bag of potato chips and began watching the hot scene while enjoying the chips.","Standing behind her, Sala blushed and said, “Ahh! Why don’t you shoot them!”","Covering her face, Sala wished that she could burn this despicable couple to death.","After watching the mature content, Ezio climbed to the cell which was situated on the top of the tower.","Although the original game provided all kinds of handholds for players, the players in the new version had to make their own handholds and footholds by sticking daggers into the wall. It was a test of physical strength and climbing skills.","As a skillful assassin who mastered all sorts of related techniques, Elina climbed all the way to the top. This time, she was even more cautious. Holding throwing knives with her left hand and a hand crossbow with her right hand at the same time, she silently killed a guard who was standing on the roof and a hidden guard in the distance.","On the screen, a white figure flew down from the sky. Then, Elina controlled Ezio to jump-kill a patrolling guard.","“Awesome!”","“Of course!” As a professional assassin, she was talented in this area.","“Sala, what are you watching?” A few other elves walked over.","“Look at this lady; her assassination skills are awesome!” Sala avidly watched Elina assassinate another patrolling guard.","In Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood, the players could fight in some places. But in other places, they must stay hidden and not be discovered. Otherwise, they would lose synchronization.","Gripping two throwing knives, Elina walked along the corridor cautiously, listening for the slight sounds of steps coming from the walls and the ground.","Then, she dashed out, throwing out the knives rapidly.","“Wow-!” The people watching behind her exclaimed when two soldiers dropped to the ground silently.","Elina then entered the cell, which signaled the end of the first stage of sneaking in. On the screen, it showed that she had achieved 85% synchronization in the whole process.","“You’re superb!” The elves who could only barge in had very low synchronization rates.","“This lady’s skills are awesome!” After all, Mr. Fang only demonstrated the skills of fighting his way in. No one had ever shown such high-level stealth skills and sneaked into a place.","“I can only barge in. How did you kill those guys with two throwing knives?” A golden griffin knight complimented her by asking. Obviously, he had never done any stealthy move with success.","“Thank you...” Elina froze for a second. In fact, she had never imagined that assassins and assassination skills would be praised by others.","If it were before, she would have been cussed at and accused of being a despicable backstabber.","However, today, the people watched and cheered for her excellent and glorious skills in stealthily moving in the dark.","It was beyond Elina’s wildest imagination.","Despite a few stumbles which exposed her several times, she managed to regain synchronization each time and finally got the prisoner out.","In a daze, the audience watched as Ezio let Caterina escape first on a horse while he blocked the pursuit of the soldiers who were swarming out of the castle.","“My Goodness!”","“Auch!” Elina exclaimed, and then her screen turned gray as she lost synchronization.","“Um... I didn’t pass this stage...” With a dark expression, she went on to do virtual training.","As an assassin, she could not be good at assassinations, but it was intolerable to have weak foundational skills! She immediately went to practice.","...","Lately, the elves dashed to the shop as soon as they washed up each morning.","“Sir! Deposit 100 magic crystals in my card!” On the next morning, Sala dumped a pile of magic crystals on Mr. Fang’s counter. With the thought that she would return to the Silver Moon Forest soon, she didn’t deposit too many crystals. However, she had been buying potato chips, spicy sticks, and milk tea, and she had spent all of the money on her card.","While pinching her cheek, Sala felt like she became fat and wondered if she would become a fat elf before her return.","But it wasn’t time to worry about that.","After entering the game, Sala sneaked into a military base with smooth moves. With a few slashes, she killed all the guards. On her screen, Ezio flew with a glider and threw bombs from the sky.","On the other side, another elf drove a disk-shaped fortress! Boom! Boom! Boom!","“Look!” A golden griffin knight yelled, “Oh! I’ve recruited some beautiful blonde girls! Would you like to hear my tips?”","On the screen, he was surrounded by a group of blonde girls in assassin cloaks.","“...”","Elina, who was passing by, was almost blinded by the sight.","“Pu!” Is this still a Brotherhood?!","Even Mr. Fang’s face twitched.","...","“Emm...” The golden morning sunlight shined through the window into a room inside the group of castles on the top of the mountain and rested on an exquisite sleeping face. Long lashes fluttered, and Sala slowly opened her eyes.","“Haya!” With a yell, she almost jumped out from the bed, doing a counterattack move with her hands.","She froze for a second and looked at the quilt that had slipped down the bed and her pure-white pajamas, and she woke up completely.","“No... Today, we are returning to Silver Moon Forest!”","They had come to this city to investigate something. Now that the work was done, they had postponed their journey back home long enough. It was time to return.","On this vast continent, humans hadn’t conquered every part of the land. Darkness still existed under the sunshine, and all kinds of magic beasts were concealed in the deep and dense forests. One of the reasons that elves seldom traveled to human nations was because the journey was long and difficult.","At this moment, as the envoy from the Judgement Godly Palace, Luther had arrived at Silver Moon Forest with a large team of guards from the Judgement Godly Palace.","This fat envoy sized up this land with glints flashing in his eyes. Silver Moon Forest was like a radiant jade inlaid in this bountiful and beautiful land. This clan with the natural gift of a longer lifespan than humans had been living on this land since ancient times."]},{"number":626,"title":"Chapter 626 - The War of Faith","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","There had been conflicts on this land since ancient times, and some dark marks of those conflicts were still left in some places. This time, the envoys from the Judgement Godly Palace brought light with them.","“I pray to God that he will dispel the gloominess from this land!” Luther chanted. It was his first time entering a land inhabited by non-humans.","It wasn’t spring, but the winds here were balmy with all kinds of flower fragrances. The cities were built on both sides of the rivers with all kinds of plants covering the buildings.","Under the elves’ meticulous care, the plants looked organized and beautiful. The path of gravel traveled through the forest with the group of buildings winding their way down the mountains without the restrictions of city walls. This was Auderalei, one of the elf cities. Its name meant ‘a small creek with clear and white-water ripples.’ Therefore, it was also called White Creek City.","As time went by, the creek had turned into a wide river, but people still called it with the old name.","The elf clan didn’t have a large population. In Silver Moon Forest, one could count the number of cities of this scale with one hand. The elves living out of the cities mostly lived in their own groups. Obviously, few humans could enter this forest.","If one day, a human nation could gain permission from the Elf Council of Elders and build magic teleportation arrays to connect this forest with the human world, it would be a major event that would shock the whole world.","St. Heinz sat in his grand and glorious godly palace with a chessboard before him. One half of the chessboard was white with lively sculptured pieces of knights and mages. In the middle stood a dignified-looking noble man holding a scepter.","The other half was black, and the knight standing in the center raised a longsword.","He placed a white chess piece on the black area opposite to him.","It was obvious that the white chess pieces had the upper hand.","Sitting across to him was a holy-looking old man wearing a snow-white priest robe. He stroked his beard and said with a smile, “Mr. St. Heinz, your chess skill is as stunning as usual.”","“I heard that the result of your research has even amazed many saints, Mr. Dulan?” St. Heinz said mildly.","“Hahahaha...” The white-haired old man laughed and said, “They were arguing about a useless problem, and their eyes almost popped out when they saw my conclusion. In this area, I’m confident in my abilities.”","His smile oozed confidence.","“By the way...” St. Dulan said, “The envoys are about to reach Silver Moon Forest, My Lord.”","St. Heinz said calmly, “They brought the best products of the Dulan Workshop with them.”","“They are the products of my disciples; I just gave them some tips. They are nothing.” St. Dulan shook his head with a chuckle, giving the impression that he was looking down from the peak of the tallest mountain.","St. Heinz said with a smile, “I think the elves will feel fortunate to get advice from St. Dulan.”","...","For elves, they treated every visitor as their guest, which was a tradition of this ancient and polite clan. They welcomed any visitor who showed no hostility.","While welcoming this big team of visitors, a cheerful atmosphere permeated the streets in the entire city as if the elves were celebrating a grand festival.","“Welcome, Mr. Luther.” The elves were friendly to any visitor who had the permission to enter their cities.","Cheers and elegant harp music floated in the clear sky. With squinted eyes, Luther looked around with his right hand behind his back in a loose fist as he walked forward with the sincerest smile he could muster.","“Elder Sewell.” Luther dismounted from his winged lion and slightly bowed at the group of elves who were walking up to him.","“I’m pleased to see you, Mr. Luther.” The leader was an elf woman whose age was indeterminable at first glance. With the spirit of a teenage girl, she had the calm presence and mature grace of a woman in her thirties. She had long blond hair resting on her shoulders, and she wore a deep green body-fitting robe which accentuated her elegant and slim figure. Each move of hers looked extremely graceful and wise.","Her tone was mild while she said, “I’m surprised that Mr. Luther would make a journey to our place in person. But as you know, we don’t welcome missionaries.”","“Of course,” Luther said, “But I come to Silver Moon Forest as a merchant. I hope you don’t have the wrong impression about the purpose of my trip, Elder.”","“Oh...?” This female elf elder looked surprised. “I didn’t know that you’ve changed your profession, Mr. Luther.”","Since the elf clan wasn’t self-sufficient with everything, they traded merchandise with humans while the relationship between the two races gradually eased in. It was true that they seldom mingled with humans, but this freedom-loving clan didn’t impose many restrictions on the interchange of goods.","However, foreign missionaries were not allowed to preach in Silver Moon Forest. Although there were no written rules forbidding it, this behavior was frowned upon as a blasphemy to the elves’ own god.","“I brought a brand-new cultivation mystical realm with me! It is so advanced that it will feel like it is from the next era.” While they walked toward the Elder Council Hall in White Creek City, Luther announced in a loud voice, “It’s the newest product of the Dulan Workshop. I think everyone can appreciate a good product, including elves.”","“We welcome you as our guest, but I think we have our own cultivation mystical realms and don’t need one from outside.” Elder Sewell obviously had no interest in the new stuff since the elf clan had bountiful inheritances and great skills in making this stuff.","Luther seemed very eloquent with words. “Maybe... you can just try it and see if our mystical realm is as good as yours. If possible, I think the wonderful people of your clan wouldn’t mind having another option.”","Sewell’s gaze wavered as if she were thinking of something.","At this moment, another elf said mildly, “Although I don’t think we need it, I think Mr. Luther is right. Our people will make the choice for themselves. If it is truly an excellent product, we can’t stop people from using it. Anyway, we are confident in our own crafts.”","The speaker was a male elf who appeared to be in his thirties. With a smile, he said the words as if he were making a statement.","“Zizz is right.” Obviously, many people agreed with this male elf. “We are confident in our own crafts, right?”","Elder Sewell frowned slightly since she had sensed the meaning behind Luther’s words.","Proud and reserved, the elves had their own long-standing combat techniques and magic spells which enabled them to gain a high standing on the continent. They were proud of their own cultivation mystical realms and didn’t think that they need to import such things.","However, Luther claimed that he had brought a mystical realm as good as theirs.","It was not only a sales tactic; it was also a concealed provocation.","While the realization dawned on her, the situation seemed to begin to slide out of her control.","At this moment, in the glorious grand hall in the Judgement Godly Palace, St. Heinz put down another chess piece.","“The elves are indeed smart, but they are also overconfident and overly prideful, which makes them arrogant and conceited,” St. Dulan said with a smile, “That elder is intelligent, but the other elves are not so smart. Besides...”","An indescribable smile appeared on his face as he said, “This move is indeed excellent, My Lord.”","“But I think you have more plans for them, right,” St. Dulan continued.","“You saw through it?” St. Heinz said expressionlessly, “If it’s only a mission to bring the cultivation mystical realm to other races, it doesn’t need me planning everything.”","“This is the beginning of the war of faith.” He put down another chess piece lightly, but the move seemed to hold weight as it felt like thunder rumbled behind him.","St. Dulan froze for a moment. Then, he inhaled deeply with a solemn expression as if the whole chess game became grand and majestic because of this sentence."]},{"number":627,"title":"Chapter 627 - The Chains of Faith","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","– Meanwhile, in the Elder Council Hall in the center of White Creek City –","Elder Sewell obviously couldn’t find a good excuse to decline. After all, the most important reason the elves had was that they didn’t think it was necessary to import any cultivation mystical realm since they believed that their ancient crafts were more advanced than that of humans.","Elves could make the decision by themselves, and several elite elves supported this suggestion due to their pride.","“Since Mr. Luther has such great confidence in the product from the Dulan Workshop, I think we can’t refuse the offer.” Elder Sewell stood up and said, “But are you sure that anyone from our clan, including elf guards and ordinary citizens, can try it out?”","“Of course.” Luther’s puffy face smiled. “We are well prepared and are highly confident in the product and in St. Dulan.","Sewell looked surprised. She knew that the Dulan Workshop was an organization under that famous saint level master, but everyone thought that he hadn’t gotten involved in the business for years.","“I didn’t know that it was a product created by that entity.” Elder Sewell looked grim, but she was still confident in her clan’s strength and craftsmanship. “I’ll give you three days, Mr. Luther. If you can prove that your cultivation mystical realm is as good as you claim, I don’t think I will refuse your offer to bring this good item to our people.”","“Thank you!” Luther got up with a smile. “You’re a wise person.”","Elder Sewell instructed a male elf behind her, “Please bring Mr. Luther to the Spellcaster Square.”","...","Spellcaster Square was a place often visited by the elf mages. Only around this square could people see cultivation mystical realms.","In the center of the huge square was a statue of a female elf who had a flower wreath on her head and a scepter lifted high in her hand. On the base of the sculpture was a huge flowerbed, and several elf poets sat around it, playing harps.","Of course, the most common visitors were elf rogues with longswords hanging at their belts and big bows on their backs as well as elf mages with magic staves.","“Do you need a cultivation room?” Elder Sewell asked.","“No, we don’t,” Luther said with a chuckle, “St. Dulan gave it a new feature which enables us to launch it on the square.”","Soon, several godly palace knights set up the mystical realm on the rectangle-shaped tall platform on the east side of the square. Behind the white curtains was a fixed magic array disk engraved with complicated and beautiful pale golden array patterns. Luther asked smugly, “Do you guys want to try it? It’s much more convenient than traditional cultivation mystical realms. Believe me; it’s a product of the next era.”","Seeing the hesitation in the elves, Luther beckoned to a godly palace knight and said, “Please try it out for us.”","He took out a crystal from his storage space and put it on the stone table which was especially set up to hold this crystal.","The light emitting from the crystal soon turned into a curtain of thick mist through which a clear image gradually appeared.","It seemed that the original space had been erased, and in its place was the clear scene from another world.","Obviously, it was an advanced Spiritual Spell Visual Projection.","At this moment, they saw that the knight had changed into ordinary leather armor on the screen, and there were eight teleportation arrays in this misty fantasy world.","Luther explained, “Each teleportation array can turn into a different mystical realm. This is a compound mystical realm designed by St. Dulan from the assassination attempts that he experienced and the related conspiracies. In this mystical realm, we’ll encounter several assassination attempts and some battles between small-scale legions. Of course, during your leisure time, you can practice your skills by hunting magic beasts in the forests. We even put in the extremely useful anti-assassination spiritual spells and the optimized casting methods. These spells include Radiant Light Detection, Energy Resonance, Darkness Dispel, etc.”","While he talked, Luther was satisfied to see the surprise on Elder Sewell’s face.","“If my memories are right, Radiant Light Detection and Energy Resonance are the godly palace’s secret spiritual spells, right?” Elder Sewell asked.","“You’re right,” Luther said in a loud voice, “But St. Dulan is generous. To remove all the despicable sneak-attackers, he decided to share these spiritual spells with the public.”","Luther continued, “But this mystical realm has more than advanced spiritual spells.”","“It can decide what level of mystical realm to use according to the user’ strength.” At this moment, the knight entered a strange-looking secret chamber through a teleportation array.","In the secret chamber, they could see a grand human city.","The setting sun created a long shadow of the city.","On the wide street in the center of the city, the knight acted as a guard in a team of officials from the godly palace.","“...” Looking at the high-resolution images, Elder Sewell was even more astonished.","“Look! He is a level 6 knight, so he is protecting a senior priest instead of St. Dulan.”","“After all,” He chuckled and said, “Not every ordinary person can enter a battle involving Mr. Dulan.”","He continued, “Here, we can arrange the positions of the guards in the team. Of course, the current arrangement is quite good, but the mystical realm gives other options for you to choose. You can also choose to be assassins to check the effectiveness of our guards.”","Luther continued with great passion, “Regardless if you’re a mercenary or an elf guard, it’s necessary to learn how to protect a group of people and fight with attackers. The combat techniques learned from real combat are much more dependable than those in ordinary one-to-one training or solo training.”","He became even more smug when he saw Elder Sewell look more astonished each second. “I think this is what a real cultivation mystical realm should look like.”","“It looks very good.” Elder Sewell hid her astonishment, not expecting the Dulan Workshop to make such a great improvement in the production of cultivation mystical realms. “But to see if a mystical realm is a good one or not, we don’t look at its convenience. The most important feature is the design of battles. Some mystical realms look good but have battles too good to be true. Besides, assassinations are full of unexpected elements, and you never know what kind of enemies you will meet.”","“Then, why don’t you try it?” Luther smiled with confidence. After the assassination attempt on him, the Dulan Workshop had further strengthened the anti-assassination abilities in this mystical realm. “I dare to say that no one understands this area more than we do. I’m sure that no assassins can break this cultivation mystical realm.”","– Meanwhile, in St. Heinz’ palace –","When a white chess piece was put down on the black section of the chessboard, that place emitted a vague white light.","St. Heinz said mildly, “Only when they are convinced will they accept the beliefs. When they begin to believe, the faith will be slowly attached to them like chains on their necks.”","“If some fanatic believers appear in this clan...” Even St. Dulan had a thread of excitement in his voice."]},{"number":628,"title":"Chapter 628 - Even Master Assassins Can’t Pass This Mystical Realm","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","People couldn’t preach their beliefs in the nation if they couldn’t open the gates.","Luther believed that the mystical realm was an excellent item that would help them move into the elf clan. After all, the elves had no reason to refuse it.","This was the first and the most important step which would eventually give them the opportunity to obtain the treasures that they wanted in this rich and beautiful land which had never been exploited before.","I’ll amaze these ignorant elves with the great advancements that we have achieved on the continent. Luther squinted his small eyes and smiled. He seemed to foresee the scene in which this rich land gradually submitted to them in St. Heinz’ subsequent plans, and the elves called for the God of Radiant Light Judgement. “This is our best training method for guards, and we’ve designed and optimized plans to handle all kinds of emergencies. Now, is there anyone who wants to try it? I’m sure you’ll like it.”","At this moment, many elves had gathered on the square. In the past, they had seen humans coming here to sell their products, but none of them were this big in scale.","Like favored treasures of nature, the elves were all exquisite and beautiful. These audience members created a gorgeous scene while they stood on the square and watched the show.","“By the way,” Luther said, “I’m sure that you don’t know those dark spiritual spells, so we’ve prepared all kinds of stealth spiritual spell scrolls for the people who intend to play as assassins.”","“As for the knights, we will only use the spiritual spells that you’re familiar with, including the Radiant Light Detection, Energy Resonance, and Darkness Dispel instead of godly spells to counter the stealth spells. To be fair, we can put the venue in the forest.”","“This is...” Elder Sewell was a bit embarrassed, thinking that the conditions were too good to decline. Although assassins were at the disadvantage, things would be different when the battle venue was put in the forest.","“We’ll try it!” A small team of elves stood out.","“Please.” Luther gestured gracefully.","...","“The cultivation mystical realm in that shop is truly interesting.” A small team of elves was advancing slowly along the winding river toward the center of the city.","Elf Girl Sala still looked groggy since she hadn’t slept well last night; she gave a very unladylike yawn. “Yawn...”","Noticing her teammates’ baffled glances, the elf girl who always took care of herself to maintain a ladylike image instantly woke up.","“Yeah. I hope that we’ll go and visit that shop again when we have time.” The Team Captain looked at the blue sky reminiscently. “I do miss the spicy sticks. They are an ultimate delicacy.”","He brought out a bottle of iced red tea and took a sip of it with great enjoyment.","“I heard that that despicable Luther has come to our elf clan,” Sala said in displeasure, “This big liar did his best to belittle the people in another continent. Instead, I only saw courage, elegance, and power in those people.”","“Ugh? Why are they all running toward that direction?” An elf young man beside Sala pointed forward and asked curiously, “What’s happening?”","Soon, they pushed their way into the inner circle of the crowd and heard a wave of exclamations before they could stand still.","In the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection, the elves had been butchered by the team of knights wearing godly palace armor.","With a huge sword in hand, one knight killed the last elf, and the blood sprayed all over the projection.","“Are they... the Elder Guard Team?!” Sala yelled in alarm.","“My goodness!”","“So powerful...”","“How can it be?!”","“This is the third attempt. Do you want to have one more try?” While looking at the result of the battle on the screen, Luther said with a laugh, “You sent the Elder Guard Team. This time, will you try it yourself, Elder?”","“What is this despicable guy up to this time?” The newly arrived elf team members frowned at the scene before them.","“Regardless of how you hide yourselves, you’ll always leave behind a clue.”","On the screen, the knight walked under a big tree.","“Look. He can still detect a very tiny fluctuation of a spiritual spell. This one hid himself well but he still was discovered by our knights,” Luther explained as if these elves, regardless of how they hid themselves, were just a joke to him.","“Then, they’ll engage in upfront battle.” Luther continued to explain from his experience, “Regardless of how the elves attack, the knights can immediately find the best formation and combat techniques to use to fight back.”","He said proudly when he got to this point, “I can say with pride that our mystical realm is absolutely the best in the whole world.”","At this moment, St. Dulan activated a Spiritual Spell Visual Projection to show the scenes sent back by Luther.","“How are things going with the Elf Clan?” St. Heinz asked mildly.","“Hahaha!” While watching the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection, Dulan laughed and said, “From the looks of it, things are going very well for us. All the elves watching the mystical realm are stunned by our creation. Maybe the news has even spread to the Elf Royal Palace by now.”","“I wonder... if the Elf Queen Her Majesty will be angry about this,” Dulan laughed heartily.","...","Meanwhile, a hearty laugh sounded on the square in White Creek City. “I invite anyone here to check out our perfect defense system. I dare to say that even the most powerful assassin can’t leave this mystical realm alive. Yes, the most powerful assassin will definitely become a corpse in this mystical realm. Do you guys want to train in this mystical realm...”","“Nonsense!” A furious voice came from the crowd.","Sala pushed out from the crowd and said angrily with her hands on her waist, “The method shown in this mystical realm can’t block any real assassins!”","“...”","Everyone looked over and saw that it was a young elf girl.","“Isn’t this the Snow Pigeon Team? How come they are here?”","Luther’s small eyes squinted. “It’s easy to bluff. Little Girl, it’s a pity that there’re no real master assassins among us. Otherwise, I will show you how they are defeated in this mystical realm.”"]},{"number":629,"title":"Chapter 629 - Elf assassins who were led to the wrong path by Mr. Fang","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","The knight captain on the side added, “Any assassination skills and stealth movements are only jokes in front of this mystical realm.”","Walking out of the crowd, Lance bowed at Elder Sewell and said, “I think we can have a try.”","“You...?” Elder Sewell obviously knew Lance.","“Elder, we’d like to have a try.” Sala walked up as well. “Didn’t he say that anyone can check it out?”","“Little Sala...” Elder Sewell patted Sala’s head. This young elf had grown up under her eyes, but...","She shook her head and said, “It’s not a game. Even the Elder Guard Team failed...”","“Please... just let us try!” Sala used her secret technique, which was begging and acting cute.","“Um...”","Luther was displeased with this interruption since he was about to end this session with success.","He asked casually, “Little Girl, do you know this stuff?”","“A little bit,” Sala said, “Before I returned, I met two masters named Altair and Ezio, and they taught me some basic skills.”","Watching the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection, St. Dulan froze. “There are such assassins?”","Elder Sewell frowned slightly, wondering how Sala managed to mingle with human assassins during her trip. After all, assassins had a bad reputation among humans.","At this moment, a peaceful round lake was also projecting the scene happening in White Creek City. This lake was surrounded by beautiful and grand buildings that were a part of the Elf Royal Palace which seemed like they were built in ancient times.","“Altair? Ezio? When did the humans have these master assassins? Are they frauds?”","Luther laughed and said, “Okay. But I must tell you that I’ve never heard of their names before. I hope these two unknown people helped you and can make you last one minute in the mystical realm, cute girl.”","Soon, Sala entered the cultivation mystical realm.","Elder Sewell looked at the young elf captain in bafflement as she asked, “What are you guys waiting for?”","“If we all enter, it’s impossible to assassinate...” The elves looked exasperated.","“Ugh...?”","Luther froze as well. While looking at the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection, he asked, “She will enter alone?”","“Right,” the other elves said calmly.","“I wonder if the little girl came here to joke around?” Behind Luther, the knight captain also grinned.","Suddenly, exclamations rose in the square in White Creek City.","The audience watched while the elf girl on the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection walked directly toward the dense forest with a sword in her hand.","“!!??”","“What is she doing?!”","“She doesn’t even know how to hide herself!”","“Go up and hide on a tree!” Elves usually got up into the big trees and shot at their enemies with arrows.","Protecting several red-robed priests, a team of about 20 knights in armor came along the forest path toward Sala.","Elder Sewell’s face darkened at this scene.","Are you here to make more trouble for me?","She glared at the other elves beside her and asked, “What’s happening?!”","“She’s doing it to avoid her opponents’ spiritual spell detection,” one young elf answered.","“...” Elder Sewell turned livid in fury, wondering how someone could dodge detection this way!","With a smile, Luther watched the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection as if he were waiting to see this reckless elf girl humiliate herself.","He was sure that the Elf Queen must be watching this battle in her royal palace as well.","He wondered what expression she had at this moment.","“Mr. Luther, your tea.” A knight brought Luther a cup of tea so that he could ease his thirst after talking for so long.","“She will just follow the others and humiliate herself,” Luther chuckled and removed the cup lid while his eyes were glued on the screen.","On the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection, the team of knights had obviously seen the girl walking toward them.","The knight at the foremost of the team roared and hacked down his huge sword with a horrifying whistling sound. “Wind Roar Hack!”","Sala raised her long sword. When she played Assassin’s Creed, she couldn’t use her essence, but it was different now. She wondered what would happen when she added her powerful strength to the excellent skills she learned from the game.","While recalling the things that she had learned in the virtual reality training, Sala circulated the essence in her body.","“Speed up! Wind Power!”","Sala took a swift stride forward, instantly getting close to that knight. Then, she pushed her slim sword against her opponent’s sword handle with a slight force.","Boom!","The huge sword suddenly moved to one side and heavily crashed into the ground beside Sala. Under the strong momentum, the knight couldn’t withdraw his sword, and he watched as Sala’s sword stabbed into his chest in horror.","Counterattack!","Before the others could attack, her blade that was covered in blood instantly slit open another knight’s throat.","She moved slightly and stabbed her sword into the chest of a knight on her left.","Remembering the extremely cool combo that the shop owner had demonstrated, she decided to copy them.","Combo skill begin!","The audience heard Sala murmur while she slashed and hacked, “Don’t assassinate; use musou!”","The sword in her hand looked like an instrument of great precision.","Seeing Sala killing five knights, Luther froze with the teacup in his hand after having taken one mouthful of tea.","Tink!","A crisp noise sounded.","“Oops! My combo kills are not connected. I’m sorry.” Her sword pierced forward again into the knight’s chest.","Elder Sewell’s eyes almost popped out, and she thought, You killed five of them with one strike each and feel sorry for being slightly on the defense?!","“There’s not enough time for you to move in stealth. Just fight and kill. Stealth is useless since you’ll be discovered sooner or later!”","While Sala said those words, she had downed about nine knights.","“Killing everyone who saw you is the perfect assassination, right?” When she finished, no one was standing.","“What did I see...?!” The elf audience on the square froze at the scene.","In St. Heinz’ palace, Dulan and Heinz exchanged a look of disbelief.","What’s happening?! Ahh!","In the Elf Royal Palace, a gaze that was as cold and proud as a goddess shot across the mirror-like lake surface and saw the scene.","“...”","The gaze froze.","Is this really our little elf?!","Luther exchanged a look with the knight captain beside him.","Half a minute later, Sala came out from the cultivation mystical realm and said, “Mr. Luther, if we learn the things shown in this mystical realm, we can’t even block one assassin.”","“Pu-!","Luther spewed tea over the knight captain’s face.","..."]},{"number":630,"title":"Chapter 630 - Assassin’s Creed Is Spreading in the Elf Clan","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","At this moment, the whole square in White Creek City fell silent.","All the elves watched the scene in stupefaction.","“There’s not enough time for you to move in stealth?”","“Stealth is useless because you’ll be discovered sooner or later.”","The people savored the words while feeling stunned.","St. Heinz and St. Dulan stared at each other in a daze.","What the heck?!","Elder Sewell snapped back to her senses and murmured, “What she said seems to be sensible.”","“Yeah... Very sensible...” The elves on the square nodded.","Besides, how can she play an assassin character with such magnificence?! Don’t people say that human assassins are a bunch of despicable sneak-attackers? It doesn’t seem true at all!","How come this elf had only learned a few basic skills and can look so dashing?!","The group of people had tears on their faces while they watched.","Meanwhile, Luther’s expression turned unreadable.","Where did she come up with this?! She just hacked her way from the outside to the center and killed them all?","Then, you tell me that it was an assassination!?","“No! It’s not an assassination!” Luther said loudly, “Our... our mystical realm teaches skills against assassins!”","“Why isn’t it an assassination?” Sala said with a snort, “Mr. Luther, tell me who else in the mystical realm saw me killing these people.”","“...” Luther’s face darkened, and he felt a little dizzy.","It seems like I can’t come up with a rebuttal! No one alive had seen her kill those people, which means that it was indeed an assassination!","“The mystical realm that Mr. Luther brought indeed showed us the great craftsmanship that the Dulan Workshop has regarding alchemy.” With a smile, Elder Sewell changed the subject and said, “But I think this mystical realm has big defects as we all have seen.”","“Our elf clan has never imported cultivation mystical realms before,” Elder Sewell continued, “So we must consider this issue carefully. I’ll gather the opinions of the citizens in White Creek City and talk about it with other elders. I’m sure that we’ll come up with a decision very soon.”","“I think we’ll be fair, but we only accept truly excellent products. I don’t hold high hopes for the mystical realm that Mr. Luther brought; it has major defects.”","With the last sentence, she was obviously asking Luther to back off.","In the past, the Elf Clan had formed friendships with other races but had been hurt many times, which was why they were cautious with each visitor. However, they would treat each friendly visitor with equal friendliness.","Their caution came from the lessons that they had learned in the past. After all, not every race loved peace as much as they did.","“...” Although he had anticipated this outcome, Luther’s face still darkened. He couldn’t understand what had gone wrong.","At this moment, St. Heinz had turned off the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection.","He never expected that the simple mission of opening the gate of the Elf Clan would fail so miserably.","With the first step being blocked, he couldn’t launch any of his perfect subsequent plans!","He clenched his fists, which seemed to emit golden lights of fury. Like a blazing golden fire, the whole palace seemed to shake under his anger.","“My Lord, what should we do now?” The white-haired old man, St. Dulan, asked in a deep voice.","St. Heinz paused for a moment. His god-like and holy-pure face looked thoughtful. “Now that this move failed, we must find out the reason behind this unexpected failure.”","“Ask Luther to move his butt back here and investigate.” He continued after a pause, “Besides... I’ll meditate in seclusion for a while. If I’m lucky, I might receive instructions from that ultimate supreme existence as for the next steps that we should take.”","“I hope you’ll obtain holy inspirations,” St. Dulan said with a bow.","...","“I think we’ll leave now!” Luther’s fat face looked so chilly that it seemed like ice could be scraped off of it.","“Won’t you stay for a few days?”","“No, thank you.” Luther left in a huff.","Seeing the overbearing godly palace knights leaving in dejection, Sala jumped and cheered.","At this moment, Elder Sewell heaved a sigh of relief. In fact, when more and more elves began to gather on the square, she had found that the situation had gotten out of her control.","However, she still had confidence in their own crafts before the test, but the subsequent try-outs shattered her confidence and hope.","If Luther succeeded with his scheme, the Elf Clan’s mystical realm industry would receive a huge blow.","However, if she chose to kick them out by force at that stage... She couldn’t go back on her words; it was something that didn’t fit their personalities and culture.","She had a vague feeling that the Judgment Godly Palace had a hidden agenda behind this trip, but now she was relieved that the issue was solved to her advantage even though she still didn’t know what it was.","The sensitive elves also seemed to feel that a wave of gloomy mist had evaporated. The grim atmosphere on the square was now replaced by the usual tranquil peacefulness.","Beautiful harp music sounded on the square.","“We’re fine now, guys!”","“How did she do that?!”","“What’s up? Elder Sewell.” With her hands clasped behind her back, Sala looked at the beautiful woman before her curiously while the latter observed her up and down in bafflement.","“How come you seem quite different after your trip?” Elder Sewell looked Sala up and down as if she was trying to confirm that this girl was indeed the one who had grown up under her eyes.","“Uh? Maybe I grew taller?” Sala smirked.","“No!”","“Um...”","“The two masters you mentioned, Master Altair and Master Ezio...” Elder Sewell said, “Do humans really have such powerful master assassins?”","Elder Sewell looked surprised.","Besides her, some other elves were also curious about these assassins.","“Also...” Elder Sewell asked again, “How did you push away the Wind Roar Hack?”","Remembering how the knights stood there dumbly, basically waiting to be killed, she felt incredulous and couldn’t believe her eyes.","“It’s the counterattack; you have to use the right force at the right place and the right time.”","“You learned it from those two masters as well?”","We’re masters too, but how come we don’t know this fancy skill?","Obviously, although they were all called masters, they had different levels in different worlds.","“Can you tell us about them...”","“It’s a long story about faith in freedom...” Sala said smugly, “Elder Sewell, do you want to hear the story?”","“Um...” Elder Sewell froze for a moment. I told stories to this girl when she was little. How come something seems a bit strange?","Soon, Sala began to tell the story of Assassin’s Creed starting from Altair."]},{"number":631,"title":"Chapter 631 - The Imminent Arrival of the Elf Clan and...the Tragedy for Assassins","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Animus? And what? Pieces of Eden?” Having never played the game, Elder Sewell was baffled as soon as she started listening. “You mean... you entered another mystical realm inside a strange mystical realm?”","“Yes. This series of mystical realms is very interesting; I’ve moved to the second mystical realm already, and I can drive tanks and fire machine guns... um... things like the dwarf’s magic guns,” Sala told them as if she were listing her treasures.","“This mystical realm... has so many things?” As an elf elder who had done deep study on cultivation mystical realms, Elder Sewell knew that the more complicated the mystical realms were, the more difficult it was to make them look real. If someone wanted to achieve both, they must have extraordinary skills in this area.","Obviously, although the Elf Clan had great skills in this area, from what she heard about Assassin’s Creed from Sala, this mystical realm seemed even better than the products of the Dulan Workshop.","“Of course.” Seeing Elder Sewell’s astonishment, Sala was secretly pleased. “Besides these things, the mystical realm also has a thing called Eagle Vision which is super useful. Oh, and there is also the leap of faith.”","After Sala’s lengthy description, Elder Swell finally had a general idea about this mystical realm. “You mean Master Altair used the Eagle Vision to see through the illusions created by his mentor with a Piece of Eden, and he defeated his mentor and sealed that Piece of Eden which contained extremely great power. This means that he couldn’t use this power himself?”","“Right. In Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood, I understood that this master didn’t indulge in the power of being the leader of the Brotherhood. Instead, he went to other countries and helped the brotherhoods in those countries free themselves and spread the meaning of the creed.” Sala brought her hands together before her chest and said in excitement and admiration, “He’s truly an admirable man.”","“He’s indeed admirable.” Elder Sewell nodded and asked in amazement, “What happened after that?”","“The sequels haven’t been released yet!” Sala said in anger, “I could only hear somethings from the era that Master Ezio was in. I wish the shop owner would have released the other mystical realms as early as possible.”","Then, she turned sulky. “But it doesn’t matter anyway since I have no time to visit Canglan City.”","She looked sullen.","Looking at Sala’s sulky face, Elder Sewell chuckled and said, “You just want me to give you more time to play in that human city, right?”","“Well-!” Sala’s pretty face blushed when her little scheme was seen through.","From Sala’s descriptions, Elder Sewell realized that this weird mystical realm seemed to have no loopholes.","After all, even the Dulan Workshop and the biggest alchemist workshops on the continent had to admit to the public that their cultivation mystical realms couldn’t avoid loopholes. Neither could the mystical realms made by the Elf Clan.","“The humans on the continent have achieved such a high level with their alchemy craftsmanship?” Elder Sewell was surprised. She had thought that the mystical realms made by the Dulan Workshop were a product of the next era, but it seemed that this Assassin’s Creed was even better?","Just the Dulan Workshop had given her such a headache, let alone this Assassin’s Creed. If these new cultivation mystical realms all swarmed into the Elf Clan one day, she was afraid that they wouldn’t be able to resist them.","Elder Sewell smiled bitterly and said, “It seems it’s time to take the kids out and experience the world. Otherwise, we’ll be left behind.”","“Ahh!” Hearing Sewell’s words, Sala exclaimed, “Awesome! We can play the multi-player mode then!”","“Um? Multi-player mode?” What’s this thing?","Then, Sala explained to Sewell how to play this multi-player mode.","“It’s simple. We can do multi-player missions, which means that we can do assassinations together in a team...”","“Oh...”","“Oh...”","Soon, Elder Sewell got dizzy with all kinds of new words.","...","Meanwhile, Fang Qi was reading the information on the System Interface.","He found that his privileges had been upgraded again.","Now, his privilege level was level 8.","[Privilege Level 8: you have the right to decide when to release movies and games, the right to livestream on the big screen, the right to decorate the inside of the shops...]","After reading through the privileges that he had gained before, Fang Qi saw a new one: [Level 1 right to unlock new items.]","Level 1 right to unlock items in the System Store.","Other than the items that Fang Qi had unlocked, he could only unlock two items with the new privilege right now. One was cappuccinos and the other was lattes.","The items would consume one million and 1.2 million crystals respectively to activation. After activation, each cup would consume a few crystals to make. The prices were 20 crystals and 24 crystals per cup respectively.","Of course, Fang Qi could also reunlock Sprite, which the shop once sold with the same selling price.","In the old shops, the System had accumulated about 50 million crystals, and it was the number after spending money on the expansion of the new shop and the production of new games and movies.","With more customers visiting the new shop, the number of magic crystals that the shop had earned grew to the equivalent of over one million crystals. Fang Qi had noticed that the currency exchange rate between magic crystals and crystals was 1:8 for him.","In fact, the value between the two was about 1:10. On this continent, there were minerals similar to crystals which had more impurities than ordinary magic crystals, and people had to spend some of its value on the refinery process to remove these impurities. In contrast, the System didn’t have to worry about this issue.","He could now unlock some items in the System Store. At the current level 1, Fang Qi could only unlock things for his own use if he didn’t want to invest large sums of money.","At level 1, he could unlock only a few things, including the Owner-brand cigarettes that he had smoked before.","However, Mr. Fang didn’t have much money on him right now.","Mr. Fang had used his own money to expand the size of the E-sports competition. Since he himself had been an active professional player before he traveled through space and time, he didn’t mind spending money on this.","After he came to this continent, he had bought a shop in the center of the city, which left him with little savings left. Therefore, Mr. Fang decided not to buy the items in the System Store for the time being.","However, he thought that he could unlock one of the new items for the shop.","After all, it would use the System’s funds.","Of course, he couldn’t use too much of the funds that the System had since the money was required to be transferred into energy to activate the defensive mechanisms inside the shops.","So, he decided to release one item.","“I’ll release... Cappuccino first...” Mr. Fang murmured to himself.","...","By now, Luther had returned from the territory of the Elf Clan.","Sitting in the godly palace, his face was chilly. “What happened?! How did a handful of elves achieve that?!”","“Sir, please calm down!” a knight captain said.","“Who’s that Altair?! Where did this assassin come from?! How come I’ve never heard of him before?” Luther knocked down the tea cup on the table and shouted, “Go and find it out!”","“Yes!”","“By the way.” Luther stopped the knight captain and said, “Bring the assassins who we captured last time from the cells. I’ll interrogate them with torture! I believe that they will confess everything they know!”"]},{"number":632,"title":"Chapter 632 - Elves Moving out in a Group","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“St. Dulan, this is the information about the usage of the new cultivation mystical realm in different areas.” A priest bowed and handed a document to Dulan.","If it were before, Dulan wouldn’t have read such documents since he was confident of the forefront position of the Dulan Workshop’s cultivation mystical realms.","But things had changed after he witnessed the failure of his new mystical realm in the Elf Clan.","Reading the numbers on the document, he heaved a sigh of relief when he found that it seemed like this failure had no impact on the mystical realm of the Dulan Workshop.","Obviously, word couldn’t travel so fast since people had to spread them to one another.","Dulan’s face was still dark. He had participated in St. Heinz’ plans which had consumed them lots of time and energy. It was only natural for him to feel furious that their carefully made plans were disrupted by two unknown assassins.","Perhaps he had to make changes and create new plans. Meanwhile, he issued the order, “Find out who botched everything!”","“Yes!”","“Wait!” When the priest bowed and was about to leave, Dulan said, “I’ve never heard of the two assassins before, but that elf girl didn’t look like she was lying. The names might be fake names or nicknames for two assassins in the Underground Council.”","He waved his hand and said, “Go and find out the background of this Altair! Interrogate those assassins in the cells and see if you can find some clues!”","...","It was another sunny morning.","Joseph, Ron, and their peers had just finished their training. Walking on the wide street in the city center, they suddenly exclaimed, “How come the elves are here again?!”","A large group of elves, at least dozens of them, came to Canglan City.","“My goodness! So many elves!” A passing mercenary gasped and was dumbfounded.","“On my ancestors! I’ve never seen so many elves before!” A passing mage gaped at them.","“Okay! Okay! Little Sala. It’s just a shop that is operating a few cultivation mystical realms. Is it really as awesome as you say?” Elder Sewell looked doubtful as the little elf babbled all the way into the city.","She admitted that the shop had good stories and good mystical realms, but she felt like Sala was piling too many compliments on it. Sala boasted about spicy sticks being more delicious than the Mystic Taste Fruit, iced red tea being better than the spring water brewed with the Leaves of Life, instant noodles being tastier than fruits from the Earthly Tree, and Coke which could instantly lift one’s mood!","After all, it is only a shop for mystical realms! It isn’t a snack shop! Furthermore, even if it is a snack shop, its snacks can never compare with the green, natural delicacies in the Elf Clan. She is making it sound like these snacks are more tempting to elves than the Spring of Life!","Elder Sewell didn’t believe Sala and ignored all the non-important stuff. She was just here to see how far the cultivation mystical realms had progressed in the human world instead of eating snacks.","The several elves in the Elder Guard Team who came along also looked disdainful. One of them was an elf guard wearing elegant and exquisite light armor, and his long brown hair was tied behind his head, making him look elegant. He said, “Humans only pay attention to the taste instead of its value when cooking. In fact, I don’t think their food is tasty at all.”","“I once tried a delicacy cooked by a human master chef. I truly doubt that the salty and spicy food is edible.”","The elf said with a faint smile on his face.","“Hahahaha...” Beside him, an elf took out a piece of green fruit and said, “Fortunately, I came prepared.”","He bit into it with enjoyment while a refreshing fragrance floated off from the crisp and juicy fruit.","Laughter sounded among the elves.","...","At this moment, Mr. Fang lazily stretched in the morning sunshine and finally opened the door.","Elina and the other assassins entered the shop at this moment. Helen, Commander Elven, and other members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion had the habit of having breakfast in the shop before going to their training.","“Hi! Good morning, Sir!” A girl wearing a black mage robe greeted him and entered the shop.","“Good morning...” Mr. Fang froze for a second. It seemed like he didn’t know every customer and was only familiar with a few of them.","It reminded him that the few elves who had visited the shop every day in the past while had been missing in the last couple of days.","With this thought on his mind, Mr. Fang was about to return to his seat. Then, he rubbed his eyes, afraid that his eyes were playing tricks on him.","“Sir!” The elves who hadn’t visited this shop for a few days came back with a large group of elves.","It was a grand scene to see as a big group filed into the shop.","“So many?! How did you lure them here?!”","“Humph!” Sala said smugly, “I brought my elders here. I’m good, uh?”","Mr. Fang had never seen so many elves in his life! This was a big team of elves!","Despite the turbulence and thoughts inside, Mr. Fang managed to remain calm and nod coolly.","This shop owner can remain calm and cool... Elder Sewell nodded to herself and thought, He indeed looks like a master.","Could it be that he is the master who created Assassin’s Creed?","Meanwhile, several people stood at the counter and asked, “Sir, what’s this Cappuccino thing?”","In the old shops, some people stood around the counters as well.","None of them had heard of such a weird name before. The names of the products in the shop were getting stranger and stranger.","“Ugh? The shop owner released something new?” Elf Girl Sala immediately looked over.","“It seems to be food,” Helen answered, startled to see Sala coming back. When she turned around, she froze and thought, How come there are so many elves in the shop?!","Are the elves all moving around in large groups now?!","“Food?” Sala’s eyes lit up as she asked, “The shop now has a new delicacy?”","“Yes,” Helen said, “I’m going to try it and see if it’s as good as instant noodles.”","“If it’s as good as spicy sticks, I’m sure that I’ll come and buy it everyday.” Elina got in the line.","“Do you guys want to try it?” A few elves got in line as well and asked the other elves.","“Forget it. I’d rather die than try these human delicacies.” The elf who had criticized human food said, “When I traveled on the continent, I used to buy fruits on the roadside instead of buying such food that isn’t edible.”","“I have some fruits of the Earthly Tree!” One elf took out his fruits and bit into one with enjoyment. “Mr. Ginz, do you want one?”","Then, he handed one to the elf in the Elder Guard Team who said that he would rather die than eat human food."]},{"number":633,"title":"Chapter 633 - Do You Know Who Altair Is?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","While the elves talked among themselves, Commander Elven, who stood first in line, paid and took out an exquisite coffee mug from the cabinet next to the counter.","The rich milk fragrance mingled with coffee aroma permeated the air.","“Sniff!” In the new shop in Canglan City, the elves sitting on the sofa sniffed forcefully.","“What’s it?”","“Ugh? How come it smells so good?!” The elves sitting on the couches with disdain on their faces looked over.","The elf who brought fruits with him also looked over in puzzlement, pausing in his act of biting into his fruit.","Soon, they saw Sala and other elves walking over, each holding a mug of Cappuccino.","The members of Golden Griffin Knight Legion each had one mug of Cappuccino as well.","The rich aroma of milk and coffee filled the whole shop.","The elf eating fruit inhaled deeply twice.","The elf named Ginz in the Elder Guard Team was at a loss for words.","Lance, the captain of Snow Pigeon Team, also sat down with a mug of Cappuccino and casually sipped with enjoyment.","The soft milky flavor melted on their tongues, and the bitter taste of coffee turned into the rich and lingering aftertaste. “Ahh...”","They almost screamed at the great taste!","How come it tastes so good?","“??!!” Seeing their intoxicated expressions, the other elves who hadn’t drank it yet swallowed their saliva silently. “Um... Hahahaha! This smells so good! Should we try it too?”","“What’s this?! Cheese?! How come there’s a floral pattern on it?” Elder Sewell’s beautiful big eyes stared at Sala’s coffee and saw the image of a small black cat on the top.","Isn’t it a beverage?! How come it looks so cute?","Immediately, they each bought one mug and began sipping with great enjoyment. “Ah! It smells so good!”","...","While the elves, knights, and assassins enjoyed their beautiful morning, some people were not so lucky.","At this moment, Luther sat in the underground prison in Grey Eagle City with a ferocious expression on his face.","His face was distorted in a fury.","These damn assassins! If not for these people, I wouldn’t have been moved to this place! As an ambassador of the Radiant Light Godly Nation, I was actually sent to this desolate place to do the investigation, which will indefinitely postpone my own work!","He couldn’t bear it.","Before him was the assassins who they had captured earlier.","Covered in wounds, some of them seemed to have passed out.","“Mr. Luther!” A knight hurried in. “I’ve got some clues!”","“Ugh?” Luther’s small eyes rolled and turned to him as he asked, “What clues?”","The knight quickly whispered something to him.","“We found that Altair seems to be these assassins’ pioneer. They follow the creed of ‘nothing is true, everything is permitted’”","Soon, the knight told him every detail that had been found out. “My men overheard these from the conversations among the assassins; I think most of the information is true.”","Luther nodded and then gestured to one guard. “Wake him up.”","Nodding, the guard woke the prisoner up with a bucket of cold water.","The assassin opened his eyes slowly and saw a fat guy leaning over to him and asking, “Who is Altair?”","“Um... I don’t know.” He shook his head repeatedly.","“Ahh-!” He screamed when the whip lashed on him.","“I ask again; who is Altair?” Luther’s voice was colder.","“Ah! I don’t know who Altair is!” The assassin screamed when another lash landed on him viciously.","“You don’t know?! I will tell you the consequences of you not knowing?!”","More screams rose. A long while later, Luther asked again coldly, “Do you know Altair?”","“I... do.”","“Who is he?” Pleased, Luther leaned over him immediately and asked.","“Um...” The assassin was stupefied. “I really don’t know about this!”","“Whip him! You don’t know the great mentor and pioneer of you assassins? Are you an assassin or not? Are you kidding me?! Whip him harder!”","“Ahh-!” More shrill screams came from the cell.","– Three minutes later –","“Do you know who Altair is?” Luther looked even colder.","“I...do!”","“Who is he?!”","“He’s the great mentor and pioneer of our assassins!” The assassin yelled.","“Humph! It seems like you know him!” Luther sneered. “You dare to play tricks on me and play dumb? Now I ask you – do you know who Ezio is?”","“I don’t know...” The assassin looked baffled.","“Ah-!” He screamed when another lash landed on him.","“You are telling me that you don’t know the master assassin, the great Eagle of Florence?!” Luther roared in fury, “Whip him!”","– Three minutes later –","“Do you know who Ezio is?”","“I... I do!” The assassin howled immediately.","“Tell me!”","“He’s our master assassin and the great Eagle of Florence!” the assassin howled immediately as if he was scared of being slow.","“Then, tell me about their plans!”","“This... I really don’t know... Ahh–!”","“Hit him! Beat him hard!”","– Ten minutes later –","“Ahh-! I’ll tell you everything!","“Altair is our great assassin mentor and the pioneer of assassins! He changed the code of conduct for assassins in every respect and understood the real assassin’s creed...”","“Ezio is the great Eagle of Florence and a master assassin! It was him who reassembled the Brotherhood and understood the true meaning of ‘nothing is true, everything is permitted’...”","He was fluent with his answer without being asked.","Greatly satisfied, Luther nodded and said with a cold smile, “See? You know everything... Now, tell me...”","“I...”","“!!??” These are the things that you told me; what else can I tell you?!","The assassin’s face turned ashen, and he passed out.","“Mr. Luther, he passed out...”","“If I continue beating him, would he...” The knight was afraid that they couldn’t get anything useful if they beat the prisoner to death.","“I’ll interrogate that one!” Luther pointed at another assassin.","After waking him up with cold water, Luther glared at him with a distorted expression as he asked, “Do you know who Altair is?!”","“I...”","“???”"]},{"number":634,"title":"Chapter 634 - The Shadow from Ancient Times","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“When you stare at the abyss, the abyss is staring right back at you.”","On this continent, the relationship between the humans and other races wasn’t so tense that they waged war against each other all year round. However, this world wasn’t as peaceful as it looked either.","Through the mirror-like lake in the center of the eternal-looking Elf Royal Palace, one could see the entire beautiful Silver Moon Forest.","It was inlaid in the land like a piece of beautiful jade inlaid in a beautiful dress.","However, a few impurities lurked in this jade, and unknown gloomy auras flowed in several areas.","It embodied a huge catastrophe.","Even if the remnant presence had been dispelled little by little, it stuck around on the land stubbornly. It would be a long time before it was completely erased.","In the Royal Palace, several elf elders gathered.","Some of them appeared to be of the same age as Elder Sewell, and some of them looked ancient.","Among them was an extremely old man. With his long white beard touching the ground and his back bent, he still looked hale and high spirited while wearing a spotless snow-white robe.","At this moment, he stood before the Silver Moon Lake and stared at the reflection of the beautiful forest in the lake.","At this moment, he asked, “The Snow Pigeon Team has searched several cities in the Morning Light Empire and didn’t find a single clue... I wonder...”","“Maybe we are too paranoid.” Another elf elder shook his head, looking uncertain.","“I hope so.” The oldest elf looked grim at this moment.","...","Meanwhile in the godly palace, Luther had interrogated all of the captured assassins.","Although he couldn’t find more information about Altair and Ezio, he got some clues about those assassins who had gotten away.","“Perhaps they haven’t left the Morning Light Empire yet,” Luther said in a cold voice, “Find them for me!","“These damn assassins! I’ll let them have a taste of my power!” He roared with a chilly expression, “I’ll let these bugs know that they can’t afford to mess with us!”","...","In the human nations, one rarely saw elves, but it wasn’t unusual to see other races in some cities.","Black Iron Castle was such a place. It was a city to the north of Canglan City and was called the Capital of Craftsmen.","It was a human city mostly inhabited by craftsmen and alchemists, but one could also see dwarf workshops here.","Due to the mix of inhabitants, this city was one of the few gathering places for assassins in the nation.","Other unknown things were also lurking in this place.","Yes, unknown things.","After all, even the huge organizations such as the Judgement Godly Palace didn’t dare to claim that they knew everything about the world, let alone others.","Under the gloomy sky stood the tallest steeple in the Black Iron Castle. It was said that this building had sealed an ancient and horrifying monster before the Morning Light Empire was established.","It was a monster from ancient times, and it was heard that it had brought blazing hell to every place it had gone to and burned down most of the places on the continent. It was a horrid disaster.","Of course, many people had just regarded this as a legend or even a rumor since they had heard many other similar tales from bards.","After all, bards loved to gather and tell such tales that were unrealistic.","Since no one had ever seen the things told in the tales, the people here had never blindly believed these stories.","A huge shadow engulfed the castle silently like a dark curtain falling from the sky.","A dark voice roared in an unknown space, “I’ve slumbered for thousands of years... Soon... Very soon, I’ll recover my strength. Then, I’ll turn this nation into hell! I’ll eat all the humans in this place! I’ll show these damn humans the price that they have to pay for angering me!”","...","On the other side of the nation, Mr. Fang was leisurely standing in the corridor of the internet café with a mug of Cappuccino in his hand, watching the elves play games.","“Wow...” Mr. Fang sipped the coffee and sighed, enjoying the rich and fragrant milk and coffee spreading on his tongue.","At this moment, the elves had formed a team to play Assassin’s Creed.","“We finally come to this place...”","Before them was the grand Pantheon.","Crowds thronged on the square outside this temple.","“Hey! I saw this scene in the cinematic trailer!” Sala yelled in excitement.","“Right! Right! Right! This is the one... an assassin walked out of the crowd while soldiers and others back away from him!” another elf exclaimed, “It’s so cool!”","“Who? Who is he?” Captain Lance’s face twitched.","“I don’t know; I only know that he’s the one wearing a red robe...”","At this moment, Elder Sewell was playing as Ezio while the others played as unknown assassins in the Brotherhood.","“Come on, Elder, we’ll bring you to do a perfect assassination! I promise you that it will be super cool!” An elf in the Snow Pigeon Team offered.","“How do we assassinate?” As a new player, Elder Sewell was still confused.","“Elder, you walk down other there!” The elf directed. “We’ll get up and set an ambush. Come on! Come on! Come on!”","Captain Lance said, “Here is how it goes. You walk out alone, and the people will back away in fear since they are afraid of you.”","“He’s the Eagle of Florence after all.” Sala obviously understood it. “Just as demonstrated in the trailer, the people will get scared and call for elite soldiers.”","“Then, you give us a signal, and we will shoot arrows from the roof, killing all of them!” The elf captain added. Obviously, he had watched and studied the trailer many times.","“Oh...” Elder Sewell looked at the big group of elite templar knights and the royal guards armed to their teeth around the core position. “I’ll just walk up... they will back away in fear... because I’m Ezio, the Eagle of Florence...”","“That’s it!” Sala said with a nod, “Then, we’ll swarm up after you send us the signal! We’ll land from the sky!”","Having spent lots of time in the internet café, she had obviously picked up some slang."]},{"number":635,"title":"Chapter 635 - The End of Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Mr. Fang just stood behind the elves and watched them play. Obviously, these people had completed the script of the show.","“Now, get ready.”","“Do you see that place?” Sala pointed up. “That spot is good; we’ll go up there later.”","Controlling a female assassin, Sala got up to the roof and advanced to the direction of the Pantheon.","Other elves followed her closely.","“Are you guys ready?” Elder Sewell asked.","“In a minute. Elder, you can go out now. We’ll find good shooting positions.” The elves killed some templar knights on the roof facing away from the street; these people were blocking their way. Professionally, they sneaked into the best positions they could find.","“I’ll walk out now!” Elder Sewell yelled.","“Okay! Okay!”","They worked together in a seamless and harmonious way.","When the pope’s carriage team came, Elder Sewell controlled Ezio to stride out from the hiding place.","Just as in the trailer, the crowds backed away from him.","At this moment, the other elves had come to an empty residential house to dodge people’s eyes.","“Hey! This door is locked!”","“How do I open it...”","“It seems that we need assassin’s special lock picking tool...”","“Let me try it. We’ll open this door and set the ambush on the balcony...”","A lock picking tool was stuck into the keyhole.","– Ten seconds later –","“Are you in position?” Elder Sewell strode on while a large group of templar knights surrounded her.","“Ugh... Almost!” Captain Lance had cold sweat on his face. “Let me do it.”","“Are you there or not?!” On the square, a big group of templar knights ran after Ezio and hacked at him.","“Almost there! Almost!” Sala said, “Get off! Let me do it; I know how to open it!”","Captain Lance moved away, and Sala tried her hand at the lock.","Snap!","“Um... it’s stuck.” Sala looked embarrassed.","“Forget it.” Captain Lance walked up. “Let me do it.”","Bang! Bang! Bang!","Boom! Boom! Boom!","They hacked at the door.","“Assassins! There are assassins here!”","“My goodness! Run! Run!” As if they poked a hornets’ nest, the elves ran wildly while a group of people chased after them.","“Can’t outrun them! Fight! Fight! Fight!”","“Are you in position or not!?” On the square, Elder Sewell ran while being chased by as many as 100 royal guards.","“??? Where are you guys?! Talk to me!”","The other elves were busy hacking and slashing.","“Auch!” Elder Sewell screamed.","“...” On the other side, the elves panted. “We finally got rid of them.”","“Can we continue sneaking up?”","“Let’s go! No one discovered us...”","“How come it feels different from the scene in the trailer...”","“Let’s go and protect Elder Sewell...”","“Ugh? Where’s Elder Sewell?”","Mr. Fang was watching Elder Sewell putting down her virtual reality headset and standing up in confusion.","On her screen, Ezio had been hacked to death on the square.","“...” Mr. Fang almost fell to the ground while laughing.","...","With a mug of Cappuccino in his hand, Mr. Fang rubbed his belly which was still hurting due to his uncontrollable laughter. Then, he watched while the elves began another round of assassination.","Meanwhile, the assassins born on this continent had gained great improvements in all kinds of skills.","At this moment, the excellent assassins such as Elina and Harrison had come to the end of the game.","“How did they make this Apple of Eden?” A few people exclaimed. On the screen was the battle freeing Rome. Ezio activated the golden apple, and everything around him seemed to move in slow motion. The sphere emitting golden light suddenly shot out golden lightning energy, knocking down all the soldiers who were charging at him from all sides.","At this last moment, the game was less difficult to play.","As a godly artifact left by the First Civilization, the powerful Apple of Eden had the ability to foresee the future.","Surrounded by the Assassin Brotherhood and its allies, Cesare was soon defeated and captured.","Cesare had once gotten the golden apple and seemed to know that he wouldn’t be chained or die in others’ hands.","Sure enough, Cesare escaped on the same day that he was captured. With the power from the Apple of Eden, Ezio found him and tossed him down a cliff, leaving his fate to the Heavens.","Obviously, the Heavens decided to let the cruel tyrant die. Ezio’s foe finally ended his life in this place.","After that, this master assassin decided to retire. In this place, he did the most glorious and the greatest things in his life and brought freedom to the people.","Without a backward glance, Ezio followed the path of his ancestor Altair to find the truth hidden in the Apple of Eden, and the Apple of Eden was sealed inside a secret chamber near the Roman Amphitheater.","When Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood came to the end, Elina felt emotional.","As real assassins who had been looked down on simply because of their identity, people like Elina had different feelings about the game.","Just a moment ago, she had experienced the most glorious moment in this master assassin’s life in another world.","What she had obtained wasn’t great power but a spiritual inheritance.","Her deep understanding of ‘nothing is true, everything is permitted’ and the powerful spirit shown in the game dispelled the darkness from her heart like a blazing torch.","These assassins had been living in permanent darkness and couldn’t reveal their true names and looks to people.","Indeed, they were dark and despicable, and they could only sneak-attack from darkness.","Their lowly status in the world in turn darkened their mind and chilled their hearts. Although there were exaggerated parts in the negative rumors about assassins, not all of them were made up stories.","Since they had no faith or code of conduct to bind them, they were outlawed.","But now, Elina thought of things differently. In the past, she didn’t understand the true meaning of being an assassin, thinking that her job as an assassin was just taking missions and killing targets.","But now, she realized that assassins could represent a spirit and a will; they could live gloriously like the assassin ancestors in the game.","If they understood this and fought for their faith, they were still assassins even if they fought and killed their way to their targets using musou.","She thought that maybe this was what Assassin’s Creed tried to express.","...","It was time to close for the night. Mr. Fang walked to the door and was about to lock up the shop.","Then, he saw a bunch of flowers neatly placed before the door.","“To the great assassin pioneer Master Altair – From an anonymous assassin.”","“To the eternal Eagle of Florence, Master Ezio – From an anonymous assassin.”","“...”"]},{"number":636,"title":"Chapter 636 - The Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","While wishing that the figures in another world could receive the admiration, Mr. Fang carefully picked up the flowers and locked the door. With the lights turned off, the shop merged into the darkness in the city.","...","For the cultivators and warriors in the old shops, they had experienced many legends in the games. However, they were still moved and inspired by Assassin’s Creed.","On the Cloud Ocean Square outside Yuanyang City, cultivators came and went. Some young people including a few people of the Ultimate West Realm were standing on the edge of the square and looking down at the deep creek under the cliff.","“Ahhh...” They leaped down.","Then, they flew back up on sword energies and leaped down again...","“Ahhh...”","“Strange... How come I can’t master this leap of faith...?”","Tang Yu stared at the wall intently while yelling, “Eagle Vision!”","“Eagle Vision! Open!”","His eyes almost broke since he was staring so hard. “What’s wrong?!”","Sia spoke the Spiritual State language with an awkward accent, and she said, “How come I can’t master it?!”","She looked frustrated.","Meanwhile, Loli Jiang Xiaoyue was sitting on a couch in the shop with a mug of Cappuccino in her hands. On the top of the coffee was the pattern of a pretty white rabbit.","She also looked frustrated. On one hand, she was eager to sip the coffee as she was even drooling. But on the other hand, she just couldn’t bear to eat this cute rabbit.","“Auwu!” Beside her, the big white deer had gulped down the coffee and was almost done.","...","For players of Dungeon Fighter Online, today was obviously another hopeful day. A man covered in bandages limped into the shop.","Seeing the janitors doing the cleaning, he yelled, “Morning, homies.”","Damn it! Who are your homies!","The janitors had tears on their faces.","“I say, little guy. You didn’t bring granddaddy to that war. Otherwise, we would have slaughtered them all!” the godly swords began to babble again.","“...” Ignoring them, Gabriel chose a seat and entered the game, continuing his journey in the abyss.","“Items! Give me items!” He instantly killed an Abyss Demon with a powerful skill, and his eyes became bloodshot.","...","Nalan Hongwu used to practice sword techniques in the morning in his own place before coming to the shop. But lately, he had changed the practice venue to the open ground before the shop.","Now, wearing a loose white robe, he stood in front of the shop with a sword in his hand.","Meanwhile, Song Qingfeng was sitting on a couch in the shop. While eating instant noodles, he took out his new communication jade and recommended to Su Tianji sitting across from him, “Sister Su, this anime is good! This Naruto is super cool! I highly recommend it!”","“It is not that good, and you can only unlock one episode per week.” Dong Qingli also took out her new communication jade and said, “Look at Pokémon! These pokémons are super cute!”","“I wonder when the shop will award people with pokémons?” She looked expectant.","...","– In the Half City Shop –","A black cloud held a mug of Cappuccino in its arms. “Wow... so good...”","It lounged on a computer chair with joy and pleasure.","“How can a Smirk Face Emoji know what it tastes like?” Ruan Ning, the girl from next door who had turned into a full-time shop clerk, looked down at it. “Where did you get the money anyway?”","On its screen was a livestream room named, [Almighty Demon God – Professional Technical Streamer.]","It had just won a match.","“Hahaha... um... Thanks to Noob Player White Hand’s 66 goose eggs.”","“Thanks to New Player Really Can’t Play’s 666 goose eggs.”","“Ahahaha! Thanks to Smirk Face Emoji Not Funny’s 6666 goose eggs.”","“Ugh...? This name...” It froze.","Then, after checking its membership card, it was pleased that the money on his account had grown a bit. “Get me another bottle of iced red tea!”","“This works?!” The people watching from behind all froze.","...","At this moment, Mr. Fang was dazedly staring at the System Interface.","[You have a new task.]","Clearly, Mr. Fang had received a new task.","[New Task: Online Communication in This World","Task Content: Host, please promote the harmonious relationship between the old shops and the new shop","Task Privilege: The right to release the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4","Host can achieve the first step by introducing the customers in the new shop to another culture.","Task Reward: One System Gift Bag, and three days of access to the Game Cultivation Room]","Mr. Fang’s face twitched. “...”","As the owner of an internet cafe, he knew which games were good, but he had never heard that an internet café owner had such an responsibility on his job description.","“System, this goes beyond the responsibilities of an internet café owner, right?” Mr. Fang didn’t know what to say.","The System replied, [As an outstanding cross-continental internet club, it must have a smooth working internet and a harmonious online atmosphere.]","“...” Fortunately, he had chosen a remote place with cute peace-loving elves and bright-looking knights who were obviously not in the same category as the people of the Judgment Godly Palace. Otherwise, the task would be quite difficult to complete.","With the current customers in the new shop, Mr. Fang was quite confident that he could complete the task.","While congratulating himself for his great vision, he began to consider how to do the task.","...","– Meanwhile –","“Mr. Luther.” At this moment, Luther had returned to Grey Eagle City after his interrogation of the assassins. The next step was catching the assassins who were running free and finding clues to the two master assassins who had disrupted their big plans.","Although the two failures had nothing to do with his competence, the godly palace still made him stay in Grey Eagle City to investigate, which meant that his status had become much lower compared to before.","“Damn it!” Luther tightened his grip on the wineglass, shattering it instantly with the wine still in it.","“These damn assassins!”","“According to our recent investigation, a place in Canglan City seems to be protecting assassins. We almost got them last time but were stopped by these people. Besides,” the knight said while lowering his voice, “we found that the two so-called master assassins you want to find seem to be related to this shop.”","“Shop? What does this shop do?” Luther asked with chilly eyes.","“It seems to be a shop of cultivation mystic realms...” the knight said, “Those two master assassins are related to these mystic realms, but I still don’t know who they really are.”","“Cultivation mystic realms?” Luther frowned. It would be easy for them to capture an ordinary person, but anyone who could run cultivation mystic realms wasn’t ordinary.","“This shop seems to have a good reputation...” the knight said, “But I think that as a new workshop, its influence isn’t as great as ours. If we stir up people against this shop, maybe... we don’t need to lift a finger...”"]},{"number":637,"title":"Chapter 637 - Mr. Fang’s Hometown?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Across the ocean to the east of the vast continent was an ancient and mysterious continent – East Continent.","According to the legends circulating around the two continents, there was a world rotating around the two continents like the sun, moon, and stars.","Yes. Many legends said that the sun, moon, and stars rotated around the land. Therefore, many people thought that it was the same with these magical worlds.","Despite the lack of evidence to support this theory, most people believed it and took it as is.","“What kind of person do you think the shop owner is...?” On one leisurely morning, the elves sipped Cappuccino and talked among themselves in low voices.","“Ah... the milky fragrance mingling with the pure herb scent. This is a delicious beverage made with pure natural ingredients.” The elves looked intoxicated. “It’s said that it’s a mixture of a bean powder and milk. I thought we knew all the plants in the world.”","“They are called coffee beans,” Sala told them, “I wonder if it’s a plant from the East Continent.”","“I don’t think so... the great assassin pioneer Altair doesn’t look like a person from the East Continent.”","“But we’ve never heard of places such as Rome or Florence on our continent,” one elf said with a shrug.","The humans here regarded the humans living in the East Continent almost in the same way as they regarded the elves and the dwarves who were other races.","Living so far from them, the humans on the East Continent were even more mysterious than the rarely seen elves.","After watching the war waged by the Judgement Godly Palace, they realized that the people from that continent were obviously of the same race as the people in the East Continent.","After the war, they had a clearer impression of these people who were vague in their minds.","They used mysterious and powerful ‘magic spells’ and could fly while stepping on sword-shaped ‘magic artifacts’.","They had excellent combat techniques and powerful ‘magic weapons’.","They had dignified and elegant manners. For example, the white-clothed old man had discussed about the meaning of Sword Dao before the battle.","They proved with action that all the descriptions about them from the churches and rumors were all lies that could be easily shattered.","“Do you think the shop owner has a magic item that can fly as well?”","At this moment, Mr. Fang was having his morning tea all by himself on a couch, not realizing that these people were talking about him.","“Sir.” While sipping her Cappuccino, Sala ambled over and sat down next to Mr. Fang’s lone figure before asking, “Do you have a mystic realm that features... the specialities of your hometown?”","After spending so much time in the shop, they had become quite familiar with the shop owner, even though this unyielding man never gave frequent customers any discounts.","At this moment, Elina said, “You’re from the East Continent; how come there is nothing with the style of the East Continent?”","Obviously, she was curious about this new stuff.","By now, she had played Assassin’s Creed and Assassin’s Creed: Brotherhood twice and was challenging a higher difficulty level.","Elder Sewell said, “Um... we’ve been out for a long time now. It’s time to go back to the Silver Moon Forest.”","“Can’t we stay here a bit longer?” Sala exclaimed in alarm.","“Of course not!” Elder Sewell said solemnly, “I have things to do, and you have missions to finish.”","“Oh... Elder...” Sala looked sulky, feeling like she hadn’t been here long enough yet!","She wished that she could live here.","Despite her badgering, Elder Sewell was unmoved. Discouraged, Sala changed the subject and asked, “Sir, I asked you a question!”","Sitting next to her on the couch, Mr. Fang sipped his Cappuccino and froze. “My hometown?”","“Do you have such mystic realms?” Commander Elven who had been busy sipping tea looked up subconsciously, curious about this distant and mysterious East Continent.","“Are you talking about the next new mystic realm?”","“Ugh? Do you really have one?” Sala asked immediately, “What does it look like?”","“It’s called the Legend of the Sword and Fairy.” With while his face twitched, Mr. Fang wondered how he could describe the game with words. “You’ll know what it looks like after you try it.”","“Great!” After playing two games of Assassin’s Creed series and Resident Evil, Commander Elven obviously had confidence in the quality of the ‘cultivation mystic realms’ in this shop.","People liked the mystic realms in this shop since they had complete stories which were deep and vivid enough to touch their hearts.","“Elder Sewell, can we have a look of the new mystic realm before we return? Please?” Sala quickly begged.","“...” Elder Sewell looked frustrated, and she budged a little. “Only one look, and then we’ll leave.”","“Can we play it for a while...?”","“No!” Not sparing her a glance, Elder Sewell sounded very firm.","...","Meanwhile, the news had spread to the players in the old shops.","Everyone was talking about it in the ‘The Legend of the Sword and Fairy’ group chat in QQ.","Su Tianji asked, [The Legend of Sword and Fairy 4?!]","Nalan Hongwu chimed in, [When will it be released?]","Tang Yu said, [F*ck? The fourth sequel of The Legend of the Sword and Fairy will be released?]","Sia shouted, [Buy! Buy! Buy! I’ll buy it! I swear!]","Gabriel said, [😢I shattered several weapons while reinforcing them... I hope the new game is not too expensive. I’m poor.]","He posted a meme of himself sleeping on a pile of hay with the illustration, [I wish I didn’t reinforce the weapons to level 13. I’m starving for days now...]","Song Qingfeng said, [😏 Who photoshopped this photo? Awesome...”","Luo Piaoling said, [When you want to photoshop a picture, go to Xiaoyue. Do you guys know when the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 will be released? @ Mr. Fang]","...","Meanwhile, many people in the new shop were also badgering Mr. Fang with the same question.","“Still not released?” Sala was a bit disappointed. Remembering the trailer before the release of Assassin’s Creed, she asked immediately, “Does it have a trailer?”","She looked very hopeful.","“This one doesn’t have a trailer. I think it will be released in one week,” Mr. Fang said calmly.","Hearing his words, people were instantly unhappy.","The customers in the old shops were also displeased when they heard the news in the group chat, [Can’t you release it today?!]","[I demand it to be released today!]","“Sir, can’t you tell us something about it? Only a little will do!” Sala was impatient, wondering how she could wait a week for it.","“We’re friends now; can’t you do me a favor?” She tried to play soft with Mr. Fang.","“Not today.” Mr. Fang was unmoved.","Well! This shop owner is stiff with his ways! Why!","They felt like beating Mr. Fang.","At this moment, even though the players in the old shops and the new shop hadn’t met each other, they were now all glaring at Mr. Fang with furious eyes."]},{"number":638,"title":"Chapter 638 - Lava Workshop","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Since the players in the new shop hadn’t had any previous experience with the Legend of the Sword and Fairy, and there was a big culture difference, Fang Qi decided to let their anticipation build up for a while before releasing the game.","“East Continent?” There were many followers of the Judgment Godly Palace in Canglan City, and some of them were even aristocrats of the city.","The Knight Captain named Glass had been resentful of the shop which operated an ‘assassin mystical realm’. “Under its influence, many people faked being assassins, and the damn real assassins took the opportunity to slip from our grasp. Now, it even angered Mr. Luther. I think it’s in big trouble now!”","The Dulan Workshop had large groups of customers in each city. It had an even bigger group of customers in Canglan City, a big city with advanced cultivation mystical realms.","Not only mages and warriors from different places, but half of the aristocrats in the city often visited these cultivation mystical realms.","At this moment, they were gathered together.","One aristocrat said disdainfully, “I heard that someone tried to release a mystical realm about assassins; is this shop still in business?”","“I heard that the owner of the shop is a foreigner; he doesn’t understand the rules in the city and wants to release a mystical realm with the style of the East Continent! What a joke!”","“We’ll greatly promote the mystical realms of the Dulan Workshop.” Obviously, they hadn’t seen the performance of this mystical realm in the Elf Clan. As loyal fans of the Dulan Workshop, they would have found excuses for it even if they had seen the failure.","“It’s just a small workshop; it’s nothing compared with the Dulan Workshop. I wonder why those powerful people of the Dulan Workshop in Canglan City suddenly mentioned this shop.”","“I think it’s because that small shop overestimated itself. Right after the Dulan Workshop released the anti-assassination content, that small shop released the so-called ‘assassin mystical realm’. Pooh!”","Meanwhile, the representative of the Lava Workshop, a world-famous alchemy workshop, entered the godly palace in Canglan City.","The Lava Workshop was an alchemy workshop that used dwarf alchemy crafts. The Dwarf Clan had their own alchemy system, but different from the Elf Clan who kept their mystical realms to themselves, the Dwarf Clan also spread their cultivation mystical realms to different nations.","With the most dependable crafts in the whole world, the Dwarf Clan had established representative offices in each country to run the mystical realms for them. This tall and thin aristocrat dressed in a formal suit was the representative of the Lava Workshop in Canglan City.","He said coldly, “Mr. Glass, you called us here for this small issue? What does an insignificant foreigner know about cultivation mystical realms?”","“East Continent style?” It must be noted that the dwarves had once released a dwarf-style mystical realm that they made with their most advanced techniques, but it ended up in complete failure.","Even the world-famous dwarves had failed with their techniques, let alone a foreigner from nowhere.","He said with a snicker, “This kid will probably go broke one day and return home with heavy debt.”","“Just hear the name... The Legend of the Sword and Fairy?” He sneered and asked, “What kind of name is this? No one would want to visit such a mystical realm.”","“Unfortunately, Mr. Leo,” Glass said solemnly, “This kid got lucky and drew some aristocrats to his shop. With quite a few civilians visiting his shop regularly, he earns enough to keep the business open even though he has much fewer customers than the big workshops.”","“But I think the situation will change soon because of you, me, and everyone else in the room,” Glass said, “I think we must let them know what the good mystical realms look like.”","The two ‘master assassins’ might be related to the shop, but Glass still thought it was a coincidence that their mystical realm failed that day. The main reason was that the knights in the mystical realm were caught off guard by the unusual moves of the elf who had excellent combat techniques and talent.","He thought that it was just a loophole in the mystical realm, and the elves had taken advantage of it. After all, the figures in the fantasy world were not real people, and it was natural to have some small loopholes since it wasn’t yet comparable to the real world.","That was the only explanation. He would never believe that the elves obtained the victory because of that damn mystical realm in that shop. It was even less believable than the high tales made up by the bards.","“Mr. Leo, if I’m right, the Lava Workshop is about to release a new mystical realm.”","The Dulan Workshop released no more than one cultivation mystical realm each year, so Glass held no hopes that it would release another mystical realm after such a short time.","However, other workshops were different.","The Lava Workshop was an alchemy workshop as good as the Dulan Workshop and had a new mystical realm that was going to be released soon, which made it a perfect partner for Glass.","“I wonder what content this new mystical realm of the Lava Workshop has?”","Leo nodded and said proudly, “This new mystical realm doesn’t only focus on cultivation; it also contains the Dwarf Clan’s crafts in alchemy, blacksmithing, and manufacturing. It’s a comprehensive mystical realm combining combat techniques and other skills.”","“Excellent!” Glass exclaimed, “I’m surprised that the dwarves are generous enough to put in the skills that they have such pride in! I think those people will be stunned by this new mystical realm!”","Leo said with a smirk, “I guess my employers got frightened when they heard that the Dulan Workshop planned to build an unprecedented comprehensive mystical realm; it seems that their brains aren’t all made of muscles.”","His words showed no respect for his employers.","“Do you want us to compete with that shop?” Leo said in disdain, “To be frank, if our cultivation mystical realm is released a few days earlier than theirs, I’m sure that no one will visit their cultivation mystical realm.”","Although Origins Internet Club was not a small shop in Canglan City and even had customers from the Elf Clan, its competitors were huge organizations that provided mystical realms to nations all over the world.","“Mr. Leo, you’re the person responsible for all the businesses in Canglan City on behalf of the Lava Workshop. I believe in your abilities,” Glass said with a smile.","“It has nothing to do with my abilities,” Leo said while shaking his head, “I’m just not interested in dealing with these minor beings.”","As if he had anticipated this situation, Glass clapped his hands, and a few knights soon carried out a chest of treasures.","Then, Leo frowned and said with a smirk, “I think we’ll have a nice partnership.”","Meanwhile, Luther was playing with an exquisite wineglass in his hand. Hearing the news, he narrowed his eyes and murmured, “Now, we can eliminate both the assassins and the damn shop which dares to protect the assassins!”"]},{"number":639,"title":"Chapter 639 - Azure Wave Sword Tune and Immortal Dream; The Primeval Qionghua’s Appearance","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","At this moment, Fang Qi’s shop finally released the first trailer.","Sitting at the computers close to the counter, Elina and the other assassins who received no assassination missions lately had come into the shop early. Then, they clicked open the new trailer eagerly.","The godly palace knights were still searching for assassins on the streets all over the city. However, these bold assassins were still playing games and watching trailers in the shop like usual.","At this moment, the members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion had also come into the shop to have their morning tea.","The mercenaries including Big Sword Crete all came up subconsciously when they saw that someone was watching the new trailer.","“How come there are many people standing there?” Elder Sewell came early today. After all, she didn’t have to handle the affairs of the Elf Clan all day long while she was taking the young elves on a field trip.","“Ah! My goodness!” Sala exclaimed, “Is this the trailer for the new mystical realm?!”","“Right.” At this moment, the blue sky and white clouds on the screen condensed into a blue-and-white logo. Seeing many people watching from behind, Elina turned on the speakers.","On her screen, a pretty figure stood under a fiery-red phoenix flower tree. Her black and thick hair was pulled up in a bun behind her head. When the music rose, the figure in the white-and-blue clothes lifted her jade-like hand, and a white butterfly rested on her fingertip.","When the music continued and got louder, Fang Qi recognized it to be the Azure Wave Sword Tune. Under the dreamy fiery red phoenix flower tree, the elegant and pretty figure glanced back, fixing her wind-blown hair with her fingertips. Her jade-like and celestial look was stunning in this backward glance.","“My goodness!”","“So beautiful!”","Even the beauty-loving elves widened their eyes.","“Wow...!” Sala exclaimed.","The camera zoomed out to the distance as if someone was in a dream. While the wave-like clouds floated in the air, celestial mountains emerged. The Kunlun Mountain was the tallest of all mountains in the area, and its peak penetrated the clouds. The tranquil and vast Jade Lake could be seen in the mountain, and a river winded at the foot of the mountain. It was a beautiful scene.","“My goodness! Is it the place where immortals live?!” The audience was stunned.","Even Elder Sewell was stupefied. “This mystical realm... This...!!??”","At this moment, words appeared on the screen, [The magnificent, unparalleled, and celestial Kunlun Mountain is the most beautiful place between heaven and earth. The Qionghua Faction has always excelled in sword creation. Their swords sweep across the mountains and rivers and eliminate demons and devils.]","The screen flashed, showing the scenes of ancient people making the Xihe Sword and the Wangshu Sword, which stunned the heaven and earth and created phenomenons.","In the grand palaces on the celestial mountains, celestial spiritual spells and demonic spells flashed at the same time.","The magnificent Temple of the Sky stood at the peak of the mortal world and looked as if it were hovering in space and standing above the time-space continuum. The Wangshu Sword and Xihe Sword swept up tremendous immortal force on the Cloud Platform, and the Aurogon roared in the sky above Buzhou Mountain, bringing lightning bolts and strong gusts!","[TL Note: Aurogan, also known as Zhulong and Torch Dragon, was a giant red solar dragon and god in Chinese mythology. It supposedly had a human’s face and snake’s body, created day and night by opening and closing its eyes, and created seasonal winds by breathing.]","The music turned even more high-pitched and passionate.","At this moment, everyone seemed to choke with turbulent emotions inside.","They almost roared in their minds.","Isn’t it a cultivation mystical realm?!","How can a cultivation mystical realm be so stunning?!","They were dumbstruck.","“What’s this?!” Seeing the Aurogon Dragon on the screen, Sala froze in fear.","The other elves behind her were also stupefied when they saw the mountain-like head and the huge body hidden in the clouds.","“Don’t be afraid!” A golden griffin knight said with forced calmness, “It’s just a virtual image, not a real thing! It is made for you to watch; there’s nothing to be afraid of!”","“Right! Right!” While calming themselves and telling themselves not to be afraid, the elves continued to watch without blinking.","At this moment, the passionate music slowed down while an ethereal music floated over from the misty white clouds until everything turned quiet. It felt like the previous scenes were not real and just a dream.","With the melodious and haunting flute music, it felt like a permanent-looking ink painting was spread out quietly.","At this moment, the elves and mercenaries didn’t know if they were stunned or shocked. The elegant and beautiful music of Immortal Dreams rose while a green verdant forest appeared before them, bringing them back to that small wooden cottage in the mountains. The green stone steps winded up the mountainside while the waterfall crashed down with booming sounds, shooting pure waterdrops in all directions. The erhu music floated up with faint sadness while the gurgling creek flowed into the distance and got covered by white clouds. Then, the screen dimmed.","For some reason, an indescribable emotion rose in their minds. They hadn’t played this game yet but could feel that it contained a magnificent yet sad and touching story.","Through the short scenes and music, they seemed to have experienced the most miraculous and magnificent adventure in their lives, and it would linger in their mind forever.","They probably realized at this moment that the Legend of the Sword and Fairy was totally different from Assassin’s Creed. The former expressed a faith and a belief to them, and the latter seemed like a grand but melodious and gentle poem.","This is how the new mystical realm looks like?!","The grand and vast mountains, rivers, and land, the glimpse at the huge beast hidden in the clouds, and the poetic scenery as if it were an ink painting.","“What a miraculous world!”","“Unbelievable!”","The scenes in the trailer filled their minds.","“It’s even grander than I imagined...” Sala exclaimed.","“It’s as magnificent as the great legends told in the books...”","“This is the next mystical realm?!” Commander Elven yelled, “I think I need to calm down.”","Then, he took several deep breaths.","“I saw some people making two swords of different colors,” Elf Captain Lance asked, “Are they making magic items? Is this mystical realm a comprehensive mystical realm containing forging and alchemy crafts?”","“Um... something like that. It’s called artifact-making.” Fang Qi remembered that the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 had a complete forging system when he played it before he traveled through space and time.","After all, the Qionghua Faction was a big faction famous for its abilities in creating swords.","...","At this moment, exclamations also filled the old shops.","“My goodness! Is this the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4?”","“How come it doesn’t look like Shu Mountain Faction?”","“...” Nalan Mingxue seemed to notice something and swiftly said in the chat group, [It seems to be Qionghua...]","[Qionghua? I know it’s Qionghua. Any problem with that?] Song Qingfeng replied.","[Didn’t your read the documents in Shu Mountain Faction?] Nalan Mingxue said, [Primeval Qionghua, the faction that had disappeared for unknown reasons.]","[My goodness?! There’s records about this faction?!]","[F*ck?!😲] Even Zong Wu emerged in the group chat with a curse.","Gu Tingyun emerged as well. [The Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 is telling the story about a primeval faction?!]"]},{"number":640,"title":"Chapter 640 - Expectation","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","The elves and knights on the Nora Continent hadn’t experienced this stuff before. The celestial mountains in the clouds, the sword forging process, the huge mountains and wide rivers, all kinds of mountain spirits and demons, and the glimpse of Aurogan left deep impressions on their minds.","The grand mountains and rivers were even vaster and more miraculous than the dream-like fairy world that they had imagined.","Still savoring the scenes shown in the trailer, Elder Sewell glanced at Mr. Fang and then at the screen in confusion.","After a long pause, she snapped back to reality.","Looking calm and collected, she chuckled and said, “Hehehe... This new mystical realm is indeed good!”","However, she had complicated feelings inside. If her emotions were all displayed, there would be excitement, thrill, and shock, etc.","How come humans are so powerful now? It doesn’t feel right!","Besides... Have the cultivation mystical realms in the East Continent progressed to this high of a level?!","We can try this mystical realm immediately?","No... The shop owner still hasn’t set the release date yet!","Should I recommend it to other elders when I go back?","No! I must try it first here!","No! I have to return to the Silver Moon Forest soon...","But... I must try it before returning...","Ahh! So frustrating!","With all kinds of thoughts flashing across her mind, she looked very uncertain and anxious.","...","While Elder Sewell mulled over these thoughts, she glanced at the harmless-looking Mr. Fang suspiciously, wondering how this young shop owner had achieved such high-level alchemy skills.","Is this shop a representative shop of the East Continent?","Elder Sewell thought that it was quite possible. Many alchemy workshops put logos in their mystical realms. For example, the Dulan Workshop’s mystical realms had an exquisite logo of sunlight and land upon entry, and the Lava Workshop had a logo of flames. She remembered the ‘Ubisoft’ logo at the beginning of Assassin’s Creed and wondered if the mystical realm were a product of the Ubisoft Workshop.","What a strange name...","Obviously, the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 also had a logo; it was in the colors of blue and white.","Hiss-! It seems that one shop can represent more than one workshop in the East Continent? Elder Sewell was puzzled. The people in that continent do things this way?","Since Elder Sewell wasn’t too familiar with humans, she gave up on the thought. After all, she would try it and then return home.","However...","“Um...? Sir, when will you release this new mystical realm?” Elder Sewell went straight to the point.","“Right! When are you going to release it?!” Hearing the question, everyone turned to Mr. Fang, afraid to miss the newest information about this game.","These people wished that they could play it... oh, no... cultivate in this mystical realm right now.","Yes, we are here to cultivate! Regardless if we were learning how to fight like a berserker or how to achieve stealth and move like the assassins in Assassin’s Creed, we were doing legitimate training and cultivation!","At this thought, they justified their eagerness for the new mystical realm.","However, Mr. Fang thought, Games... you need to understand them before getting to play them. Otherwise, how can you understand the culture that is totally different from the one that you grew up in?","“Um... The second trailer will be released in a couple of days, “Mr. Fang said.","“Ahh-!” Not only the knights and mercenaries, but even the elves had the urge to beat Mr. Fang! What did he say?! Even the second trailer will take a few days to release, let alone the game?!","“I heard that the Lava Workshop will release its new mystical realm.” When Mr. Fang still refused to give them a release date, Sala threatened in a huff, “If you release it later than them, we’ll go and try their mystical realm instead!”","Different from elves who were cold to most humans and were only friendly toward a few, the hearty and meticulous dwarves were on friendly terms with all other races despite their occasional disheveled looks.","The Lava Workshop had a large representative shop in this city.","Humph! I’ll see if this shop owner is afraid of the competition! Sala thought angrily","Hearing her words, the others’ eyes brightened as well. However, then they saw Mr. Fang finishing his Cappuccino and sitting down leisurely on his leather-sofa-style computer chair","“Okay! Everyone, this is all the content for today.” Then, he entered Assassin’s Creed. It was his third round of playing this game, and he intended to finish the whole process with 100% synchronization.","He began to play proficiently.","!!! Instead of worrying about the competition, this guy is now playing the game as if nothing had happened?!","I can’t bear it! Sala was beyond furious. She moved to Mr. Fang and then walked to the door intentionally. “Sir, we’re really going to Lave Workshop to experience its new mystical realm!”","At this moment, Mr. Fang had killed several templar knights in stealth.","“Sir!” Sala was now standing at the door while cussing silently, How come this despicable shop owner isn’t asking me to stay?!","Then, she looked back and saw the sequence results appearing on Mr. Fang’s screen; it was the perfect 100% synchronization.","“Puchi-!” The others couldn’t help laughing when they saw this elf blushing.","“Ms. Sala is so cute.”","“The shop owner is too stiff and stubborn in his ways. We’ve been here for so long; why can’t he make an exception for us once in a while.”","“Ya! You guys are still laughing at me!” Sala had the urge to run up to them and use musou like a berserker.","“Ah... I really want to try it...” Seeing the beautiful palaces in the clouds, the grand spiritual spells, and sword techniques, and the magnificent mountains and rivers, they were eager to enter this realm and play in it. Right now, they felt ticklish as if a kitten was scratching their minds.","Mr. Fang said, “You must be patient; there is a process. Otherwise, you’ll feel befuddled when you play it.”","He looked solemn as if he were doing it for the sake of these lovely elves. However, the elves, knights, mercenaries, and assassins were unmoved, wishing that they could sleep in the shop until the despicable shop owner released this new game.","...","Meanwhile, in the representative shop of the Lava Workshop, the tall and thin man named Leo had received the news.","“Mr. Leo,” Glass said with a laugh, “I believe that you’ve got a plan for this?”","“It seems like this person is still oblivious of his imminent doom... he’s still playing trailers?” Leo chuckled and said, “Don’t worry.”","He was sure that after his new mystical realm was released, this unknown small workshop would vanish from this market."]},{"number":641,"title":"Chapter 641 - More Fun in the Game","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","In this prosperous city, people from different places thronged on the streets.","One could always hear news about the neighboring nations while being here.","“What’s happening?” Seeing the godly palace knights all over the streets, one mercenary complained.","“Didn’t you hear that the Judgement Godly Palace is searching and arresting assassins all over the world?” another mercenary whispered, “I wonder what the assassins did to them. Obviously, the assassins enraged the people of the godly palace.”","“I heard that they were humiliated by an assassin in the Elf Clan; I wonder if that’s true...” the mercenaries talked among themselves in low voices.","“It might be true...” another person surmised, “It’s no wonder that they are making a big deal of it. I remember the Dulan Workshop once boasting about bringing their new mystical realm into the Elf Clan, but they no longer talk about it anymore.”","Obviously, these mercenaries were not stupid and could figure out the rough edges of the whole situation from some clues.","“But I think... this is about it; they don’t dare do anything outrageous here,” a mercenary wearing dark brown leather armor glanced around and said.","“Our Morning Light Empire is a free nation that allows people to believe anything they want, which is why we don’t see anything outrageous here. You can go and have a look in the neighboring nation. It’s a nation that believes in the God of Judgement, and the whole nation is helping them capture the assassins. There’s no hiding place for assassins in that nation! I heard that they had captured many assassins and planned to execute them together.”","“More! I heard that those assassins captured during the assassination attempt of Luther in Grey Eagle City will be executed too.”","At this moment, a few figures passed them, and they suddenly stopped.","Harrison clenched his fists, and his shoulder shivered slightly.","“Calm down! They want to lure us over!” Another assassin tightly grabbed onto him.","“I know...” Harrison roared hoarsely, “But they are our peers! Our brothers and sisters! Does the Brotherhood know about it?! They should fight for freedom instead of being hung on the godly palace’s scaffold!”","The low-profiled, middle-aged assassin who had grown up in a slum lost his usual composure.","“We should let more peers know about free will and the master assassins. I think they will like this place as we do!” Harrison said, “We’ll move in stealth and perform the leap of faith together; it doesn’t matter even if we’re discovered.”","“During our free time, we can drink Cappuccino and talk about the stories in Assassin’s Creed.” He described his ideal life in a mild voice. Then, this middle-aged man’s voice broke into a sob. “I want them to know that we’re not lowly and filthy mice; I want them to know that being an assassin is a great profession! Do you know... I have plans for them...”","“They shouldn’t be hung on the damn scaffold!”","...","“Ugh? How come this shop is closed?” While they talked, the mercenaries passed a shop selling alchemy items and found that it had been shut down.","“Isn’t this the Merlin Workshop’s alchemy item shop? How come it’s closed?” Obviously, this mercenary used to buy alchemy items from this shop. “What happened...”","“I wonder how the people in this shop had dealings with assassins?” At this moment, another group of people passed the shop, pointing at it while they talked.","“I have no idea. But I heard that one assassin used a sword made by the Merlin Alchemy Workshop in an assassination attempt on some priests and even broke a priest’s protective godly spell with this sword...”","“The Rebel’s Blade?” The Rebel’s Blade had once appeared in a rebellion in the Radiant Light Godly Nation, and this blade full of curses had once broken the godly spell barrier set up in the anti-mage array.","“It seems similar, but it obviously isn’t as powerful as that legendary sword,” another person said.","“But I heard that the owner of the shop hasn’t been captured yet, so he probably escaped to another nation, which is why all the shops have been closed.”","“It’s a good shop though... Alas! Let’s move on.”","...","“Sir, is the trailer out today?”","“Sir, it’s still not released today?”","Almost everyday day, the elves came into the shop eagerly in anticipation.","So did the mercenaries who lived in the city and the knights of Golden Griffin Knight Legion.","Obviously, today’s trailer was more informative.","In fact, Fang Qi was watching it too since this trailer wasn’t introducing the game’s background; Fang Qi knew those things too well.","This trailer showed how to play the game and operate in the game.","Obviously, the new version of the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 not only increased the degree of freedom and openness but added extra content and details.","For example, in the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 1, Li Xiaoyao was the only main character, and players could only choose him to play the game.","In the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 3, there were two main characters which were Jing Tian and Xu Changqing. The story was told from their respective perspectives in alternation.","However, when the players played as Jing Tian, they didn’t know what Xu Changqing was doing and couldn’t choose to play Xu Changqing either. The same happened when they played Xu Changqing.","The system remake of the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 was different.","In the trailer, everyone watched Murong Ziying practicing sword techniques in the Qionghua Faction and saw some scenes about his daily interaction with his nephew-disciples. Those scenes happened before he met Yun Tianhe. The players could unlock the storyline of Murong Ziying and play the game from his perspective after playing as Yun Tianhe to a certain level.","Besides, the trailer demonstrated how to play as Liu Mengli and Han Lingsha whom could only be played by female players.","Different from the original game in which the players could only choose one of the four characters to play, the trailer showed that in the new version, four players could enter multi-player mode and control Yun Tianhe, Murong Ziying, Liu Mengli, and Han Lingsha respectively.","However, in this mode, the players had to trigger different plots and interactions. In single-player mode, most of the events were trigger automatically and were as real as possible.","Of course, if the four players controlled the four characters to go anywhere and do whatever they wanted, the plot of the Legend of the Sword and Fairly 4 couldn’t continue properly, which was why the system had improved the game mode while giving players a greater degree of freedom.","It was a blessing to the players who liked to play the games together with their friends."]},{"number":642,"title":"Chapter 642 - You Will Miss an Opportunity to Become Rich","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","In the game, players could have flying sword races and matches between the disciples of the Qionghua Faction, and many other things were added.","On the other hand, the system version re-created all the details in the forging and spirit injection of weapons.","In other words, unlike Diablo 2, the players didn’t have to spend lots of time to find the details and materials about the production of items and only start researching it after getting everything that they needed. Also, unlike Dungeon Fighter Online, they didn’t have to toss their items into a machine and leave their fate to chance. This time, they could experience and control the whole process of making items.","This was an artifact making skill for cultivators, and it wouldn’t be available to players until Murong Ziying joined the team. After all, only Murong Ziying knew this skill among the four teammates.","...","In the castle sitting in the highest position of the city, a middle-aged man dressed in an elegant aristocratic tuxedo was silently sitting behind a desk. His black tuxedo was exquisitely tailored, and his square face was wrinkled. However, his grey mustache gave him a genial and graceful look.","At this moment, a figure had just left in a huff, slamming the door behind him.","Indifferent, the man stood up and tended to the potted plants on the windowsill as if these flowers and plants were the center of his world.","These were not precious flowers but looked like the wild pale-yellow flowers that were blooming everywhere in the city.","Of course, it might be that these flowers were seen everywhere since they were his favorite.","Then, a woman wearing knight armor and with her blond hair pulled up in a pigtail walked in.","“Oh...? I don’t remember that a junior knight can enter the City Administrator’s Office at will,” the middle-aged man said without turning his head.","“I also don’t remember those promises that a man said to Mother before he forgot them the next second.” Helen didn’t look a bit meek.","“Um...” The middle-aged man’s calm expression turned stiff before he said in a deep voice, “You should call me Father.”","Helen turned her head sideways, and stubbornness appeared on her pretty face.","After a long pause, the middle-aged man seemed to give in first. He said mildly, “The messenger of the Judgement Godly Palace came to me a moment ago.”","“What did he want?” Seeming concerned, Helen turned her head back and asked the question.","“Shut down,” the middle-aged man said. “He asked me to shut down the shop with official force.”","Seeing Helen’s intense gaze on him, he shook his head and said, “I refused.”","Seeming to sense her displeasure, he continued, “I didn’t do it to help you. After all, our Morning Light Empire is a nation of free faith, and it’s not right to allow the Judgement Godly Place to dominate others.”","“This is not the Radiant Light Godly Nation, and they can’t do whatever they want in this place.”","“It’s your decision; don’t expect gratitude from me.” Helen opened the door and walked out. When one of her feet was outside the door, she added, “That damn shop owner seems powerful; I don’t think he needs anyone’s help.”","“Okay.” Looking at Helen who was walking away, the middle-aged man shook his head and chuckled.","...","“Damn it! He just married into power; he’s just a stupid lowly ant! What is he without the Hymia Family! What right does he have to refuse me?!” A vicious roar sounded in the godly palace; it came from Glass.","“We have other plans.” At this moment, the red-robed senior priest walked over. “Anyway, we must deal with the assassins first. Without assassins, that shop’s assassin mystical realm will have no reason to exist.","“Believe me, that shop owner is only an ignorant alchemist seeking his death. Anything is void before the force given by the almighty god. He will end up like the alchemist named Merlin from the Stan Kingdom.”","At the mentioning those lofty existences, he sounded extremely reverent.","Glass asked, “When will the assassins be executed?”","“Two to three weeks later.”","“So long?” Glass asked in surprise.","“Be patient,” The red-robed senior priest said, “We set up a great trap for them under the direction of St. Dulan. We’ll give the assassins more time to come and rescue the prisoners.”","“Of course. This way, we’ll capture all these damn assassins!” Glass sneered, “They probably don’t know. We must reserve many things and not show them to the public.”","For example, they didn’t put every anti-assassination skill in their newly released mystical realm.","The red-robed senior priest said in a chilly voice, “If they think that those skills are all that we have, then they must pray to their great predecessor Altair to protect them in Hell! Hahaha!”","“Of course! We’ll have a real battle instead of a practice.”","Laughter sounded in the palace.","...","Mr. Fang got up quite early this morning. It could be that the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 would be finally released today, or it could just be that it was a day with nice weather. Anyway, Mr. Fang walked downstairs before the opening time.","Used to Mr. Fang’s punctuality since he always opened the shop on time, no customers came to the shop at this hour.","It was quiet in the shop. After opening the door, Mr. Fang sat down on a couch with his breakfast; a bowl of instant noodles and a sausage.","At this moment, a handsome young man who looked to be in his twenties stopped at the door. He was wearing a white mage robe with blue edges and a pointy mage hat.","Travel-fatigued, he paused for a while outside the door before walking in.","At first glance, this man looked very young, but his eyes appeared as deep as the starry night sky. Also, he moved with a maturity and confidence that didn’t belong to a young man.","“Sir, you run cultivation mystical realms?” He looked around the shop in surprise.","Waiting for the instant noodles to be ready, Mr. Fang drank a mouthful of Sprite and nodded casually.","“Your shop... has little business...” This young man smiled as if he was trying to decide on what to say. After a while, he continued, “I think you need some help, maybe some guidance to success.”","“A guidance to success?” Mr. Fang looked at him in surprise.","“Yes!” The ‘young mage’ who appeared to be in his twenties said, “I think you’re in luck, young man. With my help, your shop will be popular very soon.”","While being stunned, Fang Qi carefully studied the customer before him.","“??” While he was in a daze, the ‘young man’ took out a magic staff from his inner pocket as if he intended to add to his credibility and demonstrate something to convince Fang Qi.","He looked around and outside the door. After making sure that no one else was watching, he took out a stone and waved his magic staff, saying, “Do you see this stone? I’ll transform it into a magic crystal.”","“...”","After pausing for a while, Mr. Fang seemed to finally understand, and he said, “I got it. You’re...”","“Of course I am!” While saying that, he thought, Now you know that I’m a great alchemist!","“You’re a scammer, right?” Mr. Fang said.","“Pu-!” This ‘young man’ almost dropped to the ground.","What?! I’m Merlin, a lofty level 9 mage. And you, a young shop owner, dare to call me a scammer?!” Do I look like a scammer?","You will miss an opportunity to become rich!"]},{"number":643,"title":"Chapter 643 - Major Streamers Began to Broadcast the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Mr. Fang stood up and pulled the man to the door. While pushing two magic crystals into this man’s hand, Fang Qi waved his hand and said, “Go and find another shop.”","Mr. Fang looked frustrated at this moment. It was early morning, and a scammer insisted to show him how to transform a rock into a magic crystal.","If he can do that, then I can transform a rock into a piece of gold! Damn it!","I pushed two magic crystals into his hand; now he can go and perform in another shop.","Clank!","With two low-level magic crystals in his hand, the supreme level 9 mage and master alchemist found that the door closed in his face before he could understand the situation.","This situation is strange!","Seeing a grand alchemist who can turn rocks into magic crystals, the owner of this small shop with little business was not even a little tempted?","With his great skills in alchemy and magic spells, he was welcomed in every nation as an VIP. He could make a pile of low-level cultivation mystical realms that were operated by a small shop like this one.","Merlin stood at the door with a dark expression.","Forget it!","He had planned to help this shop grow popular, and he was sure that it would be full within three months and be known all over Canglan City in one year.","With my alchemy and magic spell knowledge, this little shop owner will be terrified!","During the process, he would have a hiding place for himself...","But this shop owner just refused such a great opportunity! A gold mine!","Do you know what you’ve missed?! A big opportunity to get rich quickly","Even he felt anxious and pitiful for the shop owner.","Just when he was about to leave, something flashed in his peripheral.","He turned around and saw a big group of knights dressed in luxurious armor and riding on precious mounts while moving toward him slowly.","So many knights?! Looking at the golden griffin badges on their chests, he knew that they were high-level knights.","Was my identity exposed?!","No. This nation protects people’s freedom of religious beliefs! When did the Judgement Godly Palace obtain such great influence in this place?!","While he was hesitating if he should make a move, the knights made a turn and passed him. Then, they all stopped and dismounted from their precious mounts.","All these knights swarmed into the shop behind him.","“Sir! Is the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 released today?!”","“Sir! You promised that the new mystical realm would be released today! Is it released or not?!”","While Merlin gaped at the knights and wondered what was going on, a big group of elves hurried toward the shop.","Elder Sewell was determined to play the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 today!","She had waited so long! They wouldn’t return to the Silver Moon Forest until they played it!","In a daze, Merlin turned his head and looked at them. ... When did a human city have so many elves ?","There is even an elf elder among them!","While he was wondering about the situation, a large group of mercenaries and mages swarmed over as well.","My goodness! He felt incredulous. They seem to be talking about a mystical realm...?! What? The mystical realm in this shop is so popular?!","This great alchemist who was also a mage was at a loss for words.","Do you guys know what a truly great mystical realm looks like?!","You all swarmed into this small shop and left me, a lofty existence and a great alchemist master, outside?!","Suddenly, a thought dawned on him. Is this shop owner so sure of his own alchemy skills that my skills are beneath his level, and he doesn’t want to bother with me?!","If the shop owner were just an ignorant ordinary person, he would just laugh it off.","But now, he found that the situation was too outrageous to be ignored.","He strode back into the shop and shouted, “Sir, let me try that mystical realm too!”","...","After waiting in line for a while, Merlin finally got to activate the mystical realm named the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4.","“Is this cultivation mystical realm any different from all the others that I have played?” Doubting its quality, he found a seat and entered the game.","At this moment, the players in the old shops had eagerly entered the game.","In the new shop, the most popular game was still Assassin’s Creed, and almost every customer played it. Even though the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 was released today, many people continued playing Assassin’s Creed while they waited to see the effects of the new game.","But in the old shops, the situation was different. The Assassin’s Creed series was indeed good and had many fans, but the Legend of the Sword and Fairy series was among the hottest games. Its huge group of fans instantly ignited the atmosphere in the shops.","Some players couldn’t come to the shops every day due to their busy schedules. After all, the shops were here and wouldn’t move away. But today, even the ancient family masters in the Spiritual State put aside their daily business and came to the shop.","After all, the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 was released today, and they must show their support!","By now, the old shops had been divided into many zones with space-folding technology, but they were still crammed with customers today.","The Jiuhua City Shop was even busier. Many civilian players who didn’t have membership cards almost broke the counter.","“Calm down! Calm down, everyone!” While waving his folding fan, Xiao Yulv sweated profusely as he said, “I promise you that everyone can play the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 today. Those who are waiting can go to the lounge area to take a break and watch the livestreams, which will help you play the game better when it’s your turn, right?”","“In a while, the big streamers will play the game in their livestream rooms.” Right now, the Jiuhua City Shop was being managed by two senior clerks, Xiao Yulv and Yu Zhiwei. Yu Zhiwei also yelled, “Anyone who doesn’t have a seat can go and watch the livestreams first. Our popular streamer, New Snow, will give us a livestream! I wonder what amazing plays New Snow will show us today! Everyone, please go and support her!”","“I heard that the big streamers of Dungeon Fighter Online such as Rosen Rain and Zhu Yanxiao will stream the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 too!” Xiao Yulv said, “I’m sure that their livestreams will be excellent! Don’t miss these shows!”","“By the way, our Sister Su, Su Tianji, will put the whole process on the livestream too!”","“So many people doing livestreams?!”","“Really?!”","“Rosen Rain hasn’t done livestreams for a long time, right?!”","“I want to watch New Snow’s livestream!”","“Let’s go and watch Elder Su’s livestream! Maybe we can see her land on her face when using the leap of faith again!”","“???” Sitting near the counter, Su Tianji put down her virtual reality headset and looked back. She seemed to hear some strange words about her.","Seeing that there were no seats available, many people went to watch the livestream.","Of course, some people just watched while standing behind the computers. For example, Su Tianji and Nalan Mingxue now each had a large group of people standing behind them."]},{"number":644,"title":"Chapter 644 - Elder Su Is Being Mocked Again","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","In the past, Mr. Fang had to try the game first to show everyone. Otherwise the customers wouldn’t know how to play. Now that the shop had released trailers showing the background of the game and the proper controls, Mr. Fang had much less work to do when the game was formally released.","By now, many players had clicked on the logo on the desktop and entered the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4.","The melodious flute tune together with the faint erhu notes felt like light floating clouds, and they brought the players to an ancient-looking square mirror. The mist and cloud in the mirror seemed to draw them into a dream-like fantasy world.","My goodness... Upon entering the game, Merlin had the feeling that this was a grand production. While scratching his head, he wondered, This is ...!!?? When did the cultivation mystic realms of this city advance to this high of a level?!","If a small workshop in this city can reach this high of a level, then I, a level 9 alchemist, probably can only be a little clerk in such a shop to survive.","How can it be?!","Astonished, he began the new game.","The elves and members of the knight legion had also entered the game.","However, the assassins including Elina and Harrison didn’t have time to play this game yet since they put all their time on practicing the assassination skills in Assassin’s Creed.","However, they were still curious about this new game. Right now, they stood behind the elves and watched them play with bowls of instant noodles in their hands.","“Oh! Is this the immortal realm?!” Commander Elven had just clicked on [New Beginning] when he was driven into the ancient mirror by a powerful force. The mirror fluttered like the surface of a lake, and he found that he was inside the world in the ancient mirror!","“The music is so good!” The art-loving elves found the melodious flute tune and the low and sad erhu notes harmonious and beautiful like flowing water and breezes in nature, even though they didn’t know the names of the instruments.","“Are they the musical instruments from the East Continent? One of them sounds like a fipple flute?” Obviously, Elder Sewell was a music lover. She could play beautiful music with a leaf from the Silver Moon Forest. “I wonder what instrument this is. I want to try it...”","Everything looks so real! While flying through the ocean of clouds into the immortal world behind the white clouds, Merlin was stunned to his core. As a supreme-level mage, he had experienced all the things in the world that most people could never experience. However, he had never heard about any other cultivation mystic realm that could be this real!","As a master alchemist, he knew how difficult it was to achieve this level of realness.","Perhaps the East Continent had achieved a great breakthrough only in this one area. He thought as he continued the game.","Grand and beautiful buildings and palaces stood in the immortal mountains. When the players looked down, they saw many disciples wearing blue-and-white Daoist robes and standing on a platform that was surrounded by faint mist and guarded by auspicious beasts. From the distance, the disciples looked like troops that were in compact formations.","A huge lotus-shaped platform made of green and white jade hovered in the sky. Two ethereal voices came from the platform while two immortal swords, Wangshu and Xihe, emitted bright immortal light!","With spiritual essence flowing inside, the two immortal swords were engulfed by orange-red flame-like light and icy-blue frost-like light respectively.","“This is the scene shown in the trailer!” Seeing this familiar scene, the elves almost leaped up in excitement.","“I see this too!” Sitting across from them, Mercenary Crete yelled in elation as well.","The two swords came together, and a tremendous streak of spiritual essence traveled through the center of the Cloud Platform into the array pattern in the center of the stone platform surrounded by lotus flowers.","Immediately, two dazzling sword beams shot up into the sky!","The whole sky seemed to be pierced open, revealing a magical, dream-like world!","“Are they mages of the East Continent?!”","Obviously, there were many things that the players didn’t understand.","However, this gave them a sense of mystery and didn’t hinder the gaming experience. Subconsciously, they yelled in excitement, “Oh!”","“Elf God Almighty!” Elder Sewell was also stunned by this scene.","“What am I looking at?!”","“Don’t... be afraid! It’s just a mystic realm! A... fantasy world for us to...watch,” a few golden griffin knights who were less sensitive hurried to explain.","At this moment, Zhu Yanxiao started his livestream in the old shop. While recovering from his shock, he stroked his short hair and said, “As you can see, this game is really awesome! Considering the high quality of the two previous games of this series, I suggest you guys try it if you’re still hesitating.”","At this moment, Nalan Mingxue was obviously calmer than the others in her livestream. “That’s why I call the Legend of Sword and Fairy series the most anticipated work. They are exciting at the very beginning.”","“I have to take a break and eat some potato chips to calm down.”","“Aowu!” Then, she stuffed some potato chips into her mouth.","“Gongzi Xiao.” At this moment, Mu Donglai was sitting on a couch, not able to find a seat since he was late. “I heard that you’re very familiar with these livestreams. Can you recommend one to me?”","“Of course.” Obviously, Xiao Yulv was well informed in this area. “According to my observation of their daily livestreams, I divide them into several big categories.”","“If you want to watch excellent details, granular control, and ultimate plays, you can watch the livestreams hosted by Rosen Rain, Lord Nalan, Almighty Demonic God, and Ms. Sprite. Um, as everyone know, Almighty Demonic God is also called Almighty Smirking Face Emoji, and Rosen Rain usually works together with a dark-faced man in her livestreams.”","“However, they are all ultimate professionals and have great technical foundation. It is not useful to low-level players since ordinary people can’t copy their plays,” Xiao Yulv said with great knowledge, “So, I usually watch Zhu Yanxiao and New Snow’s livestreams since those players are easy to copy.”","“Xiaoyue has a very cute style and good skills. You can watch her livestream if you like, but she doesn’t livestream often.”","“The livestream of Hardworking Fairy Liu is quite interesting too.”","“These are streamers who I watch quite often,” Xiao Yulv said, “Besides, there are streamers such as the King of Rangers and Mad Butcher. They have good skills, but I don’t watch them often.”","Mu Donglai said curiously, “How come you didn’t mention Elder Su, Gongzi Xiao?”","“She’s a idle-style streamer,” Xiao Yulv whispered, “Don’t tell anyone I said that...”","Mu Donglai’s face twitched as he thought, Um... This... Is it really proper to mock Elder Su this way?"]},{"number":645,"title":"Chapter 645 - Kui Zhao Materialized in Rock Creek Cave","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","At this moment, many huge demon beasts flew down from the world that appeared in the sky. In legend, tapirs were rare beasts that swallowed dreams. The dream tapirs from the Fantasy Netherworld was obviously fiercer and more elegant than those in legends. With lean and long bodies, fox-like heads, long tails, rainbow-colored feathers, and mountain-like size, they landed among the disciples of the Qionghua Faction, causing a bloody catastrophe.","Paws slashed out with blood spraying in all directions, and swords whistled, mixing with the roars of wild beasts.","The ethereal figures on the mountaintop among the clouds moved, and the sharp sword beams and chilly and alluring demonic spells formed a grand battle between immortals and demons.","The elves and mercenaries gaped at the scene with shock and awe on their faces.","The knights who were used to seeing many similar battles found that even a story in the game could be so grand and majestic!","Although they didn’t understand it yet, the players felt awe-struck!","“Ugh? That’s all?!” While they were enjoying it, the scene suddenly dimmed before them.","“That’s the end?!”","“Who won the battle anyway?!” They had seen the moment when Chan You faked defeat and then sneak-attacked the Taiqing Spiritual Master.","[TL Note: Taiqing Spiritual Master is also known as the Grand Pure One.]","“What’s happening?! Damn it! The scum shop owner did it again! We are left hanging again!?”","Mr. Fang told them that it wasn’t his fault, and he thought, “The game is created Softstar; why are you blaming it on me?”","He looked sulky.","After the opening cinematics, the game started.","“Oh... This person who looks to be a faction chief was killed by the demon.” In her livestream room, Su Tianji finished watching the cinematics while eating potato chips. She explained the scenes while watching it, looking quite professional.","Then, a crude wooden house appeared in everyone’s eyes. Yun Tianqing’s memorial tablet was placed on the table in the house, and smoke floated from the sandalwood incense sticks. Beside the table was a small boar that had been tied up for sacrifice.","“Um, how come this person looks like a savage, uh?”","On the screen was a good-looking young man with messy hair. With animal fur draped on his shoulders, the young man was wearing crude cotton clothes, and he kneeled before the memorial tablet with a dull expression. “Dad, I know I’m in the wrong. Last night, the boar’s loud screams kept me up for most of the night, which is why I’m late for burning the incense sticks for you this morning. Spring passed already, so I don’t know why it’s screaming so much!”","The small boar that was tied on the side honked.","“Dad told me to burn three incense sticks for him in the morning and night.” It seemed like he was talking to the boar. “You don’t know how terrifying he looked when he got angry.”","“Is he the main character?” Su Tianji ate another potato chip and said, “How come he looks so dull?”","After all, the main characters in the Legend of Sword and Fairy 1 and 3 are all clever, but this guy...","Su Tianji touched her head and thought, How come he looks as dull as a cattle?","...","– Meanwhile, in the new shop –","Mage Merlin was also puzzled. How come this mystical realm is different from all the others that I had seen.","The elves, knights, and mercenaries had also come to this part.","Then, they heard low roars of a boar outside the door. Obviously, the young man drew out the big boar after catching the small one.","“Great! I captured a boar, and another came for free!” Pleased, Yun Tianhe ran out the door.","Now, it was time for the players to control the main character.","“Can we use both the bow and sword?” Seeing Yun Tianhe taking out his bow, the elves who were archery masters were eager to try.","In the room, there was also a rusty thin sword. It looked old and wasn’t well-maintained.","“Can we use these two weapons?” Elina and the other assassins who were watching from behind looked eager. After all, bows and swords were common weapons used in Assassin’s Creed.","“I wonder how it feels to use these weapons...”","“I saw this scene in the trailer!” The players’ spawn place was on Green Bird Peak which was covered by giant ancient trees that looked like screens. Behind the wooden house was a huge waterfall with a stone bridge connecting the banks of the river beneath the waterfall. Before the house was an ancient path made of green stones. Further away, there was a tall cliff. Looking over, there was the misty and beautiful scenery.","All the grass and trees in this place looked natural. For the elves, this place had a type of beauty different from the kind that they were used to seeing.","“Oh! I thought Moonlight Lake in Silver Moon Forest was the most beautiful place that I’ve seen...” Sala’s pretty eyes looked at the picturesque Green Bird Peak in pleasant surprise. “So beautiful!”","For elves who loved art and nature, they would never miss such an opportunity to enjoy the rare natural beauty of this place.","As for the task and plot?","They would think about them later...","Yes, they were the legendary fans of beautiful scenery.","They must enjoy the natural beauty first!","The female boar had run into the Rock Creek Cave in which Yun Tianhe’s father’s tomb was located, but these elves ignored it and just ran around Green Bird Peak, wishing to take screenshots of each place they went.","As for the golden griffin knights and Mage Merlin, they liked the scenery as well, but they weren’t as crazy over it as the elves.","“Is this just a low-level mystical realm used to practice skills...?” Merlin was puzzled. According to the previous grand battle they had just watched, this mystical realm should be a high-level one.","How come the strange savage that I’m controlling only has a little bit of strength in his body?","Were those prior images just a bluff?","...","Helen had come to this part too. In her eyes, the main character was totally different from the characters in other games, and he was extremely funny. Hahaha! This guy... how did he mistake a girl for a big wild boar?!","“He thinks that she’s a demon boar; so hilarious...”","In the cave that appeared to be covered by ice crystals and ebony jade, Helen watched the conversation between this young man and a girl, and she almost spewed out iced red tea with laughter.","“Hiss-! What’s this?!”","At this moment, in Rock Creek Cave, an inhuman voice sounded.","“Summoning storms and thunder with a whisper. Reaching Heaven and Earth and entering the netherworld. Changing at will into anything I like.”","She looked over and saw a faint white shadow appearing before her. It had a body but no feet, looking like a spirit or a ghost with white flames burning around its body.","“Is it a ghost?” She looked shocked. As an aristocrat knight born and raised in Canglan City, she had never seen such things before!","“I’m Kui Zhao. I’m guarding this place at my master’s order, and I will kill any trespassers!”","“My goodness! Look! What’s this thing?!” Helen’s alarming shout drew the eyes of all the people around her.","Soon, they saw the white talisman spirit which looked like an immortal.","Helen’s sword techniques were good, but when she struck her sword at this thing, she found that her blade went through the body of the talisman spirit!","“This is... an alchemy creature?!” Merlin froze and then yelled, “This must be an alchemy creature; a high-level one too! It is a high-level alchemy creature immune to damage!”","Isn’t this a basic mystical realm?! How come it has such things?!","Besides... Is this the alchemy of the East Continent? Their skills have advanced to such a high level?!"]},{"number":646,"title":"Chapter 646 - Five-Spiritual Immortal Spell","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","By now, the regular players in the new shop sat together but had made different progress in the game. For example, after traveling around in Green Bird Peak, the elves had just entered Rock Creek Cave. Meanwhile, Helen and the other golden griffin knights who were faster than them had triggered the talisman spirit in Rock Creek Cave.","Still not understanding this game, the elves and mages only knew that the dull-looking main character seemed to have a powerful father. There were memories of his parents in Tianhe’s mind, and the players only got a rough understanding of it. Overall, they got the feeling that this young man couldn’t meet his parents’ expectations for him.","In Assassin’s Creed, the two main characters were masters at the beginning of the games, but this person was an orphan without any self-defense abilities. Although he was cute in a dull way, it was his life that was on the line!","Hearing Helen’s scream, everyone around her looked over at the horrifying talisman spirit on her screen, wondering if she would die soon!","At this critical moment in the game, Helen was oblivious of her surroundings.","Finding that she could move again, she began to run while pulling Han Lingsha with her.","“Ugh?” Han Lingsha looked puzzled, and she asked, “Didn’t you say that nothing is as scary as your dad?”","While her face twitched, Helen looked embarrassed and said, “Girl, please stop talking. I’m protecting you right now!”","“Auch!” Kui Zhao summoned two ordinary talisman spirits to sweep toward them swiftly as a mass of white mist with faint spiritual light.","Gusts howled and sword energies whistled around them. It was obvious that with their speed, they couldn’t come out of Rock Creek Cave alive under Kui Zhao’s spiritual spells.","They had no choice but to fight.","With the inhumane training from Assassin’s Creed, Helen used the little strength in her body and controlled Yun Tianhe to stop. At this moment, Yun Tianhe turned and dodged Kui Zhao’s attack at the last moment while stabbing his sword into Kui Zhao’s body.","“She got it!” Many people’s eyes brightened when they saw that Kui Zhao didn’t dodge.","The sword pierced into its vital point. If Helen were in Assassin’s Creed, this would be a perfect counterattack!","However, everyone saw the long sword piercing through Kui Zhao’s body in the next moment, inflicting no damage to the creature.","Meanwhile, Yun Tianhe felt an excruciating pain all over him as Kui Zhao went through his body!","Different from the original version, the talisman spirits had no solid forms in the system version, and their ordinary attacks could do damage to the players’ souls.","“I told you!” Merlin said while watching the scene, “This one is absolutely an alchemy creature! A high-level alchemy creature who is immune to damage and can cast spiritual spells!”","On the screen, Yun Tianhe, who was under Helen’s control, had been severely injured, and Han Lingsha pulled him to flee. Meanwhile, the audience looked toward Merlin and asked, “You know about this creature?”","“Of course!” Merlin was sure of himself. “This alchemy creature must be a powerful monster created to guard a tomb or something.”","“Ugh...?” The mercenaries, knights, and elves looked at the ‘young man’ curiously. They thought, He isn’t old. Is he...","“Are you an alchemist?”","“Of course!” Merlin was touched by the fact that he was recognized. He thought, These elves sure know what is going on.","“Do you know how to deal with these creatures?” Sala and the other young elves asked expectantly.","“I can if I encounter them. After all, I’m a master alchemist,” Merlin said calmly and thought, Aya! I’m finally being recognized and valued! I’ll see if the damn shop owner dares to treat me as a scammer again!","“Then...” Elina pointed at the two people running for their lives on the screen and asked, “Can you help them?”","“No!” Merlin shook his head with absolute certainty.","“Then, you’re useless!” Not only Elina, but the elves around Merlin looked at him in disdain.","You little girls...!!?? Don’t you have any respect for your seniors and compassion for juniors?!","With a dark expression, Merlin pointed at the screen and said, “In this situation, even a supreme level 9 master can’t do anything about it!”","He just told them the facts.","The moment he said it, Han Lingsha said in the screen, “No. We’ll both die here if we keep this up. We must use whatever method we can think of, regardless of how far-fetched they may seem.”","“Hey! Calm down and listen to my incantation! We’ll deal with it with an immortal spell!”","Everyone froze at her words. What is going on?","“Dao combines Heaven, Earth, and people to achieve essence. Heaven circulates with essence, Earth moves with essence...”","“Daoist spells sense everything through essences!”","What’s this thing?!","Everyone was stupefied. Are you two young people who don’t know anything? How come you suddenly took out such advanced things?","They didn’t understand a single sentence, but they felt like the incantation was extremely profound and lofty!","Merlin who had declared that no one could find a solution to this situation was also stupefied. With his high-level skills in spiritual spells, he could sense the power contained in the mysterious words even though they came from another system which was totally different from his.","“Smooth water penetrates all holes, burning flames burn all things, fierce lightning shatters all tough materials, sweeping winds travel through all barriers, and nurturing earth merges all things!”","“Ahh-!” The moment Han Lingsha finished chanting, Helen yelled, “I seemed to have mastered this spiritual spell!”","“What-?!” Merlin yelled in astonishment! How is this possible?","Han Lingsha had just taught Yun Tianhe the general guideline of the Five-Spiritual Immortal Spells. All the spells later in the game had to be derived and learned from this general guideline.","This was why the players could comprehend all kinds of advanced immortal spells later.","The system version of the game gave the players a greater degree of freedom in this area.","For example, these spells would be comprehended by players with their own abilities and experience, which meant that different players would obtain different understandings and different things.","For example, Helen circulated the spiritual essence in her body with the incantation after screaming. Then, she lightly placed her left palm on the sword blade and yelled in a low voice, “Lightning Spell!”","A streak of faint lightning energy appeared on the blade the moment she uttered the incantation. The sword in Yun Tianhe’s hand emitted a wave of pale blue light.","With the same basic incantation and the same lightning spell, different people would use it in different ways after they understood it from the spiritual spell general guideline."]},{"number":647,"title":"Chapter 647 - Gradually Merging In","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Hahaha! Check out my new spiritual spell!” Looking at the slim lightning energy on her sword, Helen was thrilled.","Mr. Fang who was standing behind her glanced at it. “...”","Recalling the thick blue lightning beams of the Lightning Spell in the original game, he was speechless when he saw this...","However, Helen was thrilled. With a clear yell, she went into battle again!","While the lightning bolts flashed on her sword, three talisman spirits roared together and swept the air in the cave into howling gusts which in turn transformed into destructive hurricanes!","The sword skills that the players had learned in Assassin’s Creed were efficient skills to kill enemies, but the targets were all humans. Since talisman spirits didn’t have vital organs, these skills were not enough to deal with them.","Helen’s fierce attacks afflicted no damage on the talisman spirits. In contrast, Yun Tianhe who was under Helen’s control received many wounds.","Still, Helen fought hard and killed one talisman spirit, giving the audience a glimpse of hope of turning the tables. Of course, it was only a small hope.","“This is good!” Helen said excitedly, “I think I can pass this one if I become more proficient with this spiritual spell!”","While being cautious, she ducked the attacks and tried to find a chance to fight back.","“Can we learn spiritual spells this way?!” Merlin froze. Although the players were placed in a weird world, everything felt real with a vivid storyline running through the whole game while they were forced to understand and learn spiritual spells under the pressure of life-or-death situations. “In this situation, if you don’t win, you’ll die. So, the people cultivating in this mystical realm must focus all their attention on the stuff they need to learn and thus achieve a level of learning efficiency at least twice as much compared to the usual situations!”","At this moment, Helen had totally merged herself with the character in the game.","“This way, one can obtain more understanding efficiently...”","More importantly...","“Smooth water penetrates all holes, burning flames burn all things, fierce lightning shatters all tough materials...” Merlin murmured the words in an awkward accent. This language was stored in Yun Tianhe’s memory, and it wasn’t difficult for this supreme mage to learn a new language.","The deep and mysterious general guideline immediately drew his attention.","Other than Merlin, the Elf Elder Sewell and the knights of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion had also resumed the game.","The mages were all amazed. “Are these spiritual spells from the East Continent?!”","“Miraculous!”","On the screen, the second talisman spirit dropped to the ground under the sword attacks engulfed by lightning bolts.","However, what happened next went beyond the players’ imagination!","Violent winds filled the Rock Creek Cave. It seemed that Kui Zhao had just begun using its true power.","On the screen, the audience saw that Han Lingsha and Yun Tianhe couldn’t even get close to the talisman spirit.","“So powerful...” The gusts instantly sent them flying like cannonballs.","The essence and spirit in Yun Tianhe’s body had almost run out.","At this moment, the Wangshu Sword in Yun Tianhe’s hand suddenly lit up.","Kui Zhao finally stopped its attacks and bowed while saying, “Wangshu? It’s you, Master.”","“Master?!” The audience who had thought that the main character was dull and weak were stupefied.","After all the dangers they experienced, the players found out that this powerful alchemy creature was a subordinate of this sword?!","“It turns out that this savage is quite powerful...” Elina whispered.","“No. It’s his father who’s powerful!” Merlin commented, “He must be a very powerful alchemist. Also, this sword must be a very powerful magic item!”","On this continent which had different knowledge and cultures, it was natural for the people to use the terms such as ‘alchemist’ and ‘magic items’ to describe what they saw.","At this point, the players began to have a general idea about this game.","“I think I get it. This is a story about a great alchemist and his son!” Merlin commented solemnly.","“I can’t wait to see if someone is going to teach magical alchemy skills in the game!”","Mr. Fang put his hand on his forehead. “...”","In fact, before Fang Qi traveled through time and space, he had met many foreign friends who didn’t know the difference between Wuxia and Xianxia. However, this didn’t dampen their enthusiasm for the games.","Despite their many misunderstandings, these new players enjoyed the game very much.","“I’m going to fight this powerful alchemy creature now!” Elf Girl Sala said eagerly, “Pray for me. Will it submit to me after I show this powerful sword to it?”","“Oh! Haha! We can have such a shortcut?”","“Let me try it!”","...","In the system version, despite the greater degree of freedom, the players still had to do certain things such as learning spiritual spells.","The players couldn’t expect Kui Zhao to submit to them the moment that they took out the Wangshu Sword.","While retaining its high degree of freedom, the system had used all kinds of methods to avoid certain situations.","In fact, the players had only one sword, which was Wangshu, from the very beginning. Helen had battled Kui Zhao with Wangshu, but the latter showed no reaction to the sword at that time.","This was an issue with the activation and awakening of power in the Wangshu Sword. In the original version, the sword woke up the moment Yun Tianhe encountered Han Lingsha, the destined person.","However, in the system version, the sword had just been activated once by accident. If the players wanted to activate it again before Kui Zhao, they must know how to use the force of the spells.","Right now, Yun Tianhe only had one sword at his disposal, which meant that his spiritual spell had to travel into the body of the sword and meet the requirement for activation.","So, it was impossible to skip the learning of the spiritual spell.","At this moment, Kui Zhao vanished while a yellow talisman paper floated down from the air.","“Oh! This is miraculous!” Elves watched the scene in amazement. They couldn’t believe that such a powerful monster actually...","“It just turned into a piece of paper?!”","“This is... um...” Merlin pointed at the talisman paper on the screen and said, “This must be a special spiritual spell scroll. Yeah, it must be!”","“Amazing!”","The players led by the elves exclaimed in surprise.","In their eyes, this world was full of natural beauty that paused their steps and also miracles they had never seen before.","For them, this was a place full of surprises.","Yes, surprises were everywhere.","Before they knew it, they merged into the game with their own understanding."]},{"number":648,"title":"Chapter 648 - Monsters at Nest Lake; the Sword Immortal Emerges!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Um... Who are the sword immortals this girl keeps talking about...”","“Are they the people who can fly on swords?”","“She seems to be looking for sword immortals...”","“She said that the true sword immortals can control swords with essence and travel 1,000 kilometers in one breath! They sound powerful...”","“I would like to see such a sword immortal too...” Sala said excitedly, “It would feel great to fly while standing on a sword!”","“It seems that Yun Tianhe’s parents are... sword immortals?”","“Ya-! Then, will Yun Tianhe become a sword immortal too?!”","While playing the game, the elves talked animatedly with the knights and mercenaries.","Of course, some people were not interested in this idea. For example, Commander Elven said, “Our golden griffins are our life-long battle companions. Flying on swords sounds cool, but the honor of knights doesn’t allow us to abandon our battle companions. I think we must check out something else.”","“Haha! Yun Tianhe is so silly! I wonder how his father taught him...”","“‘I’d rather learn some self-defense sword skills to kill wild boars...’ Hehe, he’s funny.”","Remembering how Yun Tianhe mistook Han Lingsha as a demon boar, Elina became amused as well. “Haha! I think this guy has dealt with demon boars all his life. He knows nothing but wild boars or demon boars.”","“This Lingsha keeps talking about looking for treasures and legends. Is she a treasure hunter?!” some elves asked curiously.","“It’s likely...”","“Hahaha! I like this kid (Yun Tianhe).” Harrison laughed as well, “He is not stupid but very honest. After all, he had to deal with wild beasts to survive from a very young age.”","The story seemed to drive some of the worries from his mind.","The enemies that the assassins would face were too powerful. Without thinking, they were certain that a big trap would wait for them when they go to try to rescue their old peers.","Only in such moments could they alleviate a portion of the mountain-like pressure that they were feeling.","“Let’s watch some more before we go and train in the virtual reality mode.”","“Wow... I never knew that a tomb chamber could be so beautiful...” The tomb chamber in the Rock Creek Cave was covered in thick ebony ice, and the sparkling lights inside the tomb chamber flew over and gathered around the blazing Wangshu Sword in Yun Tianhe’s hand.","“So beautiful...!” To see the beautiful tomb chamber, the elves had hurried into this place too.","Obviously, nothing could stop the steps of the fans of natural beauty.","Yun Tianhe waved his hand casually.","Wherever the sword energy went, the ebony ice and walls in the tomb chamber were all cut into two.","Then, the earth-shaking booming noises sounded.","“Ahhh-! The tomb is collapsing! Run! Run!” The elves ran faster than bunnies.","...","For the players in the old shops, the world of the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 was also a new backdrop. They could only find a few traces about such factions in a few scrolls in the Shu Mountain Faction.","In the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 1 era, the fall of the Qionghua Faction was an unexplainable ancient mystery.","Now, they were trying to find the answer to the mystery by tracing the footsteps of the people who were ancient even for the characters in the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 1.","[How come I feel like this story so far has nothing to do with the Qionghua Faction...?]","[Maybe Yun Tianhe’s parents are related to the Qionghua Faction...?]","In Su Tianji’s livestreaming room, all kinds of questions flooded her screen.","“Ugh...?” Su Tianji chose an option and said, “Do you see that? I can choose to control Han Lingsha!”","In the game, if the players weren’t in the important parts involving crucial events and the learning of dharma spells, they could change some of the later plot through their different actions.","If the players wanted to get the perfect ending, they could do it by looking at Han Lingsha’s actions from the perspective of Yun Tianhe. Likewise, they could choose to play as Han Lingsha and see how Yun Tianhe made his decisions.","Of course, since the players would have the memories, habits, and intuitions of these characters in their mind, they could feel what they should do next.","“I feel like I must go to a place named... Nest Lake.” While controlling Han Lingsha, Su Tianji explained, “In the Legend of Sword and Fairy game series, there are always wild animals and monsters in the wildness. I have a feeling that we can’t reach it before night. Will we encounter any dangers...”","Bullet comments shot up on the screen.","Song Qingfeng said, [It’s easy when you encounter danger. Just use the sword control technique.]","Lin Shao chimed in, [She doesn’t need the sword control technique. With a shot of the Su Tianji Cannon, she can destroy the whole lake.]","The Cloud Ocean Faction Master Ye Songtao commented, [She can swim in the lake by jumping with the leap of faith. She’ll be fine even if she lands on her face.]","“Oh! You guys!” Su Tianji had the urge to jump up and beat them.","“I remember every one of you who badmouthed me.”","“Humph!” In the game, Han Lingsha gritted her teeth under Su Tianji’s control. “Don’t let me catch you guys.","Don’t run after you get offline. These people are infuriating! If I knew a day like this would happen, I wouldn’t have livestreamed Assassin’s Creed that day!","It was night in the game.","The reeds swayed around in the lake. Putting up a bonfire and sleeping on the bank of the river in the high reeds under the moon was quite an enjoyable experience.","In the new shop, the scenery-loving elves stood by the lake and watched as the sun set in the west across the lake and moon rose high into the sky from the east.","Of course, if Yun Tianhe wasn’t starving and didn’t try to draw out male boars by copying the honks of a female boar, the players could continue enjoying the tranquil beauty.","“Oh! I didn’t know that hunting can be done this way!” The elves looked interested. After all, they had grown up in the forest, and hunting was their strong suit.","While considering trying this trick when they returned, the elves stared at the reeds intently.","“No! Intense murderous spirit!” The elves had acute senses, and so did Yun Tianhe who had grown up in the mountains; his senses were even sharper.","In a flash, Yun Tianhe rolled to one side.","A black shadow lunged out from the deep reeds. It was so swift that it brought sharp winds with it.","“Monsters!” Han Lingsha yelled in alarm.","Then, the players saw that the attackers were tigers standing on hind legs.","“Lightning Spell!” Helen had also come to this place. Bright blue lightning bolts erupted from her sword.","“Fly Feather Arrow!” Almost instantly, Elf Captain Lance controlled Yun Tianhe to dodge the attack and then pull the bow to the fullest.","Fly Feather Arrow was an archery skill that Yun Tianhe created. With his poor talent and more than a decade of hunting experience in the mountains, Yun Tianhe obviously was very skillful in archery instead of cultivation.","Likewise, these elves were also skillful archers. Elf Captain Lance had even added some of the Elf Clan’s excellent archery skills into his shooting.","Wangshu Sword shot out like a rainbow.","Swoosh!","The monster moved like a flash of lightning.","“Didn’t hit the vital point?!” Lance was startled. “These monsters are powerful!”","Fortunately, Wangshu could fly back by itself.","After catching Wangshu, Elf Captain Lance placed the sword on the bow again, feeling as if he were hunting magic beasts in the forest. “Interesting.”","On the other side, Helen and other knights dashed toward the demon beasts with the sword in hand.","Sword energies flew on the screen.","“We should be fine as long as we kill all these demon beasts?” Su Tianji also had Wangshu in her hand. Obviously, she had switched back from Han Lingsha to Yun Tianhe. “It was an accident in Assassin’s Creed, okay? Now, I’ll show you my real skill!”","With a strong gust, a monster lunged at her with a roar.","Su Tianji lifted her sword and charged.","Ear-piercing grinding noises sounded when the sword connected with the monsters’ claws. The sharp claws were swept to one side by the blade, and then a streak of blood gushed out.","A deep bloody wound appeared in the neck of one monster.","“How about this counterattack?” Su Tianji said proudly, “Who dares to call me an idle streamer?!”","“Awesome!”","“This is interesting.”","“Not as good as Senior Nalan.”","“It’s good; it is good enough. After all, Senior is a professional at using swords. No one is his match.”","Soon, she killed the second monster.","Praises instantly flooded the screen.","“Hahahaha!” Su Tianji was smug when she looked at the couple of monsters lying dead on the ground. “I can deal with 40 of such minor monsters.”","“Roar!”","Roars sounded while about 40 demon beasts charged out from the reeds.","Su Tianji gaped at the scene in a daze. “!!??”","F**k! Don’t do this to me! I’m doing a livestream!","[I want to watch how Elder Su deals with about 40 monsters alone!]","[Elder Su’s sword skills are unrivalled!]","[Elder Su: I can deal with 40 of such minor monsters.]","“!!!” Su Tianji almost jumped up from her seat.","Damn it! Can I livestream properly?!","In fact, many other players had also come to this part.","Han Lingsha had been wounded while they escaped. Yun Tianhe guarded her and didn’t have any intention to flee by himself. It seemed like they were doomed.","“My goodness...”","“What can they do now?!”","“How come there are so many monsters...”","Merlin slapped his hand on his thigh and said, “I don’t believe that they can escape this time!”","Suddenly, sword energies flashed in the sky like shooting stars.","“Look! What are those?!”","Forming a prison with sword array, many flight swords with blazing white spiritual light turned into a sword array in the sky and surrounded the demon beasts!","“Sword immortals?!” Sala and other elves instantly exclaimed."]},{"number":649,"title":"Chapter 649 - Murong Ziying","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","At this time in the new shop, the elves and some knights, mages, and assassins had come to this part of the game. A few knights of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion and Elder Sewell controlled Yun Tianhe or Han Lingsha, and they stood under the night sky.","Many people stood behind them and watched them play.","At this moment, the players looked up and saw dozens of monsters flying into the high sky while roaring.","The sword energies full of spiritual essence looked extremely bright in the pitch-black sky. More than 50 sword energies danced and surrounded the demon beasts.","The sword energies rotated and then shot across the sky like beautiful shooting stars. The demon beasts howled while the bright white sword energies pierced through their chests.","At this moment, another group of sword energies gathered and merged into a huge dazzling sword. Its radiance blinded people who looked at it directly.","Subconsciously, the players covered their eyes with their hands. Meanwhile, the huge sword crashed down like a meteorite, exploding with an overwhelming sword spirit which swallowed all the monsters in the blink of an eye!","When the light dimmed, the audience saw many monsters falling from the sky, either pierced through by sword energies or shattered by the huge sword energy. None of them survived!","At this moment, dozens of sword energies drew beautiful and elegant arcs in the sky like feathers or flowers, coming together to the center.","A figure wearing blue and white clothes floated down from the sky like a feather, lightly landing on a flying sword that was emitting a bright light.","The other dozens of sword energies danced and flew back into the blue long case behind him.","This person waved his sleeve, and nectar fell onto Yun Tianhe and Han Lingsha, healing their wounds at a visible speed.","Then, this person floated away.","“Is he a sword immortal...” All the players in the game gazed at the sky in a daze.","“This...” Commander Elven couldn’t find words to describe his feeling.","“Ethereal!” Helen looked at the illiterate commander in disdain.","“Right! Right! Right!” Commander Elven said, “He reminds me of those existences in the ancient legends and mythologies.”","“So powerful...”","Not only the knights and mercenaries, but the elves were staring at the scene in a daze as well.","“Is he a human?” Sala glanced at Commander Elven and Big Sword Crete and then at the figure on the screen.","How come I feel like humans and these humans are two different species? Is there a humanoid race named ‘sword immortals’.","Otherwise, which humans can act so elegantly and ethereally?!","Although they had seen people flying on swords in the previous war, those people were copy cats and were not nearly as graceful as this figure who mastered the authentic skill.","“They say that all the cultivators can do this...”","“Oh! Lingsha said that they will find sword immortals in Chen State. Does it mean that we can learn this while playing as Yun Tianhe?!”","If we master this skill, we can also fly around standing on swords in the game?!","Seeing such an elegant and ethereal skill, the elves were eager to try it.","“Can we do this too...? I want to try flying on swords!” Elf Girl Sala had stars in her eyes and couldn’t wait to try it.","“I’ll try it too!” After turning his dazed gaze from the screen, Merlin snapped back to reality and hurried back to his seat.","“They seem to say that... the pattern on the tombstone of Yun Tianhe’s parents looks the same as the pattern on the clothes of those sword immortals,” Helen said while she watched the story. “I got it! The following story will tell us how he finds out the things about his parents while he learns the sword control technique from these sword immortals! We’ll surely get the chance to watch how that miraculous spiritual spell is used.”","On Helen’s screen, Han Lingsha was considering how they would learn the sword control technique.","“If your parents had lived in the mountains as hermits for many years, they wouldn’t have known these people. But they might be related to this cultivation faction in some ways.” On the screen, Han Lingsha murmured to herself, “It seems like I was right. This savage’s father must have been a sword immortal. Wonderful!”","“Faction? What’s that?” Yun Tianhe looked at Han Lingsha in bafflement.","Helen was also curious, and she wondered, “Yeah... What is a faction?”","In frustration, Han Lingsha explained, “I can’t bear you... In simple terms, a faction is a group of people who gather together and cultivate.”","“So that is what it is...?” Helen understood the situation. “A faction is like a school of thought and a society in our world?”","In fact, these new players were as ignorant about this world outside the mountain as Yun Tianhe who was a young man born and raised in the mountains. With Yun Tianhe, they started to understand this world in the game step by step.","Yun Tianhe would ask Han Lingsha some basic questions that almost everyone should know. For the players in the old shop, they only felt indulgent for his ignorance of the world and even found him cute. But the elves and knights were different.","Like Yun Tianhe, they didn’t know the answers to these basic questions either.","They traveled from the Green Bird Peak to the Peace Village at the foot of the mountain, and then from Peace Village to Nest Lake to Liu Mansion in Shouyang City...","After entering the city, Han Lingsha said, “Let’s go and find something to eat in a kezhan.”","Yun Tianhe replied, “Kezhan? What’s that?”","Han Lingsha said, “Kezhan is a place for people to rest.”","“Oh... It’s an inn.” The players understood immediately.","They stood before a wanted notice.","The knights and elves controlled Yun Tianhe and walked to the poster. “Ugh? Is this Lingsha? The picture of her looks very life-like...”","Some constables walked over and asked, “Young Man, have you seen the girl in the picture?”","The knights and elves controlled Yun Tianhe and replied, “Oh! I have. She just entered the kezhan!”","They felt happy to have the chance to use this word ‘kezhan’ so soon.","Walking out of the kezhan, Han Lingsha saw this scene and was at a loss for words. “...!!”","-Inside the Liu Mansion –","Liu Shifeng, the adoptive father of Liu Mengli, said, “Come on in, Nephew. Come in...”","The knights and elves controlled Yun Tianhe and replied, “Did you call me nephew?”","Liu Shifeng said, “Hahaha! Of course. If you want, you can call me Uncle Liu.”","The knights and elves controlled Yun Tianhe and replied, “Okay. Uncle Liu.”","“...”"]},{"number":650,"title":"Chapter 650 - Execution!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Mr. Fang’s face twitched as he watched from behind. “...”","“Any problem with that?” While playing the game, Helen asked curiously, “Did I do anything wrong?”","Following Yun Tianhe’s footsteps, the players began to understand the world from the basics and learned some vague ideas about the things in the world just like the main character.","“Oh... eight hours already passed?” Sala stretched her back in comfort. Meanwhile, many others had also finished their eight hours of playtime today. They sat down on the couches in the lounge area with Sprite or red tea in their hands. Some took the opportunity to buy a mug of Cappuccino or a bag of potato chips.","A large group of players could be seen in the lounge area.","“Ugh? No...” At this moment, Helen exclaimed, “Didn’t we agreed to try this new game after breakfast and then go back for training?!”","“Um...” one of the golden griffin knights said to one of his peers with a dark expression, “I told you to remind me. Why didn’t you remind me?”","“Ugh...” The other knight looked to the other side and asked, “Didn’t I tell you to remind me?!”","“...”","“Anyway, we trained in the cultivation mystical realm! It counts as training.” Commander Elven found an excuse for themselves.","“Ahahaha! Right! I feel like my sword skills have improved!” The knights immediately said while laughing.","“Sir... Sir!” Mr. Fang was still playing the game, but he was dragged over by Elf Girl Sala to the lounge area.","“Can you tell us about it?” Elf Girl Sala patted the seat beside her on the couch while asking Mr. Fang to sit down.","Sala sat with Elder Sewell next to Mr. Fang, and she said, “I still feel like there’re many things that I don’t understand...”","“So do we...” Commander Elven said, “We indeed learned many things, but we got more questions in the process...”","“Hehehe... I’ll sit down here.” Merlin had realized that this mystical realm was quite unusual. Hearing the people talking about it, he immediately joined in.","The players asked many questions about the basics and some questions concerning the complex workings of this world.","“How about this?” Mr. Fang said, “I’ll write a knowledge post and explain all the things that you don’t understand. If you have any more questions, I’ll add them in the post later.”","Although an internet café owner wasn’t a teacher, it was clearly Mr. Fang’s job right now.","“Awesome!” The players’ eyes lit up. In the game, Yun Tianhe could bring his questions to Han Lingsha. If the players had more questions, they would find answers in Mr. Fang’s knowledge post. Everything seemed complete.","“Sir, will Yun Tianhe and Han Lingsha find the sword immortals and learn the sword control technique?”","“What kind of people do you think Yun Tianhe’s parents are?”","“Yun Tianhe’s Wangshu Sword is a powerful alchemy item, right?”","“Sir... Do you think...”","It was balmy in the afternoon. Without blazing sunshine or gloomy rain, it was a perfect time for a chat over tea.","These people talked among themselves in the lounge area with red iced tea or Cappuccino in hands. Right now, the elves, mercenaries, knights, and even assassins had only one identity – fans of the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4.","“I can’t wait to see their alchemy techniques,” Great Mage Merlin said.","“I think the archery and the sword control technique are more interesting. Don’t you think so, Sir?” Elf Captain Lance stuffed a potato chip into his mouth, obviously in a good mood.","“I think this kid Yun Tianhe is interesting,” Assassin Harrison commented in excitement behind them, “Also, that sword immortal looked so dashing. I wonder if we’ll see him again.”","“I hope so!” Joseph, Ron, and other young people said hopefully.","“...”","Before they knew it, it was late in the night.","While bugs occasionally chirped from the bushes around the flowerbed, Canglan City was as quiet as usual. Moonlight spread over the street before the shop like a silverish-white carpet.","The last few players reluctantly walked out of the shop in groups of two or three, savoring the progress that they had made today.","...","However, nothing is constant in the world. Every person had their own path. Despite their reluctance, some people had to leave to do certain things.","Inside the godly palace of Grey Eagle City.","It was late, but lights were still burning brightly inside the palace.","“I think they’re scared!”","In the palace, Luther listened to the report from the knight standing before him while sneering. “As I expected, the real aristocrats in Canglan City regard the ridiculous ‘assassin mystical realm’ with contempt, which is why they began to advertise their ‘East Continent Mystical Realm’.”","“However... the Lava Workshop is useless!” The knight captain said with a snort, “Their so-called interception plan had no effect! That person seems to have a powerful background; he is not someone broken. If we can’t destroy his business, I think we’ll have a problem, at least here in the Morning Light Empire.”","“Don’t worry.” Luther poured himself a glass of wine and said calmly, “Let this guy live a few more days. Our priority right now is to deal with these assassins.”","His expression turned cold as he said, “These lowly rats really think that we can do nothing to them? This time, I’ll show them that the reason that we haven’t destroyed them is that we don’t think garbage deserve our efforts!”","At this moment, noises came from outside the palace when several assassins were dragged over.","“These guys are well known among those bugs.” Luther gave a signal to the knight captain with his eyes, and the latter drew out his huge sword from his back and viciously smashed it onto one assassin’s hand.","With a soul-wrenching scream, the bones in the slim and nimble hand were instantly shattered and made a series of cracking noises.","“Okay! It’s time to wake up! Damn rat!” Luther said coldly, “Get the scaffolds ready. We’ve released the news long ago, and I don’t think they will sit back and watch.”","“Yes!” The knight captain immediately put the assassins into prisoner transport vehicles and brought them to the execution grounds."]},{"number":651,"title":"Chapter 651 - Rise! Assassins!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Maybe everyone in the world thinks that the Underground Council is the most elite assassin group in the whole world,” Luther sneered while lounging on a wide luxurious chair. It was a piece of cake for them to deal with a group of assassins whom were even looked down upon by ordinary people. “They will never know why their assassination attempts are just jokes to us.”","Luther glanced at the knight captain beside him and asked, “Do you want to know why?”","The knight captain said with a bow, “I don’t think I deserve to know...”","“It doesn’t matter if you know. In fact, the most ancient assassin group belongs to our godly palace,” Luther said proudly, “This is the most secretive team in our godly palace. Now that these assassins angered St. Dulan and St. Heinz, the lowly ants of the Underground Council will see what true assassins look like!”","“What Assassin Pioneer – Altair? What Eagle of Florence – Ezio?” Luther said, “They are all fledgling juniors before our assassins!”","“I think we’ll have a good show to watch!” The knight captain said with a laughter.","...","In a small, insignificant inn in Canglan City, some figures whispered about something as if they were hiding in the shadows.","“Oh! It’s truly a great story! I can feel it even though I only watched a part of it.”","“Watch it while you can. After all, people like us never know which comes first, tomorrow’s sun or our deaths. Don’t think too much of it.”","“If I can come back alive, I must try that sword control technique.”","“Haha! Maybe.” Harrison carefully packed his stuff, including the newly-made throwing knife and hidden blade. With a turn of his wrist, he shot out a chilly light into the dark night. “If I die in that damn place, remember to tell me the ending of the story by burning a paper copy of it at my tomb, Buddy.”","“I’d like that too!” another assassin said with a chuckle.","In her room, Elina swiftly changed into black assassin’s clothes which were made after the style of the Brotherhood uniform. After putting on the black robe, body-fitting pants, and leggings, she lightly pulled up her hood, revealing only the lower half of her exquisite face.","This was a battle that only belonged to assassins. It was hidden in the darkest shadows of the world, with few people knowing its existence.","It was a shadow under the sunshine.","The night in Canglan City was always quiet. Elegant aristocrats didn’t have the habit of going out during the night. As for the civilians, they thought that the quiet night was the best time for cultivation, and they didn’t want to waste it.","On White Pigeon Square, even the pigeons had left and gone home. The quiet square seemed to be telling a story of its prosperity, and it reminded the assassins of the cheers and exclamations that they had heard during the busy hours.","Harrison entered the pitch-black back alley again. It seemed like the shadows of two assassins remained here, and they were hopeful toward the future.","Standing in the back alley all by himself, Harrison brought his hands together before his chest and prayed silently, “Oh! Brother! I know this is a trap set up by those people, but I just can’t stop myself from going into it.”","“Do you know that I’ve finally understood the true meaning of being an assassin. If you want, I’ll tell you all about it...” He murmured, “I don’t know if you’re still alive. If you are, please hold on and wait for me...”","At this moment, the square became the assassins’ world.","One after another, assassins wearing white or black robes with pointy hoods came and gathered here.","Harrison also walked out of the alley and came to the square.","“Brothers!”","“Sisters!”","Elina glanced around the crowd, knowing that she must unite these assassins together for the upcoming battle.","“Fight together with me! Let them see what they get for messing with assassins!”","“Nothing is true; everything is permitted.” Harrison walked toward the crowd. In many people’s eyes, he was an elite assassin, but he was not confident due to his lowly background and poor talent. However, when he walked among his peers, he felt different. “Everyone is equal before the hidden blades!”","“It’s time! If we work together, we’re the Brotherhood!”","“Maybe we will create a miracle, something impossible that will go down in history!”","“Victory belongs to the Brotherhood!”","“Victory belongs to the Brotherhood!”","Vows echoed on the quiet White Pigeon Square.","“All members of the Brotherhood, get ready and attack!”","A clear eagle shriek resonated in the sky in the dawn, declaring the beginning of the battle.","“Mom, what’s that?” Woken up by something, Joseph rubbed his eyes and opened the window. Then he shouted in astonishment, “Eagles! So many eagles! They are flying to Grey Eagle City!”","...","“You know what to do, right?” A beam of sunlight appeared in the eastern sky.","At this moment, Luther was having morning tea in his courtyard.","“Mr. Luther.” An old man wearing a priest’s robe said respectfully, “We’ve bribed the Castellan of Grey Eagle. That man is only a despicable person who craves for riches. Today, this city will activate the highest-level anti-air magic array, under which even mages’ spell for increasing their leaping abilities, Nimble Spirit of Cat, will be turned ineffective. They can only enter through the main gate which is heavily guarded.”","Dressed in a luxurious robe, Luther looked as if he was going to host a great ceremony at this moment. “The magic traps are set up?”","“Yes sir. We set up the highest-level magic traps that even the mages’ spell, Spiritual Detection, can’t discover.”","“We even set up the anti-mage array,” the red-robed senior priest said, “After its activation, the assassins can’t use stealth spells anymore!”","“The most important thing is that all the warriors and mages will find their strength suppressed to the lowest point. Only godly spells can be perfectly used in this place.”","“The moment they show their faces, they will die!”","...","Meanwhile, several assassins in white cloaks were standing on the high walls to the east of Grey Eagle City with the golden morning sunlight shining on their backs.","They looked down on the many houses that had white walls and red tiles and the bustling crowds.","Many soldiers and godly palace knights were patrolling the streets.","The whole city was engulfed in a mysterious great magic power.","Harrison felt that he couldn’t activate any qi or essence, which was the same as he had felt in the last assassination attempt.","However, he didn’t panic this time at all.","Nothing is true; everything is permitted.","These words resonated in his mind.","“We must understand that we’re executioners of our behaviors, and we must bear the consequences regardless if they are glorious or tragedies.”","The words that he had once heard came back to him with clarity.","“These are the tenets left by our ancestors, and they are still valid.”","“First, stay your blade from the flesh of an innocent.","“Second, hide in plain sight.”","“Third, never compromise the Brotherhood.”","“Take these as your creed. Follow them and surpass them. If you break them, you must bear the consequences.”","“Rise! Assassins!”","At this moment, no fear, hesitation, or confusion could be seen in these assassins’ eyes.","They looked firm and determined. They were assassins and proud of that!"]},{"number":652,"title":"Chapter 652 - Everything Is Ready","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","In the language spoken on the Nora Continent, ‘Stan’ had the meaning of flying knights, and the Stan Kingdom could also be called the Nation of Knights.","On this continent, only the truly honorable warriors could have their own mounts.","Powerful mounts would increase the warrior’s combat strength by many folds. Also, the mounts that could fly would give a great boost to the warriors who were lower than level 7 and hadn’t mastered the ability to fly. It meant that these warriors could battle in the sky, which was a critical ability.","Therefore, flying knights, also known as Sky Knights, became another word for nobleness and prestige.","It was why this Nation of Knights was the dream place for warriors.","However, in the luxurious royal palace, the king of the nation who should be enjoying the highest position and the greatest luxuries was now anxiously waiting for something.","He seemed to be waiting for some news which had not arrived yet.","Suddenly, rapid footsteps came from outside the palace.","The old king looked up with panic and fear on his face.","Two rows of people walked in. The people on the left row all wore red robes while those on the right were dressed in radiant light armor. They followed a silver-haired young man dressed in a beautiful white robe that was embroidered with gold threads.","“I think you don’t have to wait anymore, Your Majesty.” The young man flicked imaginary dust from his snow-white robe and remained silent, but the priest beside him spoke and seemed to be passing the message for him.","“Why?” The red-robed priest looked regretful and said, “Why would someone as lofty as Your Majesty betray the glory of God?”","“Why are you here...?” The old king looked horrified.","“In the whole nation, Your Majesty probably is the only person who doesn’t know that the assassins who dared to assassinate Mr. Luther have been captured. They exposed everything under torture. Great Mage Merlin received heavy blows from Mr. Luther for working with assassins and committing treason, and it’s only a matter of time before we capture him,” one knight said with a sneer.","“The mortals should never try to test God’s power; it will only lead to your destruction.” The silver-haired man finally opened his mouth; he sounded as aloof as a lofty god.","...","At this moment, Mr. Fang was sitting before his computer and writing explanations for different terminologies.","[Cultivator: ...] Mr. Fang typed the definitions word by word, trying to include all the detailed information that he knew.","[The difference between artifact-making and alchemy: ...]","[Flying on swords: ...]","[The dragons in the world of the Legend of the Sword and Fairy: ...]","“Sir!” Someone called Mr. Fang, but the latter was so engrossed in his work that he didn’t notice it.","“What else...” Mr. Fang scratched his head, finding that his job as the shop owner was even more demanding than before. After all, his work should only be keeping an eye on the shop, right?","“Alas...” He regretted his offer of writing the knowledge post.","Of course, he knew that this work was necessary to promote communication between the new shop and the old shops.","...","Clearly, Mr. Fang didn’t notice the hustle and bustle outside the shop.","The public execution of the assassins in Grey Eagle City drew many people’s attention. Therefore, people gathered to watch around the execution ground.","Of course, the public execution wasn’t an order from the higher-ups. However, Luther thought the godly palace needed to repair its image and reputation among the nations.","He found it necessary. After all, the scandal caused by the war had almost passed, and no one dared to mention it anymore. Therefore, it seemed like the right time was now.","By executing some notorious people, they would strike fear and respect into people from all nations. The best candidates for the execution were naturally the assassins who had been audacious enough to enter the godly palaces and try to assassinate the priests.","Also, the execution would shock the assassins who disturbed his big plans.","They were only weak and lowly assassins. Luther had dealt with these stinky and detestable rats for many years and didn’t think that it was a daunting job.","He would make these assassins regret what they had done!","He was well-prepared for this public execution.","Other than the anti-air magic array, anti-mage array, and magic traps, they had another trump card.","The most secretive knight legion in the Judgment Godly Palace was classified as a ‘knight order’ but was actually the most ancient assassin group in this world!","Luther believed that if these damn lowly bugs saw these ancient assassins, their expressions would be fantastic to see.","By now, all the captured assassins had been brought to the execution platform.","“It’s you...! Mr. Luther.” Among the assassins, a middle-aged man covered in wounds looked up and smiled.","“You know me?” Luther said arrogantly.","“Of course. I remember how you yelled like a moron about those so-called barbaric natives before turning off the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection.”","Luther’s face froze.","“Hahahaha!” The assassin laughed wildly. “You guys called them ‘barbaric natives’ and invaded them with lofty excuses, but you were beaten senseless by these ‘barbaric natives’. What are you? I watched you at White Pigeon Square. You are shameless invaders! You’re dog sh*t!”","“Shut him up!” A staff hit this assassin’s face viciously, silencing him instantly. After a long while, he spat out a few bloody teeth.","With half of his face numb, this assassin still laughed and yelled, “Long live the Sunrise Empire! One day, all your despicable schemes will be exposed to everyone in the world!”","“Plug his mouth!” Luther yelled furiously.","Soon, a filthy rag was stuffed into his mouth with vicious force.","“Good!” Above the execution platform were the seats for the aristocrats of Grey Eagle City.","Luther sat in the most prominent seat in the center.","– Meanwhile, in the distant Stan Kingdom, the Nation of Knights –","Wearing prisoner uniforms and covered in wounds, many assassins were brought out onto the meadow inside the prison. Before them, a Spiritual Spell Visual Projection was taking shape.","Among them were two white-haired old men who were locked by strange black chains. They were core figures in the Elder Group of the Underground Council.","They were the assassins who had broken the godly spells and almost killed those lofty priests.","“Watch how your stupid peers die! Damn bugs!” a guard cussed viciously."]},{"number":653,"title":"Chapter 653 - Assassination","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“I think they can’t make it here to reach us.” Beside Luther, the red-robed senior priest chuckled and said, “If they dare to come here, they will end up in defeat just like before.”","“Yes. With the anti-air magic array here, they probably can’t even enter the city!” The red-robed senior priest said while laughing, “Even if they can enter by climbing the walls, which is the stupidest way they can use, they can’t get down. Otherwise, those morons will break their legs if they jumped down and can only wait to be captured!”","On the city walls in the northwest of the city, many cold corpses of patrol guards were laying on the ground. Then, several white-robed figures spread their arms and leaped down from the wall!","...","“Right. The magic arrays will allow even the ordinary soldiers to kill them with ease!” The red-robed senior priest said with confidence, “The moment they enter the city, they will die!”","At this moment, several people wearing white robes with pointy hoods walked among the bustling crowd.","They strolled forward with the crowd calmly.","Two godly palace knights who were wearing silver armor walked in from the opposite direction.","They were chatting leisurely, not taking this mission seriously. “I think they just don’t dare to show their faces after all!”","“Hahaha! Right! Those lowly rats probably can’t enter the city!”","“Mr. Luther is waiting for the morons to come into the trap! After all, we’ll soon execute their peers!”","“Hahahaha... ugh...?” Their laughter suddenly stopped. At this moment, they looked up and saw a figure in white robes standing before them, slamming his palms onto their necks.","The people in the area suddenly ran away screaming. The two godly palace knights each had a bloody hole in their necks!","“What happened?!” People looked around in alarm. Other than the fleeing crowds, they saw nothing. Meanwhile, a white-robed figure vanished in the bustling crowd.","...","Meanwhile, on the execution platform, a large fat man wearing thick armor was talking smugly, “To avoid accidents, my Grey Eagle City is even more heavily guarded compared to the last time. Don’t worry about it, Mr. Luther.”","This man was Count Savon, the castellan of this city. “There’s a guard every three meters and a post every five meters. Even the roofs are guarded by soldiers with magic firearms. They can’t escape from our notice regardless of which direction they take.”","After the restriction arrays were activated, only a few magic items could be used in the city. Magic firearms were one of them.","At this moment, on the roof of a house with white walls and red tiles, a soldier with a magic firearm spotted the white-hooded assassin walking among the crowd.","While he was aiming and about to fire, he felt a chilling sensation in his chest.","He wasn’t sure when, but a silver throwing knife was now protruding from his chest.","This soldier with the magic firearm dropped to the ground in silence.","...","“If they are discovered, they won’t be able to find any place to hide,” the red-robed senior priest continued, “Because we set up magic traps in all the possible hiding places in the city.”","Meanwhile, Elina in a set of black assassin’s clothes moved swiftly on the roofs like a black eagle.","She paused occasionally to observe her surroundings. Observing from her perspective, one would see that everything had turned blurry when she paused while the magic traps were as clear as bright lightbulbs.","...","Count Savon seemed to be showing off the military power of the city. “Even if a few of them are lucky enough to come close to the execution platform...”","He glanced around the edge of the platform and said, “Everywhere is heavily guarded by my own guard teams.”","This was an open, round square surrounded by all kinds of residential houses. There were four entrances, and each one of them was guarded by many soldiers wearing heavy armor.","At this moment, a white-robed assassin slowly walked toward one entrance with the crowds.","Since such scholarly robes didn’t exist in this world, the dozens of soldiers guarding the entrance became suspicious.","The heavily-armored soldiers tightened their grip on the halberds in their hands, and their eyes emitted chilly glints as they looked through the eyeholes of their heavy helmets.","When the white-robed assassin entered the execution platform, he was surrounded by heavily armored soldiers.","Meanwhile, the assassin who were captured in the distant Stan Kingdom and other nations were watching this scene as well.","The two grey-haired elders of the Underground Council were watching the scene intently.","Then, they looked away as if they were afraid to watch it. They seemed to foresee that the assassin would end up dying in a blood puddle.","“Damn it! You will all die pathetically!” an elder of the Underground Council cussed loudly and struggled to get up, but he was knocked down by a stick.","“Be quiet! Old Man!”","“I don’t know what good luck brought you here.” From the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection, Count Savon saw the assassin and yelled, “But your good luck will end here.”","He gestured with vicious force. “Get him!”","An eagle feather seemed to float down from the sky, and it landed on the palm of the white-robed assassin.","Before the heavy-armored soldiers could react, they stumbled back frantically. Each of them had a bloody hole in their chests!","The heavily-armored soldiers who had surrounded this assassin dropped to the ground one after another. One of them struggled forward but was pushed onto the ground by the assassin with a slight nudge, losing all senses of life.","“What’s happening?!” Count Savon stood up from his seat in horror.","He looked up and saw Elina revealing herself on the roof. As the smoke of the magic firearm rose, her fiery-red hair fluttered in the wind beneath the black hood of her black assassin’s robe. “Thank you for your firearms.”","Meanwhile, several assassins appeared from the gun-smoke like ghosts.","They wore elegant robes that looked those of scholars, and the pointy hoods looked like eagle beaks.","With the hems of the robes fluttering in the wind, the proud figures looked down at the crowds with a unique lofty presence.","“Are they... assassins?!” The aristocrats sitting above the scaffold platform and the captured assassins who were watching the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection all looked at the scene in a daze."]},{"number":654,"title":"Chapter 654 - You Might Be the Worst Group of Gamers That I Tutored!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Don’t come near! Or these assassins are dead!” Count Savon roared in fury and horror while directing the executioners, “Kill them!”","Soon, the executioners put ropes around the assassins’ necks. The moment the floor was lowered, the assassins would be hung to death!","Suddenly, many assassins leaped down from the roofs of the surrounding houses like water drops in a waterfall. While landing with neat and clean movements, they released their hidden blades, instantly killing one executioner each.","“Godly palace knights! Kill them!” Beside Luther, the red-robed senior priest roared in shock and anger. Instantly, large groups of soldiers and heavily armed godly palace knights swarmed up.","Meanwhile, the red-robed senior priest lifted his magic staff and began to chant. Soon, his magic staff released a golden light beam which landed on the armor of these godly palace knights.","Instantly, the armor of these godly palace knights emitted faint golden lights.","It was the Holy Light Armor Spell which could harden and strengthen the knights’ armor so much that even magic firearms couldn’t pierce them, let alone the assassins who were deprived of strength.","Then, another golden light beam fell.","Instantly, the knights found that their strengths grew greatly. They slashed out their huge swords and created a series of air-piercing noises!","The red-robed senior priest looked vicious. “Despite your great combat experience, you can’t kill more than seven fully-armed knights without qi or magic energy in your body. Now that I’ve empowered the knights with godly spells, I’ll see how many you can kill!”","Sure enough, an assassin unsheathed his hidden blade, and it made a crisp noise when it collided with a knight’s armor; it couldn’t even leave a scratch on the knight.","“Hahahaha!” Count Savon laughed, “They are dead!”","However, in the next instant, the assassin stabbed his hidden blade into the knight’s body through a crevice in the armor. Then, blood immediately gushed out!","The godly spells had toughened the armor and increased the knights’ physical strength but hadn’t toughened their bodies.","With the blades stabbing through the crevices every time, the armor looked as fragile as paper before them. It didn’t take the assassins more effort.","Slaughter! It was a one-sided slaughter! With their current combat techniques, the assassins could easily defeat enemies who were more powerful than them!","“This...!?”","Everyone instantly stood up from their seats.","Luther’s face became livid. “Escort me back to the godly palace. Quickly!”","On the square in the prison of Stan Nation, the captured assassins who were watching the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection while sitting on the meadow were stupefied by the scene, wondering if the people they were seeing were really assassins!","“Immediately escort Mr. Luther out of here!” Count Savon roared, and his face became wicked as the fat on his face distorted. “Elites of Grey Eagle City! Kill them all!”","“For the Brotherhood!” Harrison roared and charged into the enemies with red eyes.","“For our glory!”","“Battle until death! Kill them all!”","In each second, there were soldiers of Grey Eagle City and godly palace knights dropping to the ground. Harrison had dashed to the forefront of his group, and he used counterattacks and strung together combo kills, taking out his enemies with one strike each. The skills that he had practiced endlessly in the virtual reality training sessions replayed in his mind like flashbacks.","This combat style seemed to have merged into his blood and bones.","His hands, feet, knees, and everything he got his hands on could be turned into deadly weapons; he even felt like he could find his enemies’ weakest points with his eyes closed.","Harrison picked up the middle-aged assassin who had passed out and said, “Oh! Brother! I got you!”","“We’re late; but we’ll triumph over them! Believe us!”","“Charge!!!” His hoarse roar signaled the full-force attack.","...","At this moment, Luther was hurrying toward the direction of the godly palace.","“Mr. Luther, do you have a plan?” Count Savon said in horror, “They... are these assassins devils? How can they kill so many people?!”","Luther’s face was livid. Although he hadn’t anticipated this situation, he obviously was prepared and wasn’t panicking. “Don’t worry. The battle has just begun.”","Under the protection of godly palace knights, he walked into the godly palace.","Suddenly, the glass windows of the building shattered as dozens of assassins swarmed into the godly palace like a giant flood.","Luther, Count Savon, the red-robed senior priest, and about 20 godly palace knights were surrounded in the center.","“You can’t escape, Mr. Luther.” Elina released her hidden blade. After a long while, she finally returned to this place.","But this time, she wouldn’t flee in despair. Instead, victory belonged to them!","“Don’t be happy so soon. Damn it!” Luther said in a cold voice, “If that’s all you can do, you’ll die soon!”","The moment he said it, Elina felt a chilly sensation shooting up into her head from her heart. Used to the dangers that were hiding everywhere in Assassin’s Creed, she had obtained a faint intuitive sense of danger without using qi or spiritual spells. It was this intuitive reflex that made her lower her head without thinking.","A silent black light shot past her scalp. If she was one second late, her head would have been chopped off!","“Be careful!” Elina exclaimed in alarm.","The others were alarmed but couldn’t move fast enough. Instantly, several assassins were severely wounded!","Elina didn’t even have the slightest idea where the sneak-attackers were hiding.","These new assassins wore simple black cotton robes, looking like a group of ascetics.","No one could sense any aura coming off of them, as if they were one with the void.","Instead of the huge swords that knights liked to use, they used pure-black short swords which were designed for the killing technique that they just performed. These techniques were more advanced and ancient than those used by the assassins of the Underground Council.","“Are... they assassins too?!” On the square in the prison, the two elders of the Underground Council couldn’t believe their eyes.","They had never thought that the Judgement Godly Palace was the most powerful assassin organization in the world!","In the blink of an eye, more than 20 assassins dropped to the ground, losing all combat abilities!","Only Elina remained standing in the building, and Harrison was outside helping the captured assassins escape.","Elina looked grim. Despite the anti-mage array in the city, these assassins had sneaked up to her without her noticing.","Even Luther looked respectful. He bowed and said, “Welcome, Mr. Moody.”","“You asked me to come here to deal with these wastrels? They are so weak.” With his hands clasped behind his back, the man in the black robe looked to be the leader of these new assassins, and he glanced at the other assassins with a cold expression.","In fact, Luther’s targets weren’t only the assassins who had escaped in the last failed assassination.","His targets included Altair, who was called the Assassin Pioneer, and Ezio, who was called the Eagle of Florence.","In other words, his goal was to draw out the person who created the assassin mystical realm and taught the elves assassination skills.","Of course, he wouldn’t go to that shop himself.","Drawing out his targets was the best strategy.","The red-robed senior priest said with sudden understanding, “So, Mr. Moody is our real hidden card!”","Luther said with a laugh, “You guys can’t imagine how powerful he is!”","“In my opinion, even the so-called great Pioneer Altair or Eagle of Florence Ezio can’t block one attack from Mr. Moody.”","Hearing Luther’s introduction, everyone was astonished to learn that the godly palace had such well-hidden people.","“Do you think you need to state the fact...” Moody said mildly. But before he could finish, he suddenly stopped, turning around and revealing a throwing knife had pierced into his back and through his heart.","He collapsed to the ground instantly.","Luther instantly froze.","The red-robed senior priest and Count Savon froze too.","Looking at the black-robed man lying on the ground lifelessly, everyone’s brain turned blank.","The assassins in the Stan Kingdom stopped thinking while they watched this scene.","What happened?!","The audience members looked forward and saw a white-robed assassin directly walking through the gate.","The large group of guards standing at the gate didn’t see this assassin due to their strong desire to live.","“Hurry! Turn it off!” In the prison of the Stan Kingdom, the soldiers who were guarding the assassins and watching the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection yelled wildly, “Turn the damn visual projection off!”","“...”","...","While Mr. Fang was compiling the knowledge post, he suddenly received a task.","[New Task: The Battle of Assassins","Task Content: Complete Synchronization with Altair or Ezio","Task Target: Destroy all the assassins in Grey Eagle City who are not a part of the Brotherhood","Task Reward: Activation of the third large-scale online game, connection between all private teleportation array between all shops; Host can take one person along while using the array","Note: Using Complete Synchronization with other characters will be regarded as failing this task.]","Therefore, Mr. Fang took the chance to check up on the assassins by having a look.","Seeing the scene, Mr. Fang was at a loss for words. “You might be the worst group of gamers that I’ve ever tutored.”","“Ahhyaaa...!” Elina felt like she was going crazy as she thought, Can you show some mercy in front of so many people?!","“Luther is trying to run!”","“Hurry! Deactivate all the magic arrays!” Desperate howls came from the palace. “Deactivate the magic arrays, and we might have a chance! Turn off the anti-air magic array so that we can escape! Demons! They are demons!”","“Ahhhh!” Their defense methods now became their death curse.","Meanwhile, in a dark corner under the real grand hall which worshipped the gods inside the Judgement Godly Palace, a pair of eyes suddenly opened. “I can’t believe that I lost a figure projection this way... Who was that?!”"]},{"number":655,"title":"Chapter 655 - Only Used Two Strikes?!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Who... who are you?!” The other black-robed ascetics looked grim, astonished that Mr. Moody’s figure projection doppelganger had been instantly killed!","“Who... the heck is you?!” Different from Luther and others, these black-robed ascetics were astonished but didn’t panic like Luther and the others.","After all, different from ordinary people, their training and experience had taught them to forget life and death. These assassins knew that there were many things in the world that went beyond their understanding, which was why they regarded this unexpected accident as something not surprising. With this mindset, nothing could be a surprise.","The purpose of their existence was partly to solve these unexpected problems.","Each of them could execute missions alone. In their limited lives, they had killed horrifying monsters and lofty lords with prestigious statuses. It wasn’t beyond the ability of this group to kill a saint-level master.","Different from those soldiers, their abilities went beyond the skills that they showed.","Compared to others, they had far more advanced physical conditions.","A level 9 anti-mage scroll could turn a level 9 mage into an ordinary person and could turn a level 9 Sky Knight into a mortal with some moderate combat techniques.","Reduced to this state, supreme masters would be as fragile as mortals and would die with one stab of a sword into their vital parts.","Could one use such things to assassinate people? Of course. It was why these ascetics were absolute masters in this anti-mage realm even though their cultivation strengths were not extremely high.","Casting spells on physical bodies would change people’s physical conditions and cause great danger to these people, which was why the godly spells were usually cast on armors and weapons. That was the function for the most ordinary godly spells.","Only senior priests had the right to learn these godly spells which were extremely difficult to master.","For the fully-armed soldiers, full suit of armor strengthened by godly spells were enough for them to block any attacks.","However, these ascetics couldn’t move agilely if they wore heavy armor. With the permanent magic spells or even godly spells in their bodies, they could kill level 3 and level 4 magic beasts with bare hands.","These people’s strength, speed, and reflexes far surpassed those of ordinary people.","With curses and extreme poison on their weapons, they could kill any master whose strength was suppressed by the anti-mage array.","Their overall strength far surpassed Elina and the other assassins. With the element of surprise, they had easily wounded these assassins severely.","They didn’t think that Fang Qi could deal with them all by himself.","If their blades put one scratch on Fang Qi, Fang Qi would instantly lose all of his combat abilities.","“Don’t worry!” Since each of them had the ability to handle a situation alone, there wouldn’t be the situation where they lacked central command. Soon, one of them took over the responsibility of the team leader and said, “He’s alone.”","Meanwhile, in the prison inside Stan Kingdom.","“Who? Who dared to turn off the visual projection?”","“Beat him!”","“I’ve had enough!” The assassins suddenly erupted into a rage.","With pathetic screams, the guards were instantly knocked down by the large group of assassins.","Satisfied, the assassins resumed their seats on the square and continued to watch the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection.","“Who do you think this guy is, Mr. Altair or Mr. Ezio?” an old man asked.","“I think... he should be Mr. Ezio; I heard that Assassin Ezio wears a little white cape on his shoulder,” another old man whispered.","Meanwhile, before Fang Qi, the black-robed ascetics divided into two rows calmly as if they had done this in the past while facing enemies. They knew that the person before them was a powerful opponent, but many powerful opponents had fallen under their blades.","The whole palace was full of grim murderous spirit which almost suffocated the audience who were watching this battle.","With their strength frozen, this battle would be a fight of combat techniques, combat experience, and brute killing skills.","Fast! These black-robed ascetics moved much faster than ordinary people. The audience could only see blurry shadows sweeping toward Fang Qi.","Under Complete Synchronization with his gaming character, Fang Qi slightly shifted away. Before the audience could understand what was happening, Fang Qi grabbed the wrist of the first black-robed ascetic who was holding a sword while his short saber pierced a hole in the ascetic’s back as if this person’s body were only a piece of fragile paper.","Then, the second ascetic’s short sword reached him. Fang Qi moved his body slightly and slashed open the ascetic’s wrist with his short blade at the same time. Blood sprayed everywhere from the ascetic’s severed artery.","More attacks came one after another. The black sword shadows merged and combined into a deadly net. As people who knew all about killing, their attacks were deadly and almost impossible to dodge.","However, Fang Qi seemed to know their attacks before they used them. As if he had eyes on the back of his head, Fang Qi squatted at lightning speed as a sword slashed over his back with a deadly arc.","At the same time, Fang Qi used the forward momentum and stabbed his short blade into the foot of the black-robed ascetic who charged toward him.","His attacks were graceful and smooth with a special rhythm, making it feel like no one could interrupt.","The attacks happened at lightning speed, too fast for the audience to clearly see.","The leader’s face turned cold, knowing that it would be too late if he didn’t move now!","However, at this moment, Fang Qi leaped up high like a snow-white eagle, hacking down his short blade with vicious force!","Clank!","With crisp metal-colliding noises, the new leader blocked this heavy strike and punched his left fist toward Fang Qi with vicious force.","Fang Qi blocked the fist with his palm smoothly with momentum. Before his opponent could react, his hidden blade shot forward and pierced the ascetic’s palm. Then, he pushed his hand forward, and the hidden blade went through his opponent’s chest!","“How is this... possible!” The ascetic dropped to the ground with dazed eyes filled with disbelief.","The Judgment Godly Palace had spent an exorbitant amount of money on these assassins each year, making their physical strength, combat experience, and combat skills far surpassing those of ordinary people. However, they were just killed by this man with at most two attacks?!","The money that the Judgment Godly Palace spent on them all these years had been for nothing?!","Meanwhile, Mr. Fang also looked at this ascetic in shock. He thought to himself, With the perfect T-virus created by the system, I can kill one magic beast with one punch. I even synchronized with Ezio at the peak of his life and know all his skills, but I still can’t kill this guy with one strike?! I had to use two attacks to kill him?!"]},{"number":656,"title":"Chapter 656 - The New Task for the Large-Scale Online Game —World of Warcraft","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Is this the true power of Master Ezio?” Elina and other assassins were at a loss for words. They had only experienced such smooth moves in the game. The attacks and counterattacks were all perfectly used!","It was enjoyable to watch such perfect moves.","“Is he really an assassin?!” The assassins who were watching the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection in the prison were stunned.","Honestly, if they met these black-robed ascetics, they would have been pierced instantly.","In their mind, assassins should hide in the darkness and launch deadly attacks at the very moment that they made their appearance.","But now, looking at the corpses on the ground inside and outside of the godly palace, they wondered how this assassin could be so powerful!","In their mind, assassins should kill targets with one strike from the darkness.","In fact, most of them were born with poor family backgrounds and poor talent, and they had inferior combat techniques. This was their only way to defeat an opponent.","Becoming assassins was the last choice that these people had. After all, they could do nothing but sneak attack and assassinate others. Thus, they were looked down on by people everywhere they went.","But now... they felt like they were falling in love with this brand-new profession!","Many guards had swarmed in.","Then, they saw the assassins who had knocked down the prison. These people didn’t riot nor escape. Instead, they just sat on the square and watched the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection.","“What is so enthralling?” They looked up at the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection in the center of the square.","The assassin wearing the white hooded robe stood over the bodies of the black-robed ascetics, and Luther and the senior priest were nowhere to be seen.","What happened?! How come things had changed so drastically when our heads were turned?!","At this moment, Mr. Fang finally turned to the assassins, and the latter yelled, “Awesome!”","Mr. Fang asked, “Ugh? Where are the others? Where are those priests?”","“Oh... they seemed to have fled!” Elina pointed at the gate and said.","“Why didn’t you chase them?” Mr. Fang gaped at Elina and the other assassins. “You just let them go?!”","You guys were just yelling awesome and watched? Are you waiting for me to chase? I’ve finished my task and won’t do anything else!","“Ah...?” Elina seemed to have finally understood the situation and yelled in alarm, “Hurry... Go after them!”","“???” Mr. Fang froze for a second and wondered, How come I have such noob teammates like you?","Elina was sulky, thinking, We were... too engrossed in watching the battle! It’s not my fault!","“Hurry! Go after them!” Elina yelled immediately.","“Wait... Wait...” The severely wounded assassins of the Brotherhood struggled up and said, “First...”","Elina looked at Mr. Fang and then at the assassins on the ground.","“Help your teammates before chasing the enemies!” Mr. Fang slapped his hand onto his forehead. “Do you guys know how to play as a team?”","“Mr. Luther and the others fled?!” At this moment, the godly palace guards in Stan Nation saw this scene on the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection and yelled in alarm, “Hurry! Report to Mr. Cesare! Big trouble might be coming!”","“How about these assassins...”","“Leave some soldiers here to guard them!”","...","– Inside Grey Eagle City –","“Senior Harrison, look at this.” A young assassin handed several parchment scrolls to Harrison.","These magic parchment scrolls could record and store lots of information for a long time, which was why they were used to store documents and important information.","“These are...” Harrison was startled. “They contain the evidence of Count Savon receiving the bribery of treasures from the Judgment Godly Palace. They record how he traded official positions for money and forced people in Grey Eagle City to have one religion! Awesome!”","Meanwhile, Elina carried the corpse of the red-robed senior priest in one hand and Count Savon in the other hand.","“Where’s Luther?” Elina asked fiercely.","“Escaped!” some assassins said, “When we arrived, he had left through a teleportation array!”","...","On the next day, a huge scandal about the Grey Eagle City of the Morning Light Empire and the Judgement Godly Palace spread all over the world. The highly anticipated public execution of assassins changed into the destruction of the godly palace in Grey Eagle City by the assassins. During the process, a red-robed senior priest died, and Ambassador Luther had gone missing.","The more astonishing news was that the Judgement Godly Palace had tried to bribe the Castellan to force the citizens to believe their god and turn the whole Grey Eagle City into a small religious nation.","Facing endless blame and questions, St. Dulan lost his usual composure and looked livid.","“We can’t rule out the possibility that these damn assassins are spreading rumors to slander us. I’m sure everyone knows what kind of people they are. Of course, if this rumor turns out to be true in this isolated place, we’ll punish the related people severely!”","Soon, St. Dulan’s words were spread all over the world through the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection.","Then, St. Dulan heaved a sigh of relief. “Fortunately, these assassins didn’t have control of the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection in different places.”","He beckoned at a knight and asked, “Did anyone escape from the Grey Eagle City?”","“Yes! Mr. Luther did!” the knight reported.","“Kill him immediately!” St. Dulan inhaled deeply and then closed his eyes.","It was easy to fool ordinary people, but there were certain people who were not so dumb. Someone must take the blame. Otherwise, the Judgement Godly Palace couldn’t spread its beliefs to other nations that didn’t currently believe in their faith.","Having failed to exploit the land of the Elf Clan, they couldn’t lose their own home base!","...","Meanwhile, the task for the new large-scale online game was activated after Mr. Fang finished everything.","[New Task: Cross-Era Masterpiece – World of Warcraft","Task Target: 1. The reputation of the new shop reaches 100,000 people; 2. Players include people from other races such as elves, orcs, and dwarves","Task Privilege: receive the original cinematic trailer, the right to design your own trailer, and the right to host small-scale events","Task Reward: Upgrade and combine the TV Series and Movie Cultivation Room and the Game Cultivation Room; ten-day access to the new cultivation room]","Mr. Fang patted his forehead. “...”","Suddenly, he felt like this task was very difficult to finish.","Reputation meant that people knew what this shop did by just hearing its name. These people didn’t have to come into the shop and play games.","But 100,000 was still a big number.","As for orcs and dwarves...","He hadn’t seen any of them after he came to Canglan City"]},{"number":657,"title":"Chapter 657 - The Elves’ First-Time Using the Sword Control Technique","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“St. Dulan, these assassins...?”","“Don’t mind them now!” St. Dulan said in a cold voice.","Their top priority was to find out the background of the assassin who killed Moody’s figure projection and those assassins who wore grand hooded-robes!","Obviously, these assassins were totally different from the assassins they had captured and prisoned!","According to the information that they had received from Grey Eagle City, these assassins could move freely in the anti-air arrays. Things like magic traps, scouts, and guards were ineffective against them. They even killed soldiers who were strengthened by godly spells. How could assassins become so powerful?!","“The other thing...” St. Dulan said, “Don’t set up anti-mage realms again.”","They could still use anti-air magic arrays and magic traps. After all, there weren’t only those assassins who wore white hooded robes; there was also the Underground Council.","However, if they set up the anti-mage realm, they wouldn’t be able to escape if they encountered the white-robed assassins.","“Inform Cesare that these assassins will probably go and break free the captured assassins imprisoned in Stan Nation. He must be on guard!”","“Besides... send more forces to him from the Godly Palace!”","Without a better solution, Dulan had no choice but to add more manpower.","...","– Meanwhile, in the new shop of Origins Internet Club –","“Uh? Sir, what’s happening with you guys?” The sensitive elves such as Sala found that Mr. Fang had a friendlier relationship with Elina, Harrison, and the others.","These players were eating instant noodles with Mr. Fang while chatting and laughing.","They even treated Mr. Fang to instant noodles! How come I feel like I missed something interesting? Elf Girl Sala looked at them in suspicion.","“Um? How come you guys are sitting here together today?” Commander Elven joined them with some knights that were also holding instant noodles in their hands.","Did anything interesting happen today?","“I say... did you guys hear about the incident in Grey Eagle City?” Oblivious to what happened, Commander Elven ate instant noodles and said, “According to the rumors which spread all over the place, they tried to execute the assassins but it ended in a pathetic failure.”","“It’s said that the assassins even spread the rumors about the collusion between the Godly Palace and the count of Grey Eagle City. I wonder if it’s true...”","“I have a relative living there. The rumors are probably true!”","“The civilians in Grey Eagle City are saying that the assassins freed the city... Otherwise, no one would have found out these schemes of that count who fooled his superiors and subordinates in a long time.”","“Didn’t they say... many people died there?” Helen asked with a frown, “It’s said that Grey Eagle City was full of corpses.”","“They are all Count Savon’s personal guards as well as the knights and mages of the Judgement Godly Palace. The others didn’t get hurt,” one knight told her in a low voice.","“My goodness... when did the assassins begin doing things so cleanly and fairly?”","[First, stay your blade from the flesh of an innocent.] This was the first tenet of the Brotherhood, and the assassins all kept it in mind.","Each profession had its own code of conduct. The creed of ‘nothing is true; everything is permitted’ didn’t give them the excuse to do anything they wanted. Altair understood this creed and passed it down to other assassins, and the latter had respected and followed it.","“But... I heard that the assassins mostly wear white robes with hoods?” Merlin joined the conversation on the side.","“White robes...?” The elves exchanged a look.","“Hoods?” The knights and mercenaries looked at each other as well.","Their faces all twitched as they thought, Did a brotherhood go there to do it?! But...","“No matter who did it, I only want to say...” Commander Elven slapped his thigh and said, “Well done!”","Meanwhile, the assassins sitting near him looked at each other with a smile, hiding their identities and glories.","“Slurp! Slurp!” They even found instant noodles more delicious than ever.","...","“Today, we can play the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 again, right?” Commander Elven said while eating instant noodles.","Due to his theory of training in mystical realms, Commander Elven had decreased the time of training in the real world and set aside more time for training in the mystical realms.","Today, they would continue playing this new game!","While they played it, they would know more about this strange ‘East Continent’.","Besides, they hadn’t seen the sword control technique yet! They had been waiting!","Yesterday, the assassins had gone to rescue prisoners in the morning and returned to the shop quite late, so they didn’t know what the elves had played.","Today, they watched from behind in puzzlement.","“Who is she? She’s so beautiful!” They watched the beautiful woman beside Yun Tianhe and exclaimed.","“This is Liu Mengli, the daughter of Uncle Liu.” Obviously, the elves had toured many places and experienced many events with Liu Mengli and Han Lingsha, including the miraculous and strange Niuluo Rock, the gloomy and deep Royal Tomb of Huainan, and the sad love story of Qin Ji.","The players experienced the different hidden places and events in the world and got familiar with everyone. Everything about the game was moving.","“I’m telling you guys that this game is super fun.” While playing the game, Sala said smugly, “Yesterday, we experienced a lot of stuff, met many people, and heard many stories. Hu... I wonder how the master created this mystical realm. I feel like I’ve travelled all over the world.”","“We’re forming a group to play the game!” Helen asked, “Do you guys want to join me?”","“Can you take me?” One knight immediately lifted his hand.","“No way! Isn’t it great to play with Commander Elven!”","“How can we group with Commander Elven?” At this moment, Murong Ziying hadn’t shown up yet. The knights all looked sulky since they couldn’t play as the two female characters, Han Lingsha and Liu Mengli, and thus couldn’t play the game in a group.","“Hey! We’re friends. Can you let me join you?”","“Haha! No!” Helens said with a laugh, “No position available!”","“Puchi-!” The assassins who were watching laughed too.","“Hey! Come here!” Mercenary Crete yelled, “When Murong Ziying joins the team, two male players can play together! Do you want to join me?”","“Oh... Really? Wait for me!”","“Hurry with your game! Hurry!”","The Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 was a story about looking for immortals. The characters traveled from Green Bird Peak to Chen State and experienced many things, but their purpose didn’t change. Finally, they encountered Huai Shuo and Xuan Ji who had followed Murong Ziying in Chen State.","“When in the sky, don’t harbor any irrelevant thoughts, or you’ll fall!” On the screen, Xuan Ji said while laughing.","“Ya-!” With a scream, someone yelled, “I’m flying!”","“I’m flying while standing on the sword as well!” several knights cheered.","Although it was Huai Shuo who was commanding Yun Tianhe’s Wangshu Sword with the sword control technique.","“Is this fun?” The assassins watched them play and felt tempted.","“It’s more than fun!” Sala yelled, “It’s thrilling!”","“Ahh-! So thrilling!” The knights yelled in the shop.","“Too fast-!”","“So high-! Don’t fall!” With two people standing on a slim sword, it looked obviously more dangerous than riding on a mount. The audience exclaimed repeatedly."]},{"number":658,"title":"Chapter 658 - What Are Elves? Can We Catch Them with Poke Balls?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","The task reward of a personal teleportation array was indeed good. With this array, Mr. Fang could return to the Jiuhua City Shop, the Yuanyang City Shop, or the Half City Shop whenever he wanted.","Besides, he could travel with another person, which meant that he could bring someone here.","Who should I bring...? Mr. Fang thought about it while peeking at the messages in the group chats on his new communication jade.","At this moment, players were talking animatedly about the story of the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4 in QQ group chats. Jiang Xiaoyue jumped out with the profile photo of Liu Mengli, [Mengli is my favorite. Don’t fight with me over her! 😡]","Mr. Fang said, [Xiaoyue, do you want to come here and play?😁]","Soon, he locked his eyes on a loli and tried to capture her.","[Scummy Boss!] Jiang Xiaoyue looked at Mr. Fang who had been absent for a long time. [I don’t want to talk to you!]","“Ugh?” Mr. Fang froze.","[I support Xiaoyue! The scummy shop owner has been absent for a long time!] Dong Qingli joined the accusations.","Song Qingfeng added, [😏The scummy shop owner who has been quiet in the group finally emerged.]","Tang Yu said, [He must have been peeking at us.]","[He wants to bully Xiaoyue again!] Nalan Mingxue said, [Xiaoyue, come and play with Big Sister.]","Having been hiding in the group chat lately, Mr. Fang’s sudden emergence caused turbulent waves.","[It seems like we can go to that place now?] Demonic Woman Ning Bi joined the fun. [How is that place anyway?]","After all, they didn’t have a good impression of that place, and they thought that Mr. Fang was battling everyday.","[Right,] Jiang Xiaoyue asked curiously, [How are things going over there?]","[Sir, do you use musou in that place everyday?] Su Tianji also joined the discussion.","[Fighting for what.] Mr. Fang’s face twitched. [I live in a peaceful place. We have friendly, elegant, and peace-loving elves, assassins believing in freedom despite their newbie skills, and funny knights who leaped down buildings after playing Assassin’s Creed...]","[Elves?] Dong Qingli posted a picture of Pikachu. [Do they look like this? Do you use poke balls to capture them?]","[TL Note: In Chinese, Pokémon is translated as ‘Little Pet Elves’ in terms of literal translation, so that is why people mentioned elves.]","[We all thought that you’ve been working hard over there. However, you’ve been catching elves without us knowing?] A large group of people started to protest.","Su Tianji quickly added, [Can you catch one for me?!]","Dong Qingli said, [I want one too!]","Shen Qingqing chimed in, [🤑 Give me one!]","Mr. Fang’s face darkened. “...’","[You’re talking about Pokémon! Not elves!] Mr. Fang emphasized, [You can’t catch elves!]","He quickly killed this thought in those players’ heads before it took root.","“Do they look like this...?” Jiang Xiaoyue posted a screenshot of her playing in Dungeon Fighter Online. As a battle mage, she was a cute elf with two pointy ears.","[Ugh? Is this also an elf?] Obviously, many players knew nothing but killing monsters and making competitions. [They are just humans with pointed ears! I wondered why these people have such long and pointy ears. I never knew that they were not humans...]","Mr. Fang looked exasperated toward these people. [Can you guys be dumber?! Didn’t you read the plot at all?]","[We kill Abyss Demons everyday; why should we read the plot?] Some players who were not fans of stories declared that they were still not familiar with the plot of the game. They only knew that they were adventuring on a continent and exposing behind-the-scene schemes while they were doing so.","Nalan Mingxue concluded, [Sir, do you mean that there are cute humans with pointy ears over there?]","[Don’t they... only exist in the game...?] Su Tianji was baffled too. In the game, she also played as a female mage and had advanced to a witch who was naturally also an elf.","[Isn’t that an imaginary creature that the game created?!] The others were also baffled.","According to Mr. Fang, such creatures really exist in the world?!","Don’t lie to me!","I’ve never heard of such creatures in my whole life!","...","Meanwhile, the elves, knights, and assassins who were watching them play the game from the back also looked baffled, and they became more curious as they played. “They keep talking about demons and monsters. Some monsters are plants and animals which can turn into humans after obtaining certain levels of power?”","How could things work in this way?!","It seemed like Liu Mengli is also a demon?!","How could that be? She is a human being!","If animals can turn into humans after they obtained strength, then why can’t our griffins with high-level strength turn into humans?","On this continent, only the legendary magic beasts which had reached the saint level could speak human languages. They only heard about animals turning into humans in mythologies and legends.","The magic beasts that could speak human languages were all extremely lofty existences with great bloodline, strength, and backgrounds. No ordinary people could get in touch with them.","As for orcs, they were born that way.","As elves, they were naturally close to certain animals and plants, especially the mild-tempered, peace-loving small animals or herbivores. For example, deer and squirrels.","We deal with these animals everyday day in the forest; how come we’ve never seen one turn into a human and play with us?!","“Sir!” The elves looked disgusted. There are indeed many wonders in the world, but don’t you try to lie to us!","They immediately called the shop owner over to them.","How come the animals in your world can change into humans as if they are saint beasts?!","If that’s possible, then I would have changed all the small animals in our Silver Moon Forest into humans!","The elves couldn’t believe or understand it.","...","“Um...” Looking at the disgusted elves who thought that Mr. Fang had exaggerated things in the mystical realm, Mr. Fang looked frustrated and said, “These people don’t believe that there are elves in the world! I was trying to explain your existence to them!”","“They don’t believe our existence?!” Elf Girl Sala pointed at herself and said in a huff, “Aren’t we elves!”","“Right!” The knights around them seconded her. “If they are not elves, what are they then?”","Mr. Fang soon posted the conversation to the group chat.","Tang Yu and the others were displeased. [I’m now sitting together and playing games with a deer, and you are telling me that there are no demons in the world?! How can you explain this scene then?]","Mr. Fang glanced at his communication jade and said, [They said the same thing.]","Jiang Xiaoyue curled her lips and said, [I don’t believe it unless I see a real elf with my own eyes!]","A player with the profile photo of a big white deer also protested in the group, [I don’t believe it either!]"]},{"number":659,"title":"Chapter 659 - Dashing Sword Immortal, and Making Artifact Online","paragraphs":["Chapter 659: Dashing Sword Immortal, and Making Artifact Online","Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","At this moment, the elves also looked incredulous. “We won’t believe you unless you bring a real demon to us from your homeland, Sir.”","“No! We want to see one as cute as the one in the game!” Elf Girl Sala remembered the cute little demon that could speak the human language at Niuluo Rock.","“We also want to see one as pretty as her!” She pointed at Liu Mengli and said after a pause. “Even if you can’t find someone as pretty as her, you have to bring one on a similar level.”","Otherwise, she would say that Mr. Fang was a fraud!","Jiang Xiaoyue also said, [Unless I can touch their ears, I won’t believe that they are real!]","Exasperated, Mr. Fang acted as the messenger between both parties.","According to the result of their discussion, Jiang Xiaoyue would ask for a vacation from school and then come to the new shop with Little Bell to see elves! She would find out if the shop owner was telling the truth or not!","...","As for the new task of building a reputation for the new shop, Mr. Fang felt like it was hard to achieve.","I must manage the shop each day and stay here; how can I obtain a greater reputation?","As for dwarves and orcs, don’t I need to keep an eye on the shop? Where can I find them?","What should I do?","Mr. Fang thought for a while and said, “System, can you give me a recommendation?”","System replied, [As an excellent shop owner who can work independently, you must find a solution by yourself. I’m only responsible for setting up tasks and objectives.]","Mr. Fang was at a loss for words.","Mr. Fang would never use his brains if he could solve the problem only using his physical strength. But to complete this task set by the System, physical execution was obviously not enough.","Right now, few new players visited the shop; most of the players were old players. The number of players hadn’t grown much recently.","Of course, as a new shop, it was quite a feat that it had attracted so many players.","However, the numbers didn’t look good when compared with the truly big workshops in this city famous for their cultivation mystical realms.","In the old shops, players had swarmed into them after word about the games spread out. However, in Canglan City, there were many cultivation mystical realms, and every shop claimed that its products were the best.","Besides, the Lava Workshop was releasing its new mystical realm, so few people would pay attention to a little-known shop.","Mr. Fang considered the situation and soon found the root of the problem.","On this continent, he couldn’t rely on word of mouth. After all, the civilization development of this world was far more advanced than that in the Continent of Immortal Relics.","Mr. Fang decided to go on an errand in the morning.","...","Different from the people who went to work at around 8 AM in the world where Fang Qi came from, the warriors and mages in this world must start their training in the early morning.","Some apprentices and disciples got up at daybreak and started to do things.","The Alchemist Union, Mercenary Union, and Mage Union didn’t close doors at midnight.","This morning, the Alchemist Union was even more crowded than usual.","In this ancient and elegant hall gathered not only alchemists but mercenaries and mages as well. They were here because Leo, the representative of the Lava Workshop and a master alchemist, would demonstrate the new mystical realm of the Lava Workshop to the public.","Meanwhile, he would show his advanced alchemy skills through this perfectly-crafted new mystical realm on the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection","This was probably the most ancient building in Canglan City; it had a long history. The yellowish white walls and the brown platform and steps paved by huge rocks gave the building a low-profile elegance. In the courtyard in front of the building was a round fountain which sprayed water with magic power.","The building was permeated with the smell of ingredients and herbs, reminding Fang Qi of an ancient pharmacy shop in his world before he traveled through space and time.","As the representative of the Lava Workshop, Leo had his own Spiritual Spell Visual Projection Room in this building. Of course, since he would give the public a demonstration, he had borrowed the most eye-catching Spiritual Spell Visual Projection crystal in the center of the great hall of the Alchemist Union.","Everyone could see it when they passed the hall.","“Mr. Leo, I heard that you’ll demonstrate the Lava Workshop’s comprehensive mystical realm that contains subjects such as alchemy and forging, right?” In the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection from the crystal in the center of the Alchemist Union, an alchemist wearing a mage’s robe and a badge of the Alchemist Union asked the question.","Obviously, this man was the representative that the Alchemist Union sent over.","“Of course.” Leo was dressed in a formal luxurious mage’s robe, looking like an elegant aristocrat.","“However, I heard that a new shop released its East Continent style mystical realm a few days after the Lava Workshop released its new mystical realm. It’s also a comprehensive mystical realm with subjects such as alchemy and forging. What do you think of it?” Obviously, Mr. Fang’s shop had some reputation now.","Usually, the small shops would watch out and avoid releasing their mystical realms in the same time period as the big workshops in order to avoid unnecessary clashes and losses.","If they still wanted to do it against all odds, it meant that they were super confident in their own products.","“I only want to say that those people know nothing about the market. With our mystical realm out, there will be little business for them.”","“More hilarious is that I heard that their mystical realm contains the East Continent’s Alchemy. It’s ridiculous! I’ve never heard of anything amazing about alchemy in the East Continent.”","After all, Leo was a high-level master alchemist, and the Lava Workshop that he represented was one of the most famous mystical realm workshops on the whole continent. That explained his arrogance and why he looked down at the new shop. “I think they are stupid to do that, and I don’t think we need to show any concern to this issue.”","Meanwhile, before a service counter in a corner of the Alchemist Union, an ordinary-looking young man was applying for a position for the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection.","“Respected Mr. Alchemist, please name your content that will be displayed on the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection.”","“Dashing sword immortal, and making artifacts online,” Mr. Fang said.","Mr. Fang had played to the part in which Murong Ziying joined the team. As an expert in forging swords and making artifacts in the Qionghua Faction, Murong Ziying planned to equip the main characters with better items. Mr. Fang intended to broadcast this portion of the game to the public and see if it would bring greater fame to his shop.","Of course, he had to translate the content into the words that were easy to understand, just like how he had to tell the people in this world that the airplanes and cell phones in Grand Theft Auto 5 were artifacts.","If these people wanted to know the differences in depth, all that could come after."]},{"number":660,"title":"Chapter 660 - The Dwarf Clan","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","At this moment, the square of the Alchemist Union was crammed with alchemists and mages from nearby cities, mercenaries, and knights who were interested in this new mystical realm, and even some high-level officials of the Canglan City Branch of the Alchemist Union.","“Mr. Leo.” In the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection, the black-robed alchemist wearing a union badge said, “I’m pleased to work with you again. I heard that you’ve invited the famous Master Lam, the well-known master in forging swords in Canglan City, to demonstrate this brand-new comprehensive mystical realm.”","“Yes.” Leo nodded casually and said, “Master Lam will use the unique blacksmith and alchemy equipment in the mystical realm to make a battle sword swiftly. Then, I’ll refine some excellent extra material with alchemy and attach magic effects onto this battle sword. You’ll see how well-equipped our mystical realm is for the training of alchemy and blacksmith skills.”","“Excellent,” The alchemist of the Alchemist Union said, “I’m full of anticipation! I believe everyone here are also eager to watch it.”","“But I think our Master Lam is here right now, right?” The mage continued, “Can we ask Master Lam to come up and say hello to the people here? Let’s call out to Master Lam louder, okay?”","“Master Lam! Master Lam!” Ear-deafening shouts rose from the hall of the Alchemist Union.","Having just finished the application process, Mr. Fang walked past them with his hands covering his ears, looking a little frustrated. “What are they doing here...?”","While muttering, he walked out of the door.","“I think we should begin as soon as possible.” A brawny middle-aged man walked up, his grey tank top revealing his bulging muscles.","“Master Lam looks eager to try this new mystical realm,” The alchemist of the Alchemist Union said in a loud voice, “Then, let’s begin!”","...","“Now, we come to the ore warehouse following Master Lam.”","“These categorized materials are top-quality metal ores including black iron, mountain copper, and some rare materials such as purified gold and mystical silver,” Lam said proudly as if he had come into his own huge treasure chamber, “But our destination is not this place but the warehouse of refined materials in the front.”","“To forge a good battle sword swiftly, we can’t waste time on smelting and refining ores.”","...","“Now, we’ve arrived at Mr. Leo’s alchemy room.” The alchemist of the Alchemist Union soon came into Leo’s alchemy room. Right now, Leo was concocting a black potion with a transparent crystal bottle.","“Mr. Leo, I wonder if your work will be affected in such a situation.” The alchemist from the Alchemist Union said, “As everyone knows, alchemy is a meticulous process.”","“I can’t make high-end magic items in such a situation,” Leo said while measuring the potion, “But today, this is an easy job for me.”","“Excellent. It seems that Master Leo is very confident in his skills.”","...","The whole hall was crammed with people.","The spacious hall in the Alchemist Union was crowded as more people came in to watch the demonstration.","“Hahaha!” At this moment, hearty laughter sounded from outside the Alchemist Union.","“This way, please!” The speaker was a female mage in a moon-white alchemist robe.","Walking in with her was a white-haired and white bearded old man in a moon-white mage’s robe, and a few short and stocky figures were trailing beside him.","“Elder Sauk came here to watch the demonstration of the Lava Workshop’s new mystical realm?” The female mage asked with a smile. She was an intellectual and graceful female mage. With her light brown long hair coiled up into a bun behind her head, she looked like a royal aristocrat.","Beside her was a stocky figure with a hearty and resonant voice which could be heard clearly over the noisy crowd.","“I think this old man came to drink my black wine!” The white-bearded old man laughed.","“Hahahaha...”","The dwarf’s height only reached the female mage’s shoulder. With his beard trimmed neatly and hair tied into braids, he looked wild but not ugly in his clean, thick leather armor with black scale patterns. He looked like a rough-looking human with a stocky and short build.","Several other stocky dwarves followed him.","Sauk Stonehammer was an elder of the Stone Hammer Dwarf Tribe from Black Iron Castle. Looking at the enthusiastic atmosphere in the big hall, he laughed heartily and said, “Are these people here to watch the new mystical realm?”","“Of course!” The female mage gestured forward and said, “This way, please.”","These people moved away from the crowd and walked toward the back of the great hall.","At this moment, the dwarf elder suddenly paused his steps when he saw a Spiritual Spell Visual Projection in one corner of the great hall. On it was written, [Dashing Sword Immortal, and Making Artifacts Online]","??? What’s that?!","A few people are actually watching it with great interest?!","The female mage’s face twitched as she thought, Come one... why are you here watching this stuff instead of watching the alchemy demonstration in the center of the hall!","She also noticed that a girl in the grey mage’s robe at the counter of the material store was also watching the [Dashing Sword Immortal, and Making Artifact Online] without blinking.","Do you want to keep your job or not?!","Adolf was the vice president of the Royal Alchemy Association of the Morning Light Empire and one of the white-robed elders in the headquarters of the Alchemist Union. His position was much higher than the president of the Alchemist Union of Canglan City, and this female mage named Dicas was his disciple.","“I’ll go and see what’s happening.” With a dark expression, the old man walked over with his disciple.","“Ugh...” Elder Sauk exchanged a look with th eother dwarves. “...”","-A while later-","“What’s going on?” The dwarves who were forgotten on the side began to wonder.","“Didn’t they say that they would just take a look...”","At this moment, an old man in a blue mage’s robe hurried toward them with a group of alchemists."]},{"number":661,"title":"Chapter 661 - Making Artifact on the Heaven-Abiding Sword Platform in Qionghua Faction","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Hello, Elder Sauk.”","“Where are Mr. Adolf and Dicas?”","The dwarf elder pointed in the direction of [Dashing Sword Immortal, and Making Artifact Online] and said in bafflement, “They said that they will only go over to have a look...”","The dwarves looked over curiously and wondered, “What is taking them so long?”","“Um...” The blue-robed old man looked embarrassed.","“I’m sorry for the delay,” The old man said immediately, “We’ll go call them over.”","-Ten minutes later-","The dwarves stood on the side and exchanged a look of bafflement. “What is taking them so long...”","“My goodness! Isn’t this Elder Sauk...” At this moment, some alchemists noticed the situation over here.","“I’m surprised that you’re here!”","“Where are the people of Alchemist Union?” An alchemist frowned. “They are having less and less manners. Why didn’t they send people over to receive you guys?”","“Um...” The dwarves exchanged a look and said, “We came with Mr. Adolf. Adolf has always been our friend.”","“Oh, I see,” those alchemists asked, “Then where’s Mr. Adolf...”","Elder Sauk pointed in the direction of [Dashing Sword Immortal, and Making Artifact Online].","“Should we go over and remind him. Oh, they are just leaving our guests here, and it is improper.”","With that said, these alchemists walked over.","“...”","– Twenty minutes later –","“What’s happening?!” Totally forgotten, the dwarves scratched their heads in puzzlement.","...","In the great hall of Alchemist Union, while wearing a metal mask to protect him from the smell, Leo was holding a bottle of dark-green liquid with gurgling bubbles. “You must be careful with the poison of this Poisonous Arrow Frog. Its stinky smell might suffocate you and make you regret your existence, friends.”","“Our Master Leo is working efficiently. It seems like an excellent potion is about to be made. Let’s see what Mr. Leo is going to do with it.”","“Sharp Light Potion,” Leo said confidently, “I’ll make a Sharp Light Potion that can infuse the Ultimate Blade Spell into weapons.”","...","Meanwhile, Master Lam, the master sword blacksmith with bulging muscles, was pumping the bellows with great efforts to stoke fire over a piece of silver-colored metal. The furnace had a blue flame with white threads in it, looking different from ordinary flames.","“We’re casting an excellent compound battle sword,” Lam said while pumping the bellows, “We must hammer this block of star-patterned iron flat, so it can completely wrap around this black ink steel.”","The clanking hammering sounds came from the visual projection.","...","At this moment, the dwarves had also walked over to the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection of [Dashing Sword Immortal, and Making Artifact Online] subconsciously and began to watch.","On the screen was a huge round platform engraved with a Tai Chi pattern which contained the fish-shaped Yin and Yang.","The Yang Fish represented fire. It looked like a giant vein in earth that was filled with lava, and people could see hot lava-filled grooves on the dark-red stone platform.","On the opposite side, clear ice was situated on the edge of the heated, dark-red stone platform. The Yin Fish represented ice. Looking up, one could see that this side of the sword platform was covered and sealed in ice.","This was the Heaven-Abiding Sword Platform in the Qionghua Faction.","In the position of the fish eye on the sword platform was a huge round sword creation platform that was built on rocks.","“Now, we’ve got all the materials.” On the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection, a young man stood before the hot sword creation platform and took out all the materials he had prepared. The young man wore a blue-and-white robe and a green jade headpiece and carried a sword case on his back.","“Today, we’ll forge a Ghost Blade which is relatively simple to make.” While he spoke, he took out the materials. One was an orange-colored red iron ore which emitted traces of spiritual essence, and the other main material was an ember-colored Mystic Cloud Crystal which was as smooth as jade. He also took out two pieces of Kunwu Coal which were dark-green with a trace of purple. On the screen, Murong Ziying formed a sword-shaped hand gesture and directed the materials to float onto the sword platform with his spiritual essence.","“Then, we’ll open the sword furnace with the spell.” Murong Ziying used the sword creation spell of the Qionghua Faction. He made quick gestures, and his fingers danced nimbly like bees that were flying. Soon, the orange flames surged up in the huge sword furnace while the materials slowly melted at the bottom of the furnace.","In the furnace, flames surged up one after another like a blooming lotus flower of blazing flames.","With the movements of his fingers, pointing and directing, streaks of spiritual light fell into the lotus-flower-shaped flames, and the materials in the furnace seemed to be driven by an unknown force and began to merge, stretch, and take shape.","Finally, a thick sword embryo that looked like a red jade crystal lay on the bottom of the furnace.","“Now, this sword has taken its embryonic form. To forge it into the final form, we can use some common techniques. For example, we can hammer it with the force of wind and lightning.” Murong Ziying chanted in a low voice as a strong wind fluttered his robe and lifted him into the air. Sitting on the top of Kunlun Mountain, the Heaven-Abiding Sword Platform was very close to the sky. Soon, lightning bolts crashed down onto the sword embryo with vicious force as thunders rumbled.","Like invisible huge hammers, the crazy winds knocked onto the sword embryo with crisp and rhythmic sounds of flowing water. Gradually, the rough and cudgel-shaped sword embryo turned thinner and sharper.","At this moment, a large group of people was watching the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection.","“The alchemy in the East Continent works this way?! How come we never heard of it?!”","“It’s amazing!”","“Swords can be made like this?”","“Ahh-! I think I’ve fallen in love with this sword immortal! He’s so dashing!” a girl screamed.","The dwarves exchanged a look and then looked at Master Lam who was waving his hammer. They exclaimed with their hands on their foreheads, “My god!”","...","Meanwhile, Master Lam waved his hammer and struck the red star-patterned iron with sweat all over his body. While wiping off sweat from his forehead, he left a streak of black dust on his face.","He continued with his hammering.","Bang! Bang! Bang!","“Ladies! Gentlemen! Do you see that?! Master Lam’s masterpieces is almost ready!” The alchemist of Alchemy Union exclaimed passionately.","“...” Around the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection in the center of the great hall of Alchemist Union, there were only a couple dozens of people remaining.","“I think that the great hall in Alchemist Union must be bustling with crowds!” The alchemist yelled, “Cheer for him! Let me hear your enthusiasm!”","“Let’s go...” Some mercenaries nudged each other and said, “Let’s go and watch that ‘making artifact online’. That one is more interesting!”"]},{"number":662,"title":"Chapter 662 - Friendship in the Legend of the Sword and Fairy","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Meanwhile in the internet café, the elves and knights all stood behind Mr. Fang and exclaimed, “Swords are created this way?”","How can you people of the East Continent do things like this?","You travel in style using the sword control technique, you kill monsters in a dashing way, and you even turned the hammering process of making a sword into such a gorgeous performance?! Each of your moves screams style and elegance.","At this moment, Murong Ziying waved his right hand, and the sword body which was being forged and hammered repeatedly flew from the Sword Creation Platform in the Yang Fish into the ice pool in the Yin Fish, drawing an elegant curve in the sky.","Even Elder Sewell looked dumbfounded, let alone the young elves. They all screamed.","On the screen, Murong Ziying finally finished the basic creation of the sword, and pushed up his imaginary glasses.","Then, Mr. Fang immediately realized his mistake. How come I feel like I put up the wrong pose?","“Ahhh! How can one create swords this way?!”","Seeing the sword immortal dressed in blue and white clothes standing in the wind and lightning bolts, the Alchemist Union erupted in exclamations.","“Where is the place shown in the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection?!”","“Do you think this kind of people really exist in the world?” a male mage asked.","“Of course, they exist!” The girls glared at him with red eyes.","Especially Dicas; she already had intense murderous spirit in her beautiful eyes as she looked over. “They must exist!”","At this moment, Adolf and Elder Sauk of the Dwarf Clan exchanged a look of surprise.","“What do you think about this young man’s sword creation skill?” At this moment in the visual projection, a heavy ink-black sword with orange luster flew out from the chilly ice pool.","Of course, creating a sword wasn’t so simple. There were still processes such as creating the cross-guard, handle making, engravings, and spirit injection to be done.","“Well... Today’s livestream ends here. Thank you for watching. Tomorrow, we’ll livestream the rest of the processes, including engravings and spirit injection. Don’t miss our show.”","“That’s all?”","“Hurry! Go and find out the user of this Spiritual Spell Visual Projection! Find out the person who forged the sword in the visual projection!”","How come the Alchemy Union knows nothing about this method of alchemy?!","Adolf felt incredulous.","To them, this sword creation method combined alchemy skills and blacksmith skills. For example, with only blacksmith skills, one couldn’t merge all the materials in the sword furnace.","“I’ll go and investigate!” Dicas thought that she couldn’t sleep until she found out the source of the visual projection.","Then, many female voices rose from behind her, “We’ll help!”","“Please count me in!”","“Me too!”","...","Meanwhile, in the Origins Internet Club, Mr. Fang exited the game and stretched. “Ah... It was so tiring.”","“I hope it can bring the shop some popularity and reputation...” Mr. Fang murmured to himself.","He casually looked back and asked, “How come you’re all standing here?”","He saw a large group of people standing behind him.","“Aren’t you going to play the game today?”","Everyone froze. “Of course, we are going to play!”","“Ya! My Ziying! I’m coming!” Elf Girl Sala shrieked as she hurried to get online.","Mr. Fang was at a loss for words. “... Are you really an elf?!”","Does she still have any of the composure and reservation of an elf?","Also, didn’t you say that you would return to the Silver Moon Forest? How come you’re still here?","Mr. Fang watched while all the elves entered the game.","“Wait for me!” Helen hurried to her seat.","“Our love will continue into the next life.”","“What is love? People live and die for it.”","“With you by my side, I don’t envy anyone, not even an immortal.” Elder Sewell entered the game while humming to herself.","“Wow! You sing so well, Elder!” Sala applauded and cheered in pleasant surprise.","“Your pronunciation is so good...” Commander Elven praised as well.","It was the song ‘Seeking Love in Sword and Fairies’ played by Qin Ji.","She had even learned some ‘foreign language’ in order to sing the song, which earned her many envious glances.","“Can we learn this? It sounds so complicated... I don’t think it’s easier than the sword control technique.”","For the peace-loving elves, the sword techniques and spiritual spells were not as important or interesting as the miraculous scenery in the grand world shown in the game.","“Come and look!” Sala said in amazement, “The forbidden zone in this faction has an ice mountain, and someone is sealed in there!”","“I saw it!” Helen said, “You’ll know it when you come to Jimo; that place is super fun with a fox immortal who loves to tease people. Still, we taught this fox immortal a lesson!”","“Look! We’ll go to this small town to release flower lanterns!”","On the screen, Murong Ziying, Yun Tianhe, Han Lingsha, and Liu Mengli were walking on the street among the bustling crowds during the Lantern Festival. In this seaside town, wooden bridges zigzagged on the pier by the sea.","Han Lingsha picked up a lotus flower lantern. Looking forward, they saw pretty lotus-flower-shaped lanterns covering the sea surface under the starry nightly sky. Those lanterns were radiant, looking like stars.","“This place is so beautiful!”","“I can also take them to watch fireworks on the mountainside!” Helen said happily, “I never knew that a small town of ordinary people could be so pretty!”","“The heroes’ life goals is to eliminate evil and protect the world so that they can see this scene and the smiles on people’s faces, don’t you think so?” Standing on the side of the mountain, Murong Ziying looked down on the crowds and up at the radiant fireworks in the sky as he said.","“Okay. Let’s get serious.” Han Lingsha said, “I’m so happy today. I hope that the four of us can stay together like this and do things we need to do.”","“Hehe!” Sala chuckled and said, “I wish that I could tour the world with them each day! It’s super fun, and I can learn lots of stuff.”","“I wish we can stay together like this forever.”","While the Legend of Sword and Fairy 1 talked about fates and the Legend of Sword and Fairy 3 emphasized reincarnation, the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4 touched people with the simple yet sincere friendships that were formed among the four people as they toured the world.","[TL Note: As a game, the Legend of Sword and Fairy 2 was bad, so not many people ever played it.]","Their search for immortals and their fates were all based on their friendships which would deepen as time went by."]},{"number":663,"title":"Chapter 663 - The Ancient Legendary Place—Buzhou Mountain","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","The players in the old shop progressed much faster in the game compared to the players in the new shop.","“The Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 is a story about their search for immortals before they battle with the demon realm?” Jiang Xiaoyue was also livestreaming.","“Yohahaha! They are having so much fun!” Beside her, the big white deer had just arrived at the Jimo Lantern Festival and was enjoying itself.","“But the Qionghua Faction isn’t as good as I imagined.” Jiang Xiaoyue had progressed faster in the game. By now, she had returned to Qionghua after experiencing many events in Jimo.","By now, the Qionghua Faction had discovered Han Lingsha’s identity; she was a tomb thief, which immediately strained the relationship between the faction and her. On the other hand, the battle between the Qionghua Faction and Fantasy Netherworld was drawing near.","The first half of the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 was an uneventful Xianxia story in which the young people searched for immortals and Dao and helped the weak and the innocent together. They grew up as they met different people and experienced different things as bystanders.","While touring the world and experiencing life, the young people grew out of their innocence and began to consider the differences between humans and demons, right and wrong, and the meaning of life.","People would change and mature as they got more worldly experiences. Their views on the world were no longer simple and naïve.","For example, Murong Ziying, who was born in Qionghua, always followed the principle that demons were evil and must be eliminated.","Yun Tianhe gradually grew out of his confusion and innocence and began to form his own ideas on many things.","Perhaps there was no division between right and wrong most of the time; the difference lied in the different perspectives and choices.","Above the Cloud Platform, the gate to the netherworld opened again, and the promise that they made at the Jimo Lantern Festival which stated they would stay together all their lives wasn’t realized.","Liu Mengli finally confirmed her identity as a demon in the Fantasy Netherworld and left with sadness, returning to the netherworld reluctantly.","Maybe one day, they would face each other as enemies in the battle between the Qionghua Faction and the netherworld.","...","Outside the forbidden zone where Xuan Xiao was sealed in ice, the players finally heard the truth about the Qionghua Faction and the netherworld 20 years ago from the faction master.","Faction Master Su Yao instructed the disciples to read the confidential information in the faction scrolls and told them the truth of that battle.","“With astonishing talent and a lifetime of hard work, Daoyin Spiritual Master, the 20th master of our faction, finally understood the secret method of ascendance in his last years of life; this method requires the combination of the forces of a Yin sword and a Yang sword as well as the support of the disciples. From then on, the faction put in three generations of manpower and materials and finally made the Xihe Sword and Wangshu Sword.”","“Yin and Yang swords must be merged with the users, and the process usually takes years. On the other hand, the ultimate spiritual essence needed for the dual swords to ascend is too much for humans to cultivate. Daoyin Spiritual Master considered this for a long time and found a miraculous place while he observed the stars. This place has abundant spiritual essence and is perfect for us since it is useful to us, and we should be able to control it. However, this place belongs to the netherworld which doesn’t allow us to use it...”","“With excellent talents, Disciple Xuan Xiao and Su Yu were chosen to be the hosts for the dual swords. Three years later, the netherworld, which opens every 19 years, opened again. Xuan Xiao and Su Yu launched the dual swords and froze the netherworld to activate the powerful spiritual essence. However, the netherworld resisted us stubbornly and even killed Taiqing Spiritual Master, the 24th faction master, causing a long-lasting fierce war.”","“At the critical moment, Su Yu, the host of Wangshu Sword, became afraid and escaped with her lover and senior brother, Yun Tianqing, bringing her sword with her. Xuan Xiao, the host of the Xihe Sword, couldn’t control the netherworld all by himself. In the end, the netherworld got away from Kunlun Mountain. In the battle, more than 100 elite disciples died...”","This was the battle between humans and demons in the opening cinematics at the beginning of the game.","...","At this moment, the major streamers in the old shops had almost all come to this part.","In fact, the first half of the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 wasn’t difficult, so the players other than the elves who paused to enjoy the views had almost the same progress in the game.","“Oh... since humans can’t travel to the netherworld, if we want to find Mengli, we need to go to the ghost realm and find the Shadow Branch which can travel through any barriers?” In Su Tianji’s livestream, Elder Su looked amazed. “Then, I must take Lingsha and Ziying to the Buzhou Mountain and find the path to Inconstant Hall, right?”","“What is Buzhou Mountain...?” The players in the new and old shops were all curious. “The mountain is so powerful that it can even support the sky? Such mountains exist?”","By now, the name of Su Tianji’s livestream room had been changed into [Elder Su takes you to tour Buzhou Mountain].","At the same time, the big white deer had come to the shop early today and was exiting from the game when it saw this idle elder livestreaming. “Princess Xiaoyue, come and watch Elder Su’s livestream!”","“Ugh? Elder Su is livestreaming again? For some reason, I’m always worried that she will fall from her sword when flying with a leap of faith whenever I watch her livestream.” Murmuring to herself, Jiang Xiaoyue moved to watch the livestream.","Meanwhile in the Half City Shop, the Almighty Smirk Face Emoji was also livestreaming with the room named [The Tour of Buzhou Mountain].","“It’s said that this is the mountain that supported the sky in ancient times.” In the Half City Shop, a black cloud hovered above a computer desk with a virtual reality headset. “There might be many unknown dangers, but do you think I’ll be afraid of them? Today, I’ll bring you guys to tour this Buzhou Mountain and see what’s inside of it.”","As fans of scenery and nature, the elves hadn’t reached this part yet but didn’t want to miss the tour. Immediately, they began to watch Helen’s tour of Buzhou Mountain.","Buzhou Mountain. Bu meant not, and Zhou meant complete. Therefore, Buzhou Mountain meant Incomplete Mountain.","In the world where Fang Qi had lived before he traveled through time, there was a legend that had circulated for countless years. In the story, Gong Gong, the God of Water, crashed onto Buzhou Mountain and caused the collapse of the sky pillar, which led to the huge flood all over the world. However, this story was new to everyone in this world.","Standing on flying swords, they traveled north from the Qionghua Faction and arrived at the land of mythology half an hour later.","They stopped their flying swords on a mountain peak and looked forward. The gloomy sky and dark boulders made this place look like a wasteland full of ominous presences.","In this desolate land, there were no plants growing in it.","Near their landing spot, a dark, evil, and filthy presence swept over to them. Not far from them was a pile of skeletons, and among the bones stood a purple heavy sword that had a weird shape.","Red light flashed on the sword, making it look extremely fierce and dangerous.","“What’s this?” For players in the new shop, this sword looked strange and dangerous."]},{"number":664,"title":"Chapter 664 - Peak of Buzhou Mountain. Aurogon!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","In her livestream, Su Tianji exclaimed, “Ya!? A demonic sword?! Isn’t it Little Kui?!”","While watching the livestream, Tang Yu suddenly leaped up from his chair. “How come my Little Kui is here?!”","The Almighty Smirk Face Emoji was also surprised. “How come the demonic sword is here? Can you guess who will come out first, Red Kui or Blue Kui? You can place bets on the bottom-right corner of the livestream room!”","...","“You... don’t come close the demonic sword. I, Little Kui, don’t want to hurt more people...”","A faint voice came from the demon sword.","“Oh! It’s truly Little Kui!” The players of the Legend of Sword and Fairy 3 all exclaimed.","“She sounds like Blue Kui!”","“Little Kui! I’m your elder brother Jing Tian!” Before exploring Buzhou Mountain, Su Tianji began to play with the demonic sword. She yelled while controlling Yun Tianhe.","She was delighted to make this discovery in Buzhou Mountain.","Everyone watching her livestream froze.","Messages began to appear on the screen.","Song Qingfeng, [🤢 I’m not an asura player. Do you think I can’t see you’re Yun Tianhe?]","Zong Wu said, [The guy who insulted blind people! Don’t run!]","Tang Yu replied, [Move aside! I’m Ying Tian!]","“...” Bedlam broke out in the livestream room.","“Oh! Be quiet, guys! What’s happening? Why is the demonic sword in this place?!” Many players who were watching the livestream looked amazed.","In the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 3, Long Kui had stayed in the demonic sword for almost 1,000 years, and part of which was spent with Murong Ziying. They encountered each other in this place.","This was the beginning of another story.","After subduing the demonic sword, they continued to fly toward the center of Buzhou Mountain stepping on swords.","Suddenly, a lightning bolt struck down from the sky!","Dark clouds gathered in the sky. In the booming noises of the heavenly thunder, an imposing voice resonated from behind the thick clouds in the high and deep sky, “Mortals, why did you come to Buzhou Mountain?”","“F*ck!?”","“What’s this thing?”","“A monster?!”","Messages flooded the screens in Su Tianji and the Almighty Smirk Face Emoji’s livestream rooms.","The players in the game had cold sweat popping out on their foreheads since they felt an invisible pressure even though they couldn’t see the source of the voice. They felt as if they were mortals standing before a god or ants standing before a huge elephant.","“Be careful! There is possible danger!” Also doing a livestream, Nalan Hongwu looked grim.","At this moment, Yun Tianhe yelled, “We’re here to find a way to enter the ghost realm. Who are you and where are you?”","[...Tianhe is a bit dumb...] Comments appeared on the screen.","“What’s this?!”","“Something is coming out from the clouds,” the elves exclaimed in the new shop.","The storm clouds gathered in the sky while lightning bolts flashed one after another, turning the whole world white.","At this moment, a figure larger than a mountain appeared before them!","It had an elk’s antlers, a snake’s neck, a fish’s scales, and eagle’s claws... It looked extremely miraculous and dignified.","“What’s this?!” The elves, knights, and mercenaries in the new shop all exclaimed in alarm.","It looked like a legendary godly creature instead of a monster. Maybe, it was indeed a legendary godly creature!","Soon, the thick and wide-spread clouds revealed a huge dragon that looked like winding mountains.","“Godly dragon?!” Murong Ziying exclaimed.","The three of them had high-level cultivation strengths. But standing before this true dragon, they felt as tiny as a grain of rice in the ocean.","According to the legend, when the Aurogon opened its eyes, day time came, and when it closed its eyes, night time came. When it exhaled, summer came, and when it inhaled, winter came.","The Aurogon lived in the sunless nation located in the icy cold place in the ultimate north, and it illuminated the place with a lantern in its mouth, which was why it was also known as the Lantern Dragon. In the Legend of the Sword and Fairy, the dragon illuminated the land of the Deserted Nether Nation in the northwest wasteland.","For the cultivators in the Immortal Relic Continent, dragons were legendary holy creatures and the auspicious creatures closest to them. After all, they had seen the bones that godly dragons left in their world.","In comparison, immortals and gods were far more distant to them.","They had only heard and read about the descriptions about dragons in the scroll fragments in the relics, but they had never seen real dragons before.","Having lived for many years, Nalan Hongwu had never felt so stunned or moved before. Standing before the Aurogon, he was stunned by its ultimate grandeur and stunning beauty.","The Aurogon’s voice boomed like thunder. When it was pleased, the sky cleared; when it was angry, the sky turned dark; when it breathed, strong winds swept all over the world!","“Is... it a true dragon?!” Nalan Hongwu yelled.","“Is this a true dragon?!” Messages flooded the livestream rooms instantly.","Jiang Xiaoyue was dazed by the scene. “Ahh! My ancestor looks so miraculous and magnificent!”","The big white deer covered its head with its hooves. “Ahh! I’m scared! I’m scared!”","“Is it... a true dragon?!”","It was the Aurogon from the primeval times!","“Ghost realm? Mortals are existences that are as tiny as grains of sand in the six realms. Do you really understand what the ghost realm looks like?” The Aurogon’s voice boomed like thunder.","“I don’t know what the ghost realm looks like, but we must enter it to find a friend!” Yun Tianhe yelled as booming thunders resonated around him.","Yun Tianhe was still a little dull and innocently dumb. However, it was because of these traits that got rid of any irrelevant thoughts that usually filled an ordinary person’s mind. He only had the single-minded thought that he must find his friend even if a godly dragon blocked his way. Even though there were great dangers in the ghost realm, he wasn’t as afraid as ordinary people.","Ordinary people would turn jelly-legged and couldn’t even speak when they faced such a horrifying existence such as a true dragon.","But Yun Tianhe was brave. Even though it might be derived from his ignorance, it showed his great courage since he could speak these words before such an existence.","“I don’t dislike bold mortals but hate mortals who are loud. If you dare, come up to the Coiling Dragon Pillar!” the Aurogon’s voice boomed like thunder again. “You might not get out of Buzhou Mountain alive!”","“My goodness... What does Yun Tianhe want to do?! Does he want to challenge a godly dragon?!” The people in this world felt as if their minds had turned blank."]},{"number":665,"title":"Chapter 665 - Bold Mortals","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Fine! I’ll hold you to it! Just wait!” With that said, Yun Tianhe ran toward the Coiled Dragon Pillar.","Not only the people in this world, but Yun Tianhe’s teammates, Han Lingsha and Murong Ziying, were shocked by his audacity.","Having grown up in the wildness, Yun Tianhe was like a piece of blank paper and always said what was on his mind; he never had any wicked thoughts. His father Yun Tianqing had taught him that men should be fearless, so Yun Tianhe became such a person. When the godly dragon challenged him to go up to the Coiled Dragon Pillar, he just did it without a fuss.","The huge ancient godly dragon stone statue winded up along the deserted Buzhou Mountain and spiraled up along the Coiled Dragon Pillar to the high and distant heavens.","If the players went up along the Coiled Dragon Pillar all the way to the dragon head, they would probably reach the new immortal realm shown in the Legend of Sword and Fairy 3. The players of the Legend of Sword and Fairy 3 could see the huge dragon head when Chong Lou and Jing Tian battled many years later.","Of course, the godly dragon only challenged them to go up the Coiled Dragon Pillar to test their strength and courage and wouldn’t allow them to travel to the top.","It must be noted that in the world shown in the Legend of Sword and Fairy, there were many immortal realms, and they were not related to the abodes and residences of the immortals in the heavenly realm.","The immortal realms could be divided into heavenly immortal realms and mortal immortal realms. The latter were like blessed cave abodes in the mortal realm such as Penglai where the spiritual essence was abundant.","The new immortal realm discovered by Fei Peng and Chong Lou in the Legend of Sword and Fairy was a heavenly immortal realm which was a blessed cave abode in the heavens.","The story of the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4 happened after Immortal General Fei Peng reincarnated as Prince Long Yang of the Jiang Nation but long before Jing Tian was born, which was why the players had encountered the demonic sword and Long Kui.","It meant that even if the players could force their way up to the top, the most they could see was probably the ruins of the battle between Fei Peng and Chong Lou many years ago.","The Coiled Dragon Pillar wasn’t easy to walk on since the players couldn’t fly up with the sword control technique. The higher they went, the stronger the gusts would be. If they were not careful, they would fall and shatter into pieces. In fact, they might be knocked down by heavenly lightning bolts and encounter all kinds of demons.","Despite all these difficulties, the players and the characters in the game could still manage to pass it.","However, many people were still worried and wondered, Would we need to battle the godly dragon later?","The players in the old shops were feeling uneasy while they walked up the path. However, for the players in the new shop, they wondered, Did you say that this is a basic cultivation realm? Where is it? I don’t see it! How can anyone play this?","Even Merlin, a level 9 sky mage, felt like his legs were shaking while he walked up, let alone these knights. Saint level? If saint level masters could create such gusts by just breathing and sound like booming thunderbolts as the godly dragon did, perhaps even the gods in the world will have had to submit to these masters.","Although Merlin couldn’t imagine the power beyond the saint level, he knew that this dragon was an existence with power far greater than the saint level!","Also, Merlin had a vague feeling that even some legendary gods didn’t have such horrifying auras.","After all, there were powerful gods and less powerful ones.","“Is this a saint level mystical realm?!” He suppressed the horrifying thought and chanted silently, “This is a fantasy! It must be!”","This chant calmed him down a bit. After all, few people could face the Aurogon as fearlessly as Yun Tianhe.","“Hey! We’re up! Where are you!?” Yun Tianhe yelled at the sky.","“F*ck...” Song Qingfeng and the other players in the old shops were so scared that they almost dropped from their chairs, afraid that the ignorant Yun Tianhe would be killed by one palm strike.","For the elves, it felt the same as if they were yelling at the Elf God, “Hey! Where are you?”","Having never seen such dumb and fearless man, the players in the new shop felt their legs turning into jelly. Others would respectfully address this godly dragon, but you just walked up and said hey!","“Ahh-” With a shrill scream, Yun Tianhe was knocked down by a lightning bolt.","After a long while, Yun Tianhe got up, looking nonplussed. “Why am I always getting struck by lightning bolts since I came down from the mountain...”","Everyone put their hands on their foreheads. “...”","“Mortal, do you know how disrespectful you were when you yelled at a godly dragon? This is what you get for your rudeness.”","“I don’t know about good manners. You told us to come up, claiming that you know how to get to the ghost realm, so we hurried up to find you. What’s wrong with that?” Yun Tianhe was honest and frank; he didn’t have the concept of politeness.","This gloomy place was a portal leading to the depths of the ghost realm, and it was a very important portal between the heaven and the earth. Otherwise, it wouldn’t be guarded by the Aurogon. If it allowed people to enter this portal easily, then everyone could go to the ghost realm whenever they wanted.","Therefore, people had to pay a great price for the entry. The godly dragon demanded the life of one of Yun Tianhe’s teammates as the price. The life was useless to the godly dragon, but it would act as a warning to all others that no one could pass it with ease.","However, Yun Tianhe would never accept this condition.","“If you anger me, I’ll kill you all!” Heavenly lightning boomed, showing the godly dragon’s fury.","New to the world, Yun Tianhe knew no fear and said, “I can tell that you’re powerful, but it’s me who doesn’t want to make the choice, and it has nothing to do with them! Please don’t kill them! I won’t sacrifice my friends, and I won’t change my mind either.”","Obviously, Yun Tianhe spoke whatever was on his mind.","“...” The godly dragon was silent for a while. Perhaps it had never seen such an ignorant and ridiculously dumb mortal before. Not a blood-thirsty evil dragon, it decided to give them a chance. “Mortal, you’re very interesting. Perhaps you haven’t seen enough suffering in the world and think that everyone can solve their problems with their own power.","“Maybe you’re worthy of my appreciation, or you’re just a moron who knows nothing about the world.”","“What do you mean...” Yun Tianhe asked.","Perhaps he indeed knew nothing.","“I’ll give you a chance. I’ll release a phantom of me from hundreds of thousands of years ago before I ascended and understood Dao. If you can defeat it, I’ll send you to the Inconstant Hall in the ghost realm.”","“Really? You are willing to help us?” Yun Tianhe was delighted.","“Hahaha!” The Aurogon laughed, “I’ve guarded this place for 9,900 years and will soon finish my job with success. I’m surprised to see a ridiculous mortal like you. Should I help you guys enter the ghost realm, or should I send your souls into the ghost realm?!”"]},{"number":666,"title":"Chapter 666 - The Mystical Land in the Sky—the Temple of the Sky!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“After all the talk, we still have to fight it...?” Seeing this scene, the players’ hearts sank. Although they didn’t know the power of the phantom of the Aurogon before it ascended and understood Dao, they were sure that an ancient true dragon wouldn’t be weak even before it ascended.","“This mystical realm...?” The players in the new shop didn’t know how to continue...","Thinking that they had to battle with the phantom of an ancient godly dragon, their faces turned pale in fear.","Merlin, who had suspected that this was only a basic mystical realm, now looked ashen-faced.","However, for the players in the old shops, despite their shock, they were not as afraid since they had battled with the Prison-Guarding Wisdom King and Chong Lou, whose cultivation strength was suppressed to the peak of the mortal level.","Despite their experience, the old players were not sure that they would win. Even though it was only a phantom of the Aurogon, it excelled in the five-spiritual immortal spell. Meanwhile, its body was the toughest weapon, and its scales were a powerful defense that few mortals could break.","“What kind of spell is this?!” Players exclaimed in the new shop when they saw gusts, lightning energy, rocks, flames, and ice pallets crashing down together as the huge dragon’s claw struck outward. Everyone knew that ice and fire couldn’t be used together, but the elves and mages saw these two elements were actually not fighting each other but complementing each other, creating even greater power!","“How can we fight it?!” Looking at the words [Please Try Again] on their screens, all the players were stupefied.","[@Mr. Fang.] Players in the group @-ed Mr. Fang.","Nalan Mingxue said, [This is hard...]","Su Tianji chimed in, [It was a piece of cake until now. I feel like I don’t know how to fight anymore... I was killed instantly a moment ago...]","Nalan Hongwu said, [I think I must study it carefully, and I’m afraid that I can’t pass it for the time being.]","Su Tianji asked, [Sir, do you have a guide or something...?]","Mr. Fang replied, [I don’t have a guide for dumb people.]","[What do you mean by guide for dumb people?!] Su Tianji was displeased.","An Huwei said, [Sir, just tell us if you can livestream it!]","Jiang Xiaoyue asked, [Boss, tell us where you’re in the game!]","Mr. Fang replied, [I passed it long ago.]","Song Qingfeng shouted, [F*ck... Sir, why didn’t you put it on livestream when you did it?!]","Dong Qingli said, [Sir, you changed! Did you save before you fought it? Quickly reload and livestream for us!]","[How long has it been since your last livestream?!]","[Sir, you became lazy!]","[You’re no longer the hard-working and productive shop owner anymore!]","The people became indignant in the group chat.","[Hurry! Put it on the livestream!]","[Even Xiaoyue livestreams more frequently than you do!]","Mr. Fang looked puzzled as he asked, [What does it have to do with me that Xiaoyue is livestreaming?]","[Sir, I’m warning you. If you livestream now, we will still be friends!]","This group of people were just short of putting a knife against Mr. Fang’s neck.","“Okay! Okay! I’ll livestream.”","...","On the Coiled Dragon Pillar, Mr. Fang chose to play as Yun Tianhe.","“Ugh...? You’re playing it too, Sir?” The elves and some members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion looked toward him. “This is so difficult...”","“I wonder if the shop owner can pass it...?”","“Watch how he plays it...” Soon, many people gathered behind Mr. Fang.","“The Aurogon can use many spiritual spells,” Mr. Fang told them, “But you must pay special attention to its five spiritual immortal spells. If water, fire, wind, lightning, and earth spells are casted at the same time, anyone who is hit by it will die.”","“You have two options to deal with such spells. One is to dodge it with superior footwork and skills, and the other is the Shapeless Cancellation Technique.”","The Shapeless Cancellation Technique was a high-level spiritual spell which could block and absorb the power of the opponent’s spiritual spells and turn it into one’s own strength. If cultivators mastered this spiritual spell with proficiency, they would be at the advantage when dealing with some powerful monsters who could use immortal spells.","However, the godly dragon also knew how to use this kind of spiritual spells, so it didn’t guarantee success; the players shouldn’t grow complacent. If the dragon interrupted this spell and slashed its claws at Yun Tianhe, he would be in big trouble.","“Only after you understand this basic knowledge can you defeat the godly dragon.”","In the battle with the Aurogon, the players could fly on their swords. In the high sky, a huge dragon flew through the ocean of clouds.","In the ear-deafening thunders and dragon roars, Yun Tianhe, Murong Ziying, and Han Lingsha flew up on their swords.","Faced with the godly creature flying through the ocean of clouds, flying up to fight it required great courage.","Everyone could feel that Yun Tianhe was fearless, Murong Ziying just followed nature with the casualness of Dao, and Han Lingsha was overcoming her fear to help her friends at the risk of her life. By joining the battle, they showed their sincere care for their friends, including Liu Mengli.","This was destined to be a hard battle.","“In this battle, on top of your own strengths, you need great adaptability and fast coordination.”","...","Thunderbolts crashed down from the sky. The three sword beams danced in the sky like shooting stars, and the godly dragon slashed out its sharp claws while creating violent gusts, narrowly missing Fang Qi several times.","The five-elemental spiritual essences transformed into five streaks of horrifying forces and merged together. The dancing gusts, flashing lightning bolts, and the mixed ice and fire made the audience feel dizzy just by watching.","The players in the new shop had never seen a battle on this scale before. The dragon’s horrifying attacks seemed to be able to destroy everything they touched, but the three sword beams were as slippery as fish, slipping from the huge dragon’s claws again and again.","About fifteen minutes later, Fang Qi tore through the high sky like a sharp sword beam while flying on his flying sword.","“Here is the chance! Metal-Melting Demonic Fire!”","Meanwhile, a horrifying hurricane gathered around Fang Qi like shadows.","On top of the wind element, this hurricane also contained the fire, lightning, water, and earth elements. The variations of the five elements made this spiritual spell hard to predict.","“Use the Shapeless Cancellation Technique!”","Soon, Murong Ziying used a spiritual spell, and the violent five spiritual essence surrounding Yun Tianhe seemed to calm down.","Taking this opportunity, Fang Qi shot out with explosive fierce presence, stabbing into the vital part of the godly dragon like a lightning bolt!","...","“Good! Mortal, you worked very hard!” When the sky cleared, the Aurogon revealed its true form again.","By now, Yun Tianhe and his two companions were covered in wounds.","“Hu...” Mr. Fang exhaled deeply, feeling exhausted.","In the end, the godly dragon helped the main characters go into the ghost realm, disguising them for 24 hours so that they wouldn’t be discovered by the ghosts.","After several turns of events, the main characters finally got to the Shadow Branch in the ghost realm that could travel through the barrier of the demon realm which was known as the netherworld. In the process, they also encountered Yun Tianqing, who hadn’t entered the reincarnation yet.","Yun Tianhe finally got the chance to ask his father why his parents did what they had done in the Qionghua Faction and forced Yun Xiao to seal himself in eternal ice.","Yun Tianqing admitted that he was sorry about what happened to his senior brother and then explained why he had left with the Wangshu Sword. If they tried to seal the demon realm with the dual swords, the demon realm would refuse to submit. Only the initial battle caused the deaths of many elders and elite disciples in the Qionghua Faction including Faction Master Taiqing Spiritual Master. Even if they defeated the demon realm, only a few cultivators in the Qionghua Faction would survive the battle.","Perhaps only a handful out of the thousand disciples could survive this battle, and this was the most optimistic estimate.","For Yun Tianqing, ascendance and becoming an immortal was meaningless if it meant the destruction of almost the entire faction.","If the battle prolonged, heavy casualties would appear, and the entire Qionghua Faction would be turned into a living hell.","Since the elders were unwilling to back down from the plan, Yun Tianqing had no choice but to leave with the Wangshu Sword to end the war.","Meanwhile, Yun Tianhe’s parents happened to save a young and severely wounded demon and put it under the care of Liu Shifeng, and this demon was Liu Mengli.","This was what happened about 20 years ago.","On the Nether River, the main characters encountered Han Lingsha’s uncle, who was doing hard labor working as the boatman on the Nether River; with his help, the three young people got the chance to escape from the ghost realm.","Sometimes, fates were unpredictable. For generations, the people of the Han Family had been tomb thieves, thinking that they were doing a good thing to dig out the treasures from the tombs to help the living people.","However, due to the disturbances that they caused the dead, the people of the Han Family not only got short lifespans of less than 30 years but had to do hard labor to redeem themselves after death.","Han Lingsha had spent a lifetime searching for ways to seek Dao and become an immortal, so she could change the fate of early death for the people in her family. However, in the end, she discovered that the technique to prolong the lifespan was useless for people in her family.","Everyone had one’s own fate. Just as Han Lingsha’s uncle, Han Beikuang, had said, everyone had their own destiny; no one could change it.","...","After coming out from the ghost realm with the knowledge that her days were numbered, Han Lingsha, who had reprimanded Yun Tianhe for his recklessness, made an even bolder decision – steal from the Temple of the Sky!","The main characters had made the wish and said, “The four of us will be together like this all our lives, doing things that we need to do.”","Mengli might still have a chance to realize this wish, but Han Lingsha couldn’t live long enough to see that day.","Han Lingsha wanted to get a meaningful item to replace her company with Ziying, Tianhe, and Mengli. After a lot of thinking, she decided on the Hou Yi Sun-Shooting Bow in the Temple of the Sky.","[TL Note: Hou Yi is a mythological Chinese archer. He was also known as Shen Yi and simply as Yi. He is also typically given the title of ‘Lord Archer’. He is sometimes portrayed as a god of archery descended from heaven to aid mankind.]","Now that Yun Tianhe had a great sword made by Ziying, he still needed a good bow.","No one had imagined that such a grand tomb hovered in the sky. Like a floating city in space, this secret garden in the sky was magnificent and beautiful, ancient and vibrant!","Standing in the temple, the main characters looked forward and could see an extremely wide path leading to the heavens. Under the blue sky, they looked down and could see puffy white clouds under their feet.","Seeing this scene, the audience members’ jaws dropped, feeling like this palace with gold tiles and white walls was more stunning than anything they had seen.","Are they going to steal from such a tomb?! The players thought that either these characters or themselves had gone crazy!"]},{"number":667,"title":"Chapter 667 - Hou Yi Sun-Shooting Bow, Immortal General Gou Mang!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Perhaps the main characters had sensed the fierceness of the imminent battle between the Qionghua Faction and the demon realm. On one side was their best friend Liu Mengli, and on the other side was Qionghua, which hadn’t treated them well and seemed to have used them as chess pieces, but it was still Murong Ziying’s faction.","When they returned, regardless if they returned to the demon realm or Qionghua, they would be in danger. Han Lingsha wanted to steal the item to help her friends, but they didn’t want her to take the risk all by herself. In the end, Murong Ziying and Yun Tianhe decided to accompany her to the Temple of the Sky.","The Temple of the Sky was guarded by heavenly soldiers, which meant that regardless of who was buried in the tomb, it was a highest-ranked burial place that few existences in the whole world, both in heaven and on earth, could enjoy.","The players in the old shops had been to the outer range of the ghost realm in the Legend of Sword and Fairy 3, so this trip to the Inconstant Hall in the ghost realm wasn’t something too novel for them.","But the situation was different this time.","In the Yuanyang City Shop, Zong Wu, Gu Tingyun, and the others were sitting on the couches in the lounge area. While stuffing a couple of hot strips into his mouth, Zong Wu stared at the screen with widened eyes. “This is so grand...”","“Whose tomb is this?” Gu Tingyu also widened his eyes.","The players in the new shop didn’t quite understand the situation but were shocked by the name ‘Temple of the Sky’, the sight of this grand structure, and the big scale of the tomb.","“Is this a god’s tomb?!”","Perhaps it wasn’t a tomb, and the entity buried in the tomb wasn’t human, but it must be an ancient relic of the highest level!","Different from the original version, the system version required the players to sneak in except for the swift fight against the soldiers at the entrance. After all, if they exposed themselves and caused chaos before they got close to the treasure, they wouldn’t be able to fight their way out and would be killed even if they had ten such teams.","Obviously, Mr. Fang was quite familiar with the map. By dodging the guards, he soon led his companions to the palace in the southern corner of the Temple of the Sky.","The Temple of the Sky was a grand tomb hovering in the sky, and it was so large that people couldn’t see the end with one glance. Of course, Yun Tianhe and the others couldn’t tour every corner of this place.","On the topic of the Temple of the Sky, Han Lingsha’s grandfather had to be mentioned. Coming from a family of tomb thieves, her grandfather had had the chance to enter this place due to great fortune. After he returned, he seemed to have gone crazy and murmured to himself all the time.","Still, some members of the family got some clues from his few mentions of this trip. It seemed that Han Lingsha’s grandfather only ventured into a small part of the huge tomb, which was like the tip of an iceberg. However, in this small corner, he had seen an unimaginable treasure – the Hou Yi Sun-Shooting Bow!","According to legends, there had once been ten suns in the sky, and people in the human world suffered greatly because of them. Godly Archer Hou Yi shot down nine suns and thus eased the drought on the land and saved many people.","The main characters couldn’t see any sources of light in the ancient palace, but soft light illuminated the interior. The lighting was perfect, neither blindingly bright nor dim.","Shaped like an upside-down tower, the interior of the southern palace had no guards, but the main characters had to be careful of the restriction arrays and traps while they ventured down.","After walking down to the ground level, they could see a wide high platform in the great hall. The ancient long bow was hovering over the platform silently.","It seemed like no one was guarding it, and there were no protective measures.","The scene of nine suns in the sky and the blazing fire were engraved on the green-jade-like stone surface of the bow.","In one glance, the scene seemed to be the background of the ancient bow. For one instant, it brought the audience back to the distant ancient time.","It just hung there silently, but people could feel the streak of powerful spiritual essence in it.","They seemed to hear the hoarse roars and yells from that era of ten suns.","“Wow-!” The elves screamed. Even Elder Sewell covered her mouth, trying to suppress her thrill and shock that were pouring out.","For elves, the bow was one of their inheritance weapons since ancient times, and all of them were great archers. Although they didn’t know the history of this bow, they could still vaguely sense the grand presence from this ancient and elegant long bow at this moment.","“She came here to steal this bow and give it to Tianhe?”","Humans only had a short lifespan of about several dozens of years, but even this short lifespan was a luxury for Han Lingsha. “Regardless of how many days are left in my life, I want you to remember me as your good friend. Okay?”","At this moment, Yun Tianhe and Han Lingsha’s feelings toward each other might have gone beyond friendship, but they treated these feelings as a part of their friendship and wanted to remember each other forever.","Perhaps it was due to fate, the treasure in the Temple of the Sky happened to be a perfect weapon for Yun Tianhe. Having no good gift for Murong Ziying, Han Lingsha apologized to him.","“I don’t care about godly weapons, but you must keep your promise and stop doing tomb thefts which will further shorten your life,” Murong Ziying said, “I don’t approve of what we do today, but I’m your friend, and I will do anything for you guys and bear any consequences for taking this bow.”","At a young age, these people weren’t greedy and didn’t scheme for any personal interests, which made their friendship even more pure and precious.","In fact, Han Lingsha had given Ziying a nine-dragon silk sword tassel which was a royal item, a perfect gift for him since he had been a royal member of the Yan Nation before he joined the Qionghua Faction. She had pushed it into his hand to bribe ‘Uncle-Master Ziying’, and Murong Ziying hadn’t paid much attention to it at that time. Now that he thought about it, he suddenly found this thing quite precious due to their friendship.","Murong Ziying suddenly turned silent.","At this moment, all the players watching the scene turned silent as well.","“Then... could it be that they’ll take the godly bow just like that?” Su Tianji asked in bafflement when she watched Han Lingsha go over to take the bow.","At this moment, a voice came from the void. “Sinner! Put down the Hou Yi Sun-Shooting Bow right now!”","A god who had a human head, a pair of bird wings, and was wearing a golden headpiece suddenly appeared before them. “I’m Immortal General Gou Mang, and I’m guarding the Temple of the Sky.”","Su Tianji was at a loss for words.","Song Qingfeng said, “Elder Su jinxed it...”","“Oh! It’s not my fault!” Su Tianji rebutted, “Everyone knows that this place must be guarded by someone...”","Then, she stared at Immortal General Gou Mang and asked, “What god is this one?!”","Nalan Mingxue said, “Immortal General... Is he on the same level as Fei Peng?”","A fan of stories and plots, Shen Qingqing knew the story well and made a reasonable speculation, “They should be on the same level, but I’m afraid that this one is less powerful since Fei Peng is the No.1 Immortal General.”","Hearing her appraisal, others felt less scared and heaved a sigh of relief. Although he still seemed powerful, he didn’t seem that terrifying anymore.","However, in the new shop, the players watching the scene took a few steps backward and said, “There’s a god in this place?!”","What’s wrong with this world?! Even a tomb needs to be guarded by a god?!"]},{"number":668,"title":"Chapter 668 - Returning to Qionghua and Battling","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","On the next day, the players came early and sat in the lounge area, waiting to watch Mr. Fang’s livestream.","Gou Mang and the godly dragon shared the same opinion about mortals, and they believed that these tiny existences weren’t worth their efforts. Considering that Han Lingsha didn’t want to take the godly bow for herself, he intended to kick them out of the Temple of the Sky instead of killing them.","“Um? Godly dragon’s presence?” While Yun Tianhe activated his cultivation strength, Gou Mang sensed a special presence from him. He asked, “What’s your relationship with the Aurogon?”","“What relationship?” Yun Tianhe thought for a moment and said in confusion, “A pure fighting relationship.”","“!??”","Not only Gou Mang but the audience froze at Yun Tianhe’s words.","[Excellent!]","[Tianhe is awesome!]","[Hahaha! This fighting relationship is cool!]","The audience flooded the screen with bullet comments.","“Hahaha! Tianhe is super fun!” The elves laughed, feeling like there was nothing wrong with Tianhe’s answer. “Look at Gou Mang’s livid face! Haha”","“Hahaha! He’s really a savage! He knows nothing.”","“Such audacity!” At this moment, Gou Mang attacked again, but only to test their strengths. After finding that they were indeed powerful enough and potentially battled the Aurogon, he stopped testing and thought for a bit.","However, taking the godly bow was obviously impossible now. Gou Mang said, “A sinner (Han Lingsha) can’t touch the godly artifact. Only people with the purest mind are qualified to be its owner!”","“Ugh? Does it mean that Tianhe can take it?” In the Yuanyang City Shop, Jessica ate another slice of spiritual melon as she watched the livestream with great interest even though she wasn’t allowed to play the game. “Yun Tianhe is as pure as a blank paper; does he meet the requirement?”","Obviously, Gou Mang had also sensed the extraordinary quality in Yun Tianhe who had the presence of the godly dragon in him.","At this moment, Mr. Fang said in the livestream, “Such a situation. I can’t just take it after you say so, right?”","“You hurt Lingsha...” Yun Tianhe was obviously extremely angered. “I don’t care about it.”","The elves looked envious, wishing that they could take the bow.","On the screen, Yun Tianhe’s teammates persuaded him to take the bow. Otherwise, their efforts so far would be in vain.","Finally, he took up the Sun-Shooting Bow.","“I want to try it...” The elves were eager to try this godly artifact with their own hands.","However, these fans of natural beauty turned sulky after remembering that they hadn’t even met the godly dragon yet. It would take a long while for them to reach this part of the story.","“Let’s watch how the shop owner uses the bow...”","“Let’s see how powerful this bow is...”","“As instructed by Pan Gu, all things in the six realms have their own destinies. The movements of the sun and the moon, the change of four seasons, and everything in the world all follow their destined paths. The ultimate power is the Heavenly Dao. From now on, the Hou Yi Sun-Shooting Bow will submit to you and take you as its master.”","[TL Note: Pan Gu is the first living being and the creator of all in some versions of Chinese mythology.]","“How come it sounds so deep?” The players in the new shop looked baffled as if they were listening to God’s teaching. They had a vague feeling that these words contained ultimate truth but couldn’t really understand it. They were all awed by these words!","“The mystical realms in this shop...” The players exchanged a look and thought, How come they are so excellent?!","The Legend of Sword and Fairy 4 was a complete and vast world.","The journey to the Temple of the Sky was scary but not dangerous. With the godly dragon’s presence with them, even Immortal General Gou Mang went easy on them, respecting the godly dragon.","Therefore, compared with the battle with the godly dragon, this battle was much easier.","The power of Hou Yi Sun-Shooting Bow was determined by its owner’s strength.","In the system version, the players could make it easier by controlling Yun Tianhe to take the bow directly, but Gou Mang would still test their strengths. But this way, the players could pass this stage more easily.","When the main characters entered the demon realm again, they saw the past events with more details from the fantasy array.","After Faction Master Taiqing Spiritual Master died in the war, the demon realm hovered over all the disciples of the Qionghua Faction like a huge shadow, which caused conflicting views among them.","However, Liu Mengli’s mother, Chan Yu, the Lord of the Demon Realm, wasn’t in a better situation.","At this moment, Xuan Xiao broke out from the ice. With the Xihe Sword and Wangshu Sword in hand, he merged the yang essence of Xihe with the chilly yin essence of the Ice-Freezing Scroll in his body, reaching the peak stage of his strength.","Under the powerful force of the two swords, the barrier was broken, and many demons were killed. The Purple Crystals which was used to supply energy for the demon realm were taken away. Stimulated by the prospect of imminent ascendance, the disciples of the Qionghua Faction were mad with murderous spirits, even turning against Murong Ziying and Yun Tianhe, their peers in the fraction, as the latter tried to dissuade them.","It proved that certain things could indeed turn people into maniacs.","Demon General Gui Xie was killed at the entrance of the demon realm. The battle was happening between Chan You, the fatigued lord of the demon realm, and Xuan Xiao, who was in the prime of his life.","Everyone shivered silently as they watched the extremely powerful Xuan Xiao who emitted blazing murderous spirit. The viewers weren’t even this scared when they saw Immortal General Gou Mang.","Emitting blazing flames and chilly icy mist alternatively, Xuan Xiao’s murderous spirit almost suffocated the audience even through the screen.","At a loss for what to do in this situation that was extremely one-sided, Yun Tianhe and his friends watched many demons getting slaughtered while they tried to protect Liu Mengli and a few others.","Godly artifacts chose their owners. The Hou Yi Sun-Shooting Bow chose its owner, and so did the Wangshu Sword.","Perhaps due to the workings of destiny, Han Lingsha was the new host of the Wangshu Sword. Born at a Yin hour and a Yin moment with a life of contradictory elements, only her appearance could wake up the Wangshu Sword. Yun Tianhe had used this sword for years and didn’t see anything special in it. But after Han Lingsha appeared, he hacked open his parent’s tomb with the sword at the Rock Creek Cave.","However, due to the aggressive power contained in the Wangshu Sword, its activation would damage the vital soul of the host who wasn’t a cultivator. When the dual swords were used to trap the demon realm, it would cause even greater damage.","Yun Tianhe had given the Wangshu Sword to Xuan Xiao due to his guilt for the things that his father had done and helped Xuan Xiao break out from the ice. At that time, he didn’t know what Xuan Xiao would do with the sword.","When Yun Tianhe found out, it was too late.","“Tianhe, it’s been a while since I last saw you. Big Brother missed you.” Despite his selfish intention for using Tianhe, Xuan Xiao was still grateful to Tianhe who had helped him when he was most in need. He and Tianhe had even become sworn brothers.","Perhaps since everyone whom Yun Tianhe had met after he came down the mountains were good to him, he trusted everyone he met, including Xuan Xiao. “Big Brother... Is everything you told me a lie? Your only purpose is to take back the Wangshu Sword? You only want to take spiritual essence from the demon realm and ascend to become an immortal?”","“What happened in the past, real and fake, are not important,” Xuan Xiao said gravely, “The most important thing is that you’re still my brother. After I ascend and become an immortal, it’s a piece of cake for me to save Han Lingsha!”","Xuan Xiao even invited Yun Tianhe to ascend with him, fulfilling the great achievement that the Qionghua Faction had been working on for in the past 1,000 years."]},{"number":669,"title":"Chapter 669 - The Ascendance of the Whole Faction!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“I have a weird feeling about Xuan Xiao...” Hearing the maniac-like obsession in Xuan Xiao’s tone and seeing it on his face, the players found that he was no longer the ethereal-looking Daoist who had cultivated on the immortal mountains for years.","Even the viewers could see it through the screen, let along Yun Tianhe in the game.","Naturally, Yun Tianhe didn’t agree with Xuan Xiao and insisted on the latter returning the Wangshu Sword. With the activation of the tremendous power in the Wangshu Sword, Han Lingsha’s condition was getting worse each day. He wasn’t sure if she could survive until the day of ascendance.","Xuan Xiao who was obsessed with the ascendance wouldn’t return the sword; there was no doubt about that.","When Yun Tianhe lived on the mountains, he had nothing and knew nothing. He would be delighted by things such as catching a wild boar or a having a fine clear day.","Just as Yun Tianqing had taught him, Yun Tianhe had been a fearless man. He didn’t fear anything even when he collided with the godly dragon and faced the Immortal General Gou Mang. However, at this moment, fear suddenly struck his mind.","He was afraid that he would never see Mengli again, and he was afraid that he couldn’t stop Xuan Xiao and even more afraid that he couldn’t save Han Lingsha.","The godly dragon once said, “Perhaps you haven’t seen enough suffering in the world and think that everyone can solve their problems with their own power.”","At this moment, Yun Tianhe suddenly understood that there were certain things in the world that he couldn’t achieve even though he tried his best.","“Tianhe is still too naive...” Watching this part, the players in the new shop and the old shops all felt deeply touched. Finally, the fearless savage became afraid of something. However, what he feared wasn’t the godly dragon or a god.","“Tianhe, we’re just mortals.” Murong Ziying was obviously more open and more resigned to fate. “Everything in life including birth, aging, sickness, and death has been prearranged by the Heavens... We’re humans; how can we fight with the Heavens?”","“Yeah... It’s all fate...” In the Jiuhua City Shop, Yuanyang City Shop, and Half City Shop, people like Nalan Hongwu, Ning Bi, and Su Tianji had played the Legend of Sword and Fairy 1 and the Legend of Sword and Fairy 3. Despite Li Xiaoyao’s great power, he still couldn’t save Ling’er. Despite Fei Peng’s great power, he was still struck down into the mortal world.","Some things were just beyond the power of humans.","For the players in the new shop, even though they didn’t have concepts such as the Mandate of Heaven, they knew about destiny which was a mysterious and magical force that no one could touch.","For Helen, Commander Elven, and the others, it was as distant as a god.","For Merli,n who was a supreme existence, destiny was probably scarier than gods.","Even if they could predict something, they didn’t have the power to change it. This sense of powerlessness was enough to drive people into despair.","...","In the Breeze Stream, the main characters tried to enlist help from Chong Guang and Qing Yang, the only two elders of Qionghua who had survived the war 19 years ago. However, they found that Chong Guang was dead, and Qing Yang was severely wounded. Obsessed with ascendance, Xuan Xiao had become so evil that he had attacked these two elders so that no one could find the weaknesses in the dual swords from the forging notes left by Zong Lian.","The Qionghua Faction used several generations of accumulation and created the ultimate dual swords Xihe and Wangshu that were famous around the world. These two elders had once regarded all these glories with great pride, but they eventually realized that everything was just a dream.","The ethereal-looking faction on Kunlun Mountain was now fraught with smoke and evil.","The Qionghua Faction’s last sword maker, Zong Lian, Murong Ziying’s grandmaster, had recorded that the power in the dual swords was too aggressive in his notes. Anything too extreme will create the opposite effect. The sword hosts must be self-disciplined during cultivation. Otherwise, they would lose control of this power and get killed by it. The dual swords were spiritual artifacts that could help people ascend but could also become fierce weapons leading to catastrophes.","The dual swords were too powerful. If the power of the dual swords got out of control, there wasn’t a perfect solution. The only solution was the deaths of the hosts, which would lead to the evaporation of the power in the dual swords.","In the Boxian Town at the foot of the mountain, everyone was talking about the rumors involving the ascendance of the Qionghua Faction.","The viewers could hear mortals talk among themselves, “I heard that place is where the immortals live. They are going to return to the Heavens and abandon us and our town. They will no longer give us clean water to drink...”","Except for ascendance, Xuan Xiao had no other thoughts on his mind. After taking enough energy crystals, he did Yun Tianhe a favor and released the old, weak, sick, and crippled demons back to the demon realm and withdrew the seal that the dual sword placed on the demon realm.","In this war, the casualties of members of the demon realm were so great that only Liu Mengli and a small group of demons survived. Now, it was time for them to depart.","Liu Mengli became the new lord of the demon realm and flew away with the demon realm.","Just as the words in the song described, “Our intertwining fate will continue in the next lifetime. What is love? People live and die for it.”","Perhaps it was the main characters’ destiny to continue their fate in the next lifetime.","The memories of them touring the world, doing valiant deeds, and releasing flower lanterns were so fresh as if these experiences had just happened yesterday.","However, there were too many regrets and powerless moments in a mortal’s life.","In the sky, the huge mountain that hosted the Qionghua Faction began to slowly rise toward the radiant Kunlun Heavenly Light.","This scene stunned everyone. None of them, regardless if they were players in the old shops or the elves and knights in the new shop, had ever seen or heard of such a feat.","Their hearts trembled at this scene.","However, at the same time, a sense of melancholy filled their minds.","When the main characters flew up on flying swords, they saw the ruined walls and buildings littering the Qionghua Faction. Corpses lay in blood puddles on the square before the mountain gate, and the Qionghua Faction that was as balmy as spring all year round was now deadly silent.","The few remaining disciples were nowhere to be seen.","On the Cloud Platform, Xuan Xiao and Su Yao controlled the Xihe Sword and Wangshu Sword respectively. Although Su Yao wasn’t the host, she was the faction master and could control the Wangshu Sword with Xuan Xiao’s help, but the consumption all came from Han Lingsha.","One sword condensed chilly frost while the other released blazing fire. The tremendous power from the dual swords had far surpassed the limit of mortals!","“This... This...?!” In the new shop, all the audience members were so shocked that they were at a loss for words.","Ascendance and becoming immortals were the dream for several generations of members of the Qionghua Faction. Xuan Xiao had cultivated and became a sword host for this purpose.","Regardless of how Yun Tianhe dissuaded him, he couldn’t change Xuan Xiao’s mind.","In the previous battles, the godly dragon didn’t use its true power, and Gou Mang just used some attacks to test the main characters’ strength. But now, they faced a life-and-death battle.","In the Qionghua Faction, Su Yao was jealous of Yun Tianhe’s talent, which was why only Murong Ziying had taught him how to cultivate. Also, Yun Tianhe had learnt lots of stuff from Xuan Xiao.","Xuan Xiao was master and friend to Yun Tianhe, but now they had to meet in a battle as opponents.","Everyone felt emotional at this scene. Perhaps the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 would come to its end with this battle.","Would Yun Tianhe succeed in stopping Xuan Xiao’s ascendance? Or would Qionghua succeed in its ascendance with Han Lingsha dying during the process? It all depended on the result of this battle.","Everyone stared at the screen without blinking, afraid to miss a tiny detail."]},{"number":670,"title":"Chapter 670 - The Legend of Sword and Fairy 4 Isn’t as Good as the Previous Games in the Series?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“A senior brother? Master and father? You still want to fight me for others!” In the last 20 years while he suffered in the ice, only one person offered Xuan Xiao help, which was why Xuan Xiao only showed a sliver of kindness to Yun Tianhe.","When Yun Tianhe refused to ascend with him for the last time, Xuan Xiao became so furious that he looked like a maniac.","Many years ago, when Faction Chief Taiqing Spiritual Master died and the Lord of the demon realm lived, most disciples in the Qionghua Faction thought that it was quite probable that they would be defeated. To some extent, releasing the demon realm and ending the war had saved the whole faction. However, Xuan Xiao had suffered the burning of Xihe’s power for 20 years in the chilly ice, and there was no way around it.","Yun Tianhe had his own reasons. “You don’t want to give up ascendance... but I have to save Lingsha and others!”","In the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4, there was no final battle like the one with the ancient water demon beast in the Legend of Sword and Fairy 1, or like the one with Chong Lou, the almighty demon lord who was the most powerful across six realms at the end of the Legend of Sword and Fairy 3.","With 90 percent of his strength to keep Qionghua in the air and slowly rising toward Kunlun Heaven Light, Xuan Xiao used the remaining ten percent of his strength to fight his opponent.","However, only ten percent of his strength was still powerful. The strong ice and fire presences could turn anyone into ash or ice if they got close.","This battle wasn’t as stunning as the one fighting with the water demon beast in the Legend of Sword and Fairy 1, and it wasn’t as hearty and enjoyable as the one with the Almighty Demon Lord Chong Lou at the end of the Legend of Sword and Fairy 3.","Regardless of how this battle ended, there was no winner. The audience didn’t want to see either of them lose.","“How come the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4 is going to end like this?!” In the old shops, the players looked anxious. They would rather watch a battle with the Almighty Demon Lord Chong Lou at the end of the Legend of Sword and Fairy 3 since it was more peaceful.","“Elder Su, who do you support...?” Nalan Mingxue asked.","“I hope Yun Tianhe wins, but I will pity Xuan Xiao if he fails at this stage.”","On the Cloud Platform, sword energies swept around and crossed each other while countless blinding sword beams and sword arrays shot down like raindrops. While Murong Ziying fought Faction Chief Su Yao, the sword beams from Five Spirits Returning to Root and Thousand Fragment Light Sword engulfed the whole platform.","Yun Tianhe pulled the Hou Yi Sun-Shooting Bow to its limit.","Xuan Xiao’s ice and fire energies spread out. The ice froze everything, and fire burned everything, turning the whole Cloud Platform into a world of fire and ice!","Flying swords flew past each other, and ice and fire collided with the bow and swords. Each attack was deadly until one sword energy cut into Xuan Xiao.","Blood spilled.","Covering his wound, Xuan Xiao half kneeled on the ground and said with hatred, “Tianhe, I went easy on you, but you aimed to kill me! Good! Really good!”","It must be noted that if Yun Tianhe were defeated here, Xuan Xiao wouldn’t kill him, which made the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4 less difficult to play than the Legend of Sword and Fairy 3.","“I can only use ten percent of my strength to deal with you while using the rest to support Qionghua in the air. Aren’t you guys taking advantage of me?!”","Hearing Xuan Xiao’s furious accusations, the audience became curious and wondered, Will the game end like this?","On the screen, the conversation continued.","“Xuan Xiao... Why?! You can always find another way to ascend! I’ll go with you until we find it!”","Xuan Xiao was silent for a long time and then shook his head firmly. “You are 22 years too late! When I was in a bottleneck while cultivating with the dual swords, no one asked me to give up. When I obtained some progress and mutated my meridians, no one asked me to give up. When I lost the Wangshu Sword and burned day and night in the fire, no one cared. Now, it’s too late!”","“The story is not bad, but it’s too...” Su Tianji sighed, “How can it end like this...?”","At this moment, a wave of cold and radiant light fell from the sky. It was Kunlun Heaven Light that people of Qionghua Faction had dreamed about!","Even though Xuan Xiao was wounded, it was too late for Yun Tianhe to stop them from ascending in the last moment.","Besides, if Yun Tianhe tried, Xuan Xiao wouldn’t show any mercy anymore!","How powerful were the dual swords?! If they released their full power, it was no less than that of an immortal! An unrivaled force exploded from the swords. As the host of one of the godly swords, Xuan Xiao’s presence turned even scarier.","Soon, the Qionghua Faction would ascend with success.","In the Yuanyang City Shop, Jiang Xiaoyue sat with other students of the Heavenly Academy. “Is this the end of the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4?”","Tang Yu sent a bullet message. [It’s okay, but it’s not as good as the previous games of the series...]","In the new shop, the people were also talking among themselves. Helen of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion said, “It’s quite good, but its ending isn’t as good as that of Assassin’s Creed.”","“I have the same feeling...” Elf Girl Sala said, “The master assassins in Assassin’s Creed don’t have such great power, but their spirit and beliefs are admirable.”","Song Qingfeng said, “I feel like the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4 isn’t as good as the previous games in this series...”","At this moment, a golden godly light shot down from the sky. It was so bright that it blinded everyone here.","What kind of godly light could have such a power?","“What’s happening?!”","“What’s this?!”","“Have they successfully become immortals now?!”","“Do they have immortals to welcome them?”","Everyone exclaimed as they watched the scene.","A dignified-looking woman dressed in exquisite clothes decorated with gold and jade appeared before the characters in the game.","She seemed to have even greater godly power than Gou Mang, and no one could look directly at her noble face.","“I’m the Ninth Heaven Mystic Fairy under the Heaven Emperor, and I’m here to pass the decree from the God Realm.”","“Finally... finally...” On the screen, Faction Chief Su Yao looked thrilled that the ultimate dream of Qionghua would come true!","The players in the shops were all stunned.","“My goodness...”","“They... actually made it?!”","Although they didn’t approve of their method, the viewers were still stunned and excited about the grand feat and the success.","Nalan Hongwu said, “I’m surprised that they succeeded like this!”","However, they heard a cold reprimand, “You are ignorant mortals who have turned evil. How dare you wish to become immortals?!”","“This...!?”","“The Heaven Emperor decrees that the Qionghua Faction worked against the Heaven Dao and committed great sins. The faction will be burned by heavenly fire and fall to the ground. The disciples will be imprisoned in the East Ocean Whirlpool for 1,000 years!”","Su Yao’s heart sank and turned cold. However, she wasn’t the only one who was stunned. The audience also felt their hearts lurch. “What’s happening?!”","Aren’t they close to ascending with success?!","Aren’t they going to obtain and temper their immortal bodies?!","What’s happening?!"]},{"number":671,"title":"Chapter 671 - I Control My Destiny and Not the Heavens! The Grandest Eulogy of Humans!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","From the perspective of the Ninth Heaven Mystic Fairy, the Qionghua Faction had turned evil in their minds, and the Heavenly Dao wouldn’t allow such evil people to ascend and become immortals.","However, Xuan Xiao thought that the Heavenly Dao was only an excuse of the God Realm. How could one word from the God Realm decide the fate of mortals?","“Heaven is above me, so I respect it. However, if the God Realm wants to push me around, you can keep on dreaming!”","The Ninth Heaven Mystic Fairy’s voice remained mild, “Ignorant mortals think that their lives are as tiny as weeds and regard the gods and immortals as lofty beings. However, you don’t understand the rules of the Heavenly Dao. Even gods and immortals have to follow the Mandate of Heaven.”","The Qionghua Faction Chief Su Yao murmured, “Mandate of Heaven. Do you mean that the dream which the Qionghua Faction had pursued for generations is just a fabricated fantasy?!”","“But... our faction removed demons and protected the humans in the world. All our deeds are evil instead of virtuous?”","The Ninth Heaven Mystic Fairy answered her in a cold voice, “Humans and demons are not born with goodness or evilness in them. If the demons don’t do evil things, why should you kill them? The Qionghua Faction slaughtered the demon realm due to greediness, which makes it no different from the evil devils!”","Su Yao’s heart turned cold. On top of her, everyone in the Qionghua Faction including Murong Ziying also turned cold inside.","Eliminating devils and killing demons. The faith that the members of the Qionghua Faction had held for generations was a joke in others’ eyes!","However, they had stuck to and fought for their goal with self-righteousness for generations.","Humans were tiny and ignorant. The Qionghua Faction had explored and advanced in the darkness for generations and finally came to this stage where they could ascend as a whole; they were only one step away from becoming an immortal faction!","However, everything fell apart at this moment.","Seeing this scene, everyone was touched by an inexplicable feeling.","20 years ago, Yun Tianqing and Su Yu stopped the process of ascendance and blocked the mission.","If this mission wasn’t stopped, the ascendance would have failed anyway, and the whole faction would have been destroyed.","20 years later, Yun Tianhe tried to stop the ascendance. If he succeeded, the faction would continue its pursuit in another cycle of 19 years.","However, if Yun Tianhe failed, the Qionghua Faction would still be destroyed.","It seemed like an invisible force in the world had been leading Qionghua to its destruction. The two earth-shaking artifacts were the ultimate products of the artifact-making for cultivators, and the ascendance of a whole faction was probably the most glorious thing in human history.","Even the players had looked awed and envious when they heard about this great faction at the beginning of the game.","Many generations of people of the Qionghua Faction poured all their energies and efforts in this dream, but no one had known that it would be the cause of the faction’s destruction since the beginning!","Perhaps this was the vague and ethereal fate and destiny.","In the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4, the final enemy was neither Xuan Xiao nor anyone else. The enemy was the unfathomable Mandate of Heaven!","The heavenly fire was about to fall.","“When the heavenly fire falls, it will strike down the Qionghua Faction. But what about the people at the foot of the mountain? Will they all die...?” Yun Tianhe yelled out his question on the screen.","“I... I want to save them,” Yun Tianhe said.","There were too many powerless moments in one’s destiny. Perhaps just as Murong Ziying said, “Everything in life including birth, aging, sickness, and death has been prearranged by the Heavens... We’re humans; how can we fight with the Heavens?”","Along the way, Yun Tianhe had experienced many things and found that he could do nothing to stop Liu Mengli’s departure or Han Lingsha’s imminent demise. Now he couldn’t even save the lives of the people in Crescent Village.","“Perhaps you haven’t seen enough suffering in the world and think that everyone can solve their problems with their own power.” The godly dragon’s words replayed by Yun Tianhe’s ears, and he suddenly understood that there were so many regrets and powerlessness in life.","This was destiny.","“You can’t work against the Heaven’s will,” the Ninth Heaven Mystic Fairy said.","Xuan Xiao laughed in anger. “‘No wonder people say that ‘the Heavenly Dao is indifferent to all, and all creatures are considered straw dogs’. You are indeed merciless and cold and would kill without caring if it’s fair.”","The Ninth Heaven Mystic Fairy’s voice still sounded cold, “The Heavenly Dao is indifferent means that the gods and Heavenly Dao regard everything fairly. However, you misunderstood its meaning by so much.”","“It’s shameful that the Heavenly Dao acts in such a way!” Xuan Xiao laughed wildly as if he was a maniac. “I, Xuan Xiao, swear today with my life that since the Heaven Dao rejected me, I’d rather become a devil!”","Everyone saw the ice and fire elemental murderous energy around Xuan Xiao growing even darker and gloomier until they turned into a chilly and horrifying devilish energy!","Thunders boomed and lightning bolts flashed in the sky as if they were venting endless fury.","The lightning bolts danced like snakes in the sky, and the stars fell down, shaking the earth as if the Heavenly Dao was eager to instantly kill this devil.","Xuan Xiao’s determination and madness deeply shocked everyone.","They saw him turning into a devil under the tremendous pressure of destiny.","The stunning despair that Xuan Xiao showed stirred and saddened everyone, creating the most tragic song.","When Xuan Xiao was stuck in the bottleneck of cultivation with the dual swords, he didn’t give up. When he obtained some progress and mutated his meridians, he didn’t give up. When he lost Wangshu Sword and suffered from being burned by flames day and night, he didn’t give up. He had borne all the pain just for today.","The maniac figure under the gloomy sky and the flashing lightning bolts was printed into everyone’s mind as if he was the only person to do so.","This was the Mandate of Heaven.","Xuan Xiao’s roars which stated that he would one day kill his way to the Godly Realm and his howls that contained endless fury hammered on everyone’s heart with vicious force.","As a new-born devil, Xuan Xiao was naturally no match for the Ninth Heaven Mystic Fairy. What he got was endless imprisonment in the East Ocean Whirlpool.","20 years of burning in fire was nothing compared with the terrifying fate that awaited him.","No one made a sound. Everyone watching the scene was deadly silent and terrifyingly pale.","The Ninth Heaven Mystic Fairy was about to leave when Yun Tianhe yelled, “Wait! You haven’t told me how to save those people at the foot of the mountain yet!”","Was it truly impossible to disobey the Mandate of Heaven? Could he make a small change? A tiny small change?","“You said that everything in the world is part of the Heavenly Dao, then humans are part of the Heavenly Dao too, right? Then, why can’t humans decide our own destiny?” Yun Tianhe was ignorant of the worldly things due to his young age and inexperience, but he was more intelligent than ordinary people. “Then... I control my destiny and not the Heavens!”","What was the purpose of cultivation? What were cultivators? The elves and knights in the Nora Continent didn’t understand it.","Even the cultivators and warriors on the Continent of Immortal Relics only had vague answers to these questions.","The Shu Mountain Faction only cared only about the humans in the world and didn’t pursue for Immortal Dao.","Jing Tian was the reincarnation of an immortal general and didn’t care to ascend or become an immortal.","Under the strike of the blazing heavenly fire, Qionghua fell from the sky like a burning sun. At this moment, the whole world seemed to be roasting by this sun as if it was the end of the world!","At the foot of the mountain, people saw Yun Tianhe pulling out the arrow and drawing the bow, and they felt like they had gone back to the distant ancient time and saw the figure who shot down nine suns.","Here, a group of mortals wanted to control their own destinies!","Being born as immortals and gods with special gifts and talents wasn’t something to be proud of.","In contrast, these mortals, the dust in the six realms as called by the godly dragon, and the weak ants in Gou Mang’s eyes, were admirable and touching since they dared to do the impossible.","Everyone in the audience was also mortals and knew that many things were out of their control.","At this moment, they began to understand the true meaning of being a cultivator.","Cultivators were a group of people who tried to control their own destinies.","Then, they watched as Yun Tianhe drew the bow and shot the arrow toward the blazing heavenly fire and the Qionghua Faction which were falling from the sky.","At this moment, a mortal issued a brave challenge to destiny and the Mandate of Heaven!","At this moment, everyone stood up from their seats subconsciously.","Now, all the elves and knights felt their eyes turning moist as sudden understanding dawned on them. There are such people!","They felt like a voice was yelling in their minds, and their hearts trembled; they had never felt so stunned and thrilled before.","This spirit and this courage of challenging things beyond one’s power formed the most epic tale in human history!"]},{"number":672,"title":"Chapter 672 - What Are You Guys All Doing?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Falling from the high sky with blazing heavenly fire burning around it, the Qionghua Faction looked like a small meteor, or a sun, falling from space.","It was a catastrophe. If it landed, the surrounding area within a diameter of hundreds or even thousands of kilometers would be razed to the ground!","The strong light dyed the entire sky into fiery-red.","Knowing that it was impossible, Yun Tianhe still tried to lock horns with the great power of nature with human strength. Perhaps countless years ago, another great archer had the same feeling.","Yun Tianhe lifted the same bow that Hou Yi had used and drew it open. Everyone watched as a rainbow shot across the sky like a shooting star and pierced the sun-like Qionghua Faction.","As if it was struck by a horrifying force, the fire instantly exploded!","An earth-shaking noise sounded from the high sky.","The entire Qionghua Faction with its mountain exploded under the force of Hou Yi Sun-Shooting Bow. Everything was shattered, and countless debris shot outward like a rain of shooting stars.","At this moment, Yun Tianhe depleted all his strength and fell down in the end.","Seeing this, the players from the new shop and the old shops had tears in their eyes.","Perhaps it wasn’t sadness but of an indescribable emotion that touched their hearts.","In the end, Yun Tianhe succeeded, even though it was insignificant.","At least he had saved these mortals from being crushed to pieces by the iron hooves of destiny.","The Heavens are in motion ceaselessly; the enlightened exert themselves constantly.","Was it truly impossible for tiny humans to become immortals or gods? Were they going to remain as existences similar to dust or ants in the eyes of the gods forever?","No. With possession of such spirit and courage, there was nothing impossible in this world!","Many people felt as if a chain was unlocked in their minds, and something had loosened inside their bodies.","...","– Meanwhile, in the Yuanyang City Shop –","It was drizzling, and the puddles on the ground suddenly reflected images of two figures in black clothes and black cloaks.","The two figures walked in the drizzle leisurely. Although they were talking, they didn’t stir up any ripples in the puddles when they walked on them.","The legends said that grand masters left no footprints walking on snow, but leaving no trace on water was even rarer since it required extreme control and powerful movement techniques.","“I’m surprised to see such prosperity in this forgotten land.”","“However, the array in this city... um... is a bit out of date.” They walked while chatting leisurely with each other.","“The layout of this city...tsk, tsk... reminds me a bit of my faction, but it has gone awry!”","“It seems that they have declined generations after generations!” The tall and thin man shook his head and said with a smile.","“It seems that the people here should respectfully address us as Supreme Messenger, right?”","“This place looks like the Lower Realm. I think they should address us with this title. Hahaha!” His companion laughed, “Heavenly Academy... Good. It should be close. Although we’ve lost it long ago, since we have this opportunity, we should meet and help this branch of our faction.”","At this moment, they saw Sia passing by with a bag of spiritual melons in her hand. She murmured, “This Jessica... she always asks me to bring her melons!”","“Little Girl, do you know how to get to Heavenly Academy?” At this moment, Sia saw two guys walking over to her.","“Why are you asking?” Sia spoke with the Spiritual State language but still had the awkward accent, “It’s not time for the academy entrance test yet.”","“We’re old acquaintances of the Heavenly Academy Master,” one of them explained.","“Oh!” With sudden understanding, Sia pointed at the Origins Internet Club helpfully and said, “Academy Master Gu is in the internet café; you can find him there.”","– Outside the door of Canglan City Shop –","“Is that Murong Ziying... in this place?” The white-haired and white-robed Adolf walked over with a long magic staff and extended his neck, glancing into the door.","“How can he stay in this small shop?!” Dwarf Elder Sauk Stonehammer looked at the shop doubtfully.","“This place looks too low-end.” Mr. Fang’s shop was quite good in Canglan City, but it still looked low-end in Dicas’ eyes. After all, she was born in an aristocratic family.","A large group of people followed them. “What?! He lives in this place?!”","“We came with great expectation and awe for his abilities, but I feel like we might leave in disappointment...”","Then, the group of people pushed open the door and walked in.","With his magic staff in his hand, Adolf was the first to walk into the shop.","The others followed him closely.","At this moment, they saw a big group of people standing in one big circle while intently watching something on the big screen in the shop.","Also, some of them such as Sala and other elves were rubbing their eyes with handkerchiefs as if sand grains had entered their eyes. They continued to rub their eyes non-stop.","None of them noticed that another group of people entered the shop.","“How come these people are all like this...?”","“What’s happening...?”","Having just walked into the shop, the newcomers were puzzled by what they saw.","“Ugh?” Elder Sauk of the Dwarf Clan seemed to see a familiar face since his small eyes suddenly lit up. He walked over and said, “Isn’t that Elder Sewell of the Elf Clan?”","...","Meanwhile, the two black-cloaked messengers from another continent also pushed open the door of the Yuanyang City Shop.","They also saw a group of people standing before the big screen with tears in their eyes.","“What are they doing here?” The tall and thin messenger coughed slightly and said in a friendly voice, “Can I ask if Academy Master Gu is here?”","A white-haired old man instantly stood up with complicated emotions on his face.","Many people turned to them. One of the newcomers had shoulder-length black hair, and the other was short and fat but had a mild and smooth presence. They stood there like two Tai Mountains with magnificent presences. Obviously, they had extremely high cultivation strength, probably higher than anyone in the entire Spiritual State.","Gu Tingyun hurried over and reached out his hand while asking curiously, “Friends, do I know you?”","“Friends?” Looking at Gu Tingyun’s weird hand-shaking gesture, the two exchanged a look and chuckled. However, before they could speak, they heard Gu Tingyun letting out a long howl which was as high as the roar of an old dragon.","Then, they felt Gu Tingyu’s presence rising continuously until it reached a limit. But instead of stopping at the limit, it seemed to have broken through a threshold and grew.","Gu Tingyun’s cultivation strength had stopped at the 30th small realm of the third level of the Spiritual Void Realm, which was the eighth realm for cultivators, for many years.","But now...","The 31st...","The 32nd...","The 33th...","...","The 36th small realm.","Level 4 Spiritual Void Realm!","The first small realm of the fourth level of the Spiritual Void Realm!","The second...","The third...","“!!??” The two newcomers’ hands that just reached out froze in mid-air.","Then, more long howls sounded in the shop, and the presences all started to grow!","...","In the Canglan City Shop, Elf Elder Sewell turned her head.","The Mage Adolf and the Dwarf Elder Sauk were about to walk over when they saw Elder Sewell opening her small mouth wide.","“Ahh-!” She let out a long howl.","Suddenly, her cultivation strength suddenly rose from the second tier of level 8!","[TL Note: It seems like the levels in the new continent refers to the same thing as realms in the old continent.]","Then, they heard more howls in the shop...","“Ahh-!”","“Ooh-!”","“Yaa-!”","With the long howls, streaks of powerful presences shot up like explosive fireworks! Breakthrough!","“!!??” The two black-cloaked messengers in Yuanyang City Shop exchanged a look, and Adolf, Sauk, and the others in Canglan City Shop looked at each other and almost shouted in shock!","What are you guys all doing!!??"]},{"number":673,"title":"Chapter 673 - The Online Game About to Be Released Is Called World of Warcraft?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","In the Yuanyang City Shop, Half City Shop, and Jiuhua Shop, most of the senior players with high cultivation strength had obtained breakthroughs after a long time of accumulation. The people who hadn’t obtained breakthroughs had acquired some understandings and inspirations.","The effect was more obvious on the old and experienced cultivators and warriors such as Gu Tingyun who had accumulated strength for a long time and experienced many regrets and powerlessness in life. In comparison, the young people obtained fewer inspirations.","However, since the old shops had many players, even a small percentage of them breaking through right there caused a great upheaval.","The long howl shocked the two nonplussed black-cloaked messages so much that they almost turned and ran. What kind of weirdos are these people?!","We’ve not come to this place for many years. How come things have changed so much in this place?! How can people make breakthroughs like this?!","The newcomers in the Canglan City Shop obviously had the same feeling.","“What... what are you doing here?” the two asked immediately.","“We are watching the livestream.” Old Man Gu Tingyun was also puzzled. “I was watching Mr. Fang’s livestream and suddenly felt the knots in my heart completely unraveling when I saw the part where Yun Tianhe took the control of his destiny from the Heaven and shot down Qionghua. Um... Then, I just...”","“What... livestream? What’s do you mean by ‘I control my destiny and not the Heavens’?” The two people looked even more baffled.","“Do you want to try it...? The Legend of Sword and Fairy 4!” Gu Tingyun said.","“Let’s try it...” They walked toward the counter in doubt.","In the Canglan City Shop, a group of people were watching the scenes on the big screen with curiosity.","On the big screen, fire rained down while the Qionghua Faction exploded into many chipped rocks and debris in the high sky. While burned by blazing heavenly fire, everything falling down the sky turned into ash before landing on the ground.","Despite some damages, they were much less serious than what they could have been.","“I never recommended mystical realms that weren’t made by the Elf Clan.” Elder Sewell still looked emotional. “But you must try this Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4!”","“How can we try it?” Adolf immediately asked.","“Um... how do we pay?!” Dwarf Elder Sauk asked loudly.","Elder Sewell pointed at Mr. Fang who was livestreaming with his virtual reality headset. “Ask the shop owner to buy a membership card!”","“Sir! I want to by a membership card!” As soon as Mr. Fang put down his virtual reality headset, he saw a large group of people swarming to him.","“Get in line! One by one! Everyone can have one... Get in line!” Soon, such shouts sounded in the shop. “I’m afraid that the new shop will soon need to be expanded again.”","Tang Yu, Xun Yuan, and other disciples of the Heavenly Academy mumbled, “Let’s go! Let’s go! Let’s go to the bathroom...”","...","As mentioned before, in the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4, Gou Mang wouldn’t unleash his full force, and Yun Tianhe could still lose to Xuan Xiao, which meant that the only difficult battle was with the shadow of the godly dragon in Buzhou Mountain.","Obviously, it was less difficult to play than the Legend of Sword and Fairy 3 if the players didn’t want a perfect ending. With the previous training of skills, the veteran players could complete the game without much hassle.","With the strengthened items and spiritual treasures, the new players could also stumble to the end with success.","A few days later, the first group of players cleared stage one after one.","-100 years later in the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4-","Amid the crisp bird chirps and fragrant floral fragrance, the familiar and melodious notes of the flute song, Immortal Dream, sounded in Green Bird Peak. A White-haired Murong Ziying stood on the edge of the cliff, looking out into the drifting clouds in the valley.","The gorgeous sword immortal had grown into a grand master.","Liu Mengli walked over slowly, looking the same as she did 100 years ago.","Life was like a big dream. Youth turned into white hair in one instant. The only constant thing was the Heavenly Dao which permanently moved in cycles.","100 years later, the four people gathered again. On Green Bird Peak stood two tombs beside the sacrificed object, the Wangshu Sword. On one tombstone was engraved the words [Beloved Wife Han Lingsha’s Tomb] while the other tombstone was blank, and a pair of butterflies danced around the sword. The two looked back and saw a figure pushing open the door to the small wooden house and walking out. He still looked like the youth he had been 100 years ago, but his bright eyes were no longer there.","His eyes were tightly closed and couldn’t open. He changed the lives and destinies for many people. In the end, he had to pay the price.","Seeming to sense the presence of his old friends, a smile gradually appeared on his face.","Despite the many troubles in the world, it was a moment of happiness that his best friends could still come together after so many years.","For a moment, they seemed to return to the Nest Lake, Huainan King’s Tomb, Jimo Town, and Boxian Town...","Those were the best memories in their lives.","...","Without them knowing, tears came to their eyes and wetted their faces.","Messages appeared in the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4 group chat.","Song Qingfeng posted, [(Screenshot) It’s the end!]","“(Screenshot) Scattering flower petals for the ending!” Jiang Xiaoyue still had tears in her eyes.","– In the Canglan City Shop –","The group of elves had tissues in their hands. “Wuu... so touching...”","“I never knew that such a stirring story exists in this mystical realm...”","“Hiss-! Why did Lingsha die like that...”","“It seems that she died of old age, but I’m still sad...”","“It seems like we can finally return to Silver Moon Forest in peace...” Elder Sewell murmured.","At this moment, Commander Elven of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion asked leisurely, “Sir... will you host new games from the East Continent in the future?”","“New games...?!” What new games?!” Elder Sewell and the other elves perked up their extremely pointy ears.","...","Obviously, the melancholic elves needed something new to divert their attention and ease their sadness.","“New games?!” Many players who had cleared the game also looked over.","“Sir, will you host and run new games?”","“Or... do you have sequels of Assassin’s Creed or Resident Evil?”","The players in the old shops were also speculating.","Song Qingfeng said, “What do you think the next game in the shop will be?”","“Whatever it is...” Su Tianji rested her head on the computer desk in her Qzone and said, “I’ll buy it anyway!”","Su Tianji’s Qzone was completely different compared to before after meticulous care. Her residence was now a luxurious mansion, and the large fields of spiritual vegetables and spiritual fruits were flourishing under the care of the semi-automatic machines that she had bought.","She had several computers in her house and a small laptop for her to play and chat on QQ while lying on her bed.","Beside her lay a jade flute, and the sheet music for Immortal Dream was still displayed on the computer screen. Obviously, she had been practicing this song a while ago.","In the Yuanyang City Shop, Jiang Xiaoyue sat among her peers from the Heavenly Academy. Yue Bai stretched her back with force and said, “I’m bored! I finished the new game!”","Jiang Xiaoyue said in the group chat, [I think the next game must be a sequel of an old game.]","[I think it will be a brand-new game.] After all, the shop had released a sequel of Resident Evil, Brotherhood was a sequel of Assassin’s Creed, and the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4 was also a sequel. Nalan Mingxue said in the chat group, [I think the next one won’t be a sequel.]","[It’s more fun to speculate on the creator of the game, Blizzard, Ubisoft, or Soft Star.]","[We can use the process of elimination and rule out Soft Star first. After all, the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4 has just ended.]","Meanwhile, the new shop’s reputation had been growing, and it seemed like the task wasn’t so difficult to complete after all. Therefore, Mr. Fang gave the players a clue and said, “The new game will be an online game named World of Warcraft.”","“World of Warcraft?” The players in the new shop looked curious. “And what is an online game?”"]},{"number":674,"title":"Chapter 674 - Heated Discussions About the New Game","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“This... the mystical realm of Assassin’s Creed is about assassins...” Elina who wore the hooded assassin’s outfit asked curiously, “Does it mean that the World of Warcraft is about...”","She glanced at the direction of Dusk Forest with a frightened look. “Magical beasts?!”","[TL Note: World of Warcraft was translated into World of Magical Beasts in Chinese]","“Is it a mystical realm for magical beasts to experience life?!” Elina exclaimed.","“Not likely...” The elves were also puzzled. However, they knew that this shop, which had released an assassin-focused mystical realm and then the East Continent style mystical realm, was unique and thus couldn’t completely rule out this possibility.","“What nonsense are you talking about?!” Mr. Fang’s face twitched.","“You’ll know when the cinematic trailer is released!”","...","Obviously, the players in the old shops had also gotten the news.","By now, Lingyun Academy of Jiuhua City had established new standards for the disciples in the four houses. But still, Xu Zixin and Shen Qingqing, two of the first group of players in the shop, were about to graduate from the academy.","Meanwhile, people like Nalan Mingxue, Song Qingfeng, and even fatty Wang Tai had entered the Earth House and became senior students in the academy.","Due to the booming sales of the official novel of Diablo 2, Shen Qingqing now had a part-time job as a writer and was quite famous.","“Time flies, right? Qingqing,” Xu Zixin said with a new communication jade in her hand. “We’ll soon graduate.”","“Um...?” Shen Qingqing froze when she casually glanced at her communication jade.","“What’s it, Qingqing?”","“The shop owner replied to my message about the new game!” Shen Qingqing said in pleasant surprise, “In addition...”","“In addition??”","“The shop owner plans to release new official novels and... um... comics?”","Some games in the shop such as the Legend of Sword and Fairy series focused on the main plot of the story. However, other games had good stories which were overshadowed by other great features, and these games included Diablo 2 and Dungeon Fighter Online.","[Big news! Big news!] In the big group chats such as the Legend of Sword and Fairy and Mr. Fang’s Group Tour, Shen Qingqing posted the news, [The shop owner revealed that the next game is called World of Warcraft, a massively online game just like the Legend of Mir 2 and Dungeon Fighter Online! It’s not a single-player game!]","“According to the newest information, Dungeon Fighter Online might get an updated version!”","“A massively online game named World of Warcraft?!”","“An updated version of Dungeon Fighter Online?”","Jiang Xiaoyue yelled, “How did you all know it?! How come I know nothing about it?!”","She was angry!","“Don’t fight! What’s this World of Warcraft about?!” The person making the comment was Xi Qi, a veteran player and one of Song Qingfeng’s classmate. “Does it mean that the world is full of demons and wild beasts?”","...","In the Post Bar, many posts appeared on the forum, and some of them were titled, [Hot Headline: The Imminent New Game Is a Massively Online Game!] and [I’m Buddies with Mr. Fang Series: The Detailed Analysis of World of Warcraft with Potential Trailer Leaking out Before the Official Release]","“...” Mr. Fang looked puzzled. I only revealed the name, and you guys came up with a detailed analysis? With a trailer?!","Mr. Fang even clicked the link. When the video played, he saw a yellow mouse yelling, “Pikapika!”","“...” Mr. Fang’s face darkened and thought, Damn! What a clickbait!","Then, he deleted the post and banned the user who posted it.","...","Meanwhile, a big event seemed to have happened in the neighboring Stan Nation. The imprisoned assassins were rescued by a group of people who claimed to be from the Brotherhood.","Similar things were happening in other areas frequently as well.","“Damn it! These damn people!” Meanwhile, Head Priest Cesare of the Judgement Godly Palace in the Stan Nation was enraged and had shattered everything that he could see.","...","“Hahahaha! Another group of morons clicked my link!” In the Half City Shop, a black cloud reached out two arms condensed from black mist and clapped while laughing. “Is Pokémon interesting? I...”","Before he could finish, Ning Bi who was sitting at the computer across from him yelled, “Smirk Face Emoji, you’re banned!”","“Pu-! Who?! Who did it?!”","...","“According to the shop owner, an online game means that the players from different shops can enter the same big mystical realm...?” The players in the new shop were talking among themselves while sitting on couches. “It’s said that before the World of Warcraft is released, the shop will connect us with the players from other shops through the internet...?”","“Ugh? Is this shop very famous in the East Continent?” Sala asked curiously.","“I suppose it is,” Elder Sewell said while thinking, “Resident Evil, Assassin’s Creed, and the Legend of Sword and Fairy are all huge projects. I think this shop must be a very big agent for games... It’s no wonder that it doesn’t take names of any workshops.”","“It’s said that the creator of World of Warcraft is... um... the Blizzard Workshop? Is it better than the previous ones?”","The players who hadn’t finished the Legend of Sword and Fairy 4 were still battling in the game. As the earliest group of players, the elves and knights had finished the game and thus had more free time on hand.","Whenever they had time, these people would gather at the lounge area with a mug of Cappuccino and talk about the new game.","“It’s said that the shop will release the trailer of the new game tomorrow,” Sala said in boredom, “Why isn’t it released today?! I can’t wait to watch it!”","“It won’t be released on the big screen until tomorrow at noon,” Elder Sewell added in frustration, “Can’t it be released in the morning?”","“Ohoho!” Dwarf Elder Sauk sat on a couch with a few other stocky dwarves. “Eastern alchemy is miraculous. Oh, I should call it artifact-making skills. I look forward to trying this new mystical realm! I think I should recommend it to my people in the Black Iron Castle.”","Although the dwarves couldn’t change their profession and become artifact masters, they could get inspired and learn a few things from this new field of knowledge.","“I’ve sent a message back home, Elder Sauk.” Elder Sewell sipped her Cappuccino and said mildly, “Please don’t tell too many people about it. Otherwise, we’ll have no seats for ourselves!”","“Sorry, guys!” Old Mage Adolf walked up from behind them and said, “I think our magic communication system has spread the news all over the world! At least... many mages have gotten the news.”","“You can see the effects.” He said as he pointed at the big group of new customers who came to the shop after watching Mr. Fang’s livestream of artifact making.","“I think... tomorrow, the customers in this shop will double. Get prepared, old friends!”"]},{"number":675,"title":"Chapter 675 - The Vastest Game World!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","There was more than one big screen to watch livestreams in the old shops. Several neighboring sections shared one lounge area and one big livestreaming screen.","In the new shop, Mr. Fang expanded the space to accommodate 20,000 computers in one go. Of course, this consumed a lot of system energy.","Just like the space-folding technology used in the old shops, the shop was divided into ten sections. Since most of the sections were empty, Mr. Fang didn’t open all of them to the public. Right now, only about 2,000 computers were for public use in the new shop.","The shop barely had a full house at the busiest hours.","...","– Meanwhile, in the Yuanyang City Shop –","“Should we report this to our superiors? How come the mystical realms in this forgotten continent look more powerful than ours?!” The two black-cloaked, dignified-looking messengers came from the distant... the legendary place where ancient factions had ‘ascended’ to.","“Let’s check out World of Warcraft first!” The fat messenger said, “If it’s as good as the others, we should inform our faction by passing back a message!”","...","– Noon of the next day –","All the players in the new shop and the old shops, regardless if they had been playing games or waiting to get online, were all gathering at the lounge areas.","In the new shop at Canglan City, someone even paid to have the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection on the White Pigeon Square broadcast the trailer.","“It’s almost time!” Dwarf Elder Sauk glanced at the time and said, “Only ten seconds left.”","At this moment, many people stood before the big screens in the new shop.","“Ten!”","“Nine!”","“Eight!”","“...”","The excellence of Assassin’s Creed and the Legend of Sword and Fairy obviously gave the veteran players in the new shop great confidence in the new game. They all counted down with great anticipation.","“Three!”","“Two!”","“One!”","“It begins! It is beginning!”","“Look!”","Suddenly, sounds came, and images appeared on the big screens.","It was an old map that looked old and had a yellow-tone.","There were two huge continents on the map. In the center was a whirlpool that almost occupied the whole sea area.","“Four years have passed since the mortal races banded together and stood united against the might of the Burning Legion.” A voice introduced the background, and it felt like the curtain before a grand world was slowly lifted. “Though Azeroth was saved, the tenuous pact between the Horde and the Alliance has all but evaporated. The drums of war thunder once again.”","The initial stage of World of Warcraft didn’t begin from the war with the Burning Legion. Despite the previous great war, the game began with the conflicts between the Alliance and the Horde. It was going to start with something simple and slowly lead up to the more important issues.","When the huge map vanished, a dwarf’s face appeared on the top of the snow mountain.","“Oh! How come this guy’s nose is so big?” Obviously, the players in the old shops had never seen such people before.","The camera zoomed out and showed a dwarf with bulging muscles and a long brown beard. Dressed in leather armor, he was holding a firearm that was even taller than himself.","“A dwarf?!” Elder Sauk said loudly, “Oh! I’m sure that he’s one of us! He looks shorter than us but is very strong!”","In the snow storm, a roaring brown bear walked forward with the dwarf one step at a time.","The audience could still see a huge fortress in the distant mountains.","“Is this mystical realm... custom-made for dwarves?” Elder Sauk laughed, “There’re dwarves in it! I must try this mystical realm!”","In the next scene, a night elf who had greyish-blue skin and was wearing exquisite light armor looked around in a forest and then darted off nimbly as if she had sensed that a large group of people was looking at her.","“Is she an elf?!” Elf Girl Sala asked curiously, “How come her skin is greyish-blue?”","“And this elf’s ears are much longer and very pointy!” In the back of the audience, Elina studied the ears of the elves around her and found that none of them had ears as long or as pointy. “How come there is an elf like her.”","The night elf ran nimbly in the forest and then lunged forward, turning into a tiger.","“Oh! Did this elf transform from a tiger?!”","The elves watched the scene with great curiosity.","On a patch of withering land, a decayed, zombie-like foot stepped on this land, seeming to have left flames on the ground. Then, the land with some remnant green plants decayed and turned into a dark deathly grey.","Looking up, the audience saw a face that looked like a skull, and the Infernal behind this figure was blazing with green flames and looked like a small mountain, letting out earth-shaking roars.","“What’s this thing?!” The audience obviously had never seen the undead race.","“Ya! Look!” On the screen, an armored creature with a bullhead and a human body spread out its body slowly.","In the distance, the sun rose into the sky. Looking down from the cliff, they saw a magnificent view of a land dyed in purple by the morning sunlight. The winding rivers and mountains on the land formed a breathtaking view.","“This looks like...”","“This is the orc?!”","“Hahaha! This orc is ugly even for the orc race!”","“Hey! This is a mage!” The sharp-eyed Adolf saw a human mage on the screen. With blazing flames in his hands, he was battling with a huge Infernal. Ice and frost gathered in the mage’s hands, and snowflakes flew in the howling wind.","The mystical realm has all kinds of races?!","But...","This trailer only showed that each race could find their counterparts in the mystical realm, but...","What is special and unique about this mystical realm compared to others?","Was its only advantage over other mystical realms the many races from which they could choose?","Still, many people felt puzzled.","At this moment...","“Come and take a look! There’s an introduction on the game’s official website!” Soon, people found that an official website of the game had appeared in the shop, and they clicked on it immediately.","“World of Warcraft is a nearly complete virtual world in which you can do almost anything you can do in the real world, including touring the continents, exploring the unknown places, and living as one of the races in this world.”","As everyone knew, in the Legend of Sword and Fairy or other games, even though the players could travel 1,000 kilometers in one instant with the sword control technique, they still couldn’t travel around the whole earth. The games had restrictions in this area.","It was the same with Dungeon Fighter Online.","However, in the World of Warcraft, if the players were patient, they could travel all over the planet!","On the map, there were two huge continents on this planet. In other words, this mystical realm was vaster than everyone could have imagined! The area that the game provided for the players to explore was as big as a real planet, a small one at least.","In this game world, there lived some existences far higher than humans.","Meanwhile, the official website announced that the maximum game time for each day was extended by two hours, and the players could ‘borrow game time’ from the next day if they found that ten hours were not enough for one day.","Of course, this policy was only used for special occasions and couldn’t be used every day.","Meanwhile, the business hours of the shop were going to be modified. The operation hours were getting longer.","The information provided by the shop only showed the players an unprecedented game (mystical realm) and different races. As for what they could gain from the game and other unknown stuff, the players must find out themselves."]},{"number":676,"title":"Chapter 676 - Here Comes a Dog-Headed Man?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","It was obvious that World of Warcraft was much more massive than any of the previous games.","Its scale and magnitude surpassed all the past games.","Right now, the players in the new shop were not worried about the quality of the mystical realm, but whether this huge world frame could sustain itself or not. In other words, they wondered which superpower in the ‘East Continent’ was running this mystical realm.","As for other aspects...","If this force could produce such a huge mystical realm, its overall abilities would be at least as great as the major workshops such as the Dulan Workshop.","There was no need to worry about the quality.","At this moment, the people who had just finished watching the broadcast on White Pigeon Square in Canglan City and the players in the new shops all looked very curious.","“Blizzard Entertainment?”","The players in the new shop knew nothing about this name. They stared at the logo and wondered, What workshop is this Blizzard Entertainment? Is it really so powerful?","Meanwhile, the players in the old shops were amazed. “Hiss-! Each game created by this Senior Blizzard is a high-end product!”","They knew Blizzard was the creator of masterpieces such as Diablo 2 and StarCraft. They had been wondering what Blizzard was doing recently since nothing came out of this brand for a while, and they didn’t expect it to suddenly release such a huge game!","“Young Master Song, we must buy World of Warcraft!” Lin Shao and Xu Luo browsed the information on the official website and exclaimed repeatedly.","“It’s not a problem of buying it or not!” Song Qingfeng looked at them in disdain and said, “It seems that there are two opposing sides in World of Warcraft. If we choose different sides, according to the information on the website, we will even have a hard time talking in the game. Right now, we must consider which side we should join.”","In Dungeon Fighter Online, the players usually fought in the dungeons and the dojos, which meant that the conflicts among players were not as fierce as those in the Legend of Mir 2. It was overall peaceful.","The players could play together even if they were from different guilds.","However, in World of Warcraft, the Alliance and the Horde spoke different languages since these two sides were naturally hostile to each other. If they chose the wrong side, they couldn’t even form a team to do quests together.","“Should we consult our class president?” Nalan Mingxue had been the class president of Class A ever since they were in the Huang House. “Let’s ask Instructor Mu if she wants to play the game or not. If she does, we must join the same side!”","At this moment, in Mr. Fang’s Group Tour group chat, Black Demon of Half City posted a question with the title as Black Demon Guild President, [@Speaker of the Royal Clan Guild, which side are you guys planning to enter? How about we enter opposite sides.]","Tang Yuan, the Yuanheng Pavilion Master, immediately chimed in. [Are you ready to fight again?]","...","At this moment, Nalan Mingxue was browsing the information about the two opposing sides, classes, and races on the official website.","In the new shop in Canglan City, the elves were talking animatedly among themselves while browsing the official website. “Elder! Elder! What race do we choose?”","“We’ll certainly choose to be elves!” Elder Sewell said without hesitation, obviously very proud to be an elf.","Then, she glanced at the young elves in disdain and thought, Are you planning to choose other races?","“But...” Elf Girl Sala pointed at the information on the official website and said, “The leader of the Forsaken is also an elf...”","“Besides...” Another elf said, “Elder, this race, blood elf, isn’t open yet, but they look quite like us! The night elf has dark skin and doesn’t look good! I think we should join the Forsaken and fight with this elf leader to get familiar with this new mystical realm. Then, we can enter the advanced elf race (Blood Elf).”","“No! No!” Elder Sewell shook her head and said, “The night elves loves nature, which fits the values of our Elf Clan! We shouldn’t focus on the appearances, my children!”","“Um... there’s nothing wrong with dark skin... I think it looks good,” Mr. Fang chimed in while he walked past them.","“...”","“Humph! Human’s aesthetics!”","“It doesn’t look good at all!” They glanced at Mr. Fang in disdain.","Ignoring him, they continued their discussion.","Obviously, the elves had a heated discussion about this topic.","...","The people on the Nora Continent were used to the humanoid races living in this world.","Examples of these humanoid races were the various clans who lived in the Orc Mountains which were far from the Morning Light Empire.","It must be noted that they were not green-skinned orcs in World of Warcraft. They looked more like the beast people who had bull and wolf heads, could walk upright, and speak human languages.","That was why the players in the new shop thought that the tauren in the trailer was an orc.","The orc was a special race. It was said that their gods had gifted wild beasts with intelligence and the ability to speak human languages, allowing them to evolve from being wild beasts that drank blood and ate raw flesh. After generations of evolvement, they had obtained their current appearances.","On this extremely vast continent, they had their own kingdoms and their unique civilizations.","However, it was a pity that there wasn’t a beast-person in the shop yet.","“Ah-! Mistake! It’s a big mistake!” Mr. Fang’s head hurt when he thought of something. When he first came to the continent, he had seen many humanoid creatures with bull heads and tiger heads. But after he came to this city, he hadn’t seen any such creatures!","“Um? Sir...?” Assassin Harrison saw the painful look on Mr. Fang’s face, and he asked, “What’s wrong...?”","“Um...” Mr. Fang raised his head and said in frustration, “Do you know why we don’t see any orcs in this nation?”","“Orcs...?” Harrison asked curiously, “Why did you ask this question? The reason is simple; this nation is far from the orc kingdoms. It’s natural that we rarely see any of them here.”","“What should I do...?” Would he have to go and kidnap some orcs from another nation?","– Meanwhile, outside the gate of the Canglan City –","“My goodness! This is indeed a beautiful place! Thanks for tuning into the ‘Tour in Human Nations’ hosted by Mr. Dirk. Now, you’re looking at the prosperous Canglan City of the famous human nation, Morning Light Empire!” An orc with a head similar to that of a Shiba Inu stood before the city gate. Wearing light armor and a bright red scarf, he spread out his arms and exclaimed, “This is indeed a bustling human nation!”","Beside him was a stout and chubby orc with a black bull head. He was wearing leather armor, and he had a simple stone magic wand. This wand was stuck into the ground, and it supported a top-quality magic crystal. This crystal seemed to be able to capture all the visuals around it, working like a Spiritual Spell Visual Projection."]},{"number":677,"title":"Chapter 677 - The Undead Rogue in Deathknell","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","At this moment, besides elves, dwarves were also considering which race they should choose, dwarves or gnomes, and which class they should choose.","Meanwhile, a new group of assassins came to the shop.","They were the assassins rescued by the newly-established Brotherhood from Stan Nation and other neighboring nations.","“Before the release of the new mystical realm, you guys can try Assassin’s Creed.” Harrison, Elina, and other senior members of the Brotherhood introduced them to Assassin’s Creed.","...","The new official website had introductions of various races, classes, and race leaders.","In the days before World of Warcraft was released, many players were talking about this.","– Lingyun Academy, the main road beside the martial arts field –","At this moment, some disciples were taking a break on a slope beside the main road after the combat technique class.","“Our class president plans to choose the Horde?” Xi Qi, a veteran player and Song Qingfeng’s classmate, looked at his communication jade in surprise. “No... I don’t see any race I like in the Horde!”","[Undead is a new race that I never played before. I want to try it,] Nalan Mingxue said in the group chat.","They had only seen necromancers in Diablo 2, and the only impression of undead that the players in the old shops got was that they were all skeletons.","However, Nalan Mingxue found that the Forsaken race was very special and wanted to try it.","[I heard that the Royal Clan Guild has chosen the human race, right?]","Nalan Mingxue said, [Yeah. They talked about it for a long time before making the decision. Shengjing Academy also chose the Alliance.]","[Okay! Okay! We must stick together. Let’s join the Horde.] Song Qingfeng said in the group chat, [I’ll play a Tauren since I’ve never played such a character before...]","...","“Commander, what should we choose?” a knight of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion asked.","“Without saying, we must choose the human race and be Paladins!” Commander Elven said proudly, “This name sounds lofty with the word ‘saint’ in it. I’m sure it’s the most powerful class!”","[TL Note: Paladin is called Saint Knight in Chinese.]","“Excellent decision, Commander!” The knight yelled, “I also think that knights with the word ‘saint’ in the title are super powerful!”","In his mind, the scenario where he battled against many opponents on his own appeared.","...","“Do you know why I came to this city?” At this moment, a dog-headed man walked into the shop. With his grey hair and mane meticulously combed, he wore a set of unique silver armor. The moment he entered the shop, his eyes widened. While looking around, he said in shock, “I’m surprised! Can you believe that this shop looks more high-end than the Lava Workshop and Dulan Workshop?”","“Before I came, I asked about it and heard that this is a representative shop for the East Continent. I heard that it’s going to release a new massive mystical realm that has something to do with us orcs. So, we are coming here to check it out.” With that said, he walked deeper into the shop with the bull-headed man.","“Um...? Isn’t that Mr. Dirk?!” Helen of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion was talking about the classes in the lounge area, and she suddenly turned her head.","Mr. Dirk was a famous rogue of the Orc Clan since he liked to record his travels with Spiritual Spell Visual Projection whenever he went to a new place. Of course, this was only his hobby since...","“No wonder Mr. Dirk hasn’t done any Spiritual Spell Visual Projection for the major workshops lately...” Helen said in a huff, “It’s because he came here!”","In the distant orc kingdom, some people could afford the projection crystals which could receive Spiritual Spell Visual Projections. Many people liked to watch the Spiritual Spell Visual Projections from the nearby Alchemist Union branches. Obviously, many people were watching this scene right now.","While Helen glared at him in frustration, this beast man went directly toward the counter.","Mr. Fang was sipping his Cappuccino when he heard someone knocking on the counter. Then, he saw the head of a Shiba Inu, and he asked, “Where did this dog...”","“Pu-!” Helen almost stumbled and dropped to the ground.","She almost walked up and told Mr. Fang that this man was an orc!","“Headed man?” Mr. Fang quickly reacted and added two more words after ‘dog’, calling this guest a dog-headed man.","“Two magic crystals per hour! The activation prices for the games are on the small blackboard...” While his face twitched, he thought, How come orcs look like this?","Then, he blinked and discovered that there was a bull beside the dog. “...”","However, with their appearances, Fang Qi finally completed his task.","[New Task: Cross-Era Masterpiece – World of Warcraft (Completed)","Task Target: 1. The reputation of the new shop reaches 100,000 people (Completed);","2. Players include people from other races such as elves, orcs, and dwarves (Completed)","Task Privilege: receive the original cinematic trailer, the right to design your own trailer, and the right to host small-scale events","Task Reward: Upgrade and combine the TV Series and Movie Cultivation Room and the Game Cultivation Room; ten-day access to the new cultivation room]","Fang Qi glanced at the system version of World of Warcraft that was the reward.","The system version of World of Warcraft costs 15 magic crystals or crystals for 1350 minutes, and 30 magic crystals or crystals could buy 2700 minutes, so on and so forth.","[New Task: Cross-Era Masterpiece Following Task 1: New Chapter, Burning Crusade (it can only be released after basic requirements are met)","Task Target: The new shop’s degree of reputation reaches 500,000 people; the degree of reputation of World of Warcraft reaches 300,000","After the task is completed, the system will upgrade automatically. Then, the host can actively seek and meet the requirements for the update of other games.","After the upgrade, the shop can establish regional branch shops. The host can send employees to manage these branch shops.","Task Reward: The Ring of the Gaming King (Special item. When being worn, +5% synchronization with all game characters, +20% cultivation strength and skills gains in the cultivation room, +10% compatibility with the game characters, and -10% consumption of Complete Synchronization)","With higher compatibility with the game characters, the host will get used to the characters faster.]","Mr. Fang froze. “We have such things?!”","Obviously, this was a must-do task. Although Mr. Fang now had the right to release World of Warcraft, he decided to release it tomorrow morning.","Meanwhile, the new shop had begun recruiting employees; he would need more than one employee. Since the business hours of the shop were increasing, two shifts were required even though three shifts weren’t necessary at the moment.","For the management of the shop, Mr. Fang pulled some people from the old shops. He decided to move Li Xin’er to here from Yuanyang City Shop first. Since Xiaoyue was coming to the new shop soon, he decided to let Li Lanruo come with her as well.","Meanwhile, some people had gotten the news from Mr. Fang.","“Tomorrow?!”","“World of Warcraft will be released tomorrow?!”","“My goodness! We haven’t decided which side to join yet!” The elves exclaimed.","Mr. Fang’s face darkened. “How many days have you been talking about it?!”","...","On the next day, the number of players in the shop were obviously larger than usual with dwarves, elves, mages, large groups of mercenaries, and new assassins all coming into the shop.","In fact, there were also many new players who had come to the shop from other cities after they got the news.","Mr. Dirk of the Orc Clan was one of them.","“My goodness!” Mr. Dirk came to the shop at 8 AM sharp and found that the entrance was crammed with people.","“So many people?!”","The elves had come very early and waited by the door, looking as if they were about to break into the shop.","“What’s wrong?!” One elf checked the time. “It’s only five minutes to eight! It’s still silent inside!”","“Sir! Get up!”","“What are you yelling about!” A figure hurried down the stairs inside the shop, looking groggy. Obviously, he had just gotten up from bed.","“Lazy shop owner.” Upon entering the shop, Elf Girl Sala gave Mr. Fang a dirty look.","Before she could finish, many people behind her swarmed up to the empty seats.","“Oh-! Quickly take seats!” Sala exclaimed and dashed to a nearby seat and plunked down as swiftly as a bunny!","Then, she gave Mr. Fang a disapproving look and said, “You get up at 8 o’clock each morning! How lazy you are! You can sleep to death if you want!”","It must be noted that these elves usually cultivated during the night and came out when the sky barely got bright again.","In Silver Moon Forest, early morning was the perfect time for everything. Even the fruits tasted the best in the early morning.","They were not like the scummy shop owner who slept until 8 AM when the sun was high up in the sky.","The elves had had heated discussions over the past couple of days about which side to join!","Finally, some elves decided to join the night elf race while others joined the Forsaken race led by Sylvanas.","With a free nature, the elves wanted to try different things to make better decisions.","“Ugh?” Sala saw Mr. Fang sitting down one seat away from her. “Don’t you need to keep an eye on the shop?”","Mr. Fang pointed in the direction of the counter where two girls suddenly appeared. “I moved two employees over from the old shops.”","“So that you can play the game?” Elf Girl Sala looked at him in disdain.","Sitting between them, Helen glanced at Mr. Fang’s screen and asked, “Sir, are you going to play as well?”","“Why not?” Mr. Fang pulled his computer chair closer to the desk and double clicked on the logo on the desktop.","While the game was loading, he picked up a bottle of Sprite and took a swig.","“Sir, what class are you choosing?”","With great familiarity, Mr. Fang chose the undead race and the rogue class, and he created the ID [Midnight Pig Butcher].","Then, he entered the game and finished the process in one breath.","At this moment, Mr. Fang appeared at the spawn spot, Deathknell, which was located on Azeroth.","The elves sitting nearby were still deliberating over which face looked better. In the system version, the players could do some adjustments to their faces, and the undead players could even adjust the degree of decay. Some players even complained that the Forsaken had withered faces, sounding like they weren’t here for the gameplay in World of Warcraft.","Helen glanced at Mr. Fang and found that he appeared in the game just as a skeleton."]},{"number":678,"title":"Chapter 678 - You’re Entrusted with the Glorious Task of Saving Humans!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Hey! Hey! What classes did you guys choose?” In the Yuanyang City Shop, many disciples of Heavenly Academy had chosen to join the Alliance.","“Mage.” Xun Yuan, the genius of the Xun Family, said, “Did you have to ask?”","“I plan to play as a human warrior. What about you, Xiaoyue?” Yue Bai and Mu Qing, Jiang Xiaoyue’s good friends in the Heavenly Academy, had made their decisions.","Jiang Xiaoyue looked at their screens and then at the screen of the big white deer. “Little Bell, what did you choose?”","“I saw them all choosing the orc or tauren, so I followed suit and chose tauren too!” The big white deer complained in its baby voice, “There are only bull-headed people but no deer-headed people?”","The demon clan obviously all chose the Horde.","Meanwhile...","“Ugh? Elder Su is livestreaming again!” Obviously, some players came too late and couldn’t find a seat. For example, the disciples traveling from the distant Three Saint Gates. They had no choice but to watch the livestream first to get a glimpse of the game.","When the players chose characters in World of Warcraft, they could only choose the facial styles and make some minor adjustments. Of course, humans and night elves obviously had two different aesthetic styles. Su Tianji, who was livestreaming, looked torn. “Ugh? Can you guys help me make the choice? Which do you think looks better?”","[Let’s get out of here!]","[Trash Elder Su, some players have leveled up several times now, and you are still choosing your character.]","[Idle streamer.]","[Can’t you choose the gnome?]","Su Tianji replied, “Why! You haters! I won’t ask you again!”","...","Meanwhile, in the new shop in Canglan City, the dog-headed man looked more professional.","“Welcome to the show hosted by Mr. Dirk.”","“It’s said that this is a mystical realm consisting of two continents. I wonder if we’ll encounter friends from other continents in this mystical realm.” This orc placed a stand supporting the magic crystal beside him and said, “I haven’t learned all the functions of the high-end magic item in this shop yet, but you can see on the screen that I’ve chosen a bull-headed orc. I think this is an orc. Hiss... I wonder why the orc race in this mystical realm doesn’t include our kind. It’s strange...”","“Oh... No! No! How come the green-skinned creatures are orcs? Which clan do they come from...? I don’t remember any orcs in our clan looking like this...”","“But I think we should put more focus on their talents. It seems that each race has its own unique talents. Now, let’s first see...”","Obviously, there were many people watching this Spiritual Spell Visual Projection; they were mostly fans of cultivation mystical realms and would have discussions through the methods such as magic letters or Spiritual Spell Visual Projections.","Of course, they usually used magic letters which were more affordable.","Beside a windowsill covered by violet stock flowers, a unique quill drip pen was writing neat words on a pure white letter paper by itself as if it was alive.","After the written conversation was the signature of the writer. Of course, it was not the true name of the writer.","“What am I seeing? I’m watching Mr. Dirk enter an unknown mystical realm?” – From Minor Mage Andre.","“It’s World of Warcraft which is said to be a product of the Blizzard Workshop in the East Continent; it’s not an unknown mystical realm, Friend.”– From Sky Ocean Knight Legion.","“I heard that this mystical realm consists of two huge continents and is more massive than we can imagine. But I wonder if they are just bluffing.”– From Wolf-Headed Man.","“We can’t rule out this possibility.”– From Platinum Mage.","...","Each race in World of Warcraft had its own unique talents which could change the battle style of different classes in some degree. For example, the Shadowmeld of Night Elves could be used instantly and enable the Night Elf to slip into the shadow, thus decreasing the chance of being detected by the enemies.","It could last until the player cancelled it or upon moving.","Shadowmeld could be combined with the stealth skill of night elf rogues or druids.","Finally, with the suggestions from the viewers, Su Tianji, who wanted to play the mage class, chose to be a human mage and entered the game.","Despite their hesitation at the character-creation interface and wasting time there, most players including elves, dwarves, and orcs had all entered the game by now.","“The noble humans of Stormwind are a proud, tenacious race.” Right now, Su Tianji was watching the cinematics at the beginning of the game for the human race. Before her was a solid fortress built with huge boulders. While the huge stone statues of different races such as humans, dwarves, and elves were revealed to the players, the passionate voice narrated the past of Stormwind City. The whole fortress slowly displayed itself before the human players. “Though the recent invasion of the demonic Burning Legion decimated their sister kingdom of Lordaeron, the defenders of Stormwind stand vigilant against any who would threaten the sanctity of their lands... Stormwind City is one of the last bastions of human power in the world...”","The narrative voice grew more passionate with the rise of the music, “Backed by their stalwart allies, the armies of Stormwind have been called away to once again fight the savage Horde on distant battlefields. With the armies gone, the defense of Stormwind now falls to its proud citizens.!”","The scene slowly turned from the Stormwind City to a beautiful human female mage in Northshire Abbey. She had just created her character. “You must defend the kingdom against the foul mongrels that encroach upon it and hunt down the subversive traitors who seek to destroy it from within. Now is the time for heroes. Now humanity’s greatest chapter can be told!”","“Oh! Isn’t it me!” Su Tianji suddenly felt like someone was patting her on the shoulder, entrusting her with the responsibility of humanity’s future. “Am I so powerful?!”","She was instantly worked up. “Is it going to be similar to the Legend of Sword and Fairy later on where I can say that I control my own destiny, not the Heavens?”","She got excited by the prospect of her great achievements on this continent!","...","At this moment, the elves were also watching the cinematics after creating night elf characters or the Forsaken characters. While many players had entered the game, some dwarves and orcs had just begun watching the cinematics..."]},{"number":679,"title":"Chapter 679 - Who Is the Greatest Race?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Bound to the iron will of the tyrant Lich King...” Elf Girl Sala had chosen the Forsaken led by Sylvanas. Before her was a huge, gloomy, and decayed forest. “The vast undead armies of the Scourge seek to eradicate all life on Azeroth. Led by the banshee Sylvanas Windrunner, a group of renegades broke away from the Scourge, and freed themselves of the Lich King’s domination. Known by some as the Forsaken, this group fights a constant battle not only to retain their freedom from the Scourge, but also to slaughter those who would hunt them as monsters...”","“I think this race... is awesome!” some elves murmured to themselves while watching the cinematics.","“For ten thousand years, the immortal night elves cultivated a druidic society within the shadowed recesses of Ashenvale Forest. Yet recently, the catastrophic invasion of the Burning Legion shattered the tranquility of their ancient civilization. Led by the Arch-Druid Malfurion Stormrage and the Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind, the mighty night elves rose to challenge the demonic onslaught. Though victorious...”","“The night elves were forced to sacrifice their cherished immortality and watch their beloved forests burn ... As one of the few left in the world, it is your sworn duty to defend Darnassus and the wild children of nature against the Legion’s encroaching corruption...”","Elder Sewell and many other elves had chosen the night elf race, and they thought, “My goodness! The night elves are indeed a great race! We made the right decision of choosing it! Sala must be regretting her choice now!”","...","Meanwhile, the orcs were watching the opening cinematics of the game through the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection.","“Long ago, the orcish horde was corrupted by the Burning Legion and lured to the world of Azeroth. For generations, the orcs made war upon the human kingdoms of Stormwind and Lordaeron. Though the Horde was ultimately defeated, a visionary young warchief named Thrall rose to lead his people in their darkest hour. Under Thrall’s rule, the orcs freed themselves from the chains of demonic corruption and embraced their shamanistic heritage...”","“Based in the warrior city of Orgrimmar, they stand ready to destroy all who would challenge their supremacy!”","Looking at the huge orc city in Durotar Valley, a player yelled, “My goodness! I made the right choice! This is a huge mystical realm only a big workshop can produce. This orc looks weird, but...","“It’s compatible to the beliefs of our Orc Clan. Now, we need to defend Lordaeron...” Mr. Dirk stuck out his tongue. “No, defend Orgrimma?”","“This name is so difficult to remember... what Orgrimma... Lordaeron... The alchemists of the East Continent always like these weird names?”","“That’s embarrassing!”","“Orcs: we have a traitor among us!”","“...”","The audience from all over the world enthusiastically wrote down their comments on the magic letters.","Meanwhile, Mr. Dirk stretched his body in the game.","“You’ve finally grown up, Mr. Dirk.” Village Chief Kartuk walked up and sized up the new orc. “You can join the battle in the name of the Horde and fight for the glory of the Warchief!”","“Of course. I’ll kick out all the enemies who dare to challenge us orcs!” Mr. Dirk yelled without thinking and then froze. “Ugh? This mystical realm... is intriguing.”","Then, he glanced around and said, “So many people...! Guys, do you see them... Are they people from the East Continent? I’ll go and greet them... Of course, we might speak different languages.”","At this moment, there were many orc players in the Valley of Trials, and it was the same in the Deathknell.","The undead had high resistance against fear, sleep, and charms. When they concentrated, they were immune to most of these spells. This was their natural gift.","Regardless if they were in melee combat or ranged combat, it was deadly if the players were controlled by these spells. This gift enabled the undead to be competent for most classes.","In the Jiuhua City Shop, Nalan Mingxue controlled her little undead warrior to walk around in Deathknell.","“How come there are so many people here...?” Her companion Lan Yan had just come out of the graveyard. While looking around at the bustling mages, warriors, and undead rogues, she said, “I feel like there are more people than in Dungeon Fighter Online?”","“Everyone says that the undead are ugly, but there are so many people playing this race?!” They were dazed by the scene.","After walking out of the town, they saw tall evergreen trees and shrubs everywhere. In the dense Tirisfal Glades where no sunshine could penetrate inside, there were many zombies and skeletons as if it was a ghost town. The players were amazed that they were a part of them.","“It seems like we are a part of them.”","“But I don’t like the scenery here...” Suddenly, they saw two undead with pointy ears passing by.","The ears looked like those of an elf, but they were less pointy and shorter than those of night elves.","“Ugh...? These people...?” While rubbing her eyes, Lan Yan thought that she had seen it wrong. Immediately, she walked up and asked, “Excuse me, can we choose the elf race in the undead race? How did you choose the race...?”","“Ugh?” Sala was nonplussed. “We’re born as elves. We didn’t choose to be elves...”","After all, it was a feature that they were born with.","“Wait a second. Are you from the Elf Clan that the shop owner once mentioned?!” Nalan Mingxue froze.","“My goodness!”","“What elf?! We have elves here?!”","Immediately, many players from the old shops swarmed up.","“Are you people from... the East Continent?” Elf Girl Sala was amazed that she encountered people from a place hundreds of thousands of kilometers away.","“Do you want to join us and do quests together?” Nalan Mingxue sent an invitation.","“Can I...?”","“Of course!”","“Join the group! Join the group!” Sia quickly joined the group and went to kill mobs cheerfully.","Most elves had chosen warriors and mages. After spawning, they would watch some introductions about the undead, and they then got the quest to eliminate the brainless zombies outside Deathknell.","“Maybe they were once your peers or brothers, but they had fallen and are now slaves of the Lich King.”","Obviously, this was a process for the players to learn the history of the Forsaken.","...","At this moment, Elder Sewell put down her virtual reality headset and glanced over. “How are you doing, Little Sala? Do you want to join the night elves in the Alliance?”","“No way...” Sala was busy doing quests with her new teammates. “This Forsaken race is very powerful!”","“How can it be?” Elder Sewell said curiously, “I watched the cinematics. These savage members of the Horde were defeated in the previous war!”","“No! No! We, the Forsaken, were defeated because we were fighting both the Burning Legion and the slaves of the Lich King at the same time!” Sala refuted with the little knowledge that she just learned about the history of the Forsaken.","“Impossible! We, the night elves, defeated the Burning Legion before!”","“Oh! We also have to deal with something called the Scourge Army...” Sala was still confused with all these legions and armies which sounded quite powerful. “They are people who escaped from the evil Lich King. They were once defeated but will rally in the future! This is a great race with a strong will!”","“Hiss-! What’s going on?” Elder Sewell was baffled as she thought, Aren’t we, the night elves, the greatest race? After all, it was what the opening cinematic had said."]},{"number":680,"title":"Chapter 680 - A Totally Different Life","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","In the dark and gloomy Tirisfal Glades, the dilapidated town and the decaying houses littered this cursed land. All kinds of undead creatures bustled in this forest.","It was a brand-new feeling to wander around the huge Azeroth Continent as an undead.","“Beware the living!” In Deathknell, the players heard such warnings constantly. For the living creatures, the undead were absolutely freaks and monsters","“They themselves are monsters!” Elf Girl Sala said while fighting the mobs in the forest, “While dealing with these monsters, we have to be wary of all people. We’re all fighting the evil Burning Legion, right? Why can’t they stop bothering us?”","Those people just hate us because of our looks! Sala thought resentfully while searching for useful equipment with Nalan Mingxue and others in Deathknell.","“Excuse me, are you really an elf?” Lan Yan had been staring at the elves with great curiosity. In the game, the Horde used one language while the Alliance used another, which meant that communication wasn’t a problem for them. After all, both the Spiritual State language and Nora Continent language became the languages of the Horde and Alliance in the game.","Since the characters in the game had memories of their respective languages, the players could understand each other.","“Of course!” Soon, they each collected a bag of equipment and returned cheerfully.","Even the trash equipment could be used to trade for some items from the undead guards.","Of course, experience points were the most valuable thing.","...","“Ms. Sala, you really don’t want to join our human army of the Alliance?” The members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion sitting nearby obviously had the same grand feeling of being endowed with the task of saving the world as Su Tianji did.","Of course, they were now playing the characters who were recruited to defend the homeland and the Alliance.","Right now, Stormwind City was facing a great threat. With their army stationed overseas, their home lacked manpower, which was why the newly-recruited players must defeat the enemies from the outside and remove the internal conflicts, shouldering a portion of the responsibilities.","Obviously, it was a lofty cause to contribute to the kingdom’s prosperity and safety.","“I’m proud for making the wise decision to become a human paladin! Haha!” This identity gave these knights a sense of achievement and responsibility, and the golden griffin knights laughed.","After all, their responsibility in the real world was defending the city. With the entire city prosperous and peaceful, they were now quite idle.","A golden griffin knight had platinum-colored lights flashing on his hands. “The warm holy light can swiftly heal any injuries. Isn’t it awesome?!”","Among all the spells, the holy light spells had the fastest healing speed. There were healing spells in other games, but their healing speeds were relatively slower.","“I think our opponents will feel hopeless when we’re in real battles!” another golden griffin knight said in excitement.","“Right! May the holy light be with you!” Helen exclaimed cheerfully, “I feel like the paladins have super powerful combat techniques. Our levels are now low, but we will be unbelievably powerful when we grow stronger.”","“Ugh-?” At this moment, Commander Elven exclaimed while he stared at the quest report in his hands with widened eyes. “A report of a Duskwood wolf raid on Northshire? Does the Azeroth Continent have a Duskwood too?”","“There is a Brotherhood here too?” Right now, the golden griffin knights were doing the Northshire Abbey quest, and Helen was amazed by what she read in the report. “The humans wearing red masks... They call themselves the Brotherhood?”","“It must be a coincidence!” another golden griffin knight said casually, “It’s a coincidence of names...”","Northshire Abbey was a green valley with all kinds of thick ancient trees, and it was enjoyable to level up, kill mobs, practice skills, and do quests in this dense and vast forest. In this human territory, players could complete quests that would increase their reputation while touring the peaceful and tranquil human land.","Perhaps they would understand why they must defend this land while they toured this beautiful place.","Outside the tall city wall of the Northshire Valley, a gravel path in the forest led out to Goldshire, the biggest human town besides Stormwind City.","Surrounded by tall and thick ancient Elwynn woods, the peaceful Goldshire that was on the main road leading to Stormwind City was a miniature of the daily life of people living in Elwynn Forest. Adventurers from all over the world bustled in the inn named Lion’s Pride. Obviously, today was the busiest day in its history.","“Oh... so many people!” The knights of Golden Griffin Legion had just entered the inn, and Commander Elven called out, “A glass of Lion King black beer for each of us! Hahaha!”","They sat down at a table, feeling a bit tired after doing quests for about two hours in Northshire Abbey.","Beside them were a few members of the Royal Clan Guild such as Royal Princess Ji Yu, the Second Prince, and some disciples of Shengjing Academy. They slammed their hands on the table and shouted, “Servant! Get us your best drinks and dishes!”","The golden griffin knights gaped as they looked over. “...”","“Ugh? Anything wrong with what we said?” The members of the Royal Clan Guild froze for a moment.","Regardless of what background they came from in the real world, the players merged themselves into the game completely. Right now, they were human paladins who had just been recruited and began to learn the basic skills and combat techniques just as they had done when they first became knights.","Of course, the skills of paladins looked noble and graceful. They used the platinum-colored holy light and had the Holy Light Spell which could heal injuries swiftly and all kinds of holy seals.","“This feeling so cool!” Looking at the bustling crowds in the Lion’s Pride Inn, Elven felt as if he had returned to his youth when he had just mastered his sword techniques and came out of his home for adventuring.","Who said that one could never return to the past? Maybe in another world, people could find a totally different life."]},{"number":681,"title":"Chapter 681 - A Large Group of Newbies Arrive at the Battlefield","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Judgement...” Taking use of the brief breaktime, Commander Elven carefully read the introduction about the skills. “Release the energy of the holy seal onto the enemy and stop the target from escaping for 30 seconds. Each paladin can only use Judgment on one enemy at a time...”","“Ugh...? How come I can’t cast this spell?” Commander Elven frowned.","“Seal of Righteousness... fills you with Holy Light, causing melee attacks to deal 4 more damage to all targets within 30 seconds. Each paladin can only retain the effects of one holy seal at a time?” Helen said in sudden understanding, “Is it so...? No wonder I lost the Seal of Righteousness when I cast the Seal of the Crusader...”","In the system version of World of Warcraft, the players didn’t control the characters with a mouse and keyboard, which was why the operations were much more complicated than the original version. For example, the paladin was a class that inflicted damages mostly through auto attacks. In the system version, it was impossible to them to auto attack the enemies after casting Seal of Judgement as in the original version; they had to focus on each battle themselves.","Even without the aid of spells, they could attack with their own sword techniques and combat techniques. At this moment, the players had only a basic understanding of the skills that they had learned.","With their current sword techniques, it was no problem for them to kill the ordinary mobs. They got themselves busy with leveling and completing quests and thus hadn’t taken time to study these skills.","“The Seal of Righteousness can add more magic effects to our attacks?” another golden griffin knight said in pleasant surprise.","Knights and warriors usually cultivated qi, and their attacks could inflict magic damages only when their mages were helping them.","However, in this game, even warriors can achieve these effects on their own?","Soon, these players found that the power of Holy Light was achieved by faith. Obviously, like the freedom in Assassin’s Creed, Holy Light in World of Warcraft didn’t originate from a god.","Right now, these players only had a basic understanding about it. To them, Holy Light was a special warm light that could heal injuries with extremely great speed, and it was totally different from any light they had seen in the real world.","We can have faith in this light? How come there is such a strange belief?","This setting in the game gave these players a completely new definition of faith. In Assassin’s Creed, the faith was freedom. Now in World of Warcraft, the faith was the Holy Light?","Of course, in the game, regardless if the players had faith or not, the characters such as paladins and priests had their fixed faiths, so the players who didn’t believe in Holy Light had no problem playing their roles.","Walking out of the Lion’s Pride inn, Commander Elven came to the forest outside the town again to do the quest. “I’ll use the Seal of Righteousness first...”","It was fine to walk on the main road. But in the forest, players would encounter all kinds of dangers such as wolves, wild beasts, and rogues of Defias Brotherhood. Soon Elven encountered a Defias rogue wearing a red mask, and he came from the Defias Brotherhood which was mentioned before.","Of course, they had nothing to do with the Brotherhood in Assassin’s Creed. They were a bunch of fierce and evil people, and they sneak-attacked Elven the moment he entered the forest.","Elven’s combat techniques were excellent. With a slight shift of his body, he dodged the dagger and hacked with his double-handed big sword swiftly!","Knowing the opponent’s great speed, Elven’s strike focused on speed. Immediately, he left a long bloody wound in the rogue’s body. “So powerful?! The strength increased by 30%!”","The Defias rogue rolled on the ground and fled into the depths of the forest.","With his great speed, there was no way that a paladin could catch up to him.","At this moment, a streak of holy light shot out and knocked the escaping rogue to the ground in the blink of an eye. Then, the rogue instantly died.","“Ugh?” Elven looked down at himself in puzzlement, “How come I can use Judgement now?”","Then, he read the descriptions of the skill again. “Release the power of the holy seal onto the enemy...”","“Holy seal...?”","“I just used the Seal of Righteousness...?” Elven thought back carefully. “And then Judgement...?”","Is this what it meant by releasing the power of the holy seal onto the enemy?!","No wonder I couldn’t use it! I must use a holy seal first...?","Then, a shout sounded in the internet café. “Guys... Come and look! I mastered a core skill of paladin!”","“Awesome!”","“You mastered a core skill already?!”","“???” At this moment, Mr. Fang who was busy leveling up as an undead rogue looked over in surprise. These people are so talented? They have mastered a core skill of paladins so soon?","At this stage, they shouldn’t have learned the core skill Seal of Command yet, right?","The elves and assassins beside Elven looked over in astonishment. This middle-aged knight demonstrated the spell to them in excitement by casting a holy seal and then shooting a beam of dazzling golden light at a wolf.","With a whimper, the wolf dropped to the ground with blood gushing out of its head.","“I can use this powerful combat technique perfectly!” Commander Elven yelled in excitement.","“My goodness! Is it Judgement?!” The mercenaries yelled in surprise, “I have a less than 30% success rate in using this combat technique! You can do it whenever you want to?”","“I only managed to cast it once!” Helen was frustrated, wondering if her talent was too poor. “You have a success rate of 30%?!”","“Is this combat technique so difficult to use?” The elves exclaimed.","They felt like they had mastered all the skills after learning them, and they didn’t know that there were such difficult skills in the game.","“You can even use ranged attacks?” The assassins looked envious.","“Of course!” Commander Elven said proudly, “I just understood this powerful combat technique; it needs a holy light technique before this powerful attack named Judgement can be used!”","Mr. Fang’s face twitched, thinking, You only need to cast a holy seal as a prerequisite before using Judgement... I was foolish to believe that you guys can master deep and complex skills.","With a dark expression, he returned to his game. “...”","“What’s a holy seal?” At this moment, another mercenary asked curiously, “I only have Holy Light... How come you guys also have the so-called holy seals and judgement?”","“You can learn them with the class trainer...” Helen said, “Didn’t you do that?”","The mercenary looked at the knights in confusion. “Where can I find a class trainer...?”","“In Northshire Abbey...”","“Really?! There is such a place and person? I didn’t know that!” The mercenary yelled in surprise, “My goodness! You’re masters! You Golden Griffin Knight Legion is indeed marvelous!”","“...”"]},{"number":682,"title":"Chapter 682 - The Killing Elevator Incident in Undercity","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Tirisfal Glades, where the undead spawned, was always gloomy. The dark and dense forest was always engulfed by gloomy thick mist without any light penetrating it.","“We have a group of powerful people here...” Sala finally returned to her seat. While teaming up with the students from Jiuhua City, she said, “They have mastered a powerful combat technique called Judgement, and it seems like it can only be used with special skills. It looks very powerful! What if we encounter paladins who use holy light? They are our enemies, right?”","“Are they really that powerful?” Lan Yan charged forward and swiftly hacked down a gnoll.","“Who are they?” Although Song Qingfeng had gone to play as a tauren, Lin Shao was over here. He chuckled while hacking down the mob before him.","“We have quite a few powerful knights here,” Lance, the elf captain, answered casually.","“Don’t worry,” Lin Shao said, “We are powerful masters too.”","“You guys...?” Elf Captain Lance looked at them in puzzlement. Although they chose to be undead, they didn’t choose the appearance of a skeleton like Mr. Fang, so Lance could see that these players were young people who were about 20 years old.","Rain began to fall in Tirisfal Glades that was engulfed in chilly and damp grey mist, making these players feel a unique loneliness and sadness.","“Look! What’s that?!” A big fat figure walked up from the grey misty rain in the forest with a huge axe and a chain in its hands.","“Is it a monster?” Seeing the creepy figure, the elves felt their hearts began to race.","“Be careful!” Nalan Mingxue grew cautious.","When the figure got close, the players saw that it was a huge mountain-like monster as if it was sewed together by thick threads. It emitted a pungent smell of poison and plague, and its belly was cut open and empty. It was a horrifying and creepy scene.","“What’s this?” The elves had never seen such scary monsters before.","The monster walked toward the players and yelled in a deep and muffled voice, “We won’t harm you. Can you do us a favor? Our master needs grass, but our hands are too big to pick up the grass.”","“Ugh?” The elves froze. “Isn’t it here to eat us?”","Unconsciously, they shrunk back a little, afraid to be eaten by this monster who looked extremely terrifying.","They exchanged a look. “I think not... you can ask others to help you...”","“Okay...” The monster walked off in disappointment.","After a long while, the players began to wonder, “What was that thing...?”","“It looks scary...” Sala said, “I think it must be an evil monster trying to get close to us with some evil purposes.”","“Um... I think it only wanted to give us a quest,” Nalan Mingxue said in earnest.","“I think we must be careful.” The elves looked very wary of this kind of horrifying monsters. “How many quests do you guys have left?”","“They are all done.”","“Let’s go back and hand in the results!”","“So, we are able to go to that Undercity later?” one elf asked.","“It seems like it...”","...","Located in the east of Tirisfal Glades, Undercity was the main city for the undead race and the city that all the undead players must visit.","Going south from Tirisfal Glades, the players saw the high walls standing in the Lordaeron’s ruins.","The gloomy sky lent a grey and dark look to the city walls. When the elves came here with Nalan Mingxue and other students, they saw many undead players bustling through the city gate. With many undead guards and patrolling soldiers mingling in the crowds, the place was boisterous.","Undercity was a huge underground maze under the ruins of Lordaeron Kingdom. The large stretches of collapsed buildings and thick stone pillars covered by thriving ivies looked desolate despite the bustling players walking around them.","The road leading from the gate to the interior of the city was the road that Arthas took after he returned as the Death Knight and killed his father. Following the road, they could go all the way to the throne.","The huge bronze bell had crashed deep into the boulder, but no one bothered to get it up. Following the road, the players seemed to hear cheers and the crisp ringing of the bell when celebrating the return of the prince. They seemed to feel the people’s panic and astonishment when the prince walked over to the throne and killed his father.","Once the biggest human kingdom, even thought Lordaeron had turned into ruins, the heaviness of its history lingered in the air and the chilly rain falling from the sky gave people a special sense of sadness even if they didn’t know about the historical events.","Built in the ground under Lordaeron, Undercity could be reached through the many tunnels inside the castle.","“This must have been a prosperous kingdom.” The elves looked around the ruins while they walked, and they exclaimed as they looked at the grand city walls built with huge boulders and the dilapidated buildings.","“Ugh? Isn’t that Ms. Sala and her companions?” Elina and other assassins had also chosen the undead race and had just arrived at this city.","Following the crowd, they walked toward the entrance of Undercity. “My goodness... There are more of those horrifying monsters here!”","Two meat-mountain-like Abominations guarded the entrance.","“Do we have to pass this place that they’re guarding?” Sala yelled in fear.","“I don’t think they want to harm us.”","“Hurry up! Don’t block the way!” People behind them yelled impatiently.","Meanwhile, they saw many people walking through the entrance guarded by the Abominations without anything bad happening to them.","Sala inhaled deeply. “I’m going over!”","“Sure. Don’t be afraid!”","“I’m really going!” Sala took in another deep breath and dashed forward in a fit of boldness.","“Ugh?” The moment that she rushed through the gate guarded by the Abominations, she froze, feeling like there was nothing below her feet.","“Ahhhhhh–!” The resonate scream grew fainter as it went down.","“What’s wrong with her...” The people nearby talked among themselves.","“The elevator hasn’t come up yet, and she just jumped down...”","“Um... How many have jumped so far?”","Looking down the elevator shaft, they saw many small tombstones and an elf flat on the ground...","Nalan Mingxue and the other students exchanged a look. “...”"]},{"number":683,"title":"Chapter 683 - Leaving in Reluctance","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","It must be noted that by now, many players had finished playing Dungeon Fighter Online after getting the best equipment, and those who hadn’t were close. Therefore, many Dungeon Fighter Online players were trying World of Warcraft.","It was why each spawn place was bustling with players.","In World of Warcraft, the players could resurrect after death, but it was not as convenient as other games.","After death, the players had to choose to release their souls. The souls would resurrect in the nearby graveyard and had to return to find their corpses to resume the game.","If the souls gave up on their corpses, they could talk to the Spirit Healers who looked like angels, and they could resurrect the players with the penalty of durability loss to all items and resurrection sickness.","With resurrection sickness, the players couldn’t do quests and level up.","When Elf Girl Sala opened her eyes again, she found herself in a grey world with the huge shadow of a Spirit Healer standing by the graveyard.","Having not died before while she did quests in a team, Sala was panicking when she saw this scene. “Where am I?”","Also, she felt like her body was as light as a soul, and she was powerless.","This elf was confused and lost in this strange grey world.","“How come your World of Warcraft looks like this now?” The nearby elves put down their virtual reality headsets and looked over.","“I don’t know...” Sala looked lost. “I got here after death... I feel like I’ve become a ghost. The Forsaken is dead already, right? How come I can die again?”","“It seems like I must run back to my corpse or resurrect in this place with resurrection sickness...” Sala said, “I choose to resurrect here. Undercity looks very far from here...”","“Okay.” The other elves of the elf team said, “We’ll get ourselves familiar with the Undercity first.”","There were about 10 members in the Snow Pigeon Team of the Elf Clan. Right Now, six of them chose a different path and joined the strange Forsaken race led by Queen Sylvanas.","Including the elves outside of the Snow Pigeon Team, there were about 10 elves who had chosen this race.","They were not leveling up together; only six of them were with Nalan Mingxue, including Sala and the other two female elves, Rowling and Ace. Other than the Team Captain, there were two male elves, Roger and Slone.","However, Nalan Mingxue and her companions still couldn’t tell them apart except for the mature-looking elf captain and the vivacious Sala who had just fallen into the elevator shaft.","In fact, the elves were also confused with names such as ‘Nalan Mingxue’ and ‘Lan Yan’ which sounded quite strange to them. But it didn’t matter. After all, they had just met today. Even if they made mistakes with people’s names, it was no big deal. Instead, it might be a source of fun in the virtual reality world of the game.","“Should we tour around Undercity first?” Lin Shao suggested.","“We are thinking about it too.” Captain Lance said, “We’re new here and must get familiar with the map.”","He opened the magic map in his hand. In the system version of the game, each player had a magic map which could automatically draw out the general terrain of the surrounding area and note down the positions of teammates and the places to accept quests.","The Undercity in the system version was obviously bigger than the one in the original version. Even though the Forsaken wasn’t a race with a large population, it still had a residential zone where many members of the Forsaken lived. Like players, many ordinary undead had woken up in Deathknell.","The whole Undercity was built under Lordaeron with many tunnels leading to different places. Like a luxurious underground kingdom, its area was several times bigger than the ruins of Lordaeron Kingdom.","“According to the executive officer of Deathknell, we should go and find...” Elf Captain Lance consulted the map and said, “the...um... Bethor; it will greet us in this city?”","Lan Yan also consulted the map. “We’ll find this place soon if we go in this direction...”","Ten minutes later...","“How come we’re still not there? This is the end of the road?”","20 minutes later...","They looked at the map. “It should be here...?”","One hour later...","“Ugh... we’re lost...” They looked at the map in bafflement.","“It seems... the Undercity has another level?”","...","“Sala, are you here?” Rowling, another female elf in the team, asked.","She turned her head and looked. “How come you’re still in the graveyard?!”","At this moment, words appeared on everyone’s screen. [Your time is up.]","“...”","...","“Oh, I’m so weak... I met mobs soon after I walked out of the graveyard and died many times,” Sala got offline reluctantly and complained.","“How are you guys doing...? It’s been a long while; you must be many levels higher than me now,” Sala asked sullenly.","“We’re lost...” The elves said with dark expressions. “...”","They got offline, and some players who had been waiting in line replaced them on the computers, finally getting the chance to play World of Warcraft.","“There are so many people in this mystical realm...” Elder Sewell got offline and clicked her tongue while saying, “I’ve never seen another mystical realm with so many people before.”","Besides the elves, the dwarves, mages and even mercenaries were talking about the game while they walked out of the shop.","“You would never imagine such a mystical realm!” Dwarf Elder Sauk said to the white-haired and white-robed Mage Adolf in a loud voice, “The grand Ironforge is not like our city, but I assure you that you will fall in love with it the moment you see it! Just imagine countless diligent dwarves working hard in the castle that was dug out by our clansmen in the belly of the snowy mountains. This feeling...”","“You must go and see Stormwind City!” Adolf said with a laugh, “The statues of heroes, the busy commercial zone, the mage zone with tranquil and elegant violet-colored rooves... Oh! We also have the Wine Festival. Do you know about that?”","Walking on the street of Canglan City, Grand Mage Adolf said with excited hand gestures, “Now that we mention wine, you can’t miss the Dalaran black wine in Stormwind City. Its taste is unique and rich; you must try it.”","Although they already got offline, the players walked out of the shop reluctantly."]},{"number":684,"title":"Chapter 684 - New Paladins Discovered a Teleportation Item Named Hearthstone","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Elder, do you know the people from the other side of the ocean?” Sala asked when the other elves and Elder Sewell, who had joined the Night Elf race, got offline, “I met some of them today.”","“Did you?” Elder Sewell asked curiously, “I only saw elves. There were many night elves.”","“Um...” The elves who joined the Forsaken race looked over. “Some of them are humans from the East Continent.”","“Oh... They are humans from the East Continent...” Elder Sewell said in sudden understanding, “We were busy leveling up and didn’t notice them... We’ll reach level 8 soon.”","She said proudly since she saw that many other elves had only reached level 5 or 6.","They walked out of the shop while exchanging their experiences in World of Warcraft today.","Meanwhile...","Although the shop extended its business hours, few people borrowed time from the next day. Longer time spent in the mystical realm would indeed give them more strength, but it would also cause more mental and physical stress.","It wasn’t easy to kill mobs for a whole day in World of Warcraft.","Besides, not everyone had enough time to play ten hours each day in the game.","“Hu...!” Mr. Dirk walked out of the shop and exhaled deeply while he looked up at the darkening sky. “I spent a whole day in the game?”","“Grumble...” At this moment, a strange noise sounded.","“I have to stop the show now... This is the end of today’s show in the new mystical realm,” Mr. Dirk said, “I’ve got to get something to eat.”","[Shame on you!] The audience from different places around the world wrote in and sounded reluctant.","[Judging from today’s experience, this mystical realm is quite good.] In this world, most prosperous areas could maintain magic communication through the Alchemist Union, and magic letters were a good way for people from prosperous areas to communicate with each other.","The words leaped on everyone’s magic letters.","[I almost thought that the Orc Kingdom had built another royal city in another land! It was magnificent!]","[What kind of existence do you think the Blizzard Workshop in the East Continent is...?] – From ‘White Tulip’.","[I’m surprised that the workshops in the East Continent have advanced to this high of a level. Have you noticed that there are many East Continent people in the mystical realm?]—From ‘Observant Eye’.","...","At this moment, the two black-cloaked messengers were walking out of the Yuanyang City Shop. “Do you think that this is a mystical realm made by the West Continent?”","“It’s possible... Did you hear that some of them claimed to be people of the Nora Continent? It must be them who created this mystical realm.”","The tall and thin messenger gasped and said, “I’m surprised that the mystical realms of the West Continent have reached such a high level. I wonder if this Blizzard is a faction or an organization...”","The stout messenger said, “I think we must report this to our superiors.”","...","As the first group of players got offline, the players who had been waiting for seats finally got the chance to begin their journey on the Azeroth Continent.","It was midnight, and the shop was still bright with lights. Fortunately, Jiuhua City had lifted the night curfew. The last group of players from different big factions and families only left at 5 AM.","For now, the computers in the shop were barely enough for all players. Despite the crowdedness in the morning, there were some empty seats in the evening.","...","The first streak of sunlight appeared in the east.","“Another new day...” In their dorm rooms, several golden griffin knights leaped up from their beds.","“We can continue leveling up today...” One of them said.","“I feel more eager to get up in the morning everyday now...”","During the previous day’s gameplay, these new players had encountered the same problems, similar to the ones that Commander Elven and Elf Girl Sala had met. For example, they didn’t know how to use certain skills, they spent a long time trying to run back to their corpses, and they got lost in main cities.","Therefore, after finding that the shop had enough computers for players, they weren’t as anxious to get online today as they had been yesterday.","It was more so the case for the players in the old shops.","In the early morning, the players turned on their communication jades and saw messages jumping on the screens.","[Whose livestream should we watch today?]","[Let’s watch Nalan Mingxue’s livestream. Yesterday, they met a few elves, and one of them fell into the elevator shaft and died! It was so dumb and cute!]","[There’re really elves?!]","[Really? It’s a pity that I was busy leveling up and didn’t see it...]","[At least you were leveling up, I missed it while I watched Elder Su’s livestream!]","“...”","...","In the Canglan City Shop, Mr. Dirk came into the shop very early today. “Good morning, everyone. Now, you are watching Mr. Dirk’s journey in World of Warcraft. Yesterday, we saw the grand main city of the orc race, Orgrimmar, and I think today’s journey will be more interesting.”","With that said, he followed the crowd into the shop.","There were many people in the shop in the morning, and the elves who had intended to enter the game after breakfast had to get online first before buying instant noodles.","Then, they logged into the game while eating the noodles.","Sala found herself still sitting in the graveyard. “Forget it. I’ll recover from resurrection sickness first.”","She was sulky when she remembered her countless deaths yesterday.","“Do you want to return to the inn with a hearthstone and then come back?” Beside her, Female Elf Rowling suggested, “At least you’ll know the way.”","“What’s a hearthstone?” A few golden griffin knights sitting across from them asked casually, each with a bowl of instant noodles in their hands.","“It’s a stone that has the teleportation spell.” Sala opened her backpack and saw a round-shaped stone engraved with runes. “Don’t you know that? New Snow told me that I can use this stone to return to the nearby inn.”","“Can we do that?”","“A quest seemed to ask us to bound to a stone or something.” Commander Elven walked up from behind. “But we haven’t tried it yet. Should we try it later?”","“Ugh...? It’s true!” a knight exclaimed, “I’m surprised that I got such a high-end item upon spawn! It took only a few seconds to activate, and then I’m back in the Lion’s Pride Inn!”"]},{"number":685,"title":"Chapter 685 - The first battle begins! Warsong Gulch!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","The internet café was bustling. As soon as this treasure was discovered, it quickly spread to other players.","Of course, this was one of the basic mechanics of the game.","Many of the players in the old shops were watching Nalan Mingxue’s livestream.","[They said that there are elves. How come I haven’t seen any?]","Many people came to the livestream room early, watching the livestream cheerfully while enjoying instant noodles.","Soon, someone answered with a bullet comment.","[Maybe they haven’t gotten online yet. Be patient.]","[They’re online now! They’re online now!]","Nalan Mingxue clicked open the friends list and saw the names of the elves lighting up.","[You guys came early too?] Sala friendly greeted them.","[Yeah. We don’t have classes this morning.] Soon, she received Nalan Mingxue’s reply.","[Classes?] Sala was curious. [Are you students in an academy? Little Kids. Hehe!]","Many players in the old shops were watching the livestream, and bullet comments instantly flooded the screen.","[Hahaha! Little Kids!]","[Is she an elf? She sounds fun!]","[New Snow, ask her how old she is. She looks young too!]","[She looks younger than New Snow! Hahaha!]","It was still morning, and the livestream room was full of joyous laughter.","Nalan Mingxue sent a message over and said, “My friends said that you might be younger than me.”","“How can it be-!” Sala replied smugly, “I’ve lived more than 100 years! You guys can call me Older Sister Sala!”","Although many females were sensitive about their age, many teenagers were exceptions and were afraid to look immature to others","Although 100 years were old for humans, for elves, this age was equivalent to that of a teenager.","[The people here usually call someone over 100 years ‘aunt’.] Soon, she received Nalan Mingxue’s reply.","Bullet comments appeared on the screen.","[New Snow is still sharp-tongued. This attribute of hers will never change.]","[The elf will probably get mad if we call her aunt.]","[Does it mean that we can call Elder Su ‘Aunt Su’?]","[The person before me, are you serious? Be careful; Elder Su might appear from behind you and explode your head.]","[Don’t worry; I’m her senior brother...]","[Pu... Liuyun Daoist Palace Master?]","“...” Sala replied while hurrying toward Undercity. “You guys can go ahead and do the quests; I’ll be there soon.”","“Take your time. We’re lost, and I must study the situation first.”","“Okay...”","...","While these players wandered in Undercity, Mr. Dirk of the Orc Clan was enjoying the game with a grey tail sticking out from his robe and swaying around. “This Orgrimmar is so huge that I feel dizzy walking in it. I’ll study the map first.”","[Where’s this place, Mr. Dirk?]","Someone asked on the magic letter. After all, some audience members didn’t watch livestream everyday. It was clear that this person hadn’t watched yesterday’s livestream.","[Is he back in the Orc Kingdom?]—From Huge Sword of Krima.","[He is in a newly-released mystical realm. This seems to be a massive mystical realm made specially by the Blizzard Workshop in the East Continent. I’m sure the friend above me didn’t watch the show yesterday.] – From Observant Eye.","[My goodness! Is this a mystical realm?]","[Does the East Continent have such super-sized workshops too? How come this place looks like an orc city?] – From Huge Sword of Krima.","[This is an orc city! Each race has its own cities in this mystical realm!] – From Observant Eye.","[Really? This city looks like a real one! Are you sure that there are many such cities in the mystical realm?]","While they were talking, Mr. Dirk wandered around, and his new audience took the opportunity to enjoy a lot of the scenery of Orgrimmar. “Right now, I seem to be in the... Valley of Honor? This place looks to be an important location with so many military officers here, but they didn’t block my entrance. I wonder if there are some important quests here.”","“I’ll ask these soldiers.” Mr. Dirk was an orc soldier who was carrying a double-handed sword on his back. Controlling this little orc character who was about level 10, he walked into the Valley of Honor.","Around him were tent-like structures built with steel and huge boulders. “They seem to be talking about... a battleground? I think this is the place where they fought the Alliance.”","“Should I join them?” Mr. Dirk asked, “It looks dangerous, but I can resurrect here. Besides, those military officers told me that I will only battle with opponents on my level. Should I go in and try it?”","[Are we going to watch Mr. Dirk kill enemies and dominate the battleground?] –From White Tulip.","[Opponents of the same level are opponents of the same strength, right? Then, there’s nothing to be afraid of!] – From Huge Sword of Krima.","[We orcs are fearless! It is not fun to fight wild beasts. Finally, Mr. Dirk gets to show his real strength! Let them see the awesome sword techniques of the Orc Clan.] – From Wolf-Headed Man.","[It depends on who’s playing, Mr. Dirk or Mr. Dog-Headed Man. If it’s the latter, it will be embarrassing.] – From Sky Ocean Knight Legion.","The audience gave Mr. Dirk two identities. One was the powerful Mr. Dirk, and the other was the embarrassing Mr. Dog-Headed Man. Although the two identities were the same person, if Mr. Dirk lost a battle or made a mistake, the audience would say that he was controlled by the embarrassing Dog-Headed Man.","At this moment, the audience saw that Mr. Dirk had agreed to join the battle.","In World of Warcraft, players above level 10 could enter the first battleground named Warsong Gulch, fighting for their side. Although the system version of World of Warcraft had made everything as real as possible, it was still a game and maintained the features that were convenient for the players.","Take the battlegrounds as an example. As a small battleground, Warsong Gulch obviously didn’t need many people in it, which was why it was designed to have a separate plane for each group of Alliance and Horde players, just like the design of dungeons in Dungeon Fighter Online","At this stage, the battlegrounds in the system version of World of Warcraft divided players by every five levels, which meant that the players wouldn’t encounter opponents more than five levels higher than them. In the battlegrounds, the players would gain experience points regardless if they won or lost, making it a great opportunity to practice their combat skills.","“It seems like we need to wait for a while?” At this moment, many players had reached the required level but found that there were few people in the battleground.","“Ugh...?” Mr. Dirk suddenly felt that his body turned weightless for a second as he was teleported to a strange place. “I’m in! I have entered this battleground! Let’s see what the battleground in World of Warcraft looks like.”","Before him was a moderate-sized stone chamber with many players in it. Obviously, they had also discovered this battleground mode and entered it as the earliest participants.","...","– In the Jiuhua City Shop –","“Ugh...?” Nalan Mingxue looked around in bafflement.","Bullet comments appeared on the screen.","[Where is this place?]","[It seems like she was teleported to another place?]","Nalan Mingxue said, “I seemed to have been teleported to another place named Warsong Gulch? Only a moment ago, the military officer was explaining this to me, and here I am. How come it is so fast?”"]},{"number":686,"title":"Chapter 686 - ADHD Before Battle, and Elder Su who went AFK on the battleground","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","[TL Note: ADHD stands for attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, and AFK stands for away from keyboard.]","By now, only a small portion of players had reached level 10.","After all, World of Warcraft was more refined than the Legend of Mir 2, and it wasn’t as simple and crude. The players needed to learn lots of stuff. At this moment, like Elder Sewell, many players were still wandering in the beginners’ zone. Like the members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion, some still didn’t know how to use the hearthstones and only mastered skills such as Judgement by accident.","The players who could go to the battleground were either lucky, skillful, or had been focusing on leveling up.","For example, the Dwarf Elder Sauk in the Canglan City Shop had been teleported to the battleground as well, and he was one of the players with good skills.","In the Half City Shop, the King of Rangers, a youth who was about 14 years old, had graduated from Dungeon Fighter Online and was also trying World of Warcraft today.","There was a moderate number of viewers in his livestream room. Playing as a night elf hunter, he entered the battleground while reading the messages on the screen. “Give a show? Um... I’ll try. But I think we’ll have a big streamer on the battleground today. Don’t you think so?”","“I don’t know the situation in the new shop, but I think we might encounter masters from the outlands.” He took off his virtual reality headset and said, “I’ll eat some instant noodles first and see what happens on the battleground.”","...","Meanwhile, on the side of the Horde, the players were all teleported into a stone tower. The moment Mr. Dirk entered, he glanced around while holding his double-handed sword. “I see enemies the moment I enter the battleground. It’s indeed a dangerous place!”","“I’m using Bloodrage! Charge! Whirling Cleave! (he used his own battle technique) Execution!” He yelled repeatedly as if he was controlling his combat techniques with his voice. While hacking and slashing with his double-handed sword, he used elegant movements as he charged toward a troll.","“Attacks are ineffective?”","“Hiss! He seems to belong to the Horde too? Oh... I hacked the wrong person...” Looking at the troll who had been paralyzed by fear, the orc on the screen murmured to himself.","At this moment, each player received a prompt. [The battleground will be opened in one minute.]","“The battle hasn’t begun yet; I thought I would engage in a battle as soon as I came...”","[Embarrassing!] The audience erupted and talked amongst themselves.","[Dog-Headed Man! He’s definitely the embarrassing Dog-Headed Man!]","[He almost hacked his teammate to death...]","By now, ten teammates had all arrived, and the atmosphere became more tense during the countdown.","“Um... why does this person keep on twitching?”","– In the Jiuhua City Shop –","“Still need to wait for one minute? I’ll eat some noodles then.” While eating instant noodles, Nalan Mingxue put one finger on the keyboard and moved on the left key and right key repeatedly.","On her screen, the undead character moved to the left and then back repeatedly as if she was having a stroke.","Beside the undead, an orc wildly hacked at the door with an ax.","“The attacks are ineffective at this moment?” The troll who had been paralyzed by fear condensed a magic ball in his hand and crashed it onto the head of the man beside him.","As a veteran player, Black Demon was playing as an undead warlock. While stuffing a spicy stick into his mouth, he controlled his character to strike the magic staff onto the head of a teammate. “It seems like the attacks are ineffective here...”","Beside him, a tauren hacked at him with an axe.","The one minute was obviously a long wait for these players. Some moved from left to the right and then back, some hacked at the door wildly, and some hacked at each other with staffs and huge axes, trying to hurt each other and looking extremely violent.","This scene was ‘unbelievably pretty’.","The audience of Mr. Dirk’s livestream were dazed by the scene. “...”","Isn’t... this the battleground? The battle hasn’t begun yet; what are you guys doing?!","...","“I read the instruction...” Su Tianji’s human mage character was also on the battleground. “It said that the side which takes three flags is the winner...”","At this moment, the countdown had begun.","“Three!”","“Two!”","“One!”","The doors finally opened, and both sides dashed out at a blistering pace!","Su Tianji sat down by the Alliance’s flag all by herself. “Everyone, I’m sure that it’s not right to rush out like this. I’ll stay behind to guard the flag, so no one can steal it.”","“Awesome!”","“Elder Su is finally smart for once!”","Su Tianji was a little smug. “When someone comes here to steal the flag, you just watch my skills!”","Sitting on the edge of the night elf’s Ashenvale, Warsong Gulch was covered in green turfs with many stumps left by huge ancient trees and huge boulders that had existed for many years.","The Warsong Gulch in the system version was larger than the one in the original version, but it was an open space. When the players dashed out together, they soon spotted their opponents.","“Let’s play a war song.” Nalan Mingxue finally stopped controlling with the keyboard. “Last of the Wilds by Nightwish—the Spiritual State language version.”","When the passionate music sounded, she entered the battle while listening to the music.","On the battleground, the players who had ranged classes had begun attacking. Lightning bolts and flames of all colors shot across dozens of meters, exploding and creating many streaks of dazzling light on the ground.","Nalan Mingxue controlled her undead warrior character to observe discreetly at the edge of the battleground.","Then, she heard a bestial roar and saw an orc warrior charging out.","[I’m surprised!] Mr. Dirk’s audience was surprised that Mr. Dirk became so valiant and fierce.","[Charge of a Fierce Man!] – From Sky Ocean Knight Legion.","[Orc Sword Technique!] – From Wolf-Headed Man.","The warriors of this level were very powerful. Since the players didn’t have adequate items and proper skill sets, they were defenseless and were easy to kill when the attacks struck their vital parts.","Nalan Mingxue who was observing the battle watched the orc warrior charge and kill an Alliance mage with one strike.","“Awesome!”","“Lead the Horde to victory!” The audience exclaimed.","At this moment, the audience felt that the firepower of the Alliance was inferior to that of the Horde.","Then, this orc was swallowed by all kinds of spells.","“...”","“That’s embarrassing...”","“How come he couldn’t dodge the spells?! Can these low-level spells lock onto their targets spiritually?!”","In the system version of World of Warcraft, the magic spells could lock onto targets via spiritual energy. Even if the opponents dodged the spells, the spells would seek after them for a while. Therefore, it was hard to successfully dodge a spell. The best method was blocking them with swords or shields or countering them with attacks.","“That’s a close one...” In the flames, the orc still had a few points of HP left and immediately hid behind a boulder.","At this moment, his teammates used spells, battling their opponents and not giving them the chance to focus on him.","Meanwhile, Nalan Mingxue had moved to the back of their enemies under the cover of the small rocky hills and plants.","“???” The mage who was targeted by Nalan Mingxue casted spells while wondering, “How come I have the feeling that we should have one more teammate with us...?”","Charge!","Nalan Mingxue dashed out at great speed and struck her sword onto the mage’s chest with vicious force.","She interrupted his spellcasting!","...","While the battle went on fiercely, Su Tianji was staying behind in their home camp.","She had waited for two minutes. “Still, no one is coming?”","– Three minutes later –","“What’s wrong...?”","– Outside the battleground –","The King of Rangers said, “I told you that there’s a streamer among them. However, why do I feel like we have one less teammate?”","“We can’t hold them!”","– Ten minutes later –","Su Tianji had begun eating potato chips, and she said blurrily with chips in her mouth, “How come no one is coming?”","[Teammate: How come we’ve been fighting so long with one less player?]","[She is AFK?]","[She is going AFK so blatantly!]","[I’m shocked. Why did Elder Su go AFK on her teammates on the battleground?!]","[Awesome!]","Many bullet comments appeared."]},{"number":687,"title":"Chapter 687 - Online-Game-Scale Mystical Realm?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","In World of Warcraft, the players could obtain experience points and also honor points which could elevate their prestige ranks. Prestige ranks were required to have the privilege to buy certain items.","It was why there would be two groups of players who preferred to play PVP or PVE respectively.","On the side of the Alliance, the King of Rangers wasn’t the only one fighting. People like Dwarf Elder Sauk and Mage Adolf’s disciple Dicas were also in the battleground.","As a mage, she had more convenience in certain things compared to Mr. Dirk, who was a warrior.","For example, she had sent back the visuals of the battleground to the Royal Magic Union and some mages who were good friends of hers.","With several streamers and players who activated the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection in the battle, many people were watching what was happening on the battleground.","“What are they doing?” Some mages had just begun watching the battle.","In the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection before them, the battleground was full of flying magic spells and arrows while the players with melee characters battled fiercely.","Since several players on the Alliance’s side had resurrected several times, the battlefront was stretched very long and wasn’t as concentrated as before.","Dicas’s human priest character was chanting a spell when a black shadow lunged at her.","She waved her hands and chanted a simple incantation.","Power Word: Shield!","Faint lights instantly rose around her.","“What’s this spell?!”","“A new spell?”","“When did the Magic Union develop this new shield spell?”","“It looks to be a small spell but seems quite useful...”","Many mages watching Dicas battle on the battleground were surprised.","Power Word: Shield was different from the Magic Shield Spell in the Legend of Mir 2. The latter could weaken the opponent’s attack to an acceptable range, and the user of this spell would still be hurt by the attack.","On the other hand, Power Word: Shield could completely absorb most of the regular damage.","However, the Magic Shield Spell could allow the user to take the attack from opponents one or two levels higher, but Power Word: Shield couldn’t.","Power Word: Shield had its own advantages. For example, before the shield was broken, it could protect its caster from most of the regular attack and wouldn’t be interrupted even if the caster chanted spells right before the enemy. The Magic Shield Spell couldn’t do that.","At this moment, Dicas didn’t run. Instead, she chanted spells under the protection of this shield.","“The warrior is a bit late to charge up now, right?”","“The priest is protected by the shield. At this level, the warrior is already halfway defeated.”","The first spell that Dicas chanted was Mind Blast which took only a short time to chant. Dicas was confident in her spellcasting skills.","However, in the next moment, she found that this warrior moved around her in swift steps like a twitching phantom.","She tried for a long time but couldn’t lock her spell onto the target.","Oh! Can you stop moving?!","In the end, since she already chanted, she shot the spell forward.","Puchi!","It missed.","“...”","She felt dizzy already!","The shield was finally broken.","Nalan Mingxue’s undead warrior character slashed out her sword.","Looking at Dicas who was now lying on the ground, the mages of the Royal Magic Union asked, “What are you doing?”","“I’m fighting on the battleground!” With tears on her face, Dicas was astonished that her opponent had dodged her spell this way.","Resentfully, she returned to the graveyard and waited for resurrection.","...","Meanwhile, Su Tianji who had been guarding the flag couldn’t remain sitting anymore.","“Don’t mock me, okay?!” Looking at the haters’ comments on the screen, she stood up and said, “It is them who don’t know how to win the battle, and no one is coming to get the flag. How can you say that I’m AFKing?”","After all, she was guarding the flag! It wasn’t the same as going AFK!","“Okay! Okay!” Realizing that they were all new players, and probably no one had thought of taking the flag, she finally came out!","“Watch how I lead the Alliance to victory!”","...","“We’ll lose if we continue like this...” Dwarf Elder Sauk was not dumb, and he knew that they were at the disadvantage and would be eliminated one by one if they didn’t work together.","“The resurrected players, come here! The people in the front, come back! Let’s gather together! Don’t be alone!”","Elder Sauk played a dwarf hunter character who was using a gun as shown in the trailer.","Crack!","His firearm shot out a long stream of firelight.","Before them, Liang Shi controlled his orc warrior character to charge at the dwarf. Then, he shifted to the side and dodged the bullet.","Charge!","Liang Shi was almost before the dwarf of the Alliance when he heard a sharp sound. Then, his body turned cold, and his movements slowed down.","He turned his head and saw Su Tianji still raising her magic wand after casting the spell.","Meanwhile, Dwarf Sauk’s bear lunged at him and smashed down with his paw!","Then...","Swoosh!","A night elf hunter shot out an arrow from the cliff.","Concussive Shot!","“We must come gather.” The King of Rangers said, “Otherwise, we will lose the battle.”","Then, chilly ice spread out on the ground toward Liang Shi in waves.","Su Tianji’s Frost Nova!","Immediately, Liang Shi saw another icicle shooting toward him.","“F*ck...!”","Honorable Kill!","“Together! Come and charge together!” Su Tianji raised her arm and yelled, launching the counterattack.","“Kill the orc who is charging toward us!”","“Clear them together! Clear them all!”","The players in the Horde couldn’t understand the words of the players in the Alliance.","With his Spiritual Spell Visual Projection still on, Mr. Dirk froze when he saw arrows, bullets, and spells swarming toward him in waves. Without a chance to dodge, he was instantly killed!","The players had filed into the battleground separately, so they fought for themselves. Soon, almost half of the Horde players, including the mages, assassins, and shamans, were all killed and sent to the graveyard.","“My goodness...”","“They are so strong!”","“The embarrassing Dog-Headed Man was killed!”","Mr. Dirk’s audience was still puzzled and didn’t have the time to react. They wondered why this side seemed to be dominating a moment ago, but the opponents suddenly got more powerful.","“Assassin, go and take the flag. Others follow!” At this moment, many Horde players were still in the graveyard, and the remaining ones were instantly scattered and watched as the Alliance players took their flag.","“Oh, the battle should be fought like this?!” Resurrected, Dicas followed her teammates into the enemy’s camp without meeting any resistance.","The Alliance got one point.","– In Su Tianji’s livestream room –","[Awesome!]","[This battle is excellent!]","[Very good! Even the shop owner said it was good!]","“I told you not to mock me!” Su Tianji looked smug. “Now, who dares to call me an entertainment streamer?”","...","– Meanwhile –","“This battleground feels interesting...”","“The opponents are very strong...”","The audience members in the Royal Magic Union were eager to try the game after watching Dicas playing in this so-called ‘battleground’. “Is this also a mystical realm? Could it be a new mystical realm?”","“It’s the Blizzard Workshop’s new mystical realm called World of Warcraft.” Dicas looked at them, seeming to be judging their ignorance. “You guys don’t know about it?”","“Blizzard Workshop...?” The mages looked puzzled. “Many people are talking about this previously unknown workshop...?”","“What’s this mystical realm about? You just battle on the battlegrounds in it?”","“This is only a part of it,” Dicas explained proudly, “Battlegrounds are only a small part of the mystical realm. The races you saw come from different main cities in World of Warcraft, and some of the people in here come from the East Continent. World of Warcraft is a mystical realm that is called an online game; people from different continents can all gather in this mystical realm.”","“Wow...” They had thought little of the rumors around it. But after watching it and hearing the introduction, they exclaimed, “An ‘online game’ mystical realm...? This online game is so good?”","“Where are you now?! Where can we enter this online-game-scale mystical realm?”"]},{"number":688,"title":"Chapter 688 - This Elder Is a Muggle, and the End of Battleground Filled with Newbies","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“I’m in Canglan City.” Surprised that her team had turned the tables and won this round, Dicas explained in elation and excitement, “I’m in Origins Internet Café with my mentor. We’ve been in World of Warcraft for the last two days.”","“Your mentor...?” The mages’ expressions changed as they asked, “You mean...? Mr. Adolf is there too...?”","A mage in a black cloak asked in surprise, “Are you sure that he’s not trying the new mystical realm of the Lava Workshop in Canglan City?”","“Lava Workshop?” Dicas turned the camera to another direction. “Look! Who is he?”","The audience instantly saw an old dwarf wearing worn leather armor with a gun in his hand.","“This...!?” The mages were at a loss for words.","“Is he Elder Sauk!”","“He’s in this mystical realm too?!”","You came to another workshop’s mystical realm instead of going to the mystical realm of your Dwarf Clan?!","“You mean... Elder Sauk of the Dwarf Clan is also using the mystical realm called World of Warcraft?!”","“Keep it up! Friends!” At this moment, the dwarf elder raised his arm and yelled, “Work harder, and our Alliance will obtain victory on this battleground!”","...","– On the other side –","“We’ll lose all advantages if we continue this way...” Mr. Dirk died a moment ago. However, as a rogue who had toured many nations, he didn’t lose his cool. “Our opponents are strong and were only at a disadvantage because they had one less teammate with them. Therefore, we must change our tactics.","“They are indeed strong. Give me a moment to consider our next move.”","...","“How can you win on this battleground?” On the other side, the mages watching Dicas’ Spiritual Spell Visual Projection were eager to know the rules even though they were not in the game yet.","Knowing the rules beforehand would help them play the game better when they were in it. It was much better than going in blind.","“It seems that we need to take their army flag.” Dicas explained to them in the game. As a new player, she was still puzzled but knew that them taking the flag from their enemy seemed to be useful.","“Um...?” At this moment, several mages saw a figure passing behind Dicas in a flash!","“I saw someone pass with a flag on the shoulder...” Watching the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection, a mage said, “He was right behind you.”","“Really...?” Dicas looked around doubtfully, and then she said solemnly, “This is a battleground; don’t try to fool with me!”","At this moment, a rogue raced away right under their nose while carrying a flag on his shoulder. Carrying the flag couldn’t be done in stealth, or the flag would drop in the original version. In the system version, the players couldn’t be in stealth while carrying the flag, which meant that they could sneak in but couldn’t sneak out.","“Come and help me! I stole the flag!” Harrison howled.","“My goodness!”","“Go after him! Ahh-!”","“Our flag got stolen?”","“How come he can run so fast?!”","Seeing this scene, Su Tianji and her teammates almost dropped to the ground.","With so many people guarding the flag, it was still taken away by a rogue right under their nose?!","It was evident that Harrison’s efforts in playing Assassin’s Creed paid off. He had dodged almost everyone’s eyes.","Right now, he raced away with the flag on his shoulder.","“Someone! Anyone! Help me!”","Nalan Mingxue was considering how to fight the battle when she suddenly heard the yell. Looking up, she saw an undead rogue racing to them with tears on his face while many people chased after him. They ran around the big tree stumps, mountain boulders, and hills again and again.","“Don’t let him get away!”","“Frostbolt!”","“Concussive Shot!”","“Entangling Roots!”","“...”","“I’m going to die! I’m going to die! Ahhh!”","“Stop these Alliance people!” Nalan Mingxue finally snapped back to her senses.","“Charge!”","“Frost Nova!”","“Roar!” A druid turned into a grizzly bear and came up to stop them.","Swoosh! Swoosh! Swoosh! Black Demon’s undead warlock character was shooting Shadow Bolts repeatedly.","Both sides battled fiercely.","Barely dragging his legs from the entangling roots, Harrison continued to run.","“The thief is gone!”","“Go after him!”","Su Tianji began her Roaring Elder Su Mode. “Stop him! Anyone! I’ll control the area with a Frost Nova, and you guys go get him quickly! Ahhh–!”","Puchi!","A Shadow Bolt shot into her head.","An Honorable Kill!","“Ah! Who did it?!”","– In the livestream room –","[The idle Elder Su was killed again!]","[Elder Su: Open the ghost mode!]","[Who was it?! Come out for me!]","“Hahaha...” Lowing his head, Black Demon immediately moved to another position.","...","“What should we do now...? It seems that we’re at a draw?” Mr. Dirk still looked confused.","“Is it because we captured the flag?”","– In the center of the battleground –","“No flag now?”","“We should probably continue...”","They whispered to each other.","Both sides stood on the highlands in their home camps and faced each other from a distance.","“One, two... eight, nine...” They did the headcount. “One person is missing...?”","Now, Elder Su was sitting beside their flag again. “Just watch how I defend the flag all by myself!”","Then, she saw a female undead warrior sneaking up.","“Ugh? New Snow? You dare to come and steal my flag?”","Nalan Mingxue burst out.","“You want to charge?” Su Tianji operated her character with her voice while livestreaming. “I’ll freeze you on the spot with Frost Nova!”","“Frost Bolt! Oh!” Su Tianji stood there and cast the spell, shooting two arrows at Nalan Mingxue.","[Awesome!]","[Entertainment streamer vs. technical streamer!]","Praises flooded the screen.","“Thanks to Elder Su’s Professional Hater for sending 66 ‘Awesomes’.” Su Tianji said in satisfaction, “I’ll show you what a technical streamer looks like, okay?”","While running after Nalan Mingxue who had struggled out of the freezing effect, she said casually, “Someone asked me what I would do if I lose. You guys just have no faith in me, right? If I lose, I’m a muggle!”","The people who had watched Harry Potter were quite familiar with the word ‘Muggle’.","Suddenly, a figure dashed past her from behind.","“How come there is another one?” Su Tianji yelled in alarm. “Assassin!”","Backstab!","“Ahh!” Su Tianji yelled, “Don’t panic! I still have a chance. Watch how I fight two opponents on my own!”","Meanwhile, Nalan Mingxue slashed her with a saber!","“Auch!”","On the screen, bullet comments shot up.","[Elder Su is surrounded!]","[Elder Su is between a rock and a hard place!]","[Elder Su typed out GG!]","“...” The bullet comments flooded the screen.","– Ten seconds later –","Su Tianji fell to the ground.","“Ugh?” While waiting for resurrection, she found that someone donated to her. Sulkily, she took a quick look.","“Thanks to This Elder Is A Muggle for 100 ‘Awesome’!”","“Ugh?” Su Tianji froze. “???”","...","Before long, the battle on the battleground filled with newbies came to the end."]},{"number":689,"title":"Chapter 689 - We Discovered a Super ‘Treasure Reserves’—Deadmines!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","When entering the battleground without a team, individual strength was important but couldn’t change the overall situation, especially in a battle where all the participants were strong.","“I stole the flag!” On the other side, the King of Rangers excitedly carried the Horde’s flag out of its home camp.","“Thanks to my teammates’ coverage, I think I’ll win this round for us!”","Then, he ran into a figure.","Charge!","During the charge, this figure took out a sword and a shield. While blocking the opponent’s arrows, he killed the opponent with a slash!","Honorable Kill!","The King of Rangers was at a loss for words.","“Roar! I got the flag!” Dwarf Elder Sauk immediately ran over to help.","Although they had never met before, at this moment, they were intimate comrades.","“Come and help! I’ve controlled the undead warrior!”","“F*ck your control!” Black Demon hiding in the dark casted the spell named Corruption.","Shadow Bolt!","At this moment, Nalan Mingxue took the opportunity to charge up. At this moment, the orcs’ traits of hardness, which reduced the duration of stun effects, was quite useful!","“I must get away!” In the critical moment, Elder Sauk reacted quickly by leaping dozens of meters backward. Having dodged tons of damages, he avoided the fate of being crippled.","Only one minute was left!","“Orc sword techniques!” With a blood-curdling roar, Mr. Dirk hacked around wildly.","At this moment, a figure fell from the sky.","Puchi!","“I hacked on something?”","Honorable Kill!","“Ugh!?” In Canglan City, Dwarf Elder Sauk put down his virtual reality headset in confusion and slapped his palm on his forehead.","“What happened, Old Friend?” Beside him, Grand Mage Adolf asked curiously.","On Elder Sauk’s screen, his character lay on the ground with a red flag in his hand while an orc stood over him, waving his sword.","Looking at Elder Sauk who still had his hand on his forehead, Adolf made the connection and was speechless.","In this fierce battle full of grand masters, it was hard to notice everything and hear every sound.","“Ugh?”","“Ugh!?”","Having just killed an opponent, Mr. Dirk widened his eyes. Seeing that no one was watching, he picked up the flag and raced back.","[What a lucky dog!] The audience was amazed.","[Embarrassing dog! Waiting to get lucky!] By now Mr. Dirk’s audience obviously had summarized him and made some good quotes.","[It seems that they will win the battle?]","[The Dog-Headed Man who did nothing for the team actually won the battle?]","“Charge of a Fierce Man! Orc Sword Techniques? Ugh? You mean we won? How did we win?!”","“My teammates are so strong! All the credit should go to my awesome teammates!”","“Ahhh!” Yells came from their home camp when the two brought back the flags almost simultaneously.","The time was up!","Soon, the result showed on the interface.","The horde was victorious!","“Rewards for the first victory in the battleground?”","“The awards look plentiful...?”","The rewards for the first victory in battlegrounds were things such as extra experience points and honor points after players obtained a victory on the battleground each day. Each player could take the rewards only once per day.","“Excellent! I’ll do it again tomorrow!”","“Awesome! Anyone wants to join me and fight on the battleground together?”","The Horde players who obtained the victory were thrilled.","Meanwhile, in Elder Su’s livestream room on the side of Alliance.","[Entertainment streamer! Entertainment streamer!]","[This Elder Is A Muggle! She said that! She admitted it herself!]","Bullet comments flooded the screen.","In the King of Rangers’ livestream room.","“I was caught off guard by her attack... It was a mistake.” The King of Rangers was regretful and wanted to battle again.","...","“I leveled up!” Nalan Mingxue’s undead warrior suddenly emitted a series of light as she leveled up standing where she was!","[Where were you?] In the personal chat channel, she saw messages from some elves.","[I went to the battleground.] Nalan Mingxue replied, [I obtained a victory and got some first victory rewards which includes many experience points. I even leveled up once.]","[So fast?] The elves had started to understand the layout of Undercity. They discovered that it was divided into four floors, and the locations marked on the map could be on any of the floors. They could only travel to different floors through the ‘elevators’ in the fixed locations in the city.","Since the city was bigger than the original version, there were more ‘elevators’. After all, it was troublesome to find the locations of the quests on the map and then run back to take the same elevator up or down to find the spot.","At this moment, the elves finally found the way and arrived at the quest location.","Sala returned to her team and said, “I watched the shop owner play this and found that he is several levels higher than us.”","“What’s he doing?” Nalan Mingxue asked.","“I’ve no idea... I only saw him wandering in the wilderness...” Sala complained.","“Don’t mind him.” Nalan Mingxue said, “Do you guys want to fight on the battleground and take the first victory rewards?”","“Okay.”","...","World of Warcraft was a game with many ways of playing. The players preferring PVP could level up through battlegrounds, and there was also the regular leveling-up routes in the wilderness.","Of course, few people would level up only through fighting in battlegrounds. With this method, the players could only level up faster than the regular way by entering each battleground without waiting and winning the battles with a landslide.","The main function of the battlegrounds was leveling up the prestige ranks, which wasn’t a top priority for low-level players.","Therefore, the elves such as Sala and other players just went to the battleground to obtain the first victory before going back to their regular activities.","...","While the players of the undead race in the Horde played happily on the battleground, the Alliance players began to walk out of Stormwind City.","– In the Jiuhua City Shop –","The royal members of the Royal Clan Guild had obviously all chosen to join the Alliance. By now, they had gradually leveled up to level 13 and level 14.","“Growl...” At this moment, Royal Princess Ji Yu and the disciples of Shengjing Academy had played the game for the whole morning, and their bellies growled.","[Sir...] They sent a message to Mr. Fang. [Can’t we have two bowls of instant noodles each day in your shop? We’re now hungry!]","[You can order takeout if you have nothing to eat.] While busy killing mobs, Mr. Fang answered casually.","“Takeout?” Royal Princess Ji Yu said in puzzlement, [What’s that?]","[Touch a button on your communication jade, and your food will come.] Mr. Fang said, [Wait a minute... No one does this in Jiuhua City?]","[No...]","“...” Mr. Fang thought for a moment and then browsed his QQ.","Dong Qingli.","[Your Wind and Moon Pavilion doesn’t want to do takeout business?]","“Huh?” Dong Qingli looked baffled. [Take... what? What’s that?]","...","Meanwhile, in the Jiuhua City Shop, some members of the Royal Clan Guild were still playing World of Warcraft. Suddenly, the Second Prince yelled, “Look what I found!”","“It’s a new place... Deadmines?!”","“What’s this place for?!”","“Is it a treasure reserve...” The Second Prince looked around and saw that no one had been here yet, and this place reminded him of the mine tunnels and the Corpse King Palace in the Legend of Mir 2.","If this place also was a super treasure reserve like the Corpse King Palace...","The Second Prince sent several private messages in the game. [You guys, come and check this out! I found a super treasure reserve! Get more people here! Get more people here!]"]},{"number":690,"title":"Chapter 690 - The Beginning of ‘For the Horde!’","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","The epic legends told by the bards sounded very distant for people in this age. The deeds in the legends had been long forgotten or only existed in the fragmented tales or legends passing down from the distant past. However, part of the things told in the seemingly unreachable legends and tales had existed all the time but were not known to ordinary people.","Humans seemed to be living on an island named Ignorance in the gloomy ocean which was vast and contained endless mysteries. But luckily for most of the people, they didn’t venture too far out or examine things too carefully.","-In the Silver Moon Forest of the Elf Clan-","In the royal palace of the Elf Clan lived the royal members who enjoyed the loftiest rank within their society. Only elders and royal members could enter this place.","Standing beside the lake that was as calm as a clear mirror, a silver-haired and silver-bearded old elf seemed to be able to look through the lake and into the void with his deep eyes.","“What do you see, First Elder?” A middle-aged elf who wore the same luxurious elder robe walked up from behind.","“I see nothing... except for darkness...” that elder murmured, “How long has it been since the last time that we received a message from the Elf God...?”","Only silence answered him.","“...”","“Elder.” After a long while, an elf reported to him, “From the clues that we have gathered, we seemed to have found something new...”","The silver-haired and silver-bearded elder of the Elf Clan nodded and asked solemnly, “Where’s Elder Sewell? I haven’t seen her lately.”","“Elder Sewell went to a human nation, saying that she would try a mystical realm in a place called Origins Internet Café. She said that she will be back at the end of August.”","“What month is it now...?” The First Elder of the Elf Clan glanced around the trees. Despite the permanent spring in the forest, he could still detect the small changes.","“It’s October now, Elder.”","“Has Elder Sewell returned...?”","“Not yet...”","...","– In the new Canglan City Shop of Origins Internet Café –","At this moment, messages jumped in Mr. Fang’s QQ’s interface.","-Inside the chat box with Dong Qingli-","Mr. Fang said, [I say... Can’t you detect any new business opportunity after being a shop owner for so long?]","Dong Qingli replied, [(Pikachu’s cute emoji) What business opportunity? You won’t agree to sell me hundreds of boxes of instant noodles!]","Mr. Fang’s face twitched. [No... With so many people coming from outside the city, don’t you see their needs?]","[What needs?]","Mr. Fang replied, [... They need to eat!]","Dong Qingli said, [I know it. Many of them go to my restaurant, but the seats are not enough for them all sometimes. Later, some people have begun bringing meals with them...]","[So...] Mr. Fang suggested, [Can’t you do the takeout business?! Since you don’t have enough seats in the restaurant, you can deliver the food to them! Now that everyone has communication jades, can’t you guys use your brain and think of a solution?!]","[Um... You might be right...] Dong Qingli thought for a moment and said.","[Might be?! What do you mean by might be?] Mr. Fang’s face darkened. [Do you know how to do business? Do you need me to teach you how to run your own business?]","[No... My restaurant is managed by Wanyu and others...]","Mr. Fang was at a loss for words, [...]","– In the chat box with Shen Qingqing –","Mr. Fang said, [Do you guys have plans after graduation?]","Shen Qingqing said, [What plans?]","Mr. Fang said, [Don’t you have any ambition? What’s your dream?]","Shen Qingqing replied, [My dream is staying in Jiuhua City. After playing games for a few more years, I will become a female Emperor Warrior with my talent.]","Mr. Fang said, [Don’t you have a bigger dream?]","Shen Qingqing said, [I think this dream is very big.]","Mr. Fang looked frustrated. [You lazy people. By the way, I got the content ready for the new official novels. One is Dungeon Fighter Online and the other is World of Warcraft: Rise of the Horde.]","The plot for Dungeon Fighter Online focused on the stories of the adventurers and thus was relatively simple.","The other book, Rise of the Horde, could be seen in World of Warcraft the game. On Mr. Fang’s screen, the undead rogue was holding a damaged book – Rise of the Horde.","When he opened the book, he could read the fragments of the story.","In World of Warcraft, one could find treasure chests and treasures in the relics and caves. Likewise, there were stories about World of Warcraft in relics or libraries. They told some stirring past events relating to World of Warcraft.","“Hu...” Fang Qi exhaled deeply. He only remembered the general plot of the story. Only if he could find the original story... even a partial one would be helpful.","Of course, in the game, he could only see a damaged book written in the Horde language, which meant that he would need translators who excelled in the Spiritual State language and the Nora Continent language to do the work.","Therefore, an idea occurred to him...","At this moment, Jessica and the other janitors who were eating melons and drinking tea in the Yuanyang City Shop picked up their communication jade. “... Ugh? An opportunity to get a promotion...? Translate Rise of the Horde?”","“What’s this thing?”","...","After the teleportation array was in operation, Fang Qi could travel between his shops with ease.","In the Wind and Moon Pavilion, Mr. Fang booked a compartment.","Besides Mr. Fang, Shen Qingqing and the super janitor team including Jessica sat in it.","Mr. Fang was sulky that he, an internet café owner, had to tell stories to these people.","On second thought, he realized that it would be great for him if his games could be presented to all the players perfectly.","...","As told in the book, “This tale isn’t about the Horde as it existed today, a loose organization of orcs, taurens, forsaken, trolls, and blood elves. It is about the earliest Horde, the Horde that first rose. Like that of any infant, its birth was marked by blood and pain, and its harsh cries seeking for life meant death to its enemies.”","“This bloody story had a peaceful beginning. It was in a rolling valley in the green continent named Draenor...”","The story told how the orcs turned from a peaceful race to slaves of the Burning Legion, how they became blood-thirsty, combative, and destructive, and how Ner’zhul and Gul’dan fell and degenerated driven by their hunger for strength and power.","With a tragic tone, the book retold the gradual downfall of the Orc Clan and the helpless lamentations of all the conscientious orcs.","The exile of the Frostwolf Clan gave the orcs a sliver of hope and made them get away from the conflicts, saving the last bit of force for the orc race.","...","The following was one paragraph from the book:","Blackhand, the Warlord of Blackrock Clan, demonstrated the first group of warlocks that he had trained to other clans.","“Brothers and sisters of the orc race!” Blackhand shouted, “You gave me honor and respect, and I will not let down the countless noble warriors. We’re strengthening our weapons and armor each day. Now, we discard those unpredictable elements and possess true power, which means that we don’t have to beg from anyone for anything. This power is controlled and mastered by our warlocks! This is true power! We have a clear objective; we will eliminate the Draenei from our land! They will not be able to block the crazy herds of our warriors and warlocks. We will be their worst nightmare! Fight!”","He raised his arms and shouted, “For the Horde!”","Thousands of voices yelled with great passion, “For the Horde! For the Horde! For the Horde!”","The tragic and thrilling scene was only a small splash in the huge plot of World of Warcraft, but the words ‘For the Horde’ had since spread all over the world."]},{"number":691,"title":"Chapter 691 - The Exploitation Journey of the People in This World","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","While mentioning Deadmines, it was closely related to Stormwind City.","If a foreign traveler walked into Stormwind City through its grand main gate, the first thing that this person would see would be the grand statues in the Valley of Heroes. These Alliance heroes stood out at the critical moment and led troops to the battleground in another world named Draenor. For a long time, no one had received any word from them.","Mistakenly thinking that they had died, the Alliance set up these statues to commemorate these great heroes.","With exquisite designs, the Stonemason Guild built Stormwind City into a place with districts that had diffident functions, including the prosperous trade district, noble and elegant mage quarter, and dwarven district where the dwarf and gnome artisans lived.","The core of Stormwind City was Stormwind Keep, sitting at the highest position in the northwest district of the city; it was probably the most magnificent construction in the entirety of the Alliance.","Every human player would be stunned by this fortress-like super city after they entered Stormwind City. All the designs, executions, and construction of the city were done by the most talented Stonemason Guild in the kingdom at the time.","However, due to the instigations and conspiracies in Stormwind Kingdom, King Varian Wrynn lost his queen, and the artisan heroes of Stormwind City didn’t get their pay for their work. Instead, they were kicked out of their homes by the king.","These heroes later became the Defias Brotherhood.","For the new players in the Alliance, the most stunning thing next to the grand Stormwind City was the vast and fertile Westfall full of withering weeds.","This was the home camp of the Defias Brotherhood. Blinded by hatred, they had done many crazy things and were no longer the great and talented artisans they had once been.","They had contacted almost all the pirates and rogues in the world and recruited many of them into their brotherhood. Taking possession of most of the farmlands, mines, and villages in Westfall, they built their headquarters in the mine shafts.","It was the background of the Deadmines instance in World of Warcraft.","The players of the Royal Clan Guild obviously had found this place through a quest.","Despite the remoteness of this place, the NPC Gryan Stoutmantle at Sentinel Hill in Westfall would give quests about the Defias Brotherhood. The dwarves in the dwarven district at Stormwind City would give related quests as well. Following the instructions of the quests, the players would have little difficulty in finding the entrance.","Therefore, besides members of the Royal Clan Guild, Liu Ningyun and other disciples of the Nanhua Faction of the Morning Star Sea Realm, the mercenaries in the new shop who had chosen to join the Alliance, and mages such as Adolf and Dicas were also coming to this place.","Controlling her female warrior character of the Alliance to come before the mine shaft, Royal Princess Ji Yu saw the entrance to the deserted mine, the wagon tracks half-buried in the ground, and the deserted miner’s lamps.","Outside the gate was a dark purple vortex, looking like a magic portal.","At this moment, the Royal Clan Guild had gathered dozens of elites at this place including several princes, the Shengjing Academy Instructor Liang Heihu, and his disciple Xiao Lengyu.","They looked as if they had taken over this mine for themselves.","“We... let’s go in and see what’s behind this mysterious spiritual spell vortex!” Ji Xu said.","A big team of Royal Clan Guild elites and disciples of Shengjing Academy followed her into the vortex.","“Ugh?” The moment Ji Yu entered the ‘spiritual spell vortex’, she felt as if ...","“Senior Liang... Are you still here?”","“Ms. Xiao?”","“Captain Yu...?”","She looked around and only saw the Second Prince and the Fifth Prince. “Where are the others? How come only you two are here?”","“No idea...” The Second Prince looked nonplussed.","Fifth Prince Ji Yang said, “Is it because... we formed a team?”","“Ugh...?” Ji Yu froze. “We can’t stay together without forming a team here...? But...”","“The maximum of a team is five people!”","After all that, only five people can form a team?!","Royal Princess Ji Yu’s face darkened, realizing that it was a waste of effort and time to gather so many people here.","“...”","“Forget it...” Ji Yu said, “Let’s explore this... Deadmines ourselves.”","“If we can loot a technique book similar to Enchanting Light...”","They would be rich!","Obviously, these players were thinking of the mine tunnels in the Legend of Mir 2.","The mine tunnels with many branches were illuminated since there were people living inside. The lights were dim but were bright enough for them to see their surroundings.","“Then, we must explore this mine by ourselves,” Royal Princess Ji Yu said.","The three members of the Royal Clan Guild were all warriors.","“It seems like some people are in here...” Royal Princess Ji Yu said in a low voice.","At this moment, a few members of the Defias Brotherhood in the complex depths of the tunnels heard the tiny sounds and walked up to them.","As rogues at the headquarters of the Defias Brotherhood, they were very alert and had acute senses.","“One, two, three... there are three of them,” Royal Princess Ji Yu whispered. “Each of us take one.”","Charge!","Three figures bust out almost at the same time.","Ding!","With crisp noises, their blades were all blocked!","These humanoid mobs were many times better than the mobs outside in terms of combat skills, speed, and reflexes.","However, the players in the Royal Clan Guild were veteran fighters with a ton of experiences. When their swords were blocked, they turned their blades and slashed again.","After experiencing Devil May Cry 3, Final Fantasy 7, and The Duel, they were very skillful with both single-handed swords and two-handed swords.","Soon, the rogues of the Defias Brotherhood were no match for them. At this moment, a sword beam hacked down viciously and drew out a bright silver arc.","Executed!","Blood sprayed in all directions.","Execute was a skill for warriors: Attempts to finish off a foe, turning the remaining Rage into a ton of damage.","In the mine tunnels, many miners and foremen of the Defias Brotherhood heard the commotion and swarmed out from the many tunnels.","The miners were not strong, but the foremen had great strength.","“Hu... We killed them all?”","“They were good.” Royal Princess Ji Yu brushed the dust off her clothes and said in a cold voice, “But they were not good enough to kill us.”","Meanwhile, Liu Ningyun, Mo Xian, Yue Yan, and other disciples of the Nanhua Faction were...","“Senior Sister! Senior Sister! Cast the Frost Nova!”","“Arcane Blast! Cast an Arcane Blast!”","“Oh! Cast Polymorph: Sheep!”","They had also fought their way into the tunnel.","“The Deadmines sounds scary, but it is quite easy...” Yue Yan brushed the dust off her hands.","“Let’s go! There might be treasures inside!” The group hurried to the depths of the instance.","While they walked into the interior of the mine, the scene before them changed. Walking out of the dilapidated and dim mine tunnel, they found that the space before them turned bigger, and the huge metal archway looked like a portal leading to an underground fortress.","The entrance was guarded by a humanoid monster with greyish-red skin, and it was as tall as two men.","The huge hammer in its hand was as big as half of Ji Yu’s body. Without thinking, one strike of the hammer could smash a person into a meat pie.","Two elite Defias rogues flanked him.","“I’ll go up and cast Frost Nova and Arcane Blast!” Yue Yan walked up and said.","“Good! Good! I’ll cheer for you, Junior Sister!” Mo Xian encouraged her from behind.","-On the other side-","“Each of us charge at one of them!”","“Royal Sister, you take the big guy, ok?”","“Of course, he’s mine!” Ji Yu said proudly."]},{"number":692,"title":"Chapter 692 - The darkness that can’t be dispelled by light","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","In this world, there was a name called Shadow Hand.","Perhaps for the mercenaries and mages under level 7, they didn’t understand what this name meant.","The world was much bigger than what the low-level and mid-level people could imagine.","Only those existences above level 7 or had a lofty status knew of this name.","The name was guarded so heavily that even these people could only pick up on a few clues about it.","The people in the world would be shocked if they truly understood the meaning of the name and the truth behind the shadows.","Perhaps it was a mercy for most people that they lacked the logic and ability to put things together in the big picture.","In the Elf Clan’s Silver Moon Forest, the silver-haired and silver-bearded old elf gazed at the lake that was as tranquil as a mirror with his deep and turbid eyes.","In the reflection of Silver Moon Forest in the lake, a gloomy shadow seemed to have appeared.","“Shadow Legion...” The First Elder of the Elf Clan murmured, “I see its traces in the shadow of time.”","...","Meanwhile, Adolf, who was dressed in a white mage’s robe, was standing on the top of a high white spire.","Before him was a statue of a mage that had ancient facial features, and the statue held a crystal ball as big as a head in its hands.","As he said the incantation, the crystal ball slowly revealed a strange and ancient land.","“Do you feel that...”","In the jade-like greeneries was a layer of gloomy mist which engulfed the whole place like an invisible shadowy hand. Death and desolation covered the place without the intention of loosening their grip.","“In this world, there might be a type of darkness that even light can’t dispel...”","...","In the distant Radiant Light Godly Nation, the Supreme Holy Palace of the Judgement Godly Palace stood on the highest position in the mountain range covered in ice and snow.","St. Heinz had gone to the highest position in the Supreme Holy Palace where people could almost directly face the godly light, trying to get inspiration and messages from the gods.","At this moment, St. Dulan was chanting his prayers in the Sacrifice Hall in the Supreme Holy Palace.","He only walked out of the hall after a long time.","Then, a priest walked up and presented him with a document respectfully.","“Have you found out all about it?” Obviously, St. Dulan was quite busy; he asked while quickly striding forward.","“Yes... the Origins Internet Club seems to come from the East Continent... It’s a mystical realm agency for several ‘alchemy workshops’.”","“The East Continent...?” St. Dulan frowned.","“Yes,” the priest said in resentment, “It reached its hand into the Continent of Immortal Relics, and we can tolerate that. However, now they are reaching out their hands under our nose! Damn it!”","St. Dulan snorted heavily, “Indeed, they should be damned.”","It would be fine if it was only a small shop. But if it was backed by the forces of the whole East Continent...","“We should call for all races on the whole continent to kick out these people who came from the foreign continent. They are not welcomed here!” the priest suggested in a loud voice.","...","Meanwhile, Nalan Mingxue was livestreaming the quest that she was doing with her classmates and a group of elves.","With so many people in her team, the risk was low. Therefore, they chatted with each other while doing the quest.","Bullet comments appeared on the screen.","[It’s a bonus that we can hear stories about the Elf Clan while watching the livestream!]","[They said that many members of the Elf Clan had died while they resisted the...?]","[A knight legion joined the battle, and many knights died too...]","[It’s a sad story...]","[What sad story...?] Dong Qingli had finished her business talk with Mr. Fang and just began watching the livestream. Having not heard the story, she immediately sent a bullet message onto the screen, asking, [I’m new here; is there a new story here?]","[Hey! Don’t just lament about sadness; tell me the story!]","[Sorry, the person before me, you’re late.]","[It’s what you get for not paying attention!]","“...” Dong Qingli was frustrated. The damn Mr. Fang forced me to listen to the story about ‘Ele.me’ and kept me from watching the livestream and listening to stories. He even called me lazy. Why! Can the food delivery business be more profitable than running a restaurant?!","[TL Note: Ele.me means ‘Are you hungry’ in Chinese, and it is a large food delivery company in China.]","Feeling as if she had missed out on many good things, Dong Qingli had to wait for tomorrow’s VOD.","...","At this moment, Adolf’s disciple was playing World of Warcraft in the internet café and finally came close to level 16.","[Do you choose to release the soul?]","The screen turned grey while the mob left without looking back.","[Level 15, 99% experience points.]","“...”","[Dicas, your mage character is weak.] Obviously, many mages of the Royal Magic Union had been watching her doing quests. Right now, she was in Westfall as well.","[You progress so slowly... and your damage is weak too. It takes you a long time to kill a mob. Why did you choose this character?]","[I can’t watch it anymore. Are the mages in this mystical realm all as weak as this one?]","[Not all mages in this mystical realm are weak.] A mage who had watched the battleground said, [Only her mage character is weak. I saw another mage freeze everyone with a ring of frost. Those black magic arrows are good too, at least in terms of low-level spells.]","[Why don’t you change your character?]","[I suggest you change it.]","“Oh... you guys are so annoying.” Dicas wondered in bafflement, “But how come I feel like this priest character is leveling up slower and slower?”","She had felt fine when everyone could cast only one spell. But now, while other mages could cast several spells and could even attack a group of mobs and have crowd control, she still could cast only two spells?","The most infuriating was that when she fought several mobs, her magic energy (mana) would run out before she could kill them.","What’s this holy light or something... it’s not useful at all... how can it be named with the word ‘holy’?!","In the opening animatics, it said that I must shoulder the burden of saving the human race. How can things go awry in such a way?!","...","– Meanwhile, in the Deadmines –","“Haya!” Royal Princess Ji Yu charged first.","Charge!","In another Deadmines, Yue Yan, a mage, dashed out bravely.","Frost Nova!","Ji Yu hacked her double-handed sword onto the belly of the huge ogre with a vicious force.","Meanwhile, in another instance, chilly frost swept across the place as if it would freeze everything it touched.","“Ugh...?” The dark-red-skinned ogre lowered its head curiously.","A sword left a small scratch on the thick skin on his belly.","A shaft of frost swept across his foot, giving him a cool sensation.","“...”","It said in a muffled voice, “VanCleef will get good prices for your heads.”","The two saw a huge hammer crashing down toward them.","They dropped to the ground and couldn’t get up.","The two princes who were ready to charge at the remaining two monsters looked at Royal Princess Ji Yu. “...”","Mo Xian and others who had been watching Yue Yan trying to control the monster were at a loss for words.","While their faces twitched, they fled instantly.","“Hey! I’m still alive!” Lying on the ground, Royal Princess Ji Yu lifted her hand up and shouted.","Clank!","The hammer struck again.","The Fifth Prince Ji Yang said, “I felt like I heard something?”","The Second Prince, “I don’t know. Run!”","“You...”","Clank!","Silence permeated the area.","“...”"]},{"number":693,"title":"Chapter 693 - The Greatest Power of Holy Light: Redemption!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Where are you guys?!” Having turned into a soul, Yue Yan yelled in the group channel.","In the complex mine tunnels, other disciples of Nanhua Faction had fled for a good distance.","“Let’s see if that big guy is still there...” Having watched Yue Yan instantly getting killed by one hammer strike, Mo Xian suggested with unease.","“Um... it seems like it’s not chasing us,” a disciple of Nanhua Faction said.","The moment he said it, they heard heavy footsteps coming from the nearest corner in the mine tunnel.","A huge figure appeared at the end of the tunnel.","“My goodness... it is chasing after us!”","The group ran out of the instance, and they were out of breath.","In a huff, Yue Yan put down her virtual reality headset and said, “You bullied and deserted me, a cute and smart little junior sister! Are you still human?”","Mo Xian replied, “We chose the human race... Of course, we are human.”","“...”","...","Meanwhile, the brothers in the Royal Clan Guild were beaten so hard that they almost fell below a table.","“Big Sister... Big Sister... How come this big guy is so powerful?” After a while, Fifth Prince Ji Yang finally found a chance to change the topic while raising his arms to protect his head.","“Powerful?!” After all, she had been killed with three hammer strikes. “If you helped me, we could still fight it!”","“The problem is... If we did, we would still have to deal with the other two elite mobs...” The Fifth Prince said with a troubled expression.","At this moment, the people who had entered the Deadmines came out one after another.","They either came out shaken after having a tough time, or they came out as souls, waiting to return and pick up their corpses.","“Should we...” Fifth Prince Ji Yang said with a dark expression, “Should we find two more teammates and try it again?”","“What are you doing here?” A voice came from the nearby crowd. Nalan Hongwu glanced around the crowd with a sword in his hand, seeing that many people had gathered here.","“This mine is impossible to pass,” said Fifth Prince Ji Yang.","“Should we call the shop owner?” Ji Yu complained, “I feel like it’s not a quest for players who are level 16 or 17. There must be a problem with this quest.”","With a frown, Nalan Hongwu thought for a moment and said, “Don’t call him. I’ll go in and try it with you guys.”","When he watched and played the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4, Nalan Hongwu was deeply stunned by the human cultivators’ spirit of independence and self-improvement.","Regardless if what they did was right or wrong and what the ending was, the unyielding determination touched him more than anything else that he experienced.","It was a sensation different from the amazement he felt when playing the previous games in the Legend of Sword and Fairy series. In the past, he had only been amazed by the novel sword techniques, spiritual spells, and the great powers exhibited by the immortals and demons in the games.","Those powers didn’t belong to mortals after all. One would be extremely fortunate to learn a sliver of it.","But the spirit and the determination of overpowering the Mandate of Heaven shown in the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4 gave him a different feeling.","Mortals were born insignificant, but perhaps this willpower and spirit were what made them great.","“I think we must find a solution by ourselves this time,” said Nalan Hongwu.","“But...” Yue Yan complained, “That monster can’t be frozen, and we will be killed or severely wounded by one touch of that big hammer. I don’t know what other skills it has...”","“I think Senior Nalan is right,” Liang Heihu said in a loud voice, “Each time we meet some difficulties that seemed impossible to solve, we would ask Mr. Fang, and he would solve them with ease. What does it tell us? It means that the designs are reasonable, and we just didn’t find a way to deal with these difficulties. Knowing this, why not try it ourselves?”","Yue Yan and the others froze.","“You’re right...” Liu Ningyun suddenly nodded deeply.","Why can Mr. Fang do it? Because the mysterious senior gave him private lessons?","Why do we always think that other people, who can solve problems that we can’t, must have had private lessons or even cheated?","Mr. Fang’s proficiency in the game and familiarity with each detail couldn’t simply explained by having private lessons.","Perhaps he had experienced the same hardships and had even thought that these issues were impossible to overcome. However, he had kept working on it to accumulate experience and finally found a way to solve the seemingly impossible problems.","Perhaps it is just that we don’t know about his hard work?","Yue Yan wiped sweat off her forehead while blazing determination appearing in her eyes. “You’re right! Today, we’ll explore by ourselves! Like the people in the Legend of the Sword and Fairy 4, we must strengthen ourselves and take our destiny into our own hands!”","“Then...” Liang Heihu said with enthusiasm, “Senior Nalan, Princess Ji Yu, Fairy Liu, Mo Xian, and I will form a self-improvement team today.”","“How about me?” Yue Yan stared at them and gaped.","“Um...” Mo Xian said in a hurry, “Junior Sister, you just wait here. This self-improvement must be very tiring. When I get tired, you can take my place, okay?”","“...”","...","The knights in this world were more noble than ordinary warriors. They were usually personal guards of different forces or protectors of a certain area. For example, the Golden Griffin Knight Legion was one of the guardians of Canglan City.","In fact, even the Stan Kingdom, the nation of knights, didn’t have a clear definition for knights. Perhaps they were warriors who sat on mounts.","At this moment, a group of paladins in the Canglan City Shop finally earned enough money to learn skills.","“This... it seems like there’s a quest?” Having learned new skills, the knights chatted with the trainer who usually only shouted, “May the Holy Light be with you.” They found that they had another quest left to do. At this moment, the prompt for the quests on the interface were about to turn grey. In this online game, the grey-colored quests gave no experience points.","“If you agree, I’ll give you a book. With this book, you’ll understand what Holy Light is and its expectations for you,” the trainer said, “After understanding it and proving your abilities, you’ll obtain greater power.”","Soon, Commander Elven chose to accept it and received the quest for the Tome of Divinity, which was a special quest only for paladins.","“What’s this...?” Other knights moved over to Commander Elven and took a look.","It was an ancient and thick book with a dark green cover. The content of the book seemed to be the ancient beliefs and code of conduct for paladins.","“In all things, paladins must reflect the Light, which supplements our strength. To strive to be divine for one of our kind does not mean we strive for godhood–we strive to be good in all actions.”","“Although called upon to smite evil in these harsh times, you must always remember that it’s aiding others that will truly set you apart from the other citizens. Compassion, patience, bravery–these things mean as much to a paladin as strength in battle. Know this well, and never forget it...”","After reading this book, the paladins followed the instructions of the quest and helped pure-hearted people in difficulties. While they did these good deeds, they began to consider the meaning of being a paladin.","They felt as if they were engulfed by the warmth from the friendly smiles, sincerest blessings, and heart-felt gratitude. They felt as warm as if they were bathed in Holy Light.","Finally, after they had proven their compassion and patience, they came before the trainer again.","At this moment, they received a quest to rescue a dead person.","“It’s already a corpse... and we need to go and save it...?” The paladins exchanged a look, reading the shock and alarm in each other’s eyes.","They had heard from the trainer that he would teach them the greatest power of Holy Light. Could it be that the greatest power was...","“!!??” Their horrified expressions turned into shock!"]},{"number":694,"title":"Chapter 694 - Shadow","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","According to the legends, the Shadow Legion was also followers of gods.","However, these gods probably were not kind and friendly gods.","It was a tranquil small border town in the northeast of the Orc Kingdom.","It was evening. The setting sun shined on the small lanes in the fields, and the sunlight seemed to spread dark red blankets over them.","Some kids were frolicking tirelessly at the entrance of the village, and a butterfly lightly landed on a nearby fence which was covered by vines of morning glory.","Most of the busy villagers had walked back home after a long day.","A middle-aged shepherd hummed an unknown song while he herded a group of sheep through the fields.","Also, the hunters returned, chatting and laughing after a day of hunting magic beasts in the forest. Right now, giant grey wolves were draped over their shoulders.","Suddenly, like a dream, black winds swept across the land, and lightning bolts and thunder tore open the sky, shattering the tranquility of the small town. A thin and tall demon-like figure walked out of the darkness.","Another figure wearing a wide black mage’s cloak walked beside him. Under the cloak, nothing but a dark void could be seen.","They walked up as if they had brought death with them.","“You... you’re...” a farmer froze and asked uneasily.","“Ah... we need some...sacrifices.”","“You mean these cows and sheep?” The farmer looked at the horrifying figures with confusion and fear.","“No.”","In the shadows, it seemed like a monster opened its giant mouth.","A shrill scream rose and didn’t stop for a long time, as if this person who just screamed was being cruelly tortured. It didn’t stop even when the voice turned hoarse.","Blood sprayed all over the ground.","All the people in the town, regardless if they were civilians and warriors, screamed in fear and fled as if they had become crazy.","“Don’t waste our time,” the figure dressed in the black robe said.","“No.” Seeing the people struggling in pain, the thin and long figure said, “It’s fun, isn’t it?”","“No... don’t come closer!” Two knights drew out their longswords and demanded.","“Don’t you... want to run?”","“We’re not afraid of you!” While shaking, the two knights stood their ground with cold sweat drops sliding down their heads. They looked as if they would turn and run in the next instant.","“You are looking for me, right?” At this moment, a middle-aged knight walked out from the crowd.","“You are...” The two knights studied the bearded man whose face looked like a lion. In disbelief, they looked again to confirm and shouted, “Lion’s Heart! Are you Lion’s Heart Sutifaer, a level 9 knight?!”","“You guys back off!” The middle-aged knight looked grim.","But in the next instant...","“Uh...” With a snort of pain, the level 9 knight looked down at his chest in horror and saw that his heart was gone! Only a black claw-shaped hole was left in its place.","“Level 9... knight?” The thin and tall figure smirked and tossed away the knight’s corpse as if it was a piece of garbage. “What garbage is that?”","As if countless horrifying monsters and evil creatures struggled out from the darkness, screams and howls filled the small town which had been tranquil a moment ago. Even the frolicking kids at the entrance of the village were turned into corpses with distorted faces as if they had experienced things that were extremely painful.","The whole place was turned into a living hell of blood and death.","“We... only need a little sacrifice...”","...","No one knew about the event that was taking place on the other end of the continent.","Canglan City was as bustling and busy as usual.","It must be noted that in the period before Fang Qi traveled through time and space, the max level in World of Warcraft was level 60, and every class had its class quests every ten levels.","The quests explained each class’s code of conduct, beliefs, and the meaning of its existence. From doing these quests, the players learned that their classes weren’t just different in name; there was more to it.","Having come to this stage of their quests, the golden griffin knights had the last person to save, and it was a dwarf. The dwarf who they had saved in the Cathedral told them that some dwarves had overheard the scheme of the Defias Brotherhood by Stone Cairn Lake in the east of Elwynn Forest and tried to stop them. They were attacked during the process, and their brother, Henze, died while he tried to hold off the mages of the Defias Brotherhood.","Coming to Stone Cairn Lake, the golden griffin knights started to breathe rapidly.","“Can we really use this...” Commander Elven was uneasy while he held the Symbol of Life that the best paladin in Stormwind City had handed to him. “Can we really bring people back to life with this...?”","Chilly rain was falling in Stone Cairn Lake. At this moment, the Defias rogues had been driven away, and only a cold corpse lay in the center of the small island.","It was a stout dwarf whose clothes were soaked by the rain. With a ton of blood washed away by the rain water, this dwarf obviously had been dead for some time.","“Use this thing?” Under the gazes of other golden griffin knights, Commander Elven activated the Symbol of Life with Holy Light in his body.","Soon, his palms and body were engulfed by a wave of warm light.","The golden light seemed to have spread to the dwarf’s corpse. Then a hole appeared in the dark clouds in the sky, and a beam of golden light shined on the corpse.","Then, they watched as the ‘corpse’ recovered his senses and got up from the ground!","“Miracle! It’s a miracle!” Seeing this scene, the knights were greatly amazed and deeply touched while they witnessed the miracle under Holy Light with their own eyes!","This amazing power, and this terrifying miracle. Is this what paladins are?!","No! Even saints can’t bring the dead back to life. It was the forbidden privilege of gods!","They were elated and thrilled that they could bring a person who had been dead for a long while back to vibrant life.","They felt as if they had grasped a giant horrifying secret. They felt like it was probably the biggest miracle in the world! No thing could top it!","“Thank you.” When the dwarf stood up, most of the wounds on him were all healed. “Thank you for saving my life. Not everyone can use the Symbol of Life. The fact that you can activate it means that you have enough faith.”","“Oh! Really?!” Commander Elven looked around in disbelief.","“I also think that Mr. Elven is a humble and friendly person.”","“Oh! Hahaha! Does it mean that I can learn this ability?” Commander Elven said in elation.","..."]},{"number":695,"title":"Chapter 695 - Class Oath","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","A solemn and holy declaration resonated in the cathedral, “From now on, I’ll embrace Holy Light with my heart, protect the weak with my sword and shield, and vanquish evil with Holy Light. Humility, honesty, compassion, valor, justice, sacrifice, honor, and spirituality are the eight virtues that I’ll never forget. We’ll not fall as long as people need our protection!”","“May Holy Light be with you!”","Perhaps they have had moments of confusion and loss, but at this moment, a small flame was kindled in their hearts. It was insignificant now, but it might one day be able to emit radiant lights like the sun.","From now on, they had a new skill.","[Redemption: brings a dead ally back to life with 35% of their maximum health and mana.]","Perhaps at this moment, they truly embarked on the holy journey of paladins.","“I think we should try this!” After obtaining this new skill that was sp powerful that it could be considered a miracle, the members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion were as elated as kids who had just gotten a new toy.","Walking out of Stormwind City into Duskwood and Westfell, they cast Redemption whenever they saw a corpse. The people had died due to various reasons such as being ganged up on by mobs falling short on mana. Regardless of what caused their deaths, they were resurrected one by one.","Seeing the confusion and elation on the faces of the revived people and how they turned into gratitude in the end, the paladins felt like their hearts were wrapped in warmth.","“May Holy Light be with you!” they yelled.","“This feeling is so good.” Helen sat down on a boulder by the road and drank some water to recover her mana.","...","-Meanwhile, the exploration in the Deadmines continued-","“Stop it! Stop it!” Shouts came from the mine tunnels.","“Turn the elite mobs to sheep!” Mage’s spell, Polymorph: Sheep, was miraculous and could last a long time even at low levels. Two mages waved their wands, and the two elite monsters flanking the boss instantly turned into bleating sheep.","At this moment, the ogre roared. Bypassing Nalan Hongwu and Liang Heihu, it lunged at the two mages behind them.","Caught off guard, mages who were just above level 10 didn’t have enough physical strength to deal with the boss even if they had fast reflexes. They were smashed instantly!","Then, the whole group was wiped out.","“It’s impossible to win...” Mo Xian complained.","Obviously, it wasn’t the first time that they were wiped out.","In the system version of World of Warcraft, there were no skills to fixate aggro, which meant that the melee players must do their best to anger the target since the monsters would decide whom to attack using their own judgement. If it thought that the ranged players posed a greater danger, it would dump the melee players and lunge at the ranged players.","“I think that you warriors should have stopped it when the big guy lunged at us!”","“How could we?” Royal Princess Ji Yu said angrily, “We can only dodge its giant hammer and attack it while jumping around. I can’t block it even with my double-handed sword! Its strength is so great that even the counterforce will make us spit blood.”","“We can’t win unless our defense can block its attacks,” Liang Shi said, “But the truth is, the strength gap is too huge for us to do that.”","“How about... I will try again with a shield?” As a man who grew up in the military, Nalan Hongwu had used every kind of weapon in his hundreds of years of service in the army. Besides, there were shield soldiers in Dajin.","“Change to shields?!” Their eyes suddenly brightened.","When they entered the Deadmines again, they were more proficient. Immediately, they turned the two elite mobs into sheep, and then Nalan Hongwu charged with a shield.","Three warriors tried to battle around the ogre. Soon, the ogre lunged at the mages in the back of the formation again.","At this moment, Nalan Hongwu blocked the ogre’s way with a shield.","“Get out!” The ogre smashed its hammer onto the big shield with vicious force. Excelling in every kind of weapon, Nalan Hongwu shifted the shield slightly to the side, and the ogre’s huge hammer slid to one side while gliding on the surface of the shield. This impact only forced Nalan Hongwu to retreat a few steps.","“That’s effective!” Everyone got excited, thinking that they were closer to success!","“Continue with the DPS!” The two mages chanted the magic spells again. The ogre moved, and Nalan Hongwu moved with this monster. Meanwhile, the mages adjusted their distances continuously. Soon, the ogre was covered in wounds.","But at this moment, they suddenly found...","“No! Senior is going to fall! He can’t take it anymore!” Liang Heihu roared.","While the big shield managed to block the attacks, the huge impact force from the hammer strikes could still injure the defender’s organs.","Each player worked like a highly efficient machine, but they still were no match for the boss at the moment.","Soon, the party was wiped out again.","“Should we change to shields too?!” Waiting to recover the corpses was a long process. Each time they died in an instance, they had to release their souls and come back from the graveyard.","At this moment, a group of knights and Mage Dicas also came to this place.","“Why are you all standing here? Why don’t you enter?” Commander Elven and the other golden griffin knights looked at them curiously.","It was after 4 PM, and most of the players had spent over eight hours in the game now that the limit of daily game time was ten hours. Soon, players of all classes from different places of the Alliance gathered here.","“We’re waiting for our teammates to run back and recover their corpses...” Looking at this unfamiliar paladin, Liang Heihu said mildly.","“Run back... for corpses?” Commander Elven said friendly, “Do you need help? We can help resurrect your teammates and save you lots of time!”","Of course, another reason for his offer was that these paladins were still eager to cast this spell after using it many times!","Helen felt like screaming. Each time she resurrected a dead person, she felt like a great miracle rose right before her!","“Re... resurrection...?!” Not only Liang Heihu and his party, but all other players standing by the entrance of Deadmines looked toward them in stupefaction.","The players who had played other games in the shop knew that all the techniques, immortal spells, and artifact-making skills were not faked!","They could all be learned and used in the real world. If it was true, then...!!??","At least all the players in the new shop including Dwarf Elder Sauk, Elf Elder Sewell, and Dicas all looked at them in disbelief.","Is there really such a spell?! If it is real, then the soldiers charging and fighting on battlegrounds will never fear death again!"]},{"number":696,"title":"Chapter 696 - Warrior-Mage-Priest System. the ‘Blizzard Workshop’ Has Such a Deep Understanding of Magic?!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","“Yes. We can resurrect you and heal you with Holy Light. If there’s a monster that’s hard to deal with in the mines, I think we can help you,” Commander Elven said.","“Ugh?” Dicas looked astonished, and so were the mages who were watching her play the game through the Spiritual Spell Visual Projection, thinking that they had heard it wrong. “Your Holy Light can bring people back to life? You can heal injuries?”","“Yes. Do you have a question, Lady?”","I use Holy Light too! Isn’t Holy Light a spell used to attack enemies?","Dicas was frustrated as she thought, I can’t even properly level up, but others can even resurrect people and heal injuries!","“You mean his Holy Light can heal people, but yours can’t?” Liang Heihu asked.","“Um... there seems to be a healing spell,” Dicas said morosely, “But it’s constantly interrupted and not useful...”","“Didn’t you put any points into talents?” Royal Princess Ji Yu asked casually.","“Haven’t you learned any skills?” Liang Heihu asked as well.","Since the game was a product of Blizzard, many old players had discovered that it had a talent tree just like the skill tree in Diablo 2.","However, the newbies didn’t know that...","“I...” Dicas had tears on her face since she had died many times and used all her money to repair her items. “I saw healing skills but... I have no money to learn them...”","She felt like crying. After all, she spent all her money to learn the offensive skills and couldn’t afford to learn the healing skills which looked ineffective to her.","As a high-level mage in the Royal Magic Union, she was so poor that she couldn’t even afford to learn spells in this mystical realm?!","What kind of mystical realm is this World of Warcraft? Why is it so hard?","“What... talents?!” Dicas froze and then pulled up the interface. “I clicked on it. I clicked them all! Such as Discipline and Mind Blast, etc.”","“There are three talents in each class,” Ji Yu said, “Check and see if you have the other two talents.”","“Ah...?” Baffled, Dicas opened the interface for talents. “Other talents...?”","How come this ‘online game’ is so complicated?","I’ve never seen these things in other mystical realms...","Dicas who had never played online games before had tears on her face.","With others’ help, Dicas finally discovered that there were three specializations of talents including Discipline, Holy, and Shadow, and shields and healing could be used on allies.","The members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion discovered that paladins also had three specializations of talents.","“I never knew that the Holy Light spells should be cast this way...?” The knights and mages who had never played online games before finally understood it.","I always thought that I’m a mage (warrior), but now I finally realized that it’s a class for healing people!","“I know what to do!” At this moment, an idea dawned on Royal Princess Ji Yu. “If Senior Nalan becomes too weak to block the attacks, we can help him with healing spells!”","Standing beside her, Liang Heihu said with sudden understanding, “Combining this Ms. Priest’s shield, I’m sure that we can pass this time!”","“???”","No! I’m a mage! A mage who can cast Holy Light spells which are as golden as an immortal spell!","I’m a woman who wants to focus on DPS! How come I became a nanny!","[TL Note: Chinese players give the healing-class players the nickname ‘nannies’ and call healing spells ‘milk’.]","While Dicas was still in a daze, she was pulled into the instance.","Of course, Commander Elven’s paladin character was also pulled in since only the paladins could cast Redemption.","So, the team consisted of Nalan Hongwu as the main tank, Commander Elven as the off-tank, one nanny, and two mages.","“I’m sure that they can pass it this time!” Royal Princess Ji Yu wasn’t a part of this exploration party anymore, but she was still excited, knowing that if the plan was proved effective, she could copy it and use it in her own team.","“I also think that we’ve finally found the solution!” Liang Heihu said excitedly.","The confused Dicas who was pulled into the exploration team was at a loss for words.","The weak mobs in the mine tunnels had been cleared long ago, and the five of them soon came before the boss.","Nalan Hongwu had kept his livestream on, and there were many people watching it.","“What is Old Duke doing here?” Some newbies among the audience were puzzled.","“The technical streamer is doing exploration on livestream.” Obviously, some audience members, such as the Lingyun Academy disciple Xi Qi had watched the livestream for a while now.","“They had been wiped out all afternoon. I hope they can pass this time.”","“Is this Deadmines really so difficult?”","...","“How come there is such a big monster?” As a priest who had difficulty fighting weak monsters, Dicas was alarmed when she saw this big ogre. “Can we fight it?”","“Heal us, and I ensure you that we can do it!” Mo Xian promised her with confidence.","Nalan Hongwu charged at the ogre without a fuss.","“Mages, turn the two elite mobs to sheep. Each of you take one!”","Dicas still kept her Spiritual Spell Visual Projection on, and the mages in the Royal Magic Union who were still watching widened their eyes at this scene. “What spell is this?!”","They had instantly turned two lively and extremely dangerous enemies into harmless little sheep?!","More importantly, this spell was instantly cast!","What did it mean? In these mages’ minds, the low-level mages could only instantly cast the super low-leveled spells such as small fireballs or Burning Spell. They had to spend time on chanting and casting if they wanted to use any spells that had greater power.","Even for saint-level masters, Polymorph: Sheep was an extremely powerful spell!","Unlike the players of the old shops who had seen the transfiguration spell in Harry Potter, the mages on Nora Continent had never seen it before...","They even had the feeling that the previously unknown Blizzard Workshop knew more about magic spells than themselves!","Although these mages hadn’t seen Redemption yet, Holy Word: Heal, Frost Nova, and Polymorph: Sheep were all classic spells on their own!","“This Blizzard Workshop... what is its background?!” Getting even more astonished, the mages who were watching exclaimed, “How can it be so knowledgeable in magic spells?!”","“It’s incredible!” a male mage commented.","The spells were simple and effective for mages of all levels, including low-level mages to level 8, 9, and even higher mages. “I’m sure that such spells will create a hot new magic spell trend!”","Eagerness grew stronger in everyone’s eyes."]},{"number":697,"title":"Chapter 697 - Doing Instance Throughout the Night. You People of East Continent Cultivate So Damn Enthusiastically?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","At this moment, Dicas shielded Nalan Hongwu with Power Word: Shield.","When the ogre smashed down its huge hammer, Nalan Hongwu raised his shield and blocked it as he had done before.","He blocked the attack without making any noise when the attack was perfectly absorbed by the combination of Power Word: Shield and Nalan Hongwu’s shield defense.","With the impact force totally absorbed, Nalan Hongwu stood his ground firmly.","When his shield was broken, a streak of Holy Light would fall on him before he received another Power Word: Shield.","Everyone’s eyes lit up at this scene.","This exploration was now on a different difficulty level compared to before!","If the previous exploration was on the hellish difficulty level, then the present one was on easy difficulty.","Only Nalan Hongwu needed to keep his eye on the boss to prevent it from lunging at others. As for others in the party...","“I’m doing DPS without thinking!” Mo Xian yelled.","The group was supported by the powerful main tank. Every time the ogre tried to bypass Nalan Hongwu and lunge at the players in the back, Nalan Hongwu would take the critical position and appear in its way. If it focused its attention on attacking Nalan Hongwu, it was impossible for it to win!","The players behind Nalan Hongwu felt no pressure at all.","It seemed as if an iron wall had been put up between them and the boss!","“I feel like we’re unrivaled this time!” Mo Xian yelled.","All kinds of spells and sword and saber techniques poured toward the boss without mercy!","“We passed it!”","Elated shouts sounded.","At this moment, they were filled with an explicable thrill. It was the elation of success after overcoming a difficult challenge!","“Wahahaha!” Mo Xian almost jumped up in joy. Putting down her virtual reality headset, she turned a circle sitting in her swivel chair, feeling as if they had created a new era!","Nalan Hongwu exhaled deeply and put down his virtual reality headset as well. In his livestream room, comments such as [Awesome] flooded the screen.","Seeing powerful enemies falling before them, the other members were also thrilled, including Ji Yu and Liang Heihu who had backed out voluntarily for this new strategy.","This was the result of collective wisdom, and they deserved a portion of the credit.","Smugly, Mo Yan sent a screenshot to Mr. Fang. [Sir, aren’t we good? Isn’t it a nice surprise?! Our self-improvement team killed the boss in the Deadmines all by ourselves! We also discovered a super powerful system of warrior, mage, and priest!]","[Are you envious of us?]","Busy with the official novels, Mr. Fang suddenly saw this QQ message.","He clicked it open and read it. “Hiss...”","[(Meme of Mr. Fang clapping) Awesome! Awesome!] Mr. Fang drew on his cigarette and said deeply, [But... you are using QQ shortcut keys to take this screenshot? Aren’t you controlling your character in the game?]","[Yeah... any problem with that?] Mo Xian said smugly, [We cleared all the nearby mobs. Don’t worry!]","[Wiped out,] Mr. Fang replied.","[What wiped out?]","[Look at the game. Your party was wiped out.]","[Impossible! You’re just jealous that this fairy created a new...] While she spoke, she switched to the game. [...Era?]","Her voice turned weaker and weaker when she froze at the scene before her.","Her screen was grey.","Only Paladin Elven was still swinging his sword against waves of mobs while yelling with indignation, “Ahhh-! Where are you guys?! How come you are all AFK!”","The party was wiped out!","[The commotion of the battle in the Deadmines will easily alert the patrolling mobs behind the gate. If you guys drop your guard, you’ll be wiped out.]","Then, Mo Xian saw Mr. Fang’s reply.","“!!!”","[Why didn’t you tell me earlier!] Mo Xian was frustrated.","...","After recovering their corpses in the Deadmines with great efforts, they cleared the patrolling mobs.","After defeating the monsters guarding the door, they entered the interior of the Deadmines and discovered that the interior was a huge spacious area.","It looked like a huge underground kingdom!","Walking deeper into the tunnels, they saw a huge lumber mill. Sneed was leading its goblins to process every wood piece with great care. His huge shredder not only could be used for cutting wood but was also a powerful mecha.","Walking down the wide spiral steps, they saw a huge furnace center. Smelter Gilnid and a team of engineers were mining all kinds of minerals and ores while all kinds of machines and cannons were being developed in this place.","“F*ck! Take positions! Don’t pull the patrolling mobs!”","“Pull over here! Pull over here!”","“Dropped!” Despite the occasional wipe-outs, the players worked more smoothly after getting familiar with the system of warrior, mage, and priest.","“Luxury jewelry ring?!” A ring with a blue name appeared before everyone.","“Blue rare quality?!”","“A ring?!”","After all, the players hadn’t seen a piece of jewelry yet after playing for so long! At this moment, all players were using white common equipment and green uncommon equipment!","The loot distribution system in World of Warcraft had three methods: rolling for points, free-for-all, and assigned by the leader.","Clearly, they chose the method of rolling which was fair and just.","“Give me 100 points!” Mo Xian exclaimed, excited that the first boss dropped something good.","She rolled 30 points.","“...”","“I’ll try it?” Nalan Hongwu rolled for need.","[TL Note: In group loots, all members in the party will get a rolling window with the item and two buttons. Party members can press the dice button to NEED roll for the item, or the gold coin to Greed roll for the item, or lastly the red X close button to pass on the item. The looting will first resolve all NEED rolls, if none then Greed rolls.]","[28 points.]","“...”","“Mine! Mine!” For the mages in the real world, the magic pieces of jewelry were quite valuable. Even though this ring was only a virtual item, Dicas was still excited, which made people wonder about her purpose in the mystical realm; cultivation or something else.","She immediately clicked on [Need Roll].","[90 points!]","“Hahahaha!”","[Teammate Fairy Liu obtained the item: luxury jewelry ring.]","[100 points]!","“Ahyaaaa!” Dicas almost spewed out blood.","“This ring... can only be used in this mystical realm, right? What’s so good about it?” The mages who were watching Dicas’ Spiritual Spell Visual Projection looked puzzled.","Aren’t you in the mystical realm for cultivation?!","How come you look as if you are here just to play in this so-called ‘online game’?","At this moment, their playtime was almost up.","“Should we...”","“Borrow some time from tomorrow?” Liu Ningyun suggested.","“Let’s do it! I will give you milk!” Dicas was excited at the good item that they had looted. “I can borrow 10 hours!”","Nalan Hongwu said, “I have no objections.”","“We need to return to our faction tonight...” Liu Ningyun said, “Let’s borrow two hours. With our current pace, we can kill the next boss if we’re careful...”","“I still have training tomorrow...” Commander Elven looked worried.","“Don’t worry! We’ll play at most three to four hours! Let’s go!” Mo Xian assured him.","“Okay! Okay! We’ll finish this instance and get offline in three to four hours!”","“Sir! Add three hours for us!”","– Three hours later –","“Clear the mobs before us!”","“Don’t pull the patrolling mobs!","They roared in the game.","When the group entered the depths of the mine, the players saw a huge ship equipped with many cannons docked on the vast underground lake.","They had never imagined that there would be such a powerful weapon in the depths of the mine.","This ship was the ultimate weapon that the Defias Brotherhood intended to use to destroy Stormwind City. The gifted artisans and builders had spent the first half of their lives on building Stormwind City, and the second half of their lives were invested in this ship.","This ship’s mission was to destroy the masterpiece that they had created in the first half of their lives.","“Add... five more hours! I think we’ll finish this instance soon!”","“!!??” The mages who were watching Dicas’ Spiritual Spell Visual Projection almost wet their pants when they heard it.","“They want to continue?!”","After the players fought their way onto the battleship, they encountered four bosses including First Mate Mr. Smite, Captain Greenskin, Murloc Cookie, and Leader VanCleef.","“It’s lunging at the back! Cast shields on the players at the back!”","“Pull it! Warriors, keep the aggro!”","“Ahh-! We did it!”","Dicas, Mo Xian, and others all had dark circles under their eyes. “Ahahaha! Look at what items they dropped!”","“???” The mages, who had been watching Dicas doing this instance led by people of the ‘East Continent’, looked out at the sky dumbfoundedly. “It’s daybreak now?!”","“You people of the East Continent cultivate so damn enthusiastically?”"]},{"number":698,"title":"Chapter 698 - The Least Lucky Player and the Luckiest Player, and the War Between Two of the Least Lucky Players","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","The Stonemason Brotherhood that had created Stormwind City, the grandest keep in the Alliance, received no pay and none of the glory that they deserved.","With their abilities, they should have had a glorious legend in the history of the Alliance, but due to many reasons, these talented artisans were left forever in the depths of this mine.","At this stage, the players were still patient enough to complete the quests one by one. During the process, they witnessed the Stonemason Brotherhood’s history and how the Defias Brotherhood fell from its glory to craziness and then to destruction.","This wasn’t a great story, and there were no heroes in this story.","In this story, a group of talented but tragic stonemasons wanted to receive their proper pay, but they destroyed themselves in the end.","Most players in World of Warcraft felt that the legendary heroes and great deeds were out of their reach.","However, after entering the game, the players had experienced the long and eventful history. The heart-warming scenes when paladins did their class quest, the many mistakes the newbies made in the battleground, the rolling battle between the lucky and the unlucky players for looting, and the simple and touching stories in the quests...","Any player could experience and sense these detailed things.","Every player, even the newbies who didn’t know to add points on talents, was touched by these stories and events.","When this group passed through Deadmines, it was almost 4 o’clock in the early morning.","“Move away! Let me loot the corpse!” Having won the jewelry ring with 100 points in rolling, Liu Ningyun yelled and reached out her Lucky Hand.","“Cruel Barb?!”","[Cruel Barb","One-Hand","30 – 57 Damage","Speed 2.8]","“Great attributes!”","Although the characters in the system version didn’t have digitized bodies, the equipment still had reference data, showing the quality of each item.","Since almost everyone was still using green uncommon items, this equipment was an ultimate item for them!","“100 points! Give me 100 points!” Nalan Hongwu yelled while he chose need.","He got 11 points.","“Ah! How come it is so low!” Nalan Hongwu howled, feeling heart-broken after working hard for one night.","“Hahahaha!” Commander Elven’s heart raced when he saw this number, thinking that he would finally get a reward for resurrecting corpses for one night.","“I’ll take it then!” Commander Elven said while laughing, “Thank you! Thank you very much!”","A prompt appeared on the game interface, [Griffin Knight Elven chose Need. (Need) 1 point.]","[Liquor Sword Immortal (ID) received the equipment – Cruel Barb.]","Looking at the blue single-handed sword in his backpack, Nalan Hongwu felt as if he had just leaped up from the lowest valley to the top of the world. “Ugh?”","“Ahahahahaha...!” He was feeling so much joy that he almost went crazy.","“Ah!” Seeing the points that he rolled out, Commander Elven let out a soul-wrenching howl, looking as sad as a kid who weighed 300 pounds.","When two unlucky players tried their luck, one of them must be even unluckier. By now, the battle between two unlucky players came to an end.","“...”","...","“Tomorrow... Ugh... we’ll continue the game the day after tomorrow!”","“Okay! Okay!”","“Tomorrow, I’ll help each of you get a weapon!” Obviously in a great mood, Nalan Hongwu added all of his new teammates as his friends regardless if he knew them before this or not.","For the first time, Dicas, who had come to the end of her patience while playing was a priest, felt the friendliness and charm of the game.","After all, some quests were beyond the ability of an individual, but they still could reach the end of the journey by helping and receiving help from players whom they had never met before.","After working with each other for some time and getting along, the players began to learn to entrust their safety to others.","Since mages and priests trusted that their teammates in the front could shoulder the responsibility of protecting the whole team, they could do DPS and heal as much as they could. The melee players could only charge at the enemies without a care when they believed that the mages and priests behind them were competent enough to cast shields and healing spells on them whenever they were at a disadvantage.","In this world, a friendship going beyond distance and boundaries formed among the players who were previously strangers, and the quests and instances helped them build a trust that was rarely seen among people.","Tomorrow, the day after tomorrow, and days in the future... their friendship and trust in each other would continue. For the players who had gotten good equipment, the friendship and trust were their gifts for those teammates who had worked hard for one night but obtained no rewards that they deserved.","It was now 4 AM in the early morning.","These players had greater energy than ordinary people, but it was still a big drain of their spirit and energy after battling in the virtual reality world for 20 hours without stop.","Glassy-eyed, the members of the party that explored the Deadmines walked out of the shop.","Commander Elven looked around. “Ugh?”","He saw that all other members of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion also walked out of the shop.","“How come you guys are so late too?” Commander Elven asked in surprise.","“We don’t want to come here tomorrow on our own! It is boring without everyone there.”","“Yeah. We must do things together, so we enjoyed ourselves today too!”","“Let’s go. Let’s go!” Elven suddenly froze.","In the game, they made friends whom they had gotten to know and trust. On top of that, in the real world outside the game, they had a group of friends who would stick together through all the hardships and merriment.","The knights of the Golden Griffin Knight Legion walked out together and talked among themselves.","“Have you finished the Deathmines?”","“You know what? Today, I found a treasure chest when doing a quest... There were several gold coins in it...!”","They walked away from the shop in the darkness while talking among themselves.","“Let’s go and have breakfast.”","“Now that you mention it, I’m starving!”","...","On the other side, it was almost dawn when people such as Liu Ningyun and Mo Xian returned to the Nanhua Faction.","The distant east sky began to lighten.","A few figures hurried across the Nanhua Square.","“Hurry! Hurry!”","“The morning lesson is about to begin soon!”","“We must greet Master before that... Hurry, or we’ll be late.”","“Huh?” In her courtyard, their master, the Xichi Spiritual Master, opened her eyes in the darkness.","“How come you people came so early today?”","“Um...” Their faces froze.","They had cultivation homework to do each night.","If their master learned that they had played all night...","They might be scolded...","Each faction had its own inheritance. It wasn’t right to dump their unique ways and become a copycat. They needed to get inspirations to improve themselves and thus find their own path.","They couldn’t achieve that if they didn’t do their own cultivation work.","“Um...” Yue Yan quickly thought of an explanation. “I had a sudden understanding about the Immortal Dao, so I called over senior sisters to talk about it.”","“A collective session of cultivation?” The Xichi Spiritual Master froze for a second and then said, “Indeed. The cultivation of Immortal Dao is like sailing against the current; you’ll fall behind if you don’t move ahead. Um, good. It’s good to hear that you’re working so hard on it.”","“Eh... hehe... yeah, we worked hard on cultivation through the night.” With dark circles under her eyes, Yue Yan quickly winked at each other to pass the message.","“...”","The Xichi Spiritual Master suddenly changed the subject. “Then, have you passed the Deadmines?”","“We have!”","“Um...”"]},{"number":699,"title":"Chapter 699 - Leader, how come the milk is green?","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","The Alliance had the Deadmines, and the Horde had the Wailing Cavern. The alliance had paladins, and the Horde had shamans. Generally, both sides were in a balance.","Since many players had watched the livestream, the system of warriors, mages, and priests spread out, giving the Horde players some good inspirations to pass the seemingly-impossible instance of Wailing Cavern.","On the next day, the Brotherhood assassins who played as rogues began to copy this setup after finding this instance in the territory of the Horde.","The Undead Rogue Harrison yelled standing at the entrance of the Wailing Cavern, “Self-improvement team for the Wailing Cavern is calling for a nanny and a main tank!”","They had obviously heard the terms such as ‘main tank’ from Mr. Fang and just picked them up.","Nalan Mingxue shouted, “We have a main tank for the Wailing Cavern. We’ll begin whenever a nanny joins us!”","– On the side of the Alliance –","At the entrance of the Deadmines, some students of Shengjing Academy began yelling, “We need a mage to begin the exploration of Deadmines. Four players waiting on one!”","[Sauk Stonehammer requests to join the party.]","“Hunter?” He was rejected.","[Mage Adolf requests to join the party.]","“Mage?” Confirmed.","“Do you know how to do it?”","“Of course.” Adolf looked baffled. I’m a level 9 mage. How can I not know how to be a mage?","“Good! Come on!”","The exploration began immediately.","Two warriors, one healing paladin, and two mages reached the first boss without issues and didn’t talk as well.","“Two mages, turn the two elite mobs to sheep. I’ll hold off the boss.” Familiar with this strategy, the students of Shengjing Academy charged forward.","Meanwhile, one of the elite mobs had been turned into a sheep.","But the other elite mob remained the same...","“What sheep?” Adolf looked puzzled.","“Polymorph: Sheep!” A voice yelled.","At this moment, an arrow shot into the main tank’s shoulder.","“Do we have such a spell?” Adolf said in confusion.","“Didn’t you say that you know what is going on?” the healing paladin yelled as well.","“I’m a great mage!”","The moment he said it, a mob shot an arrow onto the healing paladin’s head.","While the healing paladin was about to cast a spell, another arrow hit him.","“Milk?! Where’s the milk?”","“Turn it into a sheep! How come the mob is still shooting at me?!”","“Mage, can you do your job or not?!”","“I can!”","“Heal us! We’re going to die!”","“Turn it into a sheep!”","The team was wiped out!","“...Damn it!”","Adolf’s game interface showed that he had been kicked out of the party.","“...”","After being kicked out several times, Adolf and Dwarf Elder Sauk met each other at the entrance. “...”","“This one... does it need several players to pass?”","“With my skills in magic spells, I’m better than these ordinary people. Let me try it first...”","One hour later, they came back after recovering corpses several times. “...”","“Forget it. Let’s level up first...”","Looking embarrassed, they went to level up.","...","– On the other side –","As the shop owner, Mr. Fang couldn’t spend all his time killing opponents every day in the wilderness. After all, these people were all players and customers of his shops.","Therefore, he created a night elf rogue character in the Alliance. When he had time, he would earn some coins, open chests, and explore the histories about different places of World of Warcraft left in the relics and libraries to improve the content of the official novels.","Meanwhile, Yu Zhiwei’s book store in Jiuhua City which sold the official novel of Diablo 2 had become one of the biggest book stores in the city.","Of course, now that Yu Zhiwei was working in Origins Internet Café, she had asked a friend to manage the book store for her.","Right now, the book store had begun selling the new official novel – Rise of the Horde.","In the new shop, only the e-book was on sale. Physical books hadn’t been published yet.","Meanwhile, Dungeon Fighter Online had launched its official website and updated the e-book of its official novel.","...","Deadmines, Wailing Cavern, Stormwind Stockade, Shadowfang Keep... the players left their footprints in every instance all over the world.","Of course, players such as Elder Sauk and Adolf were still concentrating on leveling up and doing quests after being rejected by other players.","Of course, their progresses were not slow.","Some players even concentrated on professions such as engineering, blacksmithing, and herbalism.","Lately, the number of people watching Mr. Dirk’s Spiritual Spell Visual Projection had increased.","In fact, some orcs had traveled a long distance to come to the shop, so had the mages who had watched Dicas play World of Warcraft.","There were more players in the shop now.","The busiest time in the shop was the afternoon, and it got quite boisterous during this period.","Since Li Xin’er had been moved from the Yuanyang City Shop to the new shop, Mr. Fang didn’t have to keep an eye on the shop.","“Ms. Dicas, what raid are you doing today?!”","“Ms. Dicas, do you have time to take me in your party?!”","“It’s said that Ms. Dicas is exploring the new instance Scarlet Monastery? Has she looted any good equipment?”","“I heard... the border of the Orc Kingdom had a situation lately?” Some orcs walked through the bustling crows before the gate of the shop.","“I heard about it. The people of a small town vanished for no reason. I wonder what happened.”","“The king is investigating it. It’s a minor incident.”","...","“I heard that Sala and other young people have looted many blue rare items. I can’t fall behind!” In the new shop in Canglan City, Elder Sewell of the Elf Clan sat together with other elves and entered the game with a cup of milk tea in her hand.","“Elder, I heard that raiding instances are the most popular. They got great equipment in the instances,” an elite of the Elder Guard Team said, “The most difficult one right now is Scarlet Monastery. Should we try it?”","– One hour later –","Elder Sewell gave the elves sitting around her a long look. “I think I’d better try in another party first.”","“...”","“Nanny is needed in Scarlet Monastery!”","“Healing is needed in Scarlet Monastery!”","“Four members wait for one nanny! A real healer!”","“Oh...? So, healer is a nanny? This name is so strange.” Elder Sewell looked puzzled.","“But... what do they mean by asking for real healers?” Having never raided instances before, Elder Sewell was confused and frustrated.","Adolf and Sauk were also frustrated.","Adolf even felt like his disciple was doing better than him. He didn’t like this situation!","However, he was too proud to ask his disciple to take him into her party.","“Let’s form a party ourselves!” Adolf said.","Although he hadn’t done raids before, he heard about the mechanisms and setups from his high-level disciple. Therefore, he had a rough idea of what was going on.","“I call tank.” Elder Sauk volunteered.","Adolf yelled, “Self-improvement team for Scarlet Monastery! We are looking for a nanny and a DPS!”","Soon, a rogue joined them.","The tank was a warrior of the Dwarf Clan. Obviously, Elder Sauk had enlisted one of his own men.","“Self-Improvement Team for Scarlet Monastery. Four members wait for one! We need a nanny!”","“How come they are all calling for nannies...?”","Elder Sewell glanced at her Rejuvenation and said, “I can heal too... should I...?”","“Sewell requests to join the party.”","“Druid?” Adolf and Elder Sauk exchanged a look. But looking at the name... an acquaintance?","They added her first. “Elder Sewell, we’re old friends, but we need a healer.”","“We can’t do it without a nanny,” the rogue on the side agreed. “We don’t even have to try.”","“I can heal!” Elder Sewell casually cast Rejuvenation.","Different from Holy Light, this was a life presence as if the spring returned to the land. After she cast the spell, the target of the spell, Adolf, immediately felt an intense life presence.","“Eh?” Adolf nodded and said, “This is indeed a healing spell! Now that we’ve got everyone, let’s enter together.”","“Okay! Okay!” Elder Sewell was excited that she finally found a team.","“Leader... How come her milk is green...?” At this moment, the rogue glanced at his poisoned dagger and saw that it was also green."]},{"number":700,"title":"Chapter 700 - You...Put Poison in the Milk?!","paragraphs":["Translator: Noodletown Translations Editor: Noodletown Translations","Scarlet Monastery was in the Tirisfal Glades to the northwest of Undercity, the northeast of the spawn place for undead players.","For undead players who liked to explore the land, they had found this place long ago. But due to its difficulty level, players lower than level 30 couldn’t possibly pass it, which was why no one had wasted time on this higher-level instance even though they had found it.","Only players over level 30 could enter and explore it.","Different from the Deadmines, which solely belonged to the Alliance, and the Wailing Cavern, which solely belonged to the Horde, Scarlet Monastery was accessible to both Alliance and Horde players under the instruction of their quests. Of course, since it was closer to Undercity of the Horde, it was friendlier to Horde players.","The Scarlet Crusade had fought the Scourge Legion on the front lines. Many paladins and priests, who fought in the name of the Holy Light and justice, and countless excellent warriors had joined the Scarlet Crusade with glory, loyalty, and pride in their hearts. They had the lofty dream of eliminating all the undead creatures on Azeroth.","However, they had now almost been driven to crazy by their hunger for revenge. They thought that all the people not wearing crusade uniforms had contracted the undead plague, and they mercilessly tortured the innocent people, who they suspected to have contracted this plague.","This was a super large building consisting of four instance zones. The monastery had once been the pride of the Kingdom of Lordaeron and the holy place for pilgrims. However, after the war, it became an important stronghold for the fanatic Scarlet Crusaders who were the fiercest enemies of the undead race.","This was a castle-like grand building full of Scarlet Crusaders. The portals of the four instance zones were located in the graveyard, library, armory, and cathedral respectively. The magic portals leading to the four instances were called gate 1, 2, 3 and 4 by the players in accordance to their positions. The difficulty level increased in the order of gate 1, 4, 3 and 2.","Most players wouldn’t waste their time on instance zone No.1 due to its low difficulty level and poor quality of item drops. After all, the players who had diligently explored and raided previous instances had obtained many good pieces of equipment.","Dicas’s party naturally wouldn’t enter this instance zone. After watching Dicas’s raid for a while, Mage Adolf led his party directly toward instance No.4.","“Follow me! Don’t waste time on the Horde players. Enter it directly!” Adolf obviously knew the situation.","His party had one mage, one hunter, one warrior, one druid, and one rogue.","“After we enter, we need to first clear the Scarlet Crusaders along the corridor.” While running forward, Adolf tossed orders to his team, sounding like an old timer with a lot of experience.","“Leader, are you experienced?” the rogue asked cautiously.","It was quite difficult to find a player who could pass the Scarlet Monastery at this point in the game.","“Of course!” Adolf was very confident in himself. As a grand level 9 mage, he had watched the process and was sure that this instance wouldn’t be difficult for him.","“Follow my orders, and I’ll help you pass at least two instances.”","“Okay! Okay! Okay! I’ll follow your orders all the way!” Thinking that he had found a great player, the rogue said in exhilaration.","“They are frozen by Frost Nova! Do damage now!”","“Heal the tank!”","“Missed some. Hunter, unleash the bears and stop them!”","“...”","The first part of the raid went on smoothly. Although some members hadn’t done instances before, they were masters in the real world and could easily deal with the mobs.","After the corridor, they came into a big garden-like courtyard.","The group walked across the courtyard cautiously, trying not to alert more Scarlet Crusaders as they cleared the ones in the courtyard.","Discovering the invaders, herds of Scarlet Crusaders swarmed out and attacked them in the narrow corridor.","The dwarf warrior and Elder Sauk’s bear managed to block the bulk of these fearless zealots with the advantage of the terrain. The Scarlet Crusaders who managed to bypass the two iron walls and lunged at the players at the back were frozen by Adolf’s Frost Nova and then instantly and easily killed by the rogue using his dagger with shining chilly lights reflecting off it.","Even though a few mobs managed to charge to the back, they were not enough to pose any great danger.","“How come I feel like... my HP is not right...”","The dwarf main tank who stood before the herds of mobs obviously couldn’t block and hold off all the attacks.","Although the green lights of Rejuvenation kept flashing, his HP got even lower while more wounds appeared on his body.","“Ah-!” With a scream, the dwarf warrior fell to the ground.","“How come the tank is down?”","“I’m healing...” Elder Sewell was puzzled too. Meanwhile, the mobs rushed toward the backline.","“I just cast Frost Nova!” Adolf roared immediately, “Let the bear take more of them! We will eliminate these mobs together!”","“Hurry! Hurry!”","“Healing! Heal us!”","“???” They still felt like their HPs were dropping quickly!","“Heal me!” Covered in blood, Elder Sauk battled and roared from the center of a large group of Scarlet Crusaders.","A green light bloomed and shined over his head.","The wounds on his body healed at snail speed. “???”","“Milk! Give me milk!” On the other side, the rogue had used all his skills while there were still several Scarlet Crusaders surrounded him!","About to wave her wand, Elder Sewell heard another roar. A blood-covered mage jumped out from the siege of Scarlet Crusaders while yelling hoarsely, “Milk! Give me milk-!”","“Give me milk-!” His face covered in blood, Elder Sauk yelled wildly.","“Me! Give me milk! I’m dying!” The rogue player reached out a hand from the herd of mobs and yelled with tears on his face.","“Give me milk! Ahh-!” A big herd of mobs were in hot pursue of Adolf.","Turning her eyes from Elder Sauk to the rogue to Adolf and then back to Elder Sauk, Elder Sewell felt dizzy while listening to these loud yells. “How can I give you guys milk in such a situation?!”","Her beautiful bright eyes started to turn around...!","Milk! Milk! Milk! How can I give milk to you guys at the same time!? Do I look like I have ten ‘breasts’?","Three minutes later, the five of them all had grey screens.","“What’s going on...?” They had watched Dicas do this with ease...","How come we had been wiped out!? We haven’t even seen the boss yet!","Since there were no druids in the real world, and few players chose this class in the game, these players had the feeling that there was something wrong with this ‘milk’.","In the graveyard, five transparent souls appeared. “...”","“How come the milk was not effective...?” The dwarf warrior said loudly, “My HP got lower with this milk!”","“Leader...” The rogue glanced at his poisoned dagger and remembered the green spell, and he voiced his doubt hesitatantly, “I suspect... the milk... is poisonous!”","“What?!” Remembering Rejuvenation which looked as green as a poisonous liquid, Dwarf Elder Sauk, who had been beaten so hard the mobs that his mouth was filled with blood, held his wounds and glared at Elder Sewell. “You... You put poison in the milk?!”"]}]);
